  ('A-jupiter_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"jupiter","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-jupiter_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry-jupiter-opposition-mercury', 'relationship-jupiter-opposition-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-jupiter_B-mercury_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-jupiter_B-mercury_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Jupiter Opposition Mercury', null, 'This person often challenges the scale of your thinking.

You may approach a situation by looking at what is practical, immediate, or supported by the facts in front of you, while they are more interested in where things could lead or what larger meaning might be unfolding. Conversations between you can stretch your perspective, even when you do not agree. Sometimes their outlook feels inspiring and helps you see beyond your usual assumptions. Other times, it can seem like they are overlooking important details in favor of a bigger vision.

This connection works best when you combine those different strengths. They broaden the conversation and help you consider possibilities you might not have explored, while you bring focus and help identify what is actually workable. Together, you can balance vision with practicality.

When the tension rises, both of you can become attached to your own version of the truth. They may experience you as limiting or overly cautious. You may experience them as disconnected from what is actually possible. The gift of this aspect is perspective, but under stress, perspective can harden into certainty, and certainty leaves little room to learn from one another.

The invitation here is to stop treating the difference as a problem to solve. Their perspective can open doors you would never have considered, while your judgment keeps those possibilities connected to reality. Neither view is enough on its own. The real strength of this connection comes when vision and discernment work together, turning possibility into a roadmap you can actually follow.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person often challenges the scale of your thinking.\n\nYou may approach a situation by looking at what is practical, immediate, or supported by the facts in front of you, while they are more interested in where things could lead or what larger meaning might be unfolding. Conversations between you can stretch your perspective, even when you do not agree. Sometimes their outlook feels inspiring and helps you see beyond your usual assumptions. Other times, it can seem like they are overlooking important details in favor of a bigger vision.\n\nThis connection works best when you combine those different strengths. They broaden the conversation and help you consider possibilities you might not have explored, while you bring focus and help identify what is actually workable. Together, you can balance vision with practicality.\n\nWhen the tension rises, both of you can become attached to your own version of the truth. They may experience you as limiting or overly cautious. You may experience them as disconnected from what is actually possible. The gift of this aspect is perspective, but under stress, perspective can harden into certainty, and certainty leaves little room to learn from one another.\n\nThe invitation here is to stop treating the difference as a problem to solve. Their perspective can open doors you would never have considered, while your judgment keeps those possibilities connected to reality. Neither view is enough on its own. The real strength of this connection comes when vision and discernment work together, turning possibility into a roadmap you can actually follow."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"When the tension rises, both of you can become attached to your own version of the truth. They may experience you as limiting or overly cautious. You may experience them as disconnected from what is actually possible. The gift of this aspect is perspective, but under stress, perspective can harden into certainty, and certainty leaves little room to learn from one another."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The invitation here is to stop treating the difference as a problem to solve. Their perspective can open doors you would never have considered, while your judgment keeps those possibilities connected to reality. Neither view is enough on its own. The real strength of this connection comes when vision and discernment work together, turning possibility into a roadmap you can actually follow."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-jupiter_B-mercury_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s growth meets B''s mind. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person often challenges the scale of your thinking.\n\nYou may approach a situation by looking at what is practical, immediate, or supported by the facts in front of you, while they are more interested in where things could lead or what larger meaning might be unfolding. Conversations between you can stretch your perspective, even when you do not agree. Sometimes their outlook feels inspiring and helps you see beyond your usual assumptions. Other times, it can seem like they are overlooking important details in favor of a bigger vision.\n\nThis connection works best when you combine those different strengths. They broaden the conversation and help you consider possibilities you might not have explored, while you bring focus and help identify what is actually workable. Together, you can balance vision with practicality.\n\nWhen the tension rises, both of you can become attached to your own version of the truth. Th