.","advice":"This connection can help you step outside your comfort zone and trust yourself more. It encourages growth through action, reminding you that confidence is built by taking meaningful steps forward. Be willing to take the chance when it aligns with your goals and values. Just remember that enthusiasm is most powerful when it is paired with preparation and intention.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry-mars-trine-jupiter', 'relationship-mars-trine-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-jupiter_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-jupiter_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Trine Jupiter', null, 'This person makes you believe you can do it. Their confidence feeds your drive. Your drive gives their optimism somewhere to go. Together, you tend to move toward things instead of talking yourselves out of them. What feels intimidating alone can feel possible together.

You bring out each other''s courage. You back each other''s goals, encourage each other''s risks, and make it easier to trust your own abilities. There is a natural sense of momentum here. Less second-guessing. More doing.

The challenge is that things come so easily between you that you may not push yourselves to use the gift. It feels good to believe in what is possible. It is another thing to actually commit to it.

This connection offers confidence. The invitation is to do something with it. Potential is not the same as movement. Let the encouragement land. Take the step. Trust yourself enough to begin.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person makes you believe you can do it. Their confidence feeds your drive. Your drive gives their optimism somewhere to go. Together, you tend to move toward things instead of talking yourselves out of them. What feels intimidating alone can feel possible together.\n\nYou bring out each other''s courage. You back each other''s goals, encourage each other''s risks, and make it easier to trust your own abilities. There is a natural sense of momentum here. Less second-guessing. More doing.\n\nThe challenge is that things come so easily between you that you may not push yourselves to use the gift. It feels good to believe in what is possible. It is another thing to actually commit to it.\n\nThis connection offers confidence. The invitation is to do something with it. Potential is not the same as movement. Let the encouragement land. Take the step. Trust yourself enough to begin."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that things come so easily between you that you may not push yourselves to use the gift. It feels good to believe in what is possible. It is another thing to actually commit to it."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This connection offers confidence. The invitation is to do something with it. Potential is not the same as movement. Let the encouragement land. Take the step. Trust yourself enough to begin."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-jupiter_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s growth. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This person makes you believe you can do it. Their confidence feeds your drive. Your drive gives their optimism somewhere to go. Together, you tend to move toward things instead of talking yourselves out of them. What feels intimidating alone can feel possible together.\n\nYou bring out each other''s courage. You back each other''s goals, encourage each other''s risks, and make it easier to trust your own abilities. There is a natural sense of momentum here. Less second-guessing. More doing.\n\nThe challenge is that things come so easily between you that you may not push yourselves to use the gift. It feels good to believe in what is possible. It is another thing to actually commit to it.\n\nThis connection offers confidence. The invitation is to do something with it. Potential is not the same as movement. Let the encouragement land. Take the step. Trust yourself enough to begin.","tension":"The challenge is that things come so easily between you that you may not push yourselves to use the gift. It feels good to believe in what is possible. It is another thing to actually commit to it.","advice":"This connection offers confidence. The invitation is to do something with it. Potential is not the same as movement. Let the encouragement land. Take the step. Trust yourself enough to begin.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"mars","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry-mars-conjunction-mars', 'relationship-mars-conjunction-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-mars_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-mars_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Conjunction Mars', null, 'You and this person are likely wired to take action in similar ways. When one of you feels motivated, the other usually understands exactly where that energy is coming from. Being around each other can create momentum. You may feel more confident, more focused, and more willing to go after what matters.

One of the biggest strengths of this connection is how much you can inspire each other. You recognize each other''s drive because it looks familiar. Instead of having to justify your goals, you may feel supported by someone who naturally understands ambition, initiative, and the desire to make things happen.

That shared intensity often shows up physically too. Mars is the body as much as the will, and when two drives run at the same tempo, the attraction tends to be direct and easy to feel. You may find you match each other well, that desire runs at a similar pace, and that the physical side of things needs very little translation. There is a straightforwardness here, a sense of wanting in the same key.

When you channel that energy well, you can accomplish a lot together. You may encourage each other to take risks, stay committed to your goals, and keep moving forward when things get challenging. There is a strong sense of possibility here, as if the two of you can create more together than either of you could alone.

The growth opportunity comes when your strengths become overused. Two highly driven people can easily slip into power struggles, impatience, or competition. You may both want to lead, both feel strongly about your approach, or both react quickly when frustrated. In those moments, it is important to remember that being right is not the same as moving forward.

The key is to stay focused on the bigger picture. When you direct your shared energy toward a common goal, this connection becomes incredibly productive. Instead of competing with each other, challenge yourselves to build, create, and grow together. Your greatest success comes when you act as partners, not opponents.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You and this person are likely wired to take action in similar ways. When one of you feels motivated, the other usually understands exactly where that energy is coming from. Being around each other can create momentum. You may feel more confident, more focused, and more willing to go after what matters.\n\nOne of the biggest strengths of this connection is how much you can inspire each other. You recognize each other''s drive because it looks familiar. Instead of having to justify your goals, you may feel supported by someone who naturally understands ambition, initiative, and the desire to make things happen.\n\nThat shared intensity often shows up physically too. Mars is the body as much as the will, and when two drives run at the same tempo, the attraction tends to be direct and easy to feel. You may find you match each other well, that desire runs at a similar pace, and that the physical side of things needs very little translation. There is a straightforwardness here, a sense of wanting in the same key.\n\nWhen you channel that energy well, you can accomplish a lot together. You may encourage each other to take risks, stay committed to your goals, and keep moving forward when things get challenging. There is a strong sense of possibility here, as if the two of you can create more together than either of you could alone.\n\nThe growth opportunity comes when your strengths become overused. Two highly driven people can easily slip into power struggles, impatience, or competition. You may both want to lead, both feel strongly about your approach, or both react quickly when frustrated. In those moments, it is important to remember that being right is not the same as moving forward.\n\nThe key is to stay focused on the bigger picture. When you direct your shared energy toward a common goal, this connection becomes incredibly productive. Instead of competing with each other, challenge yourselves to build, create, and grow together. Your greatest success comes when you act as partners, not opponents."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The growth opportunity comes when your strengths become overused. Two highly driven people can easily slip into power struggles, impatience, or competition. You may both want to lead, both feel strongly about your approach, or both react quickly when frustrated. In those moments, it is important to remember that being right is not the same as moving forward."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The key is to stay focused on the bigger picture. When you direct your shared energy toward a common goal, this connection becomes incredibly productive. Instead of competing with each other, challenge yourselves to build, create, and grow together. Your greatest success comes when you act as partners, not opponents."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-mars_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Your drives fire the same way. Strong physical charge, aligned energy, and head-on collision when you disagree. Great in bed, combustible in a fight. Failure mode: two people who both push and neither yields. Point the shared energy at a common goal; learn to fight without trying to win.","summaryDeep":"You and this person are likely wired to take action in similar ways. When one of you feels motivated, the other usually understands exactly where that energy is coming from. Being around each other can create momentum. You may feel more confident, more focused, and more willing to go after what matters.\n\nOne of the biggest strengths of this connection is how much you can inspire each other. You recognize each other''s drive because it looks familiar. Instead of having to justify your goals, you may feel supported by someone who naturally understands ambition, initiative, and the desire to make things happen.\n\nThat shared intensity often shows up physically too. Mars is the body as much as the will, and when two drives run at the same tempo, the attraction tends to be direct and easy to feel. You may find you match each other well, that desire runs at a similar pace, and that the physical side of things needs very little translation. There is a straightforwardness here, a sense of wanting in the same key.\n\nWhen you channel that energy well, you can accomplish a lot together. You may encourage each other to take risks, stay committed to your goals, and keep moving forward when things get challenging. There is a strong sense of possibility here, as if the two of you can create more together than either of you could alone.\n\nThe growth opportunity comes when your strengths become overused. Two highly driven people can easily slip into power struggles, impatience, or competition. You may both want to lead, both feel strongly about your approach, or both react quickly when frustrated. In those moments, it is important to remember that being right is not the same as moving forward.\n\nThe key is to stay focused on the bigger picture. When you direct your shared energy toward a common goal, this connection becomes incredibly productive. Instead of competing with each other, challenge yourselves to build, create, and grow together. Your greatest success comes when you act as partners, not opponents.","tension":"The growth opportunity comes when your strengths become overused. Two highly driven people can easily slip into power struggles, impatience, or competition. You may both want to lead, both feel strongly about your approach, or both react quickly when frustrated. In those moments, it is important to remember that being right is not the same as moving forward.","advice":"The key is to stay focused on the bigger picture. When you direct your shared energy toward a common goal, this connection becomes incredibly productive. Instead of competing with each other, challenge yourselves to build, create, and grow together. Your greatest success comes when you act as partners, not opponents.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"mars","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry-mars-opposition-mars', 'relationship-mars-opposition-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-mars_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-mars_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Opposition Mars', null, 'You and this person may push in very different ways. One of you wants to act now. The other wants to wait. One of you charges directly at the problem. The other holds position, studies the room, or refuses to be moved before they are ready.

This can be compelling because the other person has something you may not naturally use. Their boldness may pull you forward. Their patience may slow you down in a way you need. Their way of handling pressure may frustrate you, but it can also show you another kind of strength.

When this works, the two of you cover more ground together. One person brings momentum. The other brings timing. One person pushes the door open. The other makes sure it is the right door. The difference can become strategy instead of conflict.

This difference can carry into the physical side too. Mars is the body as much as the will, and here desire often runs on a little tension. One of you may move faster than the other, want when the other is holding back, or chase a rhythm the other does not quite share. That gap can be charged in a good way, but it asks you to find a pace that actually works for both bodies rather than assuming one speed fits.

The harder part is that ordinary decisions can turn into a tug of war. You want to go one way, they want to go another. You want movement, they want control. They may feel rushed by you, while you may feel blocked by them. Before long, the issue is no longer the plan. It is who gets to decide the pace.

Do not make the other person''s way of acting into the enemy. Decide what you are trying to accomplish first. Once you know the goal, the two different approaches can work together instead of pulling the relationship apart.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You and this person may push in very different ways. One of you wants to act now. The other wants to wait. One of you charges directly at the problem. The other holds position, studies the room, or refuses to be moved before they are ready.\n\nThis can be compelling because the other person has something you may not naturally use. Their boldness may pull you forward. Their patience may slow you down in a way you need. Their way of handling pressure may frustrate you, but it can also show you another kind of strength.\n\nWhen this works, the two of you cover more ground together. One person brings momentum. The other brings timing. One person pushes the door open. The other makes sure it is the right door. The difference can become strategy instead of conflict.\n\nThis difference can carry into the physical side too. Mars is the body as much as the will, and here desire often runs on a little tension. One of you may move faster than the other, want when the other is holding back, or chase a rhythm the other does not quite share. That gap can be charged in a good way, but it asks you to find a pace that actually works for both bodies rather than assuming one speed fits.\n\nThe harder part is that ordinary decisions can turn into a tug of war. You want to go one way, they want to go another. You want movement, they want control. They may feel rushed by you, while you may feel blocked by them. Before long, the issue is no longer the plan. It is who gets to decide the pace.\n\nDo not make the other person''s way of acting into the enemy. Decide what you are trying to accomplish first. Once you know the goal, the two different approaches can work together instead of pulling the relationship apart."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part is that ordinary decisions can turn into a tug of war. You want to go one way, they want to go another. You want movement, they want control. They may feel rushed by you, while you may feel blocked by them. Before long, the issue is no longer the plan. It is who gets to decide the pace."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Do not make the other person''s way of acting into the enemy. Decide what you are trying to accomplish first. Once you know the goal, the two different approaches can work together instead of pulling the relationship apart."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-mars_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Directly opposing drives. You want the same intensity aimed in opposite directions - magnetic and exhausting. Failure mode: every difference becomes a contest. Take turns leading, agree on direction first, and stop treating the relationship as a fight to win.","summaryDeep":"You and this person may push in very different ways. One of you wants to act now. The other wants to wait. One of you charges directly at the problem. The other holds position, studies the room, or refuses to be moved before they are ready.\n\nThis can be compelling because the other person has something you may not naturally use. Their boldness may pull you forward. Their patience may slow you down in a way you need. Their way of handling pressure may frustrate you, but it can also show you another kind of strength.\n\nWhen this works, the two of you cover more ground together. One person brings momentum. The other brings timing. One person pushes the door open. The other makes sure it is the right door. The difference can become strategy instead of conflict.\n\nThis difference can carry into the physical side too. Mars is the body as much as the will, and here desire often runs on a little tension. One of you may move faster than the other, want when the other is holding back, or chase a rhythm the other does not quite share. That gap can be charged in a good way, but it asks you to find a pace that actually works for both bodies rather than assuming one speed fits.\n\nThe harder part is that ordinary decisions can turn into a tug of war. You want to go one way, they want to go another. You want movement, they want control. They may feel rushed by you, while you may feel blocked by them. Before long, the issue is no longer the plan. It is who gets to decide the pace.\n\nDo not make the other person''s way of acting into the enemy. Decide what you are trying to accomplish first. Once you know the goal, the two different approaches can work together instead of pulling the relationship apart.","tension":"The harder part is that ordinary decisions can turn into a tug of war. You want to go one way, they want to go another. You want movement, they want control. They may feel rushed by you, while you may feel blocked by them. Before long, the issue is no longer the plan. It is who gets to decide the pace.","advice":"Do not make the other person''s way of acting into the enemy. Decide what you are trying to accomplish first. Once you know the goal, the two different approaches can work together instead of pulling the relationship apart.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"mars","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry-mars-sextile-mars', 'relationship-mars-sextile-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-mars_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-mars_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Sextile Mars', null, 'There is a natural sense that the two of you can get things moving together, but it tends to show up once someone takes action. The support is there from the start, yet it often needs a first step before it becomes real momentum. When one of you gets going, the other usually knows how to jump in and help.

When this works, you bring out each other''s motivation without making it feel like pressure. One person starts the engine, the other helps keep it running. You may find that projects move faster, problems feel easier to tackle, and goals seem more achievable when you''re working as a team. There is a reassuring sense that your effort won''t be wasted because the other person is likely to meet you halfway.

One of the strengths of this aspect is how practical it is. It often shows up in everyday moments rather than big dramatic ones. You help each other follow through, solve problems together, and turn plans into something tangible. Over time, that builds trust. You learn that when one of you reaches out, the other is usually willing to show up and contribute.

The physical side tends to follow the same rule as the rest of this contact. Mars is the body as much as the will, and the attraction here is real but responsive, the kind that warms up when someone leans in rather than waiting. When you actually meet each other, the chemistry tends to be there. It just rarely lights itself.

A pattern to watch for is assuming that because the connection feels easy, it will take care of itself. You may both agree on what you want, see the opportunity in front of you, and still keep putting off the first step. Not because you lack motivation, but because neither of you feels enough pressure to act right away.

The growth here comes from being intentional. Momentum builds when someone decides to start instead of waiting to feel ready. The more you support each other''s goals, follow through on plans, and turn ideas into action, the stronger this dynamic becomes. What looks like potential on paper becomes real progress when one of you is willing to get the ball rolling.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is a natural sense that the two of you can get things moving together, but it tends to show up once someone takes action. The support is there from the start, yet it often needs a first step before it becomes real momentum. When one of you gets going, the other usually knows how to jump in and help.\n\nWhen this works, you bring out each other''s motivation without making it feel like pressure. One person starts the engine, the other helps keep it running. You may find that projects move faster, problems feel easier to tackle, and goals seem more achievable when you''re working as a team. There is a reassuring sense that your effort won''t be wasted because the other person is likely to meet you halfway.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is how practical it is. It often shows up in everyday moments rather than big dramatic ones. You help each other follow through, solve problems together, and turn plans into something tangible. Over time, that builds trust. You learn that when one of you reaches out, the other is usually willing to show up and contribute.\n\nThe physical side tends to follow the same rule as the rest of this contact. Mars is the body as much as the will, and the attraction here is real but responsive, the kind that warms up when someone leans in rather than waiting. When you actually meet each other, the chemistry tends to be there. It just rarely lights itself.\n\nA pattern to watch for is assuming that because the connection feels easy, it will take care of itself. You may both agree on what you want, see the opportunity in front of you, and still keep putting off the first step. Not because you lack motivation, but because neither of you feels enough pressure to act right away.\n\nThe growth here comes from being intentional. Momentum builds when someone decides to start instead of waiting to feel ready. The more you support each other''s goals, follow through on plans, and turn ideas into action, the stronger this dynamic becomes. What looks like potential on paper becomes real progress when one of you is willing to get the ball rolling."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"A pattern to watch for is assuming that because the connection feels easy, it will take care of itself. You may both agree on what you want, see the opportunity in front of you, and still keep putting off the first step. Not because you lack motivation, but because neither of you feels enough pressure to act right away."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The growth here comes from being intentional. Momentum builds when someone decides to start instead of waiting to feel ready. The more you support each other''s goals, follow through on plans, and turn ideas into action, the stronger this dynamic becomes. What looks like potential on paper becomes real progress when one of you is willing to get the ball rolling."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-mars_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Energies that spark and cooperate. Easy physical chemistry and a knack for getting things done together. Failure mode: underusing the momentum. Take on a project or a goal together - this contact likes action.","summaryDeep":"There is a natural sense that the two of you can get things moving together, but it tends to show up once someone takes action. The support is there from the start, yet it often needs a first step before it becomes real momentum. When one of you gets going, the other usually knows how to jump in and help.\n\nWhen this works, you bring out each other''s motivation without making it feel like pressure. One person starts the engine, the other helps keep it running. You may find that projects move faster, problems feel easier to tackle, and goals seem more achievable when you''re working as a team. There is a reassuring sense that your effort won''t be wasted because the other person is likely to meet you halfway.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is how practical it is. It often shows up in everyday moments rather than big dramatic ones. You help each other follow through, solve problems together, and turn plans into something tangible. Over time, that builds trust. You learn that when one of you reaches out, the other is usually willing to show up and contribute.\n\nThe physical side tends to follow the same rule as the rest of this contact. Mars is the body as much as the will, and the attraction here is real but responsive, the kind that warms up when someone leans in rather than waiting. When you actually meet each other, the chemistry tends to be there. It just rarely lights itself.\n\nA pattern to watch for is assuming that because the connection feels easy, it will take care of itself. You may both agree on what you want, see the opportunity in front of you, and still keep putting off the first step. Not because you lack motivation, but because neither of you feels enough pressure to act right away.\n\nThe growth here comes from being intentional. Momentum builds when someone decides to start instead of waiting to feel ready. The more you support each other''s goals, follow through on plans, and turn ideas into action, the stronger this dynamic becomes. What looks like potential on paper becomes real progress when one of you is willing to get the ball rolling.","tension":"A pattern to watch for is assuming that because the connection feels easy, it will take care of itself. You may both agree on what you want, see the opportunity in front of you, and still keep putting off the first step. Not because you lack motivation, but because neither of you feels enough pressure to act right away.","advice":"The growth here comes from being intentional. Momentum builds when someone decides to start instead of waiting to feel ready. The more you support each other''s goals, follow through on plans, and turn ideas into action, the stronger this dynamic becomes. What looks like potential on paper becomes real progress when one of you is willing to get the ball rolling.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-mars_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"mars","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-mars_square', 'synastry-mars-square-mars', 'relationship-mars-square-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-mars_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-mars_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Square Mars', null, 'This person can get under your skin faster than most people. It may be the way they push for what they want, the way they challenge you, or the way they seem to do exactly the thing that makes you dig your heels in. Around them, you may find yourself reacting before you have fully decided how you feel. They have a way of hitting a nerve, and you likely do the same to them.

What makes this complicated is that the irritation is often mixed with energy. This person wakes something up in you. You may feel more driven, more alert, more engaged when they are around. They have a way of challenging your usual habits, pushing you to make a decision, take a risk, or finally do something you have been putting off. There is a charge between you that is difficult to ignore. The relationship rarely feels neutral. Even when you are frustrated with each other, there is usually something happening, something pulling your attention back, something that keeps the connection alive.

But that same charge can turn volatile fast. What starts as a minor disagreement can become a full-scale clash before either of you realizes what happened. A passing comment hits a nerve. A difference of opinion becomes a test of strength.

The deeper challenge is that conflict can start to feel like the main source of connection. The arguments create intensity. The intensity creates engagement. And over time, it becomes easy to confuse being activated with being understood. You may tell yourself the relationship is passionate when what you are actually feeling is constant friction.

The opportunity here is growth. This person has a way of bringing your triggers to the surface, just as you bring theirs to the surface. While that can be uncomfortable, it also gives you valuable insight into how you handle anger, defensiveness, and control. The more willing you are to stay curious instead of trying to win, the more this connection can teach you about yourself and how you show up in conflict.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can get under your skin faster than most people. It may be the way they push for what they want, the way they challenge you, or the way they seem to do exactly the thing that makes you dig your heels in. Around them, you may find yourself reacting before you have fully decided how you feel. They have a way of hitting a nerve, and you likely do the same to them.\n\nWhat makes this complicated is that the irritation is often mixed with energy. This person wakes something up in you. You may feel more driven, more alert, more engaged when they are around. They have a way of challenging your usual habits, pushing you to make a decision, take a risk, or finally do something you have been putting off. There is a charge between you that is difficult to ignore. The relationship rarely feels neutral. Even when you are frustrated with each other, there is usually something happening, something pulling your attention back, something that keeps the connection alive.\n\nBut that same charge can turn volatile fast. What starts as a minor disagreement can become a full-scale clash before either of you realizes what happened. A passing comment hits a nerve. A difference of opinion becomes a test of strength.\n\nThe deeper challenge is that conflict can start to feel like the main source of connection. The arguments create intensity. The intensity creates engagement. And over time, it becomes easy to confuse being activated with being understood. You may tell yourself the relationship is passionate when what you are actually feeling is constant friction.\n\nThe opportunity here is growth. This person has a way of bringing your triggers to the surface, just as you bring theirs to the surface. While that can be uncomfortable, it also gives you valuable insight into how you handle anger, defensiveness, and control. The more willing you are to stay curious instead of trying to win, the more this connection can teach you about yourself and how you show up in conflict."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The deeper challenge is that conflict can start to feel like the main source of connection. The arguments create intensity. The intensity creates engagement. And over time, it becomes easy to confuse being activated with being understood. You may tell yourself the relationship is passionate when what you are actually feeling is constant friction."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The opportunity here is growth. This person has a way of bringing your triggers to the surface, just as you bring theirs to the surface. While that can be uncomfortable, it also gives you valuable insight into how you handle anger, defensiveness, and control. The more willing you are to stay curious instead of trying to win, the more this connection can teach you about yourself and how you show up in conflict."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-mars_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Two strong wills grinding against each other. Real attraction laced with real conflict - competition, irritation, the urge to dominate. Failure mode: the relationship runs on fighting and the make-up becomes the point. Channel the heat into something built together; a constant power struggle is a cost, not chemistry.","summaryDeep":"This person can get under your skin faster than most people. It may be the way they push for what they want, the way they challenge you, or the way they seem to do exactly the thing that makes you dig your heels in. Around them, you may find yourself reacting before you have fully decided how you feel. They have a way of hitting a nerve, and you likely do the same to them.\n\nWhat makes this complicated is that the irritation is often mixed with energy. This person wakes something up in you. You may feel more driven, more alert, more engaged when they are around. They have a way of challenging your usual habits, pushing you to make a decision, take a risk, or finally do something you have been putting off. There is a charge between you that is difficult to ignore. The relationship rarely feels neutral. Even when you are frustrated with each other, there is usually something happening, something pulling your attention back, something that keeps the connection alive.\n\nBut that same charge can turn volatile fast. What starts as a minor disagreement can become a full-scale clash before either of you realizes what happened. A passing comment hits a nerve. A difference of opinion becomes a test of strength.\n\nThe deeper challenge is that conflict can start to feel like the main source of connection. The arguments create intensity. The intensity creates engagement. And over time, it becomes easy to confuse being activated with being understood. You may tell yourself the relationship is passionate when what you are actually feeling is constant friction.\n\nThe opportunity here is growth. This person has a way of bringing your triggers to the surface, just as you bring theirs to the surface. While that can be uncomfortable, it also gives you valuable insight into how you handle anger, defensiveness, and control. The more willing you are to stay curious instead of trying to win, the more this connection can teach you about yourself and how you show up in conflict.","tension":"The deeper challenge is that conflict can start to feel like the main source of connection. The arguments create intensity. The intensity creates engagement. And over time, it becomes easy to confuse being activated with being understood. You may tell yourself the relationship is passionate when what you are actually feeling is constant friction.","advice":"The opportunity here is growth. This person has a way of bringing your triggers to the surface, just as you bring theirs to the surface. While that can be uncomfortable, it also gives you valuable insight into how you handle anger, defensiveness, and control. The more willing you are to stay curious instead of trying to win, the more this connection can teach you about yourself and how you show up in conflict.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-mars_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"mars","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-mars_trine', 'synastry-mars-trine-mars', 'relationship-mars-trine-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-mars_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-mars_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Trine Mars', null, 'You and this person tend to meet action with action in a way that feels natural. One of you starts moving and the other usually falls into step. Decisions do not require much negotiation. Getting things done together often feels easier than getting things done alone.

When this works, there is very little friction around effort. You encourage each other without pushing too hard. You trust each other''s judgment under pressure. Even when you disagree, it is less likely to turn into a struggle over who gets to lead because you generally understand where the other person is coming from.

In everyday life, this can look like plans that actually happen, responsibilities that get shared without much discussion, and problems that get solved before they become bigger than they need to be. The two of you often spend more energy moving forward than arguing about how to move forward.

This ease tends to extend to the physical side as well. Mars is the body as much as the will, and when two drives move in the same spirit, attraction usually flows without much friction. You may find the physical rhythm between you feels natural and unforced, the same way the rest of your energy does. It is easy, which is lovely, and like everything easy here, it still does better when you actually keep showing up for it.

One thing to watch for is becoming comfortable with the potential instead of using it. Because working together feels so easy, you may assume there will always be time to act on your ideas. It becomes easy to talk about what you could do instead of actually doing it. Plans never quite become action. You know you make a good team, but you do not always challenge yourselves to put that strength to work.

The opportunity here is to be intentional. Give yourselves a goal that matters. Choose something you want to create, improve, or accomplish together, then take the first step. The teamwork is already in place. The more you channel it into real action, the more rewarding and productive this connection becomes.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You and this person tend to meet action with action in a way that feels natural. One of you starts moving and the other usually falls into step. Decisions do not require much negotiation. Getting things done together often feels easier than getting things done alone.\n\nWhen this works, there is very little friction around effort. You encourage each other without pushing too hard. You trust each other''s judgment under pressure. Even when you disagree, it is less likely to turn into a struggle over who gets to lead because you generally understand where the other person is coming from.\n\nIn everyday life, this can look like plans that actually happen, responsibilities that get shared without much discussion, and problems that get solved before they become bigger than they need to be. The two of you often spend more energy moving forward than arguing about how to move forward.\n\nThis ease tends to extend to the physical side as well. Mars is the body as much as the will, and when two drives move in the same spirit, attraction usually flows without much friction. You may find the physical rhythm between you feels natural and unforced, the same way the rest of your energy does. It is easy, which is lovely, and like everything easy here, it still does better when you actually keep showing up for it.\n\nOne thing to watch for is becoming comfortable with the potential instead of using it. Because working together feels so easy, you may assume there will always be time to act on your ideas. It becomes easy to talk about what you could do instead of actually doing it. Plans never quite become action. You know you make a good team, but you do not always challenge yourselves to put that strength to work.\n\nThe opportunity here is to be intentional. Give yourselves a goal that matters. Choose something you want to create, improve, or accomplish together, then take the first step. The teamwork is already in place. The more you channel it into real action, the more rewarding and productive this connection becomes."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"One thing to watch for is becoming comfortable with the potential instead of using it. Because working together feels so easy, you may assume there will always be time to act on your ideas. It becomes easy to talk about what you could do instead of actually doing it. Plans never quite become action. You know you make a good team, but you do not always challenge yourselves to put that strength to work."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The opportunity here is to be intentional. Give yourselves a goal that matters. Choose something you want to create, improve, or accomplish together, then take the first step. The teamwork is already in place. The more you channel it into real action, the more rewarding and productive this connection becomes."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-mars_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Drive and desire flow in sync. You move at the same pace, want similar things, and rarely step on each other. Failure mode: so frictionless it can lack tension. Enjoy the ease; keep some edge.","summaryDeep":"You and this person tend to meet action with action in a way that feels natural. One of you starts moving and the other usually falls into step. Decisions do not require much negotiation. Getting things done together often feels easier than getting things done alone.\n\nWhen this works, there is very little friction around effort. You encourage each other without pushing too hard. You trust each other''s judgment under pressure. Even when you disagree, it is less likely to turn into a struggle over who gets to lead because you generally understand where the other person is coming from.\n\nIn everyday life, this can look like plans that actually happen, responsibilities that get shared without much discussion, and problems that get solved before they become bigger than they need to be. The two of you often spend more energy moving forward than arguing about how to move forward.\n\nThis ease tends to extend to the physical side as well. Mars is the body as much as the will, and when two drives move in the same spirit, attraction usually flows without much friction. You may find the physical rhythm between you feels natural and unforced, the same way the rest of your energy does. It is easy, which is lovely, and like everything easy here, it still does better when you actually keep showing up for it.\n\nOne thing to watch for is becoming comfortable with the potential instead of using it. Because working together feels so easy, you may assume there will always be time to act on your ideas. It becomes easy to talk about what you could do instead of actually doing it. Plans never quite become action. You know you make a good team, but you do not always challenge yourselves to put that strength to work.\n\nThe opportunity here is to be intentional. Give yourselves a goal that matters. Choose something you want to create, improve, or accomplish together, then take the first step. The teamwork is already in place. The more you channel it into real action, the more rewarding and productive this connection becomes.","tension":"One thing to watch for is becoming comfortable with the potential instead of using it. Because working together feels so easy, you may assume there will always be time to act on your ideas. It becomes easy to talk about what you could do instead of actually doing it. Plans never quite become action. You know you make a good team, but you do not always challenge yourselves to put that strength to work.","advice":"The opportunity here is to be intentional. Give yourselves a goal that matters. Choose something you want to create, improve, or accomplish together, then take the first step. The teamwork is already in place. The more you channel it into real action, the more rewarding and productive this connection becomes.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry-mars-conjunction-mercury', 'relationship-mars-conjunction-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-mercury_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-mercury_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Conjunction Mercury', null, 'Talking to this person can bring your thoughts to the surface before you have had time to organize them. There is something about the exchange between you that invites honesty, immediacy, and response. Conversations may feel alive. They may encourage you to speak more directly, trust your instincts, and engage with what is unfolding in the moment.

This connection pushes both people to be more honest and direct. This person may challenge your thinking, question your assumptions, or encourage you to say what you really mean. The conversations between you are meant to get to the truth.

You enjoy talking to each other. One thought leads to another, and conversations tend to keep moving. There is interest, curiosity, and a sense that both people have something to contribute.

The challenge is learning when to slow the conversation down. Both of you may be quick to respond, quick to react, or quick to move to the next point before fully taking in what was said. At times, this can create unnecessary tension or make a simple difference of opinion feel bigger than it is.

This aspect invites both people to pay attention to how and when things are said.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Talking to this person can bring your thoughts to the surface before you have had time to organize them. There is something about the exchange between you that invites honesty, immediacy, and response. Conversations may feel alive. They may encourage you to speak more directly, trust your instincts, and engage with what is unfolding in the moment.\n\nThis connection pushes both people to be more honest and direct. This person may challenge your thinking, question your assumptions, or encourage you to say what you really mean. The conversations between you are meant to get to the truth.\n\nYou enjoy talking to each other. One thought leads to another, and conversations tend to keep moving. There is interest, curiosity, and a sense that both people have something to contribute.\n\nThe challenge is learning when to slow the conversation down. Both of you may be quick to respond, quick to react, or quick to move to the next point before fully taking in what was said. At times, this can create unnecessary tension or make a simple difference of opinion feel bigger than it is.\n\nThis aspect invites both people to pay attention to how and when things are said."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is learning when to slow the conversation down. Both of you may be quick to respond, quick to react, or quick to move to the next point before fully taking in what was said. At times, this can create unnecessary tension or make a simple difference of opinion feel bigger than it is."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This aspect invites both people to pay attention to how and when things are said."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-mercury_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s mind. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"Talking to this person can bring your thoughts to the surface before you have had time to organize them. There is something about the exchange between you that invites honesty, immediacy, and response. Conversations may feel alive. They may encourage you to speak more directly, trust your instincts, and engage with what is unfolding in the moment.\n\nThis connection pushes both people to be more honest and direct. This person may challenge your thinking, question your assumptions, or encourage you to say what you really mean. The conversations between you are meant to get to the truth.\n\nYou enjoy talking to each other. One thought leads to another, and conversations tend to keep moving. There is interest, curiosity, and a sense that both people have something to contribute.\n\nThe challenge is learning when to slow the conversation down. Both of you may be quick to respond, quick to react, or quick to move to the next point before fully taking in what was said. At times, this can create unnecessary tension or make a simple difference of opinion feel bigger than it is.\n\nThis aspect invites both people to pay attention to how and when things are said.","tension":"The challenge is learning when to slow the conversation down. Both of you may be quick to respond, quick to react, or quick to move to the next point before fully taking in what was said. At times, this can create unnecessary tension or make a simple difference of opinion feel bigger than it is.","advice":"This aspect invites both people to pay attention to how and when things are said.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry-mars-opposition-mercury', 'relationship-mars-opposition-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-mercury_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-mercury_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Opposition Mercury', null, 'This person may challenge the way you think. They often bring a different perspective, ask the question you were not expecting, or push back when you assume something is settled.

This can be frustrating, but it can also be clarifying. They may expose gaps in your reasoning, ideas you''ve taken for granted, or places where you are reacting instead of reflecting.

At its best, this connection sharpens both people. The tension between your viewpoints creates a fuller picture than either of you could reach alone.

The challenge is becoming attached to being right. When disagreement turns into defensiveness, the conversation stops teaching you anything.

The gift of this connection is learning through contrast. What this person questions may be exactly what helps you understand yourself more clearly.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may challenge the way you think. They often bring a different perspective, ask the question you were not expecting, or push back when you assume something is settled.\n\nThis can be frustrating, but it can also be clarifying. They may expose gaps in your reasoning, ideas you''ve taken for granted, or places where you are reacting instead of reflecting.\n\nAt its best, this connection sharpens both people. The tension between your viewpoints creates a fuller picture than either of you could reach alone.\n\nThe challenge is becoming attached to being right. When disagreement turns into defensiveness, the conversation stops teaching you anything.\n\nThe gift of this connection is learning through contrast. What this person questions may be exactly what helps you understand yourself more clearly."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is becoming attached to being right. When disagreement turns into defensiveness, the conversation stops teaching you anything."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The gift of this connection is learning through contrast. What this person questions may be exactly what helps you understand yourself more clearly."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-mercury_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s mind. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person may challenge the way you think. They often bring a different perspective, ask the question you were not expecting, or push back when you assume something is settled.\n\nThis can be frustrating, but it can also be clarifying. They may expose gaps in your reasoning, ideas you''ve taken for granted, or places where you are reacting instead of reflecting.\n\nAt its best, this connection sharpens both people. The tension between your viewpoints creates a fuller picture than either of you could reach alone.\n\nThe challenge is becoming attached to being right. When disagreement turns into defensiveness, the conversation stops teaching you anything.\n\nThe gift of this connection is learning through contrast. What this person questions may be exactly what helps you understand yourself more clearly.","tension":"The challenge is becoming attached to being right. When disagreement turns into defensiveness, the conversation stops teaching you anything.","advice":"The gift of this connection is learning through contrast. What this person questions may be exactly what helps you understand yourself more clearly.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry-mars-sextile-mercury', 'relationship-mars-sextile-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-mercury_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-mercury_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Sextile Mercury', null, 'This person helps you get to the point.

They can help you put your thoughts into words, make decisions, and move conversations forward when you''ve been going in circles. Talking to them often feels productive. Ideas turn into plans. Questions get clearer. Problems feel easier to tackle.

The potential is there, but it usually takes some effort from both people. The more willing you are to talk things through, be honest, and stay engaged, the easier it is to understand each other and make progress together.

The challenge is not settling for what''s easy. It can be tempting to stick to familiar topics or avoid conversations that feel a little more vulnerable. But this connection tends to grow when both people are willing to go a bit deeper.

Be direct. The more openly you communicate, the more useful this connection becomes.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person helps you get to the point.\n\nThey can help you put your thoughts into words, make decisions, and move conversations forward when you''ve been going in circles. Talking to them often feels productive. Ideas turn into plans. Questions get clearer. Problems feel easier to tackle.\n\nThe potential is there, but it usually takes some effort from both people. The more willing you are to talk things through, be honest, and stay engaged, the easier it is to understand each other and make progress together.\n\nThe challenge is not settling for what''s easy. It can be tempting to stick to familiar topics or avoid conversations that feel a little more vulnerable. But this connection tends to grow when both people are willing to go a bit deeper.\n\nBe direct. The more openly you communicate, the more useful this connection becomes."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is not settling for what''s easy. It can be tempting to stick to familiar topics or avoid conversations that feel a little more vulnerable. But this connection tends to grow when both people are willing to go a bit deeper."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Be direct. The more openly you communicate, the more useful this connection becomes."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-mercury_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s mind. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This person helps you get to the point.\n\nThey can help you put your thoughts into words, make decisions, and move conversations forward when you''ve been going in circles. Talking to them often feels productive. Ideas turn into plans. Questions get clearer. Problems feel easier to tackle.\n\nThe potential is there, but it usually takes some effort from both people. The more willing you are to talk things through, be honest, and stay engaged, the easier it is to understand each other and make progress together.\n\nThe challenge is not settling for what''s easy. It can be tempting to stick to familiar topics or avoid conversations that feel a little more vulnerable. But this connection tends to grow when both people are willing to go a bit deeper.\n\nBe direct. The more openly you communicate, the more useful this connection becomes.","tension":"The challenge is not settling for what''s easy. It can be tempting to stick to familiar topics or avoid conversations that feel a little more vulnerable. But this connection tends to grow when both people are willing to go a bit deeper.","advice":"Be direct. The more openly you communicate, the more useful this connection becomes.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-mercury_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-mercury_square', 'synastry-mars-square-mercury', 'relationship-mars-square-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-mercury_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-mercury_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Square Mercury', null, 'This connection creates friction in communication. The way this person speaks, questions, or responds can easily trigger a reaction in you, and vice versa.

The challenge is not necessarily what is being said, but how quickly conversations become defensive. Small disagreements can escalate. Both people may feel misunderstood, criticized, or pressured to explain themselves.

The invitation of this aspect is deeper self-understanding. It shows you where your nervous system speeds up before your mind has a chance to catch up. It reveals the stories you tell yourself about being misunderstood, criticized, or unheard. And it asks both people to become more conscious of how they speak, listen, and respond.

The growth here comes from not reacting to every disagreement. This person will get under your skin sometimes. You will probably do the same to them. If both of you can stay in the conversation instead of immediately defending yourselves, you can learn a lot from the differences between you.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection creates friction in communication. The way this person speaks, questions, or responds can easily trigger a reaction in you, and vice versa.\n\nThe challenge is not necessarily what is being said, but how quickly conversations become defensive. Small disagreements can escalate. Both people may feel misunderstood, criticized, or pressured to explain themselves.\n\nThe invitation of this aspect is deeper self-understanding. It shows you where your nervous system speeds up before your mind has a chance to catch up. It reveals the stories you tell yourself about being misunderstood, criticized, or unheard. And it asks both people to become more conscious of how they speak, listen, and respond.\n\nThe growth here comes from not reacting to every disagreement. This person will get under your skin sometimes. You will probably do the same to them. If both of you can stay in the conversation instead of immediately defending yourselves, you can learn a lot from the differences between you."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The invitation of this aspect is deeper self-understanding. It shows you where your nervous system speeds up before your mind has a chance to catch up. It reveals the stories you tell yourself about being misunderstood, criticized, or unheard. And it asks both people to become more conscious of how they speak, listen, and respond."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The growth here comes from not reacting to every disagreement. This person will get under your skin sometimes. You will probably do the same to them. If both of you can stay in the conversation instead of immediately defending yourselves, you can learn a lot from the differences between you."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-mercury_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s mind. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This connection creates friction in communication. The way this person speaks, questions, or responds can easily trigger a reaction in you, and vice versa.\n\nThe challenge is not necessarily what is being said, but how quickly conversations become defensive. Small disagreements can escalate. Both people may feel misunderstood, criticized, or pressured to explain themselves.\n\nThe invitation of this aspect is deeper self-understanding. It shows you where your nervous system speeds up before your mind has a chance to catch up. It reveals the stories you tell yourself about being misunderstood, criticized, or unheard. And it asks both people to become more conscious of how they speak, listen, and respond.\n\nThe growth here comes from not reacting to every disagreement. This person will get under your skin sometimes. You will probably do the same to them. If both of you can stay in the conversation instead of immediately defending yourselves, you can learn a lot from the differences between you.","tension":"The invitation of this aspect is deeper self-understanding. It shows you where your nervous system speeds up before your mind has a chance to catch up. It reveals the stories you tell yourself about being misunderstood, criticized, or unheard. And it asks both people to become more conscious of how they speak, listen, and respond.","advice":"The growth here comes from not reacting to every disagreement. This person will get under your skin sometimes. You will probably do the same to them. If both of you can stay in the conversation instead of immediately defending yourselves, you can learn a lot from the differences between you.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-mercury_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-mercury_trine', 'synastry-mars-trine-mercury', 'relationship-mars-trine-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-mercury_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-mercury_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Trine Mercury', null, 'You can be direct with each other without creating unnecessary conflict. Conversations tend to move quickly, honestly, and toward a solution. This person helps you say what you mean, and you help them do the same.

At its best, this aspect creates straightforward communication. Problems get discussed instead of avoided. Decisions get made instead of endlessly debated. There is a natural ability to challenge each other without taking it personally.

The strength of this connection is the way honesty can move between you without getting stuck. Conversations have a way of clearing the air. What needs to be said often finds its way to the surface, making it easier to address what matters instead of circling around it.

The gift here is the reminder that truth can be a catalyst. When you are willing to meet each other with openness and sincerity, insight becomes action, and understanding creates momentum.

Use the honesty while it is flowing. This connection works best when what gets said out loud turns into something you actually act on.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You can be direct with each other without creating unnecessary conflict. Conversations tend to move quickly, honestly, and toward a solution. This person helps you say what you mean, and you help them do the same.\n\nAt its best, this aspect creates straightforward communication. Problems get discussed instead of avoided. Decisions get made instead of endlessly debated. There is a natural ability to challenge each other without taking it personally.\n\nThe strength of this connection is the way honesty can move between you without getting stuck. Conversations have a way of clearing the air. What needs to be said often finds its way to the surface, making it easier to address what matters instead of circling around it.\n\nThe gift here is the reminder that truth can be a catalyst. When you are willing to meet each other with openness and sincerity, insight becomes action, and understanding creates momentum.\n\nUse the honesty while it is flowing. This connection works best when what gets said out loud turns into something you actually act on."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The gift here is the reminder that truth can be a catalyst. When you are willing to meet each other with openness and sincerity, insight becomes action, and understanding creates momentum."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Use the honesty while it is flowing. This connection works best when what gets said out loud turns into something you actually act on."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-mercury_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s mind. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"You can be direct with each other without creating unnecessary conflict. Conversations tend to move quickly, honestly, and toward a solution. This person helps you say what you mean, and you help them do the same.\n\nAt its best, this aspect creates straightforward communication. Problems get discussed instead of avoided. Decisions get made instead of endlessly debated. There is a natural ability to challenge each other without taking it personally.\n\nThe strength of this connection is the way honesty can move between you without getting stuck. Conversations have a way of clearing the air. What needs to be said often finds its way to the surface, making it easier to address what matters instead of circling around it.\n\nThe gift here is the reminder that truth can be a catalyst. When you are willing to meet each other with openness and sincerity, insight becomes action, and understanding creates momentum.\n\nUse the honesty while it is flowing. This connection works best when what gets said out loud turns into something you actually act on.","tension":"The gift here is the reminder that truth can be a catalyst. When you are willing to meet each other with openness and sincerity, insight becomes action, and understanding creates momentum.","advice":"Use the honesty while it is flowing. This connection works best when what gets said out loud turns into something you actually act on.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"moon","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry-mars-conjunction-moon', 'relationship-mars-conjunction-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-moon_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-moon_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Conjunction Moon', null, 'This person can get right under your skin, sometimes in a good way and sometimes not. Around them, your feelings may come up faster than usual. You may feel drawn in, stirred up, irritated, comforted, or more honest than you expected to be. It is hard to stay detached when someone touches this part of you.

There can be something very immediate about the bond. This person may make you feel wanted in a way that is hard to miss. They may not always say the softest thing, but you can feel that they are present. They respond. They engage. They do not treat your emotions like an inconvenience. If you are used to people going vague or quiet when things get intense, that can feel like a relief.

When this works, it can feel protective. You may feel like they would show up for you if something went wrong, or that they care enough to react when you are hurt. There is a kind of warmth here that is not always gentle, but still feels real.

The problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.

Notice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can get right under your skin, sometimes in a good way and sometimes not. Around them, your feelings may come up faster than usual. You may feel drawn in, stirred up, irritated, comforted, or more honest than you expected to be. It is hard to stay detached when someone touches this part of you.\n\nThere can be something very immediate about the bond. This person may make you feel wanted in a way that is hard to miss. They may not always say the softest thing, but you can feel that they are present. They respond. They engage. They do not treat your emotions like an inconvenience. If you are used to people going vague or quiet when things get intense, that can feel like a relief.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel protective. You may feel like they would show up for you if something went wrong, or that they care enough to react when you are hurt. There is a kind of warmth here that is not always gentle, but still feels real.\n\nThe problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.\n\nNotice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Notice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-moon_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s feelings. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person can get right under your skin, sometimes in a good way and sometimes not. Around them, your feelings may come up faster than usual. You may feel drawn in, stirred up, irritated, comforted, or more honest than you expected to be. It is hard to stay detached when someone touches this part of you.\n\nThere can be something very immediate about the bond. This person may make you feel wanted in a way that is hard to miss. They may not always say the softest thing, but you can feel that they are present. They respond. They engage. They do not treat your emotions like an inconvenience. If you are used to people going vague or quiet when things get intense, that can feel like a relief.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel protective. You may feel like they would show up for you if something went wrong, or that they care enough to react when you are hurt. There is a kind of warmth here that is not always gentle, but still feels real.\n\nThe problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.\n\nNotice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship.","tension":"The problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.","advice":"Notice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"moon","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry-mars-opposition-moon', 'relationship-mars-opposition-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-moon_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-moon_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Opposition Moon', null, 'This person can pull a strong reaction out of you, but relaxing into it may not always be easy. You may want closeness from them and still feel like you have to brace yourself. They may come toward you with energy when what you really wanted was patience. Or they may think they are helping, while you feel rushed, handled, or pushed past your own pace.

A lot of the tension here comes from timing. One person is ready to act, while the other is still trying to feel their way through the moment. One person wants to fix it, while the other wants to be understood first. Nobody has to be wrong for both people to end up frustrated.

When this works, it can make the relationship more honest. This person may get you to say the thing you were trying not to say. They may make it harder for you to hide behind "I''m fine" when you are clearly not fine. That can be uncomfortable, but it can also be exactly what brings the truth into the room.

The hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.

Slow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can pull a strong reaction out of you, but relaxing into it may not always be easy. You may want closeness from them and still feel like you have to brace yourself. They may come toward you with energy when what you really wanted was patience. Or they may think they are helping, while you feel rushed, handled, or pushed past your own pace.\n\nA lot of the tension here comes from timing. One person is ready to act, while the other is still trying to feel their way through the moment. One person wants to fix it, while the other wants to be understood first. Nobody has to be wrong for both people to end up frustrated.\n\nWhen this works, it can make the relationship more honest. This person may get you to say the thing you were trying not to say. They may make it harder for you to hide behind \"I''m fine\" when you are clearly not fine. That can be uncomfortable, but it can also be exactly what brings the truth into the room.\n\nThe hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.\n\nSlow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Slow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-moon_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s feelings. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person can pull a strong reaction out of you, but relaxing into it may not always be easy. You may want closeness from them and still feel like you have to brace yourself. They may come toward you with energy when what you really wanted was patience. Or they may think they are helping, while you feel rushed, handled, or pushed past your own pace.\n\nA lot of the tension here comes from timing. One person is ready to act, while the other is still trying to feel their way through the moment. One person wants to fix it, while the other wants to be understood first. Nobody has to be wrong for both people to end up frustrated.\n\nWhen this works, it can make the relationship more honest. This person may get you to say the thing you were trying not to say. They may make it harder for you to hide behind \"I''m fine\" when you are clearly not fine. That can be uncomfortable, but it can also be exactly what brings the truth into the room.\n\nThe hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.\n\nSlow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you.","tension":"The hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.","advice":"Slow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-moon_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"moon","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-moon_sextile', 'synastry-mars-sextile-moon', 'relationship-mars-sextile-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-moon_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-moon_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Sextile Moon', null, 'This connection may not announce itself as loudly as the conjunction or square, but there is something here that responds when one of you reaches for it. The warmth grows when someone checks in, speaks honestly, follows through, or shows care in a way the other person can actually feel.

This is a contact where action matters. Not dramatic action, necessarily. More like showing up when you said you would. Asking the question instead of guessing. Helping with the thing that has been sitting there too long. Making it clear, through behavior, that the other person is not dealing with everything alone.

When this works, both people feel a little more willing to engage. One person says what they want, and the other has something to respond to. One person makes a move, and the connection gets warmer. The care becomes easier to trust because it is not only talked about. It is shown.

The hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to.

Do not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection may not announce itself as loudly as the conjunction or square, but there is something here that responds when one of you reaches for it. The warmth grows when someone checks in, speaks honestly, follows through, or shows care in a way the other person can actually feel.\n\nThis is a contact where action matters. Not dramatic action, necessarily. More like showing up when you said you would. Asking the question instead of guessing. Helping with the thing that has been sitting there too long. Making it clear, through behavior, that the other person is not dealing with everything alone.\n\nWhen this works, both people feel a little more willing to engage. One person says what they want, and the other has something to respond to. One person makes a move, and the connection gets warmer. The care becomes easier to trust because it is not only talked about. It is shown.\n\nThe hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to.\n\nDo not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Do not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-moon_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plai