undle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-moon_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"moon","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-moon_square', 'synastry-mars-square-moon', 'relationship-mars-square-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-moon_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-moon_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Square Moon', null, 'This person may hit a nerve before either of you knows where the nerve is. It could be their tone, their timing, the way they push, the way they do not back off, or the way they seem to move on before you are ready. Something about them can make your feelings rise quickly.

There may also be real chemistry here, which makes the whole thing more confusing. You can feel pulled toward someone and still feel irritated by them. You can want them close and also want them to stop doing exactly what they are doing. That does not mean the connection is fake. It means the same person who wakes up your desire can also wake up your defenses.

When this works, it can bring things to the surface that needed to be said. You may stop pretending something does not bother you. They may stop letting things slide. The relationship may have a way of forcing honesty, even when neither person planned on being that honest.

The problem is when the friction becomes the main way you stay connected. If things only feel alive when someone is upset, the relationship can start to confuse tension with intimacy. You poke, they react. They push, you defend. After a while, both people are tired, but neither one knows how to get close without lighting something up first.

Catch the small thing while it is still small. Not every feeling needs to become a fight. This connection works better when both people learn how to pause before trying to win the moment.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may hit a nerve before either of you knows where the nerve is. It could be their tone, their timing, the way they push, the way they do not back off, or the way they seem to move on before you are ready. Something about them can make your feelings rise quickly.\n\nThere may also be real chemistry here, which makes the whole thing more confusing. You can feel pulled toward someone and still feel irritated by them. You can want them close and also want them to stop doing exactly what they are doing. That does not mean the connection is fake. It means the same person who wakes up your desire can also wake up your defenses.\n\nWhen this works, it can bring things to the surface that needed to be said. You may stop pretending something does not bother you. They may stop letting things slide. The relationship may have a way of forcing honesty, even when neither person planned on being that honest.\n\nThe problem is when the friction becomes the main way you stay connected. If things only feel alive when someone is upset, the relationship can start to confuse tension with intimacy. You poke, they react. They push, you defend. After a while, both people are tired, but neither one knows how to get close without lighting something up first.\n\nCatch the small thing while it is still small. Not every feeling needs to become a fight. This connection works better when both people learn how to pause before trying to win the moment."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is when the friction becomes the main way you stay connected. If things only feel alive when someone is upset, the relationship can start to confuse tension with intimacy. You poke, they react. They push, you defend. After a while, both people are tired, but neither one knows how to get close without lighting something up first."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Catch the small thing while it is still small. Not every feeling needs to become a fight. This connection works better when both people learn how to pause before trying to win the moment."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-moon_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s feelings. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This person may hit a nerve before either of you knows where the nerve is. It could be their tone, their timing, the way they push, the way they do not back off, or the way they seem to move on before you are ready. Something about them can make your feelings rise quickly.\n\nThere may also be real chemistry here, which makes the whole thing more confusing. You can feel pulled toward someone and still feel irritated by them. You can want them close and also want them to stop doing exactly what they are doing. That does not mean the connection is fake. It means the same person who wakes up your desire can also wake up your defenses.\n\nWhen this works, it can bring things to the surface that needed to be said. You may stop pretending something does not bother you. They may stop letting things slide. The relationship may have a way of forcing honesty, even when neither person planned on being that honest.\n\nThe problem is when the friction becomes the main way you stay connected. If things only feel alive when someone is upset, the relationship can start to confuse tension with intimacy. You poke, they react. They push, you defend. After a while, both people are tired, but neither one knows how to get close without lighting something up first.\n\nCatch the small thing while it is still small. Not every feeling needs to become a fight. This connection works better when both people learn how to pause before trying to win the moment.","tension":"The problem is when the friction becomes the main way you stay connected. If things only feel alive when someone is upset, the relationship can start to confuse tension with intimacy. You poke, they react. They push, you defend. After a while, both people are tired, but neither one knows how to get close without lighting something up first.","advice":"Catch the small thing while it is still small. Not every feeling needs to become a fight. This connection works better when both people learn how to pause before trying to win the moment.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-moon_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"moon","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-moon_trine', 'synastry-mars-trine-moon', 'relationship-mars-trine-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-moon_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-moon_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Trine Moon', null, 'This person may stir something in you without making you feel unsafe. They can bring out a more honest, alive version of you, but it does not have to feel like a battle. Around them, you may find it easier to say what you feel, act on what matters, or stop sitting on something that needs your attention.

There is a good kind of responsiveness here. If you are upset, they may not freeze or disappear. If something matters to you, they may take it seriously. You can feel supported by their presence because they do not just listen from a distance. They seem willing to meet the feeling and do something with it.

When this works, comfort and heat can sit together. You may feel wanted without feeling pressured. You may feel protected without feeling controlled. The connection can make both people a little braver with their feelings, not because anyone is forcing it, but because the energy between you makes honesty feel possible.

The only real risk is letting this good rhythm go unused. Because it is easier than the harder Moon-Mars contacts, you may not notice how much it helps. The support is there, but it still needs somewhere to go.

