ons or your own just to keep the peace, that is not a phase to push through. Intensity is never a reason to stay somewhere that is hurting you.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-pluto_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-pluto_opposition', 'synastry-mars-opposition-pluto', 'relationship-mars-opposition-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-pluto_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-pluto_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Opposition Pluto', null, 'This person meets your drive with a force that pulls and challenges at once.

There is a strong charge between you, often physical, often magnetic, but it rarely feels balanced. You may feel powerfully drawn to this person while sensing a contest underneath the attraction, a question of who moves first, who holds more power, who gives way. The pull is real, and so is the friction braided through it.

When this works, you sharpen each other''s strength. This person can match your intensity, push you to act, and meet you with an energy that makes you more capable than you are alone. Faced with respect, the opposition becomes a powerful partnership where each of you brings real force to the table.

The harder part is when it becomes a struggle that neither of you can put down. One person pushes, the other pushes back, and what starts as friction can build into something that feels less like conflict and more like a fight for control of the whole relationship. The reactive, buried parts of both of you surface, and they do not always stay in proportion. You may find yourselves locked together by the charge even as the connection turns corrosive, pulled back again and again into something that wears you down a little more each time, until you barely recognize how much it has cost you.

Hold your ground without needing to win, and watch honestly what this is doing to you over months, not moments. This works only when the intensity builds rather than destroys. If you are always braced, always recovering from the last round, always pulled back just when you have gathered the strength to step away, that is not a connection finding its balance. That is a pattern, and you are allowed to leave it.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person meets your drive with a force that pulls and challenges at once.\n\nThere is a strong charge between you, often physical, often magnetic, but it rarely feels balanced. You may feel powerfully drawn to this person while sensing a contest underneath the attraction, a question of who moves first, who holds more power, who gives way. The pull is real, and so is the friction braided through it.\n\nWhen this works, you sharpen each other''s strength. This person can match your intensity, push you to act, and meet you with an energy that makes you more capable than you are alone. Faced with respect, the opposition becomes a powerful partnership where each of you brings real force to the table.\n\nThe harder part is when it becomes a struggle that neither of you can put down. One person pushes, the other pushes back, and what starts as friction can build into something that feels less like conflict and more like a fight for control of the whole relationship. The reactive, buried parts of both of you surface, and they do not always stay in proportion. You may find yourselves locked together by the charge even as the connection turns corrosive, pulled back again and again into something that wears you down a little more each time, until you barely recognize how much it has cost you.\n\nHold your ground without needing to win, and watch honestly what this is doing to you over months, not moments. This works only when the intensity builds rather than destroys. If you are always braced, always recovering from the last round, always pulled back just when you have gathered the strength to step away, that is not a connection finding its balance. That is a pattern, and you are allowed to leave it."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part is when it becomes a struggle that neither of you can put down. One person pushes, the other pushes back, and what starts as friction can build into something that feels less like conflict and more like a fight for control of the whole relationship. The reactive, buried parts of both of you surface, and they do not always stay in proportion. You may find yourselves locked together by the charge even as the connection turns corrosive, pulled back again and again into something that wears you down a little more each time, until you barely recognize how much it has cost you."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Hold your ground without needing to win, and watch honestly what this is doing to you over months, not moments. This works only when the intensity builds rather than destroys. If you are always braced, always recovering from the last round, always pulled back just when you have gathered the strength to step away, that is not a connection finding its balance. That is a pattern, and you are allowed to leave it."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-pluto_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s depth and power. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person meets your drive with a force that pulls and challenges at once.\n\nThere is a strong charge between you, often physical, often magnetic, but it rarely feels balanced. You may feel powerfully drawn to this person while sensing a contest underneath the attraction, a question of who moves first, who holds more power, who gives way. The pull is real, and so is the friction braided through it.\n\nWhen this works, you sharpen each other''s strength. This person can match your intensity, push you to act, and meet you with an energy that makes you more capable than you are alone. Faced with respect, the opposition becomes a powerful partnership where each of you brings real force to the table.\n\nThe harder part is when it becomes a struggle that neither of you can put down. One person pushes, the other pushes back, and what starts as friction can build into something that feels less like conflict and more like a fight for control of the whole relationship. The reactive, buried parts of both of you surface, and they do not always stay in proportion. You may find yourselves locked together by the charge even as the connection turns corrosive, pulled back again and again into something that wears you down a little more each time, until you barely recognize how much it has cost you.\n\nHold your ground without needing to win, and watch honestly what this is doing to you over months, not moments. This works only when the intensity builds rather than destroys. If you are always braced, always recovering from the last round, always pulled back just when you have gathered the strength to step away, that is not a connection finding its balance. That is a pattern, and you are allowed to leave it.","tension":"The harder part is when it becomes a struggle that neither of you can put down. One person pushes, the other pushes back, and what starts as friction can build into something that feels less like conflict and more like a fight for control of the whole relationship. The reactive, buried parts of both of you surface, and they do not always stay in proportion. You may find yourselves locked together by the charge even as the connection turns corrosive, pulled back again and again into something that wears you down a little more each time, until you barely recognize how much it has cost you.","advice":"Hold your ground without needing to win, and watch honestly what this is doing to you over months, not moments. This works only when the intensity builds rather than destroys. If you are always braced, always recovering from the last round, always pulled back just when you have gathered the strength to step away, that is not a connection finding its balance. That is a pattern, and you are allowed to leave it.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-pluto_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-pluto_sextile', 'synastry-mars-sextile-pluto', 'relationship-mars-sextile-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-pluto_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-pluto_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Sextile Pluto', null, 'There is a strong, productive potential in the energy between you, and it switches on when you engage it well.

This person can activate your drive and meet your intensity, but the power here works best when you aim it consciously rather than letting it run hot on its own. The charge is more manageable than in the hard contacts, the kind that builds real momentum when you use it and stays workable when you do not.

When this works, this person makes you bolder and more effective. They match your energy, back your pursuits, and help you act on what you want with more force than you would muster alone. The attraction can be strong without being destabilizing, the drive shared without becoming a contest. The more deliberately you point the energy at something real, the more it tends to give.

Where it falls flat is leaving the power idle, or letting the intensity simmer into friction instead of action. You may feel the charge and never quite channel it, so the potential stays unused or leaks out as low-grade tension.

Aim the energy on purpose, and keep it pointed at what you actually want. This one turns from charged to genuinely powerful when you put the intensity to work rather than letting it work on you.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is a strong, productive potential in the energy between you, and it switches on when you engage it well.\n\nThis person can activate your drive and meet your intensity, but the power here works best when you aim it consciously rather than letting it run hot on its own. The charge is more manageable than in the hard contacts, the kind that builds real momentum when you use it and stays workable when you do not.\n\nWhen this works, this person makes you bolder and more effective. They match your energy, back your pursuits, and help you act on what you want with more force than you would muster alone. The attraction can be strong without being destabilizing, the drive shared without becoming a contest. The more deliberately you point the energy at something real, the more it tends to give.\n\nWhere it falls flat is leaving the power idle, or letting the intensity simmer into friction instead of action. You may feel the charge and never quite channel it, so the potential stays unused or leaks out as low-grade tension.\n\nAim the energy on purpose, and keep it pointed at what you actually want. This one turns from charged to genuinely powerful when you put the intensity to work rather than letting it work on you."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Where it falls flat is leaving the power idle, or letting the intensity simmer into friction instead of action. You may feel the charge and never quite channel it, so the potential stays unused or leaks out as low-grade tension."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Aim the energy on purpose, and keep it pointed at what you actually want. This one turns from charged to genuinely powerful when you put the intensity to work rather than letting it work on you."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-pluto_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s depth and power. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"There is a strong, productive potential in the energy between you, and it switches on when you engage it well.\n\nThis person can activate your drive and meet your intensity, but the power here works best when you aim it consciously rather than letting it run hot on its own. The charge is more manageable than in the hard contacts, the kind that builds real momentum when you use it and stays workable when you do not.\n\nWhen this works, this person makes you bolder and more effective. They match your energy, back your pursuits, and help you act on what you want with more force than you would muster alone. The attraction can be strong without being destabilizing, the drive shared without becoming a contest. The more deliberately you point the energy at something real, the more it tends to give.\n\nWhere it falls flat is leaving the power idle, or letting the intensity simmer into friction instead of action. You may feel the charge and never quite channel it, so the potential stays unused or leaks out as low-grade tension.\n\nAim the energy on purpose, and keep it pointed at what you actually want. This one turns from charged to genuinely powerful when you put the intensity to work rather than letting it work on you.","tension":"Where it falls flat is leaving the power idle, or letting the intensity simmer into friction instead of action. You may feel the charge and never quite channel it, so the potential stays unused or leaks out as low-grade tension.","advice":"Aim the energy on purpose, and keep it pointed at what you actually want. This one turns from charged to genuinely powerful when you put the intensity to work rather than letting it work on you.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-pluto_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-pluto_square', 'synastry-mars-square-pluto', 'relationship-mars-square-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-pluto_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-pluto_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Square Pluto', null, 'This is one of the most charged and volatile contacts there is, and it asks for real honesty with yourself.

The pull here is strong, often intensely physical, but it comes braided with friction. This person can activate you like few others, your desire, your drive, and also your defenses. You may find yourself drawn to them and set off by them in nearly the same moment, pulled close and provoked at once. The chemistry can be powerful. So can the conflict.

When this works, the friction can be a catalyst. Pushed this hard, you can break out of old patterns, face what you usually avoid, and turn raw intensity into real change. Met with maturity on both sides, even the difficulty can build something.

The harder part is what this becomes when it goes unchecked, and it can go to dark places. You may push each other''s buttons until the smallest thing detonates, get trapped in a cycle of rupture and reconnection that feels like passion but functions like a hook, and find that the connection brings out things in you, and in them, that frighten you. The intensity can stop feeling like chemistry and start feeling like something you cannot get out from under. This is the contact where people stay long past the point it is good for them, telling themselves the depth of the pull must mean something, while the connection slowly takes more than it gives.

So watch the pattern, not just the pull. Notice whether you leave feeling stronger or smaller, steadier or more afraid. Notice whether the fights ever resolve or only reset. Notice whether you have stopped telling the people who love you what actually happens between you, or whether you would be ashamed to say it out loud. If you find yourself making excuses for how this person treats you, hiding the worst of it, or feeling like you cannot leave even though part of you wants to, listen to that. A powerful pull is never proof a connection is meant to be, and it is never a reason to stay somewhere that is harming you. If you are afraid, that fear is information, and you deserve to be safe more than you need to understand the connection.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This is one of the most charged and volatile contacts there is, and it asks for real honesty with yourself.\n\nThe pull here is strong, often intensely physical, but it comes braided with friction. This person can activate you like few others, your desire, your drive, and also your defenses. You may find yourself drawn to them and set off by them in nearly the same moment, pulled close and provoked at once. The chemistry can be powerful. So can the conflict.\n\nWhen this works, the friction can be a catalyst. Pushed this hard, you can break out of old patterns, face what you usually avoid, and turn raw intensity into real change. Met with maturity on both sides, even the difficulty can build something.\n\nThe harder part is what this becomes when it goes unchecked, and it can go to dark places. You may push each other''s buttons until the smallest thing detonates, get trapped in a cycle of rupture and reconnection that feels like passion but functions like a hook, and find that the connection brings out things in you, and in them, that frighten you. The intensity can stop feeling like chemistry and start feeling like something you cannot get out from under. This is the contact where people stay long past the point it is good for them, telling themselves the depth of the pull must mean something, while the connection slowly takes more than it gives.\n\nSo watch the pattern, not just the pull. Notice whether you leave feeling stronger or smaller, steadier or more afraid. Notice whether the fights ever resolve or only reset. Notice whether you have stopped telling the people who love you what actually happens between you, or whether you would be ashamed to say it out loud. If you find yourself making excuses for how this person treats you, hiding the worst of it, or feeling like you cannot leave even though part of you wants to, listen to that. A powerful pull is never proof a connection is meant to be, and it is never a reason to stay somewhere that is harming you. If you are afraid, that fear is information, and you deserve to be safe more than you need to understand the connection."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part is what this becomes when it goes unchecked, and it can go to dark places. You may push each other''s buttons until the smallest thing detonates, get trapped in a cycle of rupture and reconnection that feels like passion but functions like a hook, and find that the connection brings out things in you, and in them, that frighten you. The intensity can stop feeling like chemistry and start feeling like something you cannot get out from under. This is the contact where people stay long past the point it is good for them, telling themselves the depth of the pull must mean something, while the connection slowly takes more than it gives."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"So watch the pattern, not just the pull. Notice whether you leave feeling stronger or smaller, steadier or more afraid. Notice whether the fights ever resolve or only reset. Notice whether you have stopped telling the people who love you what actually happens between you, or whether you would be ashamed to say it out loud. If you find yourself making excuses for how this person treats you, hiding the worst of it, or feeling like you cannot leave even though part of you wants to, listen to that. A powerful pull is never proof a connection is meant to be, and it is never a reason to stay somewhere that is harming you. If you are afraid, that fear is information, and you deserve to be safe more than you need to understand the connection."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-pluto_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Mars person''s drive meets Pluto''s power. This can become passion, ambition, and fearless action, or a battle for dominance. If conflict becomes the engine of attraction, slow the whole thing down.","summaryDeep":"This is one of the most charged and volatile contacts there is, and it asks for real honesty with yourself.\n\nThe pull here is strong, often intensely physical, but it comes braided with friction. This person can activate you like few others, your desire, your drive, and also your defenses. You may find yourself drawn to them and set off by them in nearly the same moment, pulled close and provoked at once. The chemistry can be powerful. So can the conflict.\n\nWhen this works, the friction can be a catalyst. Pushed this hard, you can break out of old patterns, face what you usually avoid, and turn raw intensity into real change. Met with maturity on both sides, even the difficulty can build something.\n\nThe harder part is what this becomes when it goes unchecked, and it can go to dark places. You may push each other''s buttons until the smallest thing detonates, get trapped in a cycle of rupture and reconnection that feels like passion but functions like a hook, and find that the connection brings out things in you, and in them, that frighten you. The intensity can stop feeling like chemistry and start feeling like something you cannot get out from under. This is the contact where people stay long past the point it is good for them, telling themselves the depth of the pull must mean something, w