ever proof a connection is meant to be, and it is never a reason to stay somewhere that is harming you. If you are afraid, that fear is information, and you deserve to be safe more than you need to understand the connection.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-pluto_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-pluto_trine', 'synastry-mars-trine-pluto', 'relationship-mars-trine-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-pluto_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-pluto_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Trine Pluto', null, 'There is a deep, powerful energy between you that flows more easily than the hard contacts.

This person activates your drive and desire in a way that tends to feel energizing rather than combative. The intensity meets your will without the constant power struggle, so you may feel strengthened by them, drawn to them physically and otherwise, capable of more with them at your side. The charge is there, but it works with you rather than against you.

When this works, you make a formidable team. You can pursue what you want with combined force, motivate each other without it becoming a contest, and bring real intensity to a shared purpose. The attraction can run deep and steady, the loyalty strong. This is the version of Mars-Pluto where the power mostly builds.

The challenge is the quieter one that comes with this much ease. Even a flowing Pluto contact runs intense, and you may take the drive for granted, or let the connection pull more of your focus and energy into its orbit than you realize. Power this comfortable can still quietly organize your life around it.

Use the energy on purpose, and keep your own footing as you do. This is the rare Mars-Pluto contact that mostly empowers rather than destabilizes. The work is channeling the intensity into what you actually want, rather than letting it run the show.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is a deep, powerful energy between you that flows more easily than the hard contacts.\n\nThis person activates your drive and desire in a way that tends to feel energizing rather than combative. The intensity meets your will without the constant power struggle, so you may feel strengthened by them, drawn to them physically and otherwise, capable of more with them at your side. The charge is there, but it works with you rather than against you.\n\nWhen this works, you make a formidable team. You can pursue what you want with combined force, motivate each other without it becoming a contest, and bring real intensity to a shared purpose. The attraction can run deep and steady, the loyalty strong. This is the version of Mars-Pluto where the power mostly builds.\n\nThe challenge is the quieter one that comes with this much ease. Even a flowing Pluto contact runs intense, and you may take the drive for granted, or let the connection pull more of your focus and energy into its orbit than you realize. Power this comfortable can still quietly organize your life around it.\n\nUse the energy on purpose, and keep your own footing as you do. This is the rare Mars-Pluto contact that mostly empowers rather than destabilizes. The work is channeling the intensity into what you actually want, rather than letting it run the show."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is the quieter one that comes with this much ease. Even a flowing Pluto contact runs intense, and you may take the drive for granted, or let the connection pull more of your focus and energy into its orbit than you realize. Power this comfortable can still quietly organize your life around it."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Use the energy on purpose, and keep your own footing as you do. This is the rare Mars-Pluto contact that mostly empowers rather than destabilizes. The work is channeling the intensity into what you actually want, rather than letting it run the show."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-pluto_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s depth and power. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"There is a deep, powerful energy between you that flows more easily than the hard contacts.\n\nThis person activates your drive and desire in a way that tends to feel energizing rather than combative. The intensity meets your will without the constant power struggle, so you may feel strengthened by them, drawn to them physically and otherwise, capable of more with them at your side. The charge is there, but it works with you rather than against you.\n\nWhen this works, you make a formidable team. You can pursue what you want with combined force, motivate each other without it becoming a contest, and bring real intensity to a shared purpose. The attraction can run deep and steady, the loyalty strong. This is the version of Mars-Pluto where the power mostly builds.\n\nThe challenge is the quieter one that comes with this much ease. Even a flowing Pluto contact runs intense, and you may take the drive for granted, or let the connection pull more of your focus and energy into its orbit than you realize. Power this comfortable can still quietly organize your life around it.\n\nUse the energy on purpose, and keep your own footing as you do. This is the rare Mars-Pluto contact that mostly empowers rather than destabilizes. The work is channeling the intensity into what you actually want, rather than letting it run the show.","tension":"The challenge is the quieter one that comes with this much ease. Even a flowing Pluto contact runs intense, and you may take the drive for granted, or let the connection pull more of your focus and energy into its orbit than you realize. Power this comfortable can still quietly organize your life around it.","advice":"Use the energy on purpose, and keep your own footing as you do. This is the rare Mars-Pluto contact that mostly empowers rather than destabilizes. The work is channeling the intensity into what you actually want, rather than letting it run the show.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-saturn_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-saturn_conjunction', 'synastry-mars-conjunction-saturn', 'relationship-mars-conjunction-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-saturn_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-saturn_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Conjunction Saturn', null, 'This person brings you face to face with the reality of your actions. Around them, you become more aware of timing, responsibility, consequences, and the effort required to make something last. If you tend to move quickly, their presence can help you slow down enough to see what you''re building. If you''re eager to act, however, it may feel as though every impulse is being asked to prove itself before it can move forward. What you want to do meets the question of what it will take to sustain it.

When this works, they help your energy find direction. Instead of acting on every impulse, you learn how to focus your effort, choose your timing more carefully, and stay with a goal after the excitement of beginning has passed. Their influence may not always feel encouraging, but it can help you develop greater self-control.

There is real value in what they offer. Desire can get something started, but it is discipline that carries it through. This person may help you develop the patience to stay with the process, the resilience to keep going when things get difficult, and the commitment needed to create results that last.

The difficulty comes when their restraint feels less like guidance and more like a barrier. You may begin to feel stopped before you have a chance to act, questioned before you have a chance to try, or made to doubt instincts that once felt clear. When every step feels subject to their judgment, resentment can grow.

Let this connection teach you how to move with more strength, but do not let it train you to stop moving.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person brings you face to face with the reality of your actions. Around them, you become more aware of timing, responsibility, consequences, and the effort required to make something last. If you tend to move quickly, their presence can help you slow down enough to see what you''re building. If you''re eager to act, however, it may feel as though every impulse is being asked to prove itself before it can move forward. What you want to do meets the question of what it will take to sustain it.\n\nWhen this works, they help your energy find direction. Instead of acting on every impulse, you learn how to focus your effort, choose your timing more carefully, and stay with a goal after the excitement of beginning has passed. Their influence may not always feel encouraging, but it can help you develop greater self-control.\n\nThere is real value in what they offer. Desire can get something started, but it is discipline that carries it through. This person may help you develop the patience to stay with the process, the resilience to keep going when things get difficult, and the commitment needed to create results that last.\n\nThe difficulty comes when their restraint feels less like guidance and more like a barrier. You may begin to feel stopped before you have a chance to act, questioned before you have a chance to try, or made to doubt instincts that once felt clear. When every step feels subject to their judgment, resentment can grow.\n\nLet this connection teach you how to move with more strength, but do not let it train you to stop moving."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The difficulty comes when their restraint feels less like guidance and more like a barrier. You may begin to feel stopped before you have a chance to act, questioned before you have a chance to try, or made to doubt instincts that once felt clear. When every step feels subject to their judgment, resentment can grow."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let this connection teach you how to move with more strength, but do not let it train you to stop moving."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-saturn_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Drive meets brake. The Mars person pushes; the Saturn person structures, slows, or stops. At best, Saturn turns Mars''s raw energy into disciplined, lasting work. At worst, the Mars person feels constantly blocked and criticized while the Saturn person feels they''re minding a loose cannon. Failure mode: Saturn controlling Mars, or chronic frustration. Build something together; don''t let one police the other''s drive.","summaryDeep":"This person brings you face to face with the reality of your actions. Around them, you become more aware of timing, responsibility, consequences, and the effort required to make something last. If you tend to move quickly, their presence can help you slow down enough to see what you''re building. If you''re eager to act, however, it may feel as though every impulse is being asked to prove itself before it can move forward. What you want to do meets the question of what it will take to sustain it.\n\nWhen this works, they help your energy find direction. Instead of acting on every impulse, you learn how to focus your effort, choose your timing more carefully, and stay with a goal after the excitement of beginning has passed. Their influence may not always feel encouraging, but it can help you develop greater self-control.\n\nThere is real value in what they offer. Desire can get something started, but it is discipline that carries it through. This person may help you develop the patience to stay with the process, the resilience to keep going when things get difficult, and the commitment needed to create results that last.\n\nThe difficulty comes when their restraint feels less like guidance and more like a barrier. You may begin to feel stopped before you have a chance to act, questioned before you have a chance to try, or made to doubt instincts that once felt clear. When every step feels subject to their judgment, resentment can grow.\n\nLet this connection teach you how to move with more strength, but do not let it train you to stop moving.","tension":"The difficulty comes when their restraint feels less like guidance and more like a barrier. You may begin to feel stopped before you have a chance to act, questioned before you have a chance to try, or made to doubt instincts that once felt clear. When every step feels subject to their judgment, resentment can grow.","advice":"Let this connection teach you how to move with more strength, but do not let it train you to stop moving.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-saturn_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-saturn_opposition', 'synastry-mars-opposition-saturn', 'relationship-mars-opposition-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-saturn_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-saturn_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Opposition Saturn', null, 'This aspect is about what happens when desire meets resistance. You may feel a strong urge to pursue what you want, while this person seems focused on limits, responsibilities, or potential consequences. Your instincts may tell you to move forward, while they question whether the timing is right. This can create tension because what feels like healthy caution to them may feel like discouragement to you.

When this works, the relationship teaches balance. They can help you direct your passion more effectively instead of scattering it, and you can help them trust action instead of remaining stuck in hesitation. One person brings movement. The other brings patience and perspective. Together, you can learn how to take meaningful action without losing sight of what it will require.

The challenge is that you want to move and they keep hitting the brakes. You get frustrated because everything feels harder than it needs to be. They get frustrated because you seem reckless or impatient. If neither of you adjusts, the relationship turns into a constant fight between action and resistance. At that point, the issue is no longer the goal itself but the struggle over how it should be pursued.

This connection works best when both people recognize that passion and discipline serve different purposes. Desire provides the motivation to move forward. Wisdom helps determine how and when to act. When those forces work together, the relationship can accomplish far more than either could alone.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This aspect is about what happens when desire meets resistance. You may feel a strong urge to pursue what you want, while this person seems focused on limits, responsibilities, or potential consequences. Your instincts may tell you to move forward, while they question whether the timing is right. This can create tension because what feels like healthy caution to them may feel like discouragement to you.\n\nWhen this works, the relationship teaches balance. They can help you direct your passion more effectively instead of scattering it, and you can help them trust action instead of remaining stuck in hesitation. One person brings movement. The other brings patience and perspective. Together, you can learn how to take meaningful action without losing sight of what it will require.\n\nThe challenge is that you want to move and they keep hitting the brakes. You get frustrated because everything feels harder than it needs to be. They get frustrated because you seem reckless or impatient. If neither of you adjusts, the relationship turns into a constant fight between action and resistance. At that point, the issue is no longer the goal itself but the struggle over how it should be pursued.\n\nThis connection works best when both people recognize that passion and discipline serve different purposes. Desire provides the motivation to move forward. Wisdom helps determine how and when to act. When those forces work together, the relationship can accomplish far more than either could alone."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that you want to move and they keep hitting the brakes. You get frustrated because everything feels harder than it needs to be. They get frustrated because you seem reckless or impatient. If neither of you adjusts, the relationship turns into a constant fight between action and resistance. At that point, the issue is no longer the goal itself but the struggle over how it should be pursued."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This connection works best when both people recognize that passion and discipline serve different purposes. Desire provides the motivation to move forward. Wisdom helps determine how and when to act. When those forces work together, the relationship can accomplish far more than either could alone."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-saturn_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Drive faces control head-on. The Mars person wants to act now; the Saturn person wants to wait and plan. Push-pull over pace, ambition, and authority, each accusing the other of the opposite flaw. Failure mode: a stalemate of force against resistance. Meet in the middle; you each hold what the other lacks.","summaryDeep":"This aspect is about what happens when desire meets resistance. You may feel a strong urge to pursue what you want, while this person seems focused on limits, responsibilities, or potential consequences. Your instincts may tell you to move forward, while they question whether the timing is right. This can create tension because what feels like healthy caution to them may feel like discouragement to you.\n\nWhen this works, the relationship teaches balance. They can help you direct your passion more effectively instead of scattering it, and you can help them trust action instead of remaining stuck in hesitation. One person brings movement. The other brings patience and perspective. Together, you can learn how to take meaningful action without losing sight of what it will require.\n\nThe challenge is that you want to move and they keep hitting the brakes. You get frustrated because everything feels harder than it needs to be. They get frustrated because you seem reckless or impatient. If neither of you adjusts, the relationship turns into a constant fight between action and resistance. At that point, the issue is no longer the goal itself but the struggle over how it should be pursued.\n\nThis connection works best when both people recognize that passion and discipline serve different purposes. Desire provides the motivation to move forward. Wisdom helps determine how and when to act. When those forces work together, the relationship can accomplish far more than either could alone.","tension":"The challenge is that you want to move and they keep hitting the brakes. You get frustrated because everything feels harder than it needs to be. They get frustrated because you seem reckless or impatient. If neither of you adjusts, the relationship turns into a constant fight between action and resistance. At that point, the issue is no longer the goal itself but the struggle over how it should be pursued.","advice":"This connection works best when both people recognize that passion and discipline serve different purposes. Desire provides the motivation to move forward. Wisdom helps determine how and when to act. When those forces work together, the relationship can accomplish far more than either could alone.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-saturn_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-saturn_sextile', 'synastry-mars-sextile-saturn', 'relationship-mars-sextile-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-saturn_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-saturn_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Sextile Saturn', null, 'This connection works because it helps action find a path forward. The support here is often subtle. Instead of creating pressure or resistance, it creates momentum that can actually be sustained. One person may provide the spark that gets things moving, while the other naturally helps shape that energy into something workable. Plans feel easier to follow through on, obstacles seem more manageable, and effort is less likely to be wasted. Together, there is a sense that progress is possible because inspiration and discipline are working in the same direction.

When this works, this person helps you trust the process. They may encourage you to take the next step instead of worrying about the entire journey. They may help you stay committed when the excitement fades, or remind you that meaningful progress is often built through small, consistent acts of devotion. Your drive remains your own, but their presence helps it find direction.

The challenge is that caution can quietly turn into avoidance. You may find yourself endlessly preparing, analyzing, or addressing one concern after another until you lose touch with the original goal. On the other side, you may dismiss their input before fully considering it because receiving guidance feels uncomfortable or limiting.

Discipline is useful when it helps you move forward. It is a problem when it becomes an excuse to do nothing.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection works because it helps action find a path forward. The support here is often subtle. Instead of creating pressure or resistance, it creates momentum that can actually be sustained. One person may provide the spark that gets things moving, while the other naturally helps shape that energy into something workable. Plans feel easier to follow through on, obstacles seem more manageable, and effort is less likely to be wasted. Together, there is a sense that progress is possible because inspiration and discipline are working in the same direction.\n\nWhen this works, this person helps you trust the process. They may encourage you to take the next step instead of worrying about the entire journey. They may help you stay committed when the excitement fades, or remind you that meaningful progress is often built through small, consistent acts of devotion. Your drive remains your own, but their presence helps it find direction.\n\nThe challenge is that caution can quietly turn into avoidance. You may find yourself endlessly preparing, analyzing, or addressing one concern after another until you lose touch with the original goal. On the other side, you may dismiss their input before fully considering it because receiving guidance feels uncomfortable or limiting.\n\nDiscipline is useful when it helps you move forward. It is a problem when it becomes an excuse to do nothing."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that caution can quietly turn into avoidance. You may find yourself endlessly preparing, analyzing, or addressing one concern after another until you lose touch with the original goal. On the other side, you may dismiss their input before fully considering it because receiving guidance feels uncomfortable or limiting."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Discipline is useful when it helps you move forward. It is a problem when it becomes an excuse to do nothing."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-saturn_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Action and discipline cooperate. The Mars person supplies energy, the Saturn person supplies structure, and together they get real things done. One of the better contacts for a working partnership. Aim the drive at a concrete, long-term goal.","summaryDeep":"This connection works because it helps action find a path forward. The support here is often subtle. Instead of creating pressure or resistance, it creates momentum that can actually be sustained. One person may provide the spark that gets things moving, while the other naturally helps shape that energy into something workable. Plans feel easier to follow through on, obstacles seem more manageable, and effort is less likely to be wasted. Together, there is a sense that progress is possible because inspiration and discipline are working in the same direction.\n\nWhen this works, this person helps you trust the process. They may encourage you to take the next step instead of worrying about the entire journey. They may help you stay committed when the excitement fades, or remind you that meaningful progress is often built through small, consistent acts of devotion. Your drive remains your own, but their presence helps it find direction.\n\nThe challenge is that caution can quietly turn into avoidance. You may find yourself endlessly preparing, analyzing, or addressing one concern after another until you lose touch with the original goal. On the other side, you may dismiss their input before fully considering it because receiving guidance feels uncomfortable or limiting.\n\nDiscipline is useful when it helps you move forward. It is a problem when it becomes an excuse to do nothing.","tension":"The challenge is that caution can quietly turn into avoidance. You may find yourself endlessly preparing, analyzing, or addressing one concern after another until you lose touch with the original goal. On the other side, you may dismiss their input before fully considering it because receiving guidance feels uncomfortable or limiting.","advice":"Discipline is useful when it helps you move forward. It is a problem when it becomes an excuse to do nothing.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-saturn_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-saturn_square', 'synastry-mars-square-saturn', 'relationship-mars-square-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-saturn_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-saturn_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Square Saturn', null, 'This person has a way of bringing you face to face with your limits. Their timing may not match yours. Their caution may feel like resistance. Their questions may arrive right when you are ready to act. You reach for movement, and suddenly you are being asked to slow down, consider the consequences, or work within a set of constraints you did not choose. This can be deeply frustrating. It can also become a teacher.

This is about frustration. You want to act, and something gets in the way.

At its best, the conflict forces you to get your act together. This person points out where you''re wasting energy, acting too fast, or chasing something without a real plan. If you want results, you have to be more disciplined.

At its worst, it''s just a power struggle. They block. You push. They dig in. You get angry. Eventually, the relationship stops being about the original issue and becomes a fight over control. This is where the aspect can become exhausting. What could have been used to build something meaningful ends up consumed by the struggle itself.

The lesson is discernment. Some limits are real. Some come from caution, uncertainty, or a desire to protect what matters. Some feedback helps you act with more strength. Some feedback reflects a different relationship to risk and timing. Learn the difference. Turn the no into a conversation when you can. Ask what the concern is protecting and what the action is trying to accomplish.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a way of bringing you face to face with your limits. Their timing may not match yours. Their caution may feel like resistance. Their questions may arrive right when you are ready to act. You reach for movement, and suddenly you are being asked to slow down, consider the consequences, or work within a set of constraints you did not choose. This can be deeply frustrating. It can also become a teacher.\n\nThis is about frustration. You want to act, and something gets in the way.\n\nAt its best, the conflict forces you to get your act together. This person points out where you''re wasting energy, acting too fast, or chasing something without a real plan. If you want results, you have to be more disciplined.\n\nAt its worst, it''s just a power struggle. They block. You push. They dig in. You get angry. Eventually, the relationship stops being about the original issue and becomes a fight over control. This is where the aspect can become exhausting. What could have been used to build something meaningful ends up consumed by the struggle itself.\n\nThe lesson is discernment. Some limits are real. Some come from caution, uncertainty, or a desire to protect what matters. Some feedback helps you act with more strength. Some feedback reflects a different relationship to risk and timing. Learn the difference. Turn the no into a conversation when you can. Ask what the concern is protecting and what the action is trying to accomplish."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its worst, it''s just a power struggle. They block. You push. They dig in. You get angry. Eventually, the relationship stops being about the original issue and becomes a fight over control. This is where the aspect can become exhausting. What could have been used to build something meaningful ends up consumed by the struggle itself."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The lesson is discernment. Some limits are real. Some come from caution, uncertainty, or a desire to protect what matters. Some feedback helps you act with more strength. Some feedback reflects a different relationship to risk and timing. Learn the difference. Turn the no into a conversation when you can. Ask what the concern is protecting and what the action is trying to accomplish."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-saturn_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Drive grinds against control. The Mars person feels slowed, judged, or thwarted; the Saturn person finds the other reckless. Real friction around effort, ambition, or sex. Failure mode: resentment and suppression, or one shutting the other down. Workable if both respect the tension; name the brake instead of fighting it in silence.","summaryDeep":"This person has a way of bringing you face to face with your limits. Their timing may not match yours. Their caution may feel like resistance. Their questions may arrive right when you are ready to act. You reach for movement, and suddenly you are being asked to slow down, consider the consequences, or work within a set of constraints you did not choose. This can be deeply frustrating. It can also become a teacher.\n\nThis is about frustration. You want to act, and something gets in the way.\n\nAt its best, the conflict forces you to get your act together. This person points out where you''re wasting energy, acting too fast, or chasing something without a real plan. If you want results, you have to be more disciplined.\n\nAt its worst, it''s just a power struggle. They block. You push. They dig in. You get angry. Eventually, the relationship stops being about the original issue and becomes a fight over control. This is where the aspect can become exhausting. What could have been used to build something meaningful ends up consumed by the struggle itself.\n\nThe lesson is discernment. Some limits are real. Some come from caution, uncertainty, or a desire to protect what matters. Some feedback helps you act with more strength. Some feedback reflects a different relationship to risk and timing. Learn the difference. Turn the no into a conversation when you can. Ask what the concern is protecting and what the action is trying to accomplish.","tension":"At its worst, it''s just a power struggle. They block. You push. They dig in. You get angry. Eventually, the relationship stops being about the original issue and becomes a fight over control. This is where the aspect can become exhausting. What could have been used to build something meaningful ends up consumed by the struggle itself.","advice":"The lesson is discernment. Some limits are real. Some come from caution, uncertainty, or a desire to protect what matters. Some feedback helps you act with more strength. Some feedback reflects a different relationship to risk and timing. Learn the difference. Turn the no into a conversation when you can. Ask what the concern is protecting and what the action is trying to accomplish.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry-mars-trine-saturn', 'relationship-mars-trine-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-saturn_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-saturn_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Trine Saturn', null, 'This person has a steadying effect on your actions. Instead of feeling restricted, you may feel supported by a sense of structure that helps you use your energy more wisely. Around them, it can become easier to focus on what truly matters, work at a sustainable pace, and remain committed to your goals. Their influence encourages patience, helping your efforts gain strength through consistency rather than urgency.

When this works, the two of you create a steady rhythm between effort and patience. You are less likely to rush into things that cannot be sustained or scatter your energy across too many directions at once. What you begin has a better chance of growing roots. What you commit to has a better chance of lasting.

There is a quiet strength in this connection. It supports follow-through. It helps you stay with the work after the excitement fades, and it reminds you that meaningful results often come from consistency more than intensity.

The challenge is remembering that caution and fear can wear similar clothes. Because the pace feels measured, it can be easy to believe that more time, more preparation, or one more adjustment will bring certainty. But certainty is rarely what gets us moving. If you''re not careful, the desire that once felt alive can get buried beneath endless refinement. What began as thoughtful timing can quietly become avoidance, and the moment you''re waiting for never quite arrives.

This connection works best when discipline gives your drive endurance, not another reason to stay still.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a steadying effect on your actions. Instead of feeling restricted, you may feel supported by a sense of structure that helps you use your energy more wisely. Around them, it can become easier to focus on what truly matters, work at a sustainable pace, and remain committed to your goals. Their influence encourages patience, helping your efforts gain strength through consistency rather than urgency.\n\nWhen this works, the two of you create a steady rhythm between effort and patience. You are less likely to rush into things that cannot be sustained or scatter your energy across too many directions at once. What you begin has a better chance of growing roots. What you commit to has a better chance of lasting.\n\nThere is a quiet strength in this connection. It supports follow-through. It helps you stay with the work after the excitement fades, and it reminds you that meaningful results often come from consistency more than intensity.\n\nThe challenge is remembering that caution and fear can wear similar clothes. Because the pace feels measured, it can be easy to believe that more time, more preparation, or one more adjustment will bring certainty. But certainty is rarely what gets us moving. If you''re not careful, the desire that once felt alive can get buried beneath endless refinement. What began as thoughtful timing can quietly become avoidance, and the moment you''re waiting for never quite arrives.\n\nThis connection works best when discipline gives your drive endurance, not another reason to stay still."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is remembering that caution and fear can wear similar clothes. Because the pace feels measured, it can be easy to believe that more time, more preparation, or one more adjustment will bring certainty. But certainty is rarely what gets us moving. If you''re not careful, the desire that once felt alive can get buried beneath endless refinement. What began as thoughtful timing can quietly become avoidance, and the moment you''re waiting for never quite arrives."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This connection works best when discipline gives your drive endurance, not another reason to stay still."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-saturn_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Energy and discipline flow together. The Mars person''s drive finds steady form through the Saturn person''s structure; ambition becomes achievable. Stable and productive. Channel it into a shared project; this combination is built to last.","summaryDeep":"This person has a steadying effect on your actions. Instead of feeling restricted, you may feel supported by a sense of structure that helps you use your energy more wisely. Around them, it can become easier to focus on what truly matters, work at a sustainable pace, and remain committed to your goals. Their influence encourages patience, helping your efforts gain strength through consistency rather than urgency.\n\nWhen this works, the two of you create a steady rhythm between effort and patience. You are less likely to rush into things that cannot be sustained or scatter your energy across too many directions at once. What you begin has a better chance of growing roots. What you commit to has a better chance of lasting.\n\nThere is a quiet strength in this connection. It supports follow-through. It helps you stay with the work after the excitement fades, and it reminds you that meaningful results often come from consistency more than intensity.\n\nThe challenge is remembering that caution and fear can wear similar clothes. Because the pace feels measured, it can be easy to believe that more time, more preparation, or one more adjustment will bring certainty. But certainty is rarely what gets us moving. If you''re not careful, the desire that once felt alive can get buried beneath endless refinement. What began as thoughtful timing can quietly become avoidance, and the moment you''re waiting for never quite arrives.\n\nThis connection works best when discipline gives your drive endurance, not another reason to stay still.","tension":"The challenge is remembering that caution and fear can wear similar clothes. Because the pace feels measured, it can be easy to believe that more time, more preparation, or one more adjustment will bring certainty. But certainty is rarely what gets us moving. If you''re not careful, the desire that once felt alive can get buried beneath endless refinement. What began as thoughtful timing can quietly become avoidance, and the moment you''re waiting for never quite arrives.","advice":"This connection works best when discipline gives your drive endurance, not another reason to stay still.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"sun","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry-mars-conjunction-sun', 'relationship-mars-conjunction-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-sun_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-sun_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Conjunction Sun', null, 'This person energizes you in a way that is hard to ignore. They can quiet the voice in your head that second-guesses everything and bring out the part of you that trusts its instincts and just goes for it. The attraction here is immediate, and so is the momentum. Things can spark quickly, heat up quickly, and take on a life of their own before either of you has time to slow down and think about where it is all going. This is not the kind of connection that likes to sit still. It wants movement, action, and the thrill of seeing what happens when neither of you holds back.

At its best, this person helps you trust yourself a little more. You may find yourself acting on things you would normally overthink, saying what you really mean, or finally dealing with something you have been putting off. It can feel good to be around someone who gets you out of your head and reminds you that you do not have to second-guess every step.

At its most challenging, the same energy can feel like pressure. What starts out exciting can turn into frustration when one person wants to move faster than the other. You may feel like they''re pushing you, while they may feel like they''re just trying to get things moving. Because there''s so much energy between you, even small disagreements can pick up speed before either of you realizes it.

The good news is that this energy does not have to turn into conflict. It works best when you channel it into something shared. Tackle a project, make plans, get out of the house, or work toward a goal together. The more you have to focus on as a team, the less likely you are to end up pushing against each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person energizes you in a way that is hard to ignore. They can quiet the voice in your head that second-guesses everything and bring out the part of you that trusts its instincts and just goes for it. The attraction here is immediate, and so is the momentum. Things can spark quickly, heat up quickly, and take on a life of their own before either of you has time to slow down and think about where it is all going. This is not the kind of connection that likes to sit still. It wants movement, action, and the thrill of seeing what happens when neither of you holds back.\n\nAt its best, this person helps you trust yourself a little more. You may find yourself acting on things you would normally overthink, saying what you really mean, or finally dealing with something you have been putting off. It can feel good to be around someone who gets you out of your head and reminds you that you do not have to second-guess every step.\n\nAt its most challenging, the same energy can feel like pressure. What starts out exciting can turn into frustration when one person wants to move faster than the other. You may feel like they''re pushing you, while they may feel like they''re just trying to get things moving. Because there''s so much energy between you, even small disagreements can pick up speed before either of you realizes it.\n\nThe good news is that this energy does not have to turn into conflict. It works best when you channel it into something shared. Tackle a project, make plans, get out of the house, or work toward a goal together. The more you have to focus on as a team, the less likely you are to end up pushing against each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its most challenging, the same energy can feel like pressure. What starts out exciting can turn into frustration when one person wants to move faster than the other. You may feel like they''re pushing you, while they may feel like they''re just trying to get things moving. Because there''s so much energy between you, even small disagreements can pick up speed before either of you realizes it."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The good news is that this energy does not have to turn into conflict. It works best when you channel it into something shared. Tackle a project, make plans, get out of the house, or work toward a goal together. The more you have to focus on as a team, the less likely you are to end up pushing against each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-sun_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s drive meets B''s identity. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person energizes you in a way that is hard to ignore. They can quiet the voice in your head that second-guesses everything and bring out the part of you that trusts its instincts and just goes for it. The attraction here is immediate, and so is the momentum. Things can spark quickly, heat up quickly, and take on a life of their own before either of you has time to slow down and think about where it is all going. This is not the kind of connection that likes to sit still. It wants movement, action, and the thrill of seeing what happens when neither of you holds back.\n\nAt its best, this person helps you trust yourself a little more. You may find yourself acting on things you would normally overthink, saying what you really mean, or finally dealing with something you have been putting off. It can feel good to be around someone who gets you out of your head and reminds you that you do not have to second-guess every step.\n\nAt its most challenging, the same energy can feel like pressure. What