Reach for it. This aspect opens when someone acts.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"The attraction is there, but it usually needs someone to do something with it. Venus and Mars support each other here, so charm and desire can work well together, but the chemistry may not fully open unless someone makes a move.\n\nThis can start in a subtle way. A little flirting, a little effort, a little willingness to show interest. The more both people participate, the more the attraction has somewhere to go.\n\nFailure mode: leaving the spark sitting there because everyone is waiting for it to become obvious on its own.\n\nReach for it. This aspect opens when someone acts."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Failure mode: leaving the spark sitting there because everyone is waiting for it to become obvious on its own."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Reach for it. This aspect opens when someone acts."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-venus_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Mars person''s initiative can wake up the Venus person''s pleasure and affection without forcing it. This is an opportunity contact: flirtation, desire, and warmth grow when someone actually reaches. Use the spark, then see whether it becomes steadiness.","summaryDeep":"The attraction is there, but it usually needs someone to do something with it. Venus and Mars support each other here, so charm and desire can work well together, but the chemistry may not fully open unless someone makes a move.\n\nThis can start in a subtle way. A little flirting, a little effort, a little willingness to show interest. The more both people participate, the more the attraction has somewhere to go.\n\nFailure mode: leaving the spark sitting there because everyone is waiting for it to become obvious on its own.\n\nReach for it. This aspect opens when someone acts.","tension":"Failure mode: leaving the spark sitting there because everyone is waiting for it to become obvious on its own.","advice":"Reach for it. This aspect opens when someone acts.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mars_B-venus_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mars","planetB":"venus","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mars_B-venus_square', 'synastry-mars-square-venus', 'relationship-mars-square-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mars_B-venus_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mars_B-venus_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mars Square Venus', 'This is attraction with some edge to it. Venus and Mars want each other, but they don''t move together easily. The chemistry is real, but it can come with irritation, mixed signals, and that feeling that the other person knows exactly how to get under your skin.', 'This is attraction with some edge to it. Venus and Mars want each other, but they don''t move together easily. The chemistry is real, but it can come with irritation, mixed signals, and that feeling that the other person knows exactly how to get under your skin.

There may be a lot of heat here, but not all heat is intimacy. Sometimes the charge comes from being challenged. Sometimes it comes from feeling provoked. The trick is knowing the difference between passion and a pattern that keeps making you tense.

Failure mode: confusing friction for chemistry and staying because the conflict makes the connection feel alive.

Use the charge for something you''re building together. Don''t keep turning it on each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This is attraction with some edge to it. Venus and Mars want each other, but they don''t move together easily. The chemistry is real, but it can come with irritation, mixed signals, and that feeling that the other person knows exactly how to get under your skin.\n\nThere may be a lot of heat here, but not all heat is intimacy. Sometimes the charge comes from being challenged. Sometimes it comes from feeling provoked. The trick is knowing the difference between passion and a pattern that keeps making you tense.\n\nFailure mode: confusing friction for chemistry and staying because the conflict makes the connection feel alive.\n\nUse the charge for something you''re building together. Don''t keep turning it on each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Failure mode: confusing friction for chemistry and staying because the conflict makes the connection feel alive."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Use the charge for something you''re building together. Don''t keep turning it on each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mars_B-venus_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Mars person''s pursuit and the Venus person''s comfort can provoke each other. The pull is real, but irritation can become part of the attraction pattern if neither person slows down. Put the charge into honest desire, not arguments that stand in for intimacy.","summaryDeep":"This is attraction with some edge to it. Venus and Mars want each other, but they don''t move together easily. The chemistry is real, but it can come with irritation, mixed signals, and that feeling that the other person knows exactly how to get under your skin.\n\nThere may be a lot of heat here, but not all heat is intimacy. Sometimes the charge comes from being challenged. Sometimes it comes from feeling provoked. The trick is knowing the difference between passion and a pattern that