  ('A-mercury_B-moon_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"moon","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-moon_square', 'synastry-mercury-square-moon', 'relationship-mercury-square-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-moon_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-moon_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Square Moon', null, 'This person may say the thing in a way that lands wrong.

They may ask a simple question and it feels like criticism. They may try to explain your feelings and it sounds like they are correcting you. They may reach for logic at the exact moment you need warmth. The problem is not always what they say. It is how it lands in your body.

This can become exhausting if it keeps happening. You may start bracing before the conversation even begins. They may feel like they are trying to help, while you feel like you are being studied. You may feel pressured to explain your emotions clearly before you have even had a chance to understand them yourself.

When this works, it can make both people more skilled. You learn to say what you feel more directly. They learn to listen without rushing to organize or solve. The friction becomes useful when both people stop defending their method and start caring about the impact.

The deeper challenge is the temptation to become certain too quickly. One person decides they already know what the feeling means. The other decides they are not being heard. Then the conversation becomes less about understanding and more about protection.

Slow down. Put comfort before analysis. Say what landed. Ask what was meant. This connection improves when both people stop treating emotional clarity as something that can be forced.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may say the thing in a way that lands wrong.\n\nThey may ask a simple question and it feels like criticism. They may try to explain your feelings and it sounds like they are correcting you. They may reach for logic at the exact moment you need warmth. The problem is not always what they say. It is how it lands in your body.\n\nThis can become exhausting if it keeps happening. You may start bracing before the conversation even begins. They may feel like they are trying to help, while you feel like you are being studied. You may feel pressured to explain your emotions clearly before you have even had a chance to understand them yourself.\n\nWhen this works, it can make both people more skilled. You learn to say what you feel more directly. They learn to listen without rushing to organize or solve. The friction becomes useful when both people stop defending their method and start caring about the impact.\n\nThe deeper challenge is the temptation to become certain too quickly. One person decides they already know what the feeling means. The other decides they are not being heard. Then the conversation becomes less about understanding and more about protection.\n\nSlow down. Put comfort before analysis. Say what landed. Ask what was meant. This connection improves when both people stop treating emotional clarity as something that can be forced."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The deeper challenge is the temptation to become certain too quickly. One person decides they already know what the feeling means. The other decides they are not being heard. Then the conversation becomes less about understanding and more about protection."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Slow down. Put comfort before analysis. Say what landed. Ask what was meant. This connection improves when both people stop treating emotional clarity as something that can be forced."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-moon_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s feelings. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This person may say the thing in a way that lands wrong.\n\nThey may ask a simple question and it feels like criticism. They may try to explain your feelings and it sounds like they are correcting you. They may reach for logic at the exact moment you need warmth. The problem is not always what they say. It is how it lands in your body.\n\nThis can become exhausting if it keeps happening. You may start bracing before the conversation even begins. They may feel like they are trying to help, while you feel like you are being studied. You may feel pressured to explain your emotions clearly before you have even had a chance to understand them yourself.\n\nWhen this works, it can make both people more skilled. You learn to say what you feel more directly. They learn to listen without rushing to organize or solve. The friction becomes useful when both people stop defending their method and start caring about the impact.\n\nThe deeper challenge is the temptation to become certain too quickly. One person decides they already know what the feeling means. The other decides they are not being heard. Then the conversation becomes less about understanding and more about protection.\n\nSlow down. Put comfort before analysis. Say what landed. Ask what was meant. This connection improves when both people stop treating emotional clarity as something that can be forced.","tension":"The deeper challenge is the temptation to become certain too quickly. One person decides they already know what the feeling means. The other decides they are not being heard. Then the conversation becomes less about understanding and more about protection.","advice":"Slow down. Put comfort before analysis. Say what landed. Ask what was meant. This connection improves when both people stop treating emotional clarity as something that can be forced.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-moon_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"moon","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-moon_trine', 'synastry-mercury-trine-moon', 'relationship-mercury-trine-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-moon_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-moon_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Trine Moon', null, 'This person may make it easier to talk about what you feel.

There is often a natural trust in the way conversation moves between you. You may feel less afraid of being misunderstood. Less worried that your emotions will be dismissed, judged, or turned into a debate. The words come more easily because the listening feels safer.

When this works, it can be deeply steadying. This person may help you name what is happening inside without making it heavier. They may ask the right question, offer the right reflection, or simply give you enough room to hear yourself. You can talk through emotional things without feeling like you are being managed.

This kind of connection can become a place of repair. Not because every conversation is perfect, but because both people seem willing to understand. Feelings do not have to become chaos. Words do not have to become weapons. There is enough care in the exchange to keep both people connected.

The challenge is that ease can make you lazy with honesty. You may assume they already know what you feel. They may assume you will say it if it matters. But even natural understanding needs real information.

Keep telling the truth in real time. Let the conversation stay alive. The gift here is not just that this person understands you. It is that the two of you can keep learning how to understand each other more deeply.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may make it easier to talk about what you feel.\n\nThere is often a natural trust in the way conversation moves between you. You may feel less afraid of being misunderstood. Less worried that your emotions will be dismissed, judged, or turned into a debate. The words come more easily because the listening feels safer.\n\nWhen this works, it can be deeply steadying. This person may help you name what is happening inside without making it heavier. They may ask the right question, offer the right reflection, or simply give you enough room to hear yourself. You can talk through emotional things without feeling like you are being managed.\n\nThis kind of connection can become a place of repair. Not because every conversation is perfect, but because both people seem willing to understand. Feelings do not have to become chaos. Words do not have to become weapons. There is enough care in the exchange to keep both people connected.\n\nThe challenge is that ease can make you lazy with honesty. You may assume they already know what you feel. They may assume you will say it if it matters. But even natural understanding needs real information.\n\nKeep telling the truth in real time. Let the conversation stay alive. The gift here is not just that this person understands you. It is that the two of you can keep learning how to understand each other more deeply."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that ease can make you lazy with honesty. You may assume they already know what you feel. They may assume you will say it if it matters. But even natural understanding needs real information."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Keep telling the truth in real time. Let the conversation stay alive. The gift here 