l, and makes the first one feel shut out. Neither of you usually means to. Both of you end up feeling unseen in exactly the place you most wanted to be understood. The shadow takes over when you fall in love with the feeling of the conversation and stop asking whether it is true. You read between the lines until the lines disappear. You decide this person wants what you want, means what you mean, sees what you see. Then the fog clears, reality arrives, and the disappointment can be brutal. There is a particular pain in realizing you were partly talking to your own dream.","advice":"Keep returning to the shore. Come back to what was actually said, not what you hoped was meant.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-neptune_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"neptune","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-neptune_sextile', 'synastry-mercury-sextile-neptune', 'relationship-mercury-sextile-neptune']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-neptune_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-neptune_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Sextile Neptune', null, 'Talking with this person has a quiet, unhurried quality, more like sitting together than trading information.

There is a soft understanding here that you do not have to work for. You pick up on each other''s moods, read the tone under the words, follow each other into dreams and half-formed ideas without anyone needing to spell things out. It is gentler than the harder versions of this pairing. No fog, no constant confusion. You can drift into the imaginative, unspoken register when you want it and come back to solid ground without trouble.

You make each other more perceptive. This person meets your impressions with curiosity instead of either dismissing them as vague or forcing them into something falsely precise. You can talk about a film, a piece of music, a dream, the things that are hard to explain to most people, and not have to justify why any of it matters. The other one already gets it.

The catch is that it sits in the background unless you use it. This kind of connection invites but does not push. It opens a door and waits. If you both keep waiting for the other to go deeper, neither of you will, and all that potential stays a pleasant background hum instead of becoming anything real. It can also fake depth if you let it. Conversations can feel meaningful while going nowhere, a warm atmosphere of shared sensitivity that never turns into an actual insight or decision. And because the mood between you is so easy, it is tempting to protect it. When something difficult needs to be said, you avoid saying it directly. Instead, you soften it, hint at it, or talk around it. Over time, keeping the peace can become more important than being honest.

Reach for it on purpose. Make something with the sensitivity you share, a project, a creative habit, a real conversation that goes somewhere. And keep checking that you actually know what the other one means, not just what they feel but what they specifically think and want. Used deliberately, this becomes one of the easiest places you have to think and create. Left alone, it stays a nice feeling and nothing more.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Talking with this person has a quiet, unhurried quality, more like sitting together than trading information.\n\nThere is a soft understanding here that you do not have to work for. You pick up on each other''s moods, read the tone under the words, follow each other into dreams and half-formed ideas without anyone needing to spell things out. It is gentler than the harder versions of this pairing. No fog, no constant confusion. You can drift into the imaginative, unspoken register when you want it and come back to solid ground without trouble.\n\nYou make each other more perceptive. This person meets your impressions with curiosity instead of either dismissing them as vague or forcing them into something falsely precise. You can talk about a film, a piece of music, a dream, the things that are hard to explain to most people, and not have to justify why any of it matters. The other one already gets it.\n\nThe catch is that it sits in the background unless you use it. This kind of connection invites but does not push. It opens a door and waits. If you both keep waiting for the other to go deeper, neither of you will, and all that potential stays a pleasant background hum instead of becoming anything real. It can also fake depth if you let it. Conversations can feel meaningful while going nowhere, a warm atmosphere of shared sensitivity that never turns into an actual insight or decision. And because the mood between you is so easy, it is tempting to protect it. When something difficult needs to be said, you avoid saying it directly. Instead, you soften it, hint at it, or talk around it. Over time, keeping the peace can become more important than being honest.\n\nReach for it on purpose. Make something with the sensitivity you share, a project, a creative habit, a real conversation that goes somewhere. And keep checking that you actually know what the other one means, not just what they feel but what they specifically think and want. Used deliberately, this becomes one of the easiest places you have to think and create. Left alone, it stays a nice feeling and nothing more."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The catch is that it sits in the background unless you use it. This kind of connection invites but does not push. It opens a door and waits. If you both keep waiting for the other to go deeper, neither of you will, and all that potential stays a pleasant background hum instead of becoming anything real. It can also fake depth if you let it. Conversations can feel meaningful while going nowhere, a warm atmosphere of shared sensitivity that never turns into an actual insight or decision. And because the mood between you is so easy, it is tempting to protect it. When something difficult needs to be said, you avoid saying it directly. Instead, you soften it, hint at it, or talk around it. Over time, keeping the peace can become more important than being honest."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Reach for it on purpose. Make something with the sensitivity you share, a project, a creative habit, a real conversation that goes somewhere. And keep checking that you actually know what the other one means, not just what they feel but what they specifically think and want. Used deliberately, this becomes one of the easiest places you have to think and create. Left alone, it stays a nice feeling and nothing more."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-neptune_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s dreams. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDe