rned by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-pluto_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-pluto_opposition', 'synastry-mercury-opposition-pluto', 'relationship-mercury-opposition-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-pluto_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-pluto_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Opposition Pluto', null, 'This person has a way of getting under your skin and into your thoughts. Their presence can challenge how you make sense of the world, how you communicate, and even how you trust your own perceptions. There is a magnetic mental connection here, but it rarely feels neutral. The Pluto person may pick up on what is left unsaid, sensing the deeper story beneath the Mercury person''s words. The Mercury person may be drawn to the Pluto person''s insight while also feeling unsettled by how easily they seem to see through the surface.

At its best, this aspect asks both people to grow beyond the stories they''ve been telling themselves. The Pluto person can encourage the Mercury person to question inherited beliefs, speak more honestly, and explore ideas that feel uncomfortable but necessary. The Mercury person can help the Pluto person give language to what has been sensed, feared, or understood beneath the surface. Together, they can uncover truths that neither would likely find on their own.

But oppositions rarely let us stay comfortable. This connection can become a struggle over whose version of reality gets to take up the most space. One person may push for answers while the other feels the need to defend themselves. Conversations can go in circles about what was said, what was meant, and who is right. When fear, insecurity, or control takes over, communication can become more about winning than understanding each other.

The invitation here is to practice curiosity instead of certainty. Both people need enough room to think, question, change their minds, and disagree without feeling diminished. The wisdom of this aspect comes from recognizing that truth is often larger than any one person''s perspective.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a way of getting under your skin and into your thoughts. Their presence can challenge how you make sense of the world, how you communicate, and even how you trust your own perceptions. There is a magnetic mental connection here, but it rarely feels neutral. The Pluto person may pick up on what is left unsaid, sensing the deeper story beneath the Mercury person''s words. The Mercury person may be drawn to the Pluto person''s insight while also feeling unsettled by how easily they seem to see through the surface.\n\nAt its best, this aspect asks both people to grow beyond the stories they''ve been telling themselves. The Pluto person can encourage the Mercury person to question inherited beliefs, speak more honestly, and explore ideas that feel uncomfortable but necessary. The Mercury person can help the Pluto person give language to what has been sensed, feared, or understood beneath the surface. Together, they can uncover truths that neither would likely find on their own.\n\nBut oppositions rarely let us stay comfortable. This connection can become a struggle over whose version of reality gets to take up the most space. One person may push for answers while the other feels the need to defend themselves. Conversations can go in circles about what was said, what was meant, and who is right. When fear, insecurity, or control takes over, communication can become more about winning than understanding each other.\n\nThe invitation here is to practice curiosity instead of certainty. Both people need enough room to think, question, change their minds, and disagree without feeling diminished. The wisdom of this aspect comes from recognizing that truth is often larger than any one person''s perspective."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But oppositions rarely let us stay comfortable. This connection can become a struggle over whose version of reality gets to take up the most space. One person may push for answers while the other feels the need to defend themselves. Conversations can go in circles about what was said, what was meant, and who is right. When fear, insecurity, or control takes over, communication can become more about winning than understanding each other."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The invitation here is to practice curiosity instead of certainty. Both people need enough room to think, question, change their minds, and disagree without feeling diminished. The wisdom of this aspect comes from recognizing that truth is often larger than any one person''s perspective."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-pluto_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s depth and power. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person has a way of getting under your skin and into your thoughts. Their presence can challenge how you make sense of the world, how you communicate, and even how you trust your own perceptions. There is a magnetic mental connection here, but it rarely feels neutral. The Pluto person may pick up on what is left unsaid, sensing the deeper story beneath the Mercury person''s words. The Mercury person may be drawn to the Pluto person''s insight while also feeling unsettled by how easily they seem to see through the surface.\n\nAt its best, this aspect asks both people to grow beyond the stories they''ve been telling themselves. The Pluto person can encourage the Mercury person to question inherited beliefs, speak more honestly, and explore ideas that feel uncomfortable but necessary. The Mercury person can help the Pluto person give language to what has been sensed, feared, or understood beneath the surface. Together, they can uncover truths that neither would likely find on their own.\n\nBut oppositions rarely let us stay comfortable. This connection can become a struggle over whose version of reality gets to take up the most space. One person may push for answers while the other feels the need to defend themselves. Conversations can go in circles about what was said, what was meant, and who is right. When fear, insecurity, or control takes over, communication can become more about winning than understanding each other.\n\nThe invitation here is to practice curiosity instead of certainty. Both people need enough room to think, question, change their minds, and disagree without feeling diminished. The wisdom of this aspect comes from recognizing that truth is often larger than any one person''s perspective.","tension":"But oppositions rarely let us stay comfortable. This connection can become a struggle over whose version of reality gets to take up the most space. One person may push for answers while the other feels the need to defend themselves. Conversations can go in circles about what was said, what was meant, and who is right. When fear, insecurity, or control takes over, communication can become more about winning than understanding each other.","advice":"The invitation here is to practice curiosity instead of certainty. Both people need enough room to think, question, change their minds, and disagree without feeling diminished. The wisdom of this aspect comes from recognizing that truth is often larger than any one person''s perspective.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-pluto_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-pluto_sextile', 'synastry-mercury-sextile-pluto', 'relationship-mercury-sextile-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-pluto_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-pluto_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Sextile Pluto', null, 'This aspect creates an opportunity for deeper, more honest communication. The Pluto person often senses what lies beneath the Mercury person''s words. They may notice the hesitation, hear what has been left unsaid, or ask the question that brings the real conversation into focus.

There is depth here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured, it can build a strong sense of trust. The Mercury person may feel encouraged to speak more openly, explore thoughts they have not fully formed, or find language for experiences that have been difficult to express. The Pluto person may discover that their deeper perceptions, instincts, and private insights are met with curiosity rather than discomfort.

One of the strengths of this aspect is its patience. It does not require immediate vulnerability. Instead, it allows intimacy to develop gradually through honest conversation. The more willing both people are to stay curious and engaged, the more meaningful the connection becomes.

The challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to appreciate the possibility of depth without fully stepping into it. If difficult conversations are continually avoided, the relationship may remain supportive and interesting, but some of its greatest opportunities for understanding and growth may never be realized.

Let the deeper conversations happen instead of always steering around them. This one rewards the choice to go there.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This aspect creates an opportunity for deeper, more honest communication. The Pluto person often senses what lies beneath the Mercury person''s words. They may notice the hesitation, hear what has been left unsaid, or ask the question that brings the real conversation into focus.\n\nThere is depth here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured, it can build a strong sense of trust. The Mercury person may feel encouraged to speak more openly, explore thoughts they have not fully formed, or find language for experiences that have been difficult to express. The Pluto person may discover that their deeper perceptions, instincts, and private insights are met with curiosity rather than discomfort.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is its patience. It does not require immediate vulnerability. Instead, it allows intimacy to develop gradually through honest conversation. The more willing both people are to stay curious and engaged, the more meaningful the connection becomes.\n\nThe challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to appreciate the possibility of depth without fully stepping into it. If difficult conversations are continually avoided, the relationship may remain supportive and interesting, but some of its greatest opportunities for understanding and growth may never be realized.\n\nLet the deeper conversations happen instead of always steering around them. This one rewards the choice to go there."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to appreciate the possibility of depth without fully stepping into it. If difficult conversations are continually avoided, the relationship may remain supportive and interesting, but some of its greatest opportunities for understanding and growth may never be realized."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the deeper conversations happen instead of always steering around them. This one rewards the choice to go there."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-pluto_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s depth and power. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This aspect creates an opportunity for deeper, more honest communication. The Pluto person often senses what lies beneath the Mercury person''s words. They may notice the hesitation, hear what has been left unsaid, or ask the question that brings the real conversation into focus.\n\nThere is depth here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured, it can build a strong sense of trust. The Mercury person may feel encouraged to speak more openly, explore thoughts they have not fully formed, or find language for experiences that have been difficult to express. The Pluto person may discover that their deeper perceptions, instincts, and private insights are met with curiosity rather than discomfort.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is its patience. It does not require immediate vulnerability. Instead, it allows intimacy to develop gradually through honest conversation. The more willing both people are to stay curious and engaged, the more meaningful the connection becomes.\n\nThe challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to appreciate the possibility of depth without fully stepping into it. If difficult conversations are continually avoided, the relationship may remain supportive and interesting, but some of its greatest opportunities for understanding and growth may never be realized.\n\nLet the deeper conversations happen instead of always steering around them. This one rewards the choice to go there.","tension":"The challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to appreciate the possibility of depth without fully stepping into it. If difficult conversations are continually avoided, the relationship may remain supportive and interesting, but some of its greatest opportunities for understanding and growth may never be realized.","advice":"Let the deeper conversations happen instead of always steering around them. This one rewards the choice to go there.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-pluto_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-pluto_square', 'synastry-mercury-square-pluto', 'relationship-mercury-square-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-pluto_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-pluto_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Square Pluto', null, 'Mercury-Pluto squares have a way of getting under the skin of a conversation. This is not the kind of connection that stays on the surface for long. The Pluto person often pushes for what is underneath the words, while the Mercury person may feel challenged to explain, clarify, or reveal more than they intended.

There can be a powerful fascination between you. The conversations may feel compelling, consuming, and difficult to walk away from. Even when an exchange becomes uncomfortable, there can be a sense that something important is trying to emerge. Hidden fears, old assumptions, and unspoken truths have a way of making themselves known here.

At its best, this aspect can transform the way both people communicate. It can expose patterns that no longer serve, reveal where honesty has been avoided, and encourage a deeper relationship with the truth. The tension itself can become a catalyst for growth.

But not every difficult conversation is a meaningful one. When this dynamic becomes unconscious, communication can turn into a struggle for control. The Pluto person may push too hard for answers, certainty, or disclosure. The Mercury person may respond by becoming defensive, guarded, or determined to prove their point. Conversations can become less about understanding and more about protecting territory. The question this aspect asks is simple: what happens when the stakes feel high? Do you move closer to honesty, or closer to strategy? Do you feel invited into deeper truth, or pressured into revealing more than feels safe?

This connection has the potential to teach both people something important about communication. Not every truth needs to be extracted. Not every disagreement needs to be won. The real work is learning how to stay present with intensity without turning every conversation into a battleground.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Mercury-Pluto squares have a way of getting under the skin of a conversation. This is not the kind of connection that stays on the surface for long. The Pluto person often pushes for what is underneath the words, while the Mercury person may feel challenged to explain, clarify, or reveal more than they intended.\n\nThere can be a powerful fascination between you. The conversations may feel compelling, consuming, and difficult to walk away from. Even when an exchange becomes uncomfortable, there can be a sense that something important is trying to emerge. Hidden fears, old assumptions, and unspoken truths have a way of making themselves known here.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can transform the way both people communicate. It can expose patterns that no longer serve, reveal where honesty has been avoided, and encourage a deeper relationship with the truth. The tension itself can become a catalyst for growth.\n\nBut not every difficult conversation is a meaningful one. When this dynamic becomes unconscious, communication can turn into a struggle for control. The Pluto person may push too hard for answers, certainty, or disclosure. The Mercury person may respond by becoming defensive, guarded, or determined to prove their point. Conversations can become less about understanding and more about protecting territory. The question this aspect asks is simple: what happens when the stakes feel high? Do you move closer to honesty, or closer to strategy? Do you feel invited into deeper truth, or pressured into revealing more than feels safe?\n\nThis connection has the potential to teach both people something important about communication. Not every truth needs to be extracted. Not every disagreement needs to be won. The real work is learning how to stay present with intensity without turning every conversation into a battleground."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But not every difficult conversation is a meaningful one. When this dynamic becomes unconscious, communication can turn into a struggle for control. The Pluto person may push too hard for answers, certainty, or disclosure. The Mercury person may respond by becoming defensive, guarded, or determined to prove their point. Conversations can become less about understanding and more about protecting territory. The question this aspect asks is simple: what happens when the stakes feel high? Do you move closer to honesty, or closer to strategy? Do you feel invited into deeper truth, or pressured into revealing more than feels safe?"},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This connection has the potential to teach both people something important about communication. Not every truth needs to be extracted. Not every disagreement needs to be won. The real work is learning how to stay present with intensity without turning every conversation into a battleground."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-pluto_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s depth and power. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"Mercury-Pluto squares have a way of getting under the skin of a conversation. This is not the kind of connection that stays on the surface for long. The Pluto person often pushes for what is underneath the words, while the Mercury person may feel challenged to explain, clarify, or reveal more than they intended.\n\nThere can be a powerful fascination between you. The conversations may feel compelling, consuming, and difficult to walk away from. Even when an exchange becomes uncomfortable, there can be a sense that something important is trying to emerge. Hidden fears, old assumptions, and unspoken truths have a way of making themselves known here.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can transform the way both people communicate. It can expose patterns that no longer serve, reveal where honesty has been avoided, and encourage a deeper relationship with the truth. The tension itself can become a catalyst for growth.\n\nBut not every difficult conversation is a meaningful one. When this dynamic becomes unconscious, communication can turn into a struggle for control. The Pluto person may push too hard for answers, certainty, or disclosure. The Mercury person may respond by becoming defensive, guarded, or determined to prove their point. Conversations can become less about understanding and more about protecting territory. The question this aspect asks is simple: what happens when the stakes feel high? Do you move closer to honesty, or closer to strategy? Do you feel invited into deeper truth, or pressured into revealing more than feels safe?\n\nThis connection has the potential to teach both people something important about communication. Not every truth needs to be extracted. Not every disagreement needs to be won. The real work is learning how to stay present with intensity without turning every conversation into a battleground.","tension":"But not every difficult conversation is a meaningful one. When this dynamic becomes unconscious, communication can turn into a struggle for control. The Pluto person may push too hard for answers, certainty, or disclosure. The Mercury person may respond by becoming defensive, guarded, or determined to prove their point. Conversations can become less about understanding and more about protecting territory. The question this aspect asks is simple: what happens when the stakes feel high? Do you move closer to honesty, or closer to strategy? Do you feel invited into deeper truth, or pressured into revealing more than feels safe?","advice":"This connection has the potential to teach both people something important about communication. Not every truth needs to be extracted. Not every disagreement needs to be won. The real work is learning how to stay present with intensity without turning every conversation into a battleground.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-pluto_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-pluto_trine', 'synastry-mercury-trine-pluto', 'relationship-mercury-trine-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-pluto_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-pluto_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Trine Pluto', null, 'This connection carries mental depth without the same level of friction. The Pluto person may understand the Mercury person''s thoughts, words, and hidden meanings with unusual ease. There is often a natural trust in conversation, as though both people can speak honestly without needing to force the truth out of each other. The Mercury person may feel safe exploring complicated ideas, private thoughts, or uncomfortable truths, while the Pluto person offers depth, focus, and insight.

At its best, this aspect can be deeply clarifying. The Pluto person may help the Mercury person think more deeply, notice patterns, and articulate things they have struggled to name. Conversations can feel meaningful without becoming heavy, honest without becoming harsh, and transformative without turning into a fight.

There is still intensity here. Pluto never keeps things entirely light. But the trine often allows the depth to move with more trust and less defensiveness. Instead of forcing mental transformation through pressure or conflict, this aspect can support it through insight, honesty, and mutual respect.

The shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to miss how much influence the Pluto person has on the Mercury person''s thinking. The Pluto person''s opinions and way of seeing things can gradually affect how the Mercury person views themselves, other people, or the relationship, often without either of them realizing it.

Enjoy how clearly you think together, and keep noticing whose conclusions you are reaching. The clarity is real when your thinking stays your own.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection carries mental depth without the same level of friction. The Pluto person may understand the Mercury person''s thoughts, words, and hidden meanings with unusual ease. There is often a natural trust in conversation, as though both people can speak honestly without needing to force the truth out of each other. The Mercury person may feel safe exploring complicated ideas, private thoughts, or uncomfortable truths, while the Pluto person offers depth, focus, and insight.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can be deeply clarifying. The Pluto person may help the Mercury person think more deeply, notice patterns, and articulate things they have struggled to name. Conversations can feel meaningful without becoming heavy, honest without becoming harsh, and transformative without turning into a fight.\n\nThere is still intensity here. Pluto never keeps things entirely light. But the trine often allows the depth to move with more trust and less defensiveness. Instead of forcing mental transformation through pressure or conflict, this aspect can support it through insight, honesty, and mutual respect.\n\nThe shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to miss how much influence the Pluto person has on the Mercury person''s thinking. The Pluto person''s opinions and way of seeing things can gradually affect how the Mercury person views themselves, other people, or the relationship, often without either of them realizing it.\n\nEnjoy how clearly you think together, and keep noticing whose conclusions you are reaching. The clarity is real when your thinking stays your own."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to miss how much influence the Pluto person has on the Mercury person''s thinking. The Pluto person''s opinions and way of seeing things can gradually affect how the Mercury person views themselves, other people, or the relationship, often without either of them realizing it."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Enjoy how clearly you think together, and keep noticing whose conclusions you are reaching. The clarity is real when your thinking stays your own."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-pluto_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s depth and power. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This connection carries mental depth without the same level of friction. The Pluto person may understand the Mercury person''s thoughts, words, and hidden meanings with unusual ease. There is often a natural trust in conversation, as though both people can speak honestly without needing to force the truth out of each other. The Mercury person may feel safe exploring complicated ideas, private thoughts, or uncomfortable truths, while the Pluto person offers depth, focus, and insight.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can be deeply clarifying. The Pluto person may help the Mercury person think more deeply, notice patterns, and articulate things they have struggled to name. Conversations can feel meaningful without becoming heavy, honest without becoming harsh, and transformative without turning into a fight.\n\nThere is still intensity here. Pluto never keeps things entirely light. But the trine often allows the depth to move with more trust and less defensiveness. Instead of forcing mental transformation through pressure or conflict, this aspect can support it through insight, honesty, and mutual respect.\n\nThe shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to miss how much influence the Pluto person has on the Mercury person''s thinking. The Pluto person''s opinions and way of seeing things can gradually affect how the Mercury person views themselves, other people, or the relationship, often without either of them realizing it.\n\nEnjoy how clearly you think together, and keep noticing whose conclusions you are reaching. The clarity is real when your thinking stays your own.","tension":"The shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to miss how much influence the Pluto person has on the Mercury person''s thinking. The Pluto person''s opinions and way of seeing things can gradually affect how the Mercury person views themselves, other people, or the relationship, often without either of them realizing it.","advice":"Enjoy how clearly you think together, and keep noticing whose conclusions you are reaching. The clarity is real when your thinking stays your own.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-saturn_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-saturn_conjunction', 'synastry-mercury-conjunction-saturn', 'relationship-mercury-conjunction-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-saturn_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-saturn_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Conjunction Saturn', null, 'This person has a strong influence on how you express yourself. Around them, you may become more aware of what you know, what you can defend, and where your thinking still feels uncertain. Conversations can feel weightier than usual. Instead of speaking on impulse, you may find yourself choosing your words carefully and thinking several steps ahead before saying anything.

At its best, this creates real mental growth. They can help you develop stronger judgment, spot weaknesses in your reasoning, and bring more discipline to your ideas. What starts as a rough concept can become something thoughtful, practical, and well-constructed through their influence.

There is a maturity to this connection. They are often less interested in quick opinions and more interested in whether something holds up over time. Because of that, they may encourage you to think more deeply, prepare more thoroughly, and communicate with greater clarity.

The difficulty comes when that pressure becomes self-doubt. You may begin second-guessing yourself before you''ve even finished a sentence. Instead of using their feedback to strengthen your ideas, you may start assuming your ideas are not good enough to share in the first place.

The strongest expression of this aspect combines accountability with self-trust. Let this person help you strengthen your thinking, refine your communication, and raise your standards, but do not become so focused on getting it right that you stop sharing ideas before they are fully developed. Growth often comes from testing, learning, and improving along the way.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a strong influence on how you express yourself. Around them, you may become more aware of what you know, what you can defend, and where your thinking still feels uncertain. Conversations can feel weightier than usual. Instead of speaking on impulse, you may find yourself choosing your words carefully and thinking several steps ahead before saying anything.\n\nAt its best, this creates real mental growth. They can help you develop stronger judgment, spot weaknesses in your reasoning, and bring more discipline to your ideas. What starts as a rough concept can become something thoughtful, practical, and well-constructed through their influence.\n\nThere is a maturity to this connection. They are often less interested in quick opinions and more interested in whether something holds up over time. Because of that, they may encourage you to think more deeply, prepare more thoroughly, and communicate with greater clarity.\n\nThe difficulty comes when that pressure becomes self-doubt. You may begin second-guessing yourself before you''ve even finished a sentence. Instead of using their feedback to strengthen your ideas, you may start assuming your ideas are not good enough to share in the first place.\n\nThe strongest expression of this aspect combines accountability with self-trust. Let this person help you strengthen your thinking, refine your communication, and raise your standards, but do not become so focused on getting it right that you stop sharing ideas before they are fully developed. Growth often comes from testing, learning, and improving along the way."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The difficulty comes when that pressure becomes self-doubt. You may begin second-guessing yourself before you''ve even finished a sentence. Instead of using their feedback to strengthen your ideas, you may start assuming your ideas are not good enough to share in the first place."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The strongest expression of this aspect combines accountability with self-trust. Let this person help you strengthen your thinking, refine your communication, and raise your standards, but do not become so focused on getting it right that you stop sharing ideas before they are fully developed. Growth often comes from testing, learning, and improving along the way."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-saturn_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Mind meets gravity. The Saturn person brings focus, depth, and seriousness to the Mercury person''s thinking; ideas get disciplined and built into something real. At worst, the Saturn person criticizes or silences the Mercury person, who starts to feel stupid or unheard. Failure mode: one mind policing the other. Great for serious work; never let it shrink anyone''s voice.","summaryDeep":"This person has a strong influence on how you express yourself. Around them, you may become more aware of what you know, what you can defend, and where your thinking still feels uncertain. Conversations can feel weightier than usual. Instead of speaking on impulse, you may find yourself choosing your words carefully and thinking several steps ahead before saying anything.\n\nAt its best, this creates real mental growth. They can help you develop stronger judgment, spot weaknesses in your reasoning, and bring more discipline to your ideas. What starts as a rough concept can become something thoughtful, practical, and well-constructed through their influence.\n\nThere is a maturity to this connection. They are often less interested in quick opinions and more interested in whether something holds up over time. Because of that, they may encourage you to think more deeply, prepare more thoroughly, and communicate with greater clarity.\n\nThe difficulty comes when that pressure becomes self-doubt. You may begin second-guessing yourself before you''ve even finished a sentence. Instead of using their feedback to strengthen your ideas, you may start assuming your ideas are not good enough to share in the first place.\n\nThe strongest expression of this aspect combines accountability with self-trust. Let this person help you strengthen your thinking, refine your communication, and raise your standards, but do not become so focused on getting it right that you stop sharing ideas before they are fully developed. Growth often comes from testing, learning, and improving along the way.","tension":"The difficulty comes when that pressure becomes self-doubt. You may begin second-guessing yourself before you''ve even finished a sentence. Instead of using their feedback to strengthen your ideas, you may start assuming your ideas are not good enough to share in the first place.","advice":"The strongest expression of this aspect combines accountability with self-trust. Let this person help you strengthen your thinking, refine your communication, and raise your standards, but do not become so focused on getting it right that you stop sharing ideas before they are fully developed. Growth often comes from testing, learning, and improving along the way.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-saturn_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-saturn_opposition', 'synastry-mercury-opposition-saturn', 'relationship-mercury-opposition-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-saturn_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-saturn_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Opposition Saturn', null, 'This connection can feel like a conversation between possibility and caution. You may need space to think out loud, to wander through an idea before you know exactly where it is going. They may want clarity from the beginning. A plan. A purpose. A reason to follow the thread. What feels exploratory to you may feel unfocused to them. What feels responsible to them may feel limiting to you.

Oppositions ask us to learn from what stands across from us. This person may help you strengthen your thinking, question your assumptions, and give shape to ideas that would otherwise drift. You may help them stay curious, flexible, and open to possibilities they would dismiss too quickly.

They may think your ideas are unrealistic. You may think they are rigid and overly controlling. Conversations can turn into arguments where both people are trying to prove the other one wrong. The opportunity here is learning to value different ways of solving problems. Some insights come from asking questions and exploring possibilities. Others come from hands-on experience, pattern recognition, or careful analysis. The strongest results often come from combining these approaches rather than treating them as competing strengths.

Let this connection teach you how to evaluate feedback without losing confidence in your own perspective. Let go of criticism that undermines your confidence or discourages you from contributing your ideas.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection can feel like a conversation between possibility and caution. You may need space to think out loud, to wander through an idea before you know exactly where it is going. They may want clarity from the beginning. A plan. A purpose. A reason to follow the thread. What feels exploratory to you may feel unfocused to them. What feels responsible to them may feel limiting to you.\n\nOppositions ask us to learn from what stands across from us. This person may help you strengthen your thinking, question your assumptions, and give shape to ideas that would otherwise drift. You may help them stay curious, flexible, and open to possibilities they would dismiss too quickly.\n\nThey may think your ideas are unrealistic. You may think they are rigid and overly controlling. Conversations can turn into arguments where both people are trying to prove the other one wrong. The opportunity here is learning to value different ways of solving problems. Some insights come from asking questions and exploring possibilities. Others come from hands-on experience, pattern recognition, or careful analysis. The strongest results often come from combining these approaches rather than treating them as competing strengths.\n\nLet this connection teach you how to evaluate feedback without losing confidence in your own perspective. Let go of criticism that undermines your confidence or discourages you from contributing your ideas."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"They may think your ideas are unrealistic. You may think they are rigid and overly controlling. Conversations can turn into arguments where both people are trying to prove the other one wrong. The opportunity here is learning to value different ways of solving problems. Some insights come from asking questions and exploring possibilities. Others come from hands-on experience, pattern recognition, or careful analysis. The strongest results often come from combining these approaches rather than treating them as competing strengths."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let this connection teach you how to evaluate feedback without losing confidence in your own perspective. Let go of criticism that undermines your confidence or discourages you from contributing your ideas."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-saturn_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Open thinking faces serious skepticism. The Mercury person wants to explore and talk; the Saturn person wants proof and caution. Useful tension that can curdle into the other feeling dismissed. Failure mode: one voice consistently overruling the other. Let Saturn''s rigor and Mercury''s range balance, not silence, each other.","summaryDeep":"This connection can feel like a conversation between possibility and caution. You may need space to think out loud, to wander through an idea before you know exactly where it is going. They may want clarity from the beginning. A plan. A purpose. A reason to follow the thread. What feels exploratory to you may feel unfocused to them. What feels responsible to them may feel limiting to you.\n\nOppositions ask us to learn from what stands across from us. This person may help you strengthen your thinking, question your assumptions, and give shape to ideas that would otherwise drift. You may help them stay curious, flexible, and open to possibilities they would dismiss too quickly.\n\nThey may think your ideas are unrealistic. You may think they are rigid and overly controlling. Conversations can turn into arguments where both people are trying to prove the other one wrong. The opportunity here is learning to value different ways of solving problems. Some insights come from asking questions and exploring possibilities. Others come from hands-on experience, pattern recognition, or careful analysis. The strongest results often come from combining these approaches rather than treating them as competing strengths.\n\nLet this connection teach you how to evaluate feedback without losing confidence in your own perspective. Let go of criticism that undermines your confidence or discourages you from contributing your ideas.","tension":"They may think your ideas are unrealistic. You may think they are rigid and overly controlling. Conversations can turn into arguments where both people are trying to prove the other one wrong. The opportunity here is learning to value different ways of solving problems. Some insights come from asking questions and exploring possibilities. Others come from hands-on experience, pattern recognition, or careful analysis. The strongest results often come from combining these approaches rather than treating them as competing strengths.","advice":"Let this connection teach you how to evaluate feedback without losing confidence in your own perspective. Let go of criticism that undermines your confidence or discourages you from contributing your ideas.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-saturn_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-saturn_sextile', 'synastry-mercury-sextile-saturn', 'relationship-mercury-sextile-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-saturn_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-saturn_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Sextile Saturn', null, 'This connection offers your mind a steady place to land. There is something supportive about the way this person thinks with you. They may help you slow down enough to hear your own wisdom. They may ask the question that brings clarity, offer the perspective that helps things click into place, or remind you that good ideas often need time, patience, and care to take shape.

When this aspect is working well, it helps you trust your thoughts. Not because every idea is perfect, but because you learn that your mind can hold both curiosity and responsibility. Conversations can feel grounding. Plans can feel achievable. What once felt overwhelming may become easier to organize and understand.

The challenge is knowing when to balance discipline with exploration. Strong planning and practical thinking are valuable, but they should not prevent you from pursuing promising opportunities. Sometimes an idea needs time, testing, and development before its value becomes clear.

The most successful growth comes from combining good judgment with a willingness to stay open to possibility.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection offers your mind a steady place to land. There is something supportive about the way this person thinks with you. They may help you slow down enough to hear your own wisdom. They may ask the question that brings clarity, offer the perspective that helps things click into place, or remind you that good ideas often need time, patience, and care to take shape.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it helps you trust your thoughts. Not because every idea is perfect, but because you learn that your mind can hold both curiosity and responsibility. Conversations can feel grounding. Plans can feel achievable. What once felt overwhelming may become easier to organize and understand.\n\nThe challenge is knowing when to balance discipline with exploration. Strong planning and practical thinking are valuable, but they should not prevent you from pursuing promising opportunities. Sometimes an idea needs time, testing, and development before its value becomes clear.\n\nThe most successful growth comes from combining good judgment with a willingness to stay open to possibility."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is knowing when to balance discipline with exploration. Strong planning and practical thinking are valuable, but they should not prevent you from pursuing promising opportunities. Sometimes an idea needs time, testing, and development before its value becomes clear."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The most successful growth comes from combining good judgment with a willingness to stay open to possibility."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-saturn_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Thinking and structure cooperate. The Mercury person''s ideas gain weight and follow-through from the Saturn person''s discipline. Quietly productive, good for study, planning, and serious talk. Use it to build ideas into something durable.","summaryDeep":"This connection offers your mind a steady place to land. There is something supportive about the way this person thinks with you. They may help you slow down enough to hear your own wisdom. They may ask the question that brings clarity, offer the perspective that helps things click into place, or remind you that good ideas often need time, patience, and care to take shape.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it helps you trust your thoughts. Not because every idea is perfect, but because you learn that your mind can hold both curiosity and responsibility. Conversations can feel grounding. Plans can feel achievable. What once felt overwhelming may become easier to organize and understand.\n\nThe challenge is knowing when to balance discipline with exploration. Strong planning and practical thinking are valuable, but they should not prevent you from pursuing promising opportunities. Sometimes an idea needs time, testing, and development before its value becomes clear.\n\nThe most successful growth comes from combining good judgment with a willingness to stay open to possibility.","tension":"The challenge is knowing when to balance discipline with exploration. Strong planning and practical thinking are valuable, but they should not prevent you from pursuing promising opportunities. Sometimes an idea needs time, testing, and development before its value becomes clear.","advice":"The most successful growth comes from combining good judgment with a willingness to stay open to possibility.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-saturn_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-saturn_square', 'synastry-mercury-square-saturn', 'relationship-mercury-square-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-saturn_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-saturn_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Square Saturn', null, 'This person will challenge your thinking, whether you like it or not. They may question your logic, point out weaknesses in your ideas, or push back on things you thought were obvious. Sometimes their feedback is valuable. Sometimes it feels like they are looking for problems instead of solutions.

The risk is that you start second-guessing yourself. You stop speaking up until every detail is perfect. You spend more time defending your ideas than developing them. That is a losing strategy. No one grows by staying silent.

The upside is that this pressure can make you better. If you are willing to do the work, this person can force you to think more clearly, communicate more effectively, and back up your opinions with substance. Weak ideas get exposed. Strong ideas get stronger.

The downside is when the criticism never stops. You bring an idea, they find a flaw. You solve the flaw, they find another one. Over time, the conversation stops being productive and starts becoming draining. You leave feeling less confident instead of more capable.

Treat this like a lesson in discernment. Some critiques arrive carrying wisdom. Others arrive carrying someone else''s fear, frustration, or need for control. Your task is not to absorb every judgment that comes your way. Your task is to know what feedback helps you grow and what feedback you should ignore. You are not here to earn this person''s approval. You are here to deepen your relationship with your own mind.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person will challenge your thinking, whether you like it or not. They may question your logic, point out weaknesses in your ideas, or push back on things you thought were obvious. Sometimes their feedback is valuable. Sometimes it feels like they are looking for problems instead of solutions.\n\nThe risk is that you start second-guessing yourself. You stop speaking up until every detail is perfect. You spend more time defending your ideas than developing them. That is a losing strategy. No one grows by staying silent.\n\nThe upside is that this pressure can make you better. If you are willing to do the work, this person can force you to think more clearly, communicate more effectively, and back up your opinions with substance. Weak ideas get exposed. Strong ideas get stronger.\n\nThe downside is when the criticism never stops. You bring an idea, they find a flaw. You solve the flaw, they find another one. Over time, the conversation stops being productive and starts becoming draining. You leave feeling less confident instead of more capable.\n\nTreat this like a lesson in discernment. Some critiques arrive carrying wisdom. Others arrive carrying someone else''s fear, frustration, or need for control. Your task is not to absorb every judgment that comes your way. Your task is to know what feedback helps you grow and what feedback you should ignore. You are not here to earn this person''s approval. You are here to deepen your relationship with your own mind."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The downside is when the criticism never stops. You bring an idea, they find a flaw. You solve the flaw, they find another one. Over time, the conversation stops being productive and starts becoming draining. You leave feeling less confident instead of more capable."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Treat this like a lesson in discernment. Some critiques arrive carrying wisdom. Others arrive carrying someone else''s fear, frustration, or need for control. Your task is not to absorb every judgment that comes your way. Your task is to know what feedback helps you grow and what feedback you should ignore. You are not here to earn this person''s approval. You are here to deepen your relationship with your own mind."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-saturn_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Communication grinds against authority. The Mercury person feels criticized, doubted, or shut down; the Saturn person finds the other''s thinking loose or unserious. Conversations go heavy or cold. Failure mode: the Saturn person belittling the Mercury person''s mind. Workable if Saturn offers structure without judgment and Mercury hears rigor, not rejection.","summaryDeep":"This person will challenge your thinking, whether you like it or not. They may question your logic, point out weaknesses in your ideas, or push back on things you thought were obvious. Sometimes their feedback is valuable. Sometimes it feels like they are looking for problems instead of solutions.\n\nThe risk is that you start second-guessing yourself. You stop speaking up until every detail is perfect. You spend more time defending your ideas than developing them. That is a losing strategy. No one grows by staying silent.\n\nThe upside is that this pressure can make you better. If you are willing to do the work, this person can force you to think more clearly, communicate more effectively, and back up your opinions with substance. Weak ideas get exposed. Strong ideas get stronger.\n\nThe downside is when the criticism never stops. You bring an idea, they find a flaw. You solve the flaw, they find another one. Over time, the conversation stops being productive and starts becoming draining. You leave feeling less confident instead of more capable.\n\nTreat this like a lesson in discernment. Some critiques arrive carrying wisdom. Others arrive carrying someone else''s fear, frustration, or need for control. Your task is not to absorb every judgment that comes your way. Your task is to know what feedback helps you grow and what feedback you should ignore. You are not here to earn this person''s approval. You are here to deepen your relationship with your own mind.","tension":"The downside is when the criticism never stops. You bring an idea, they find a flaw. You solve the flaw, they find another one. Over time, the conversation stops being productive and starts becoming draining. You leave feeling less confident instead of more capable.","advice":"Treat this like a lesson in discernment. Some critiques arrive carrying wisdom. Others arrive carrying someone else''s fear, frustration, or need for control. Your task is not to absorb every judgment that comes your way. Your task is to know what feedback helps you grow and what feedback you should ignore. You are not here to earn this person''s approval. You are here to deepen your relationship with your own mind.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry-mercury-trine-saturn', 'relationship-mercury-trine-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-saturn_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-saturn_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Trine Saturn', null, 'This person can bring stability to your thinking. Around them, it may feel easier to slow down and sort through what is actually important. They tend to encourage careful thought, realistic planning, and steady progress. Instead of pushing you to think faster, they help you think more clearly.

When this works, their influence is grounding rather than limiting. They help you organize ideas, spot practical solutions, and follow through on what you start. Conversations can feel productive because they add perspective without dismissing what you have to say.

One of the strengths of this aspect is trust. You may feel that this person listens carefully and responds thoughtfully. Their advice often comes from experience, patience, or a genuine desire to help you build something lasting.

The challenge is relying too heavily on what already feels proven. Together, you may gravitate toward familiar approaches and miss opportunities that require experimentation or calculated risk. Consistency is a strength, but long-term growth often comes from staying open to new ideas, adapting to change, and being willing to step beyond your comfort zone when the situation calls for it.

At its best, this connection helps you develop confidence in your own mind. Their steadiness gives your ideas a stronger foundation while still leaving room for curiosity, creativity, and new ways of thinking.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can bring stability to your thinking. Around them, it may feel easier to slow down and sort through what is actually important. They tend to encourage careful thought, realistic planning, and steady progress. Instead of pushing you to think faster, they help you think more clearly.\n\nWhen this works, their influence is grounding rather than limiting. They help you organize ideas, spot practical solutions, and follow through on what you start. Conversations can feel productive because they add perspective without dismissing what you have to say.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is trust. You may feel that this person listens carefully and responds thoughtfully. Their advice often comes from experience, patience, or a genuine desire to help you build something lasting.\n\nThe challenge is relying too heavily on what already feels proven. Together, you may gravitate toward familiar approaches and miss opportunities that require experimentation or calculated risk. Consistency is a strength, but long-term growth often comes from staying open to new ideas, adapting to change, and being willing to step beyond your comfort zone when the situation calls for it.\n\nAt its best, this connection helps you develop confidence in your own mind. Their steadiness gives your ideas a stronger foundation while still leaving room for curiosity, creativity, and new ways of thinking."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is relying too heavily on what already feels proven. Together, you may gravitate toward familiar approaches and miss opportunities that require experimentation or calculated risk. Consistency is a strength, but long-term growth often comes from staying open to new ideas, adapting to change, and being willing to step beyond your comfort zone when the situation calls for it."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"At its best, this connection helps you develop confidence in your own mind. Their steadiness gives your ideas a stronger foundation while still leaving room for curiosity, creativity, and new ways of thinking."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-saturn_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Mind and discipline flow together. The Saturn person gives the Mercury person''s ideas depth and staying power; the Mercury person keeps the Saturn person''s thinking current. A strong mentoring and working contact. Build serious, lasting ideas together.","summaryDeep":"This person can bring stability to your thinking. Around them, it may feel easier to slow down and sort through what is actually important. They tend to encourage careful thought, realistic planning, and steady progress. Instead of pushing you to think faster, they help you think more clearly.\n\nWhen this works, their influence is grounding rather than limiting. They help you organize ideas, spot practical solutions, and follow through on what you start. Conversations can feel productive because they add perspective without dismissing what you have to say.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is trust. You may feel that this person listens carefully and responds thoughtfully. Their advice often comes from experience, patience, or a genuine desire to help you build something lasting.\n\nThe challenge is relying too heavily on what already feels proven. Together, you may gravitate toward familiar approaches and miss opportunities that require experimentation or calculated risk. Consistency is a strength, but long-term growth often comes from staying open to new ideas, adapting to change, and being willing to step beyond your comfort zone when the situation calls for it.\n\nAt its best, this connection helps you develop confidence in your own mind. Their steadiness gives your ideas a stronger foundation while still leaving room for curiosity, creativity, and new ways of thinking.","tension":"The challenge is relying too heavily on what already feels proven. Together, you may gravitate toward familiar approaches and miss opportunities that require experimentation or calculated risk. Consistency is a strength, but long-term growth often comes from staying open to new ideas, adapting to change, and being willing to step beyond your comfort zone when the situation calls for it.","advice":"At its best, this connection helps you develop confidence in your own mind. Their steadiness gives your ideas a stronger foundation while still leaving room for curiosity, creativity, and new ways of thinking.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"sun","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry-mercury-conjunction-sun', 'relationship-mercury-conjunction-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-sun_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-sun_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Conjunction Sun', null, 'This person may seem to understand you right away. Conversation often feels easy, as if they naturally follow your train of thought and quickly pick up on what matters to you.

When this works well, it can feel deeply affirming. They may notice parts of you that often go unseen and reflect them back in a way that resonates. You might feel that they are paying close attention, not just to what you say, but to the energy, intentions, and essence behind it. Their observations can help you feel witnessed in a meaningful way, as though they are looking past the obvious and connecting with something more fundamental about who you are.

Being understood by them can feel like exhaling. You may feel less guarded, less alone in your experience, and more able to be yourself without explanation. At times, they may find the words for something you have always felt but never fully named.

Remember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.

Keep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may seem to understand you right away. Conversation often feels easy, as if they naturally follow your train of thought and quickly pick up on what matters to you.\n\nWhen this works well, it can feel deeply affirming. They may notice parts of you that often go unseen and reflect them back in a way that resonates. You might feel that they are paying close attention, not just to what you say, but to the energy, intentions, and essence behind it. Their observations can help you feel witnessed in a meaningful way, as though they are looking past the obvious and connecting with something more fundamental about who you are.\n\nBeing understood by them can feel like exhaling. You may feel less guarded, less alone in your experience, and more able to be yourself without explanation. At times, they may find the words for something you have always felt but never fully named.\n\nRemember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.\n\nKeep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Remember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Keep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-sun_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s identity. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person may seem to understand you right away. Conversation often feels easy, as if they naturally follow your train of thought and quickly pick up on what matters to you.\n\nWhen this works well, it can feel deeply affirming. They may notice parts of you that often go unseen and reflect them back in a way that resonates. You might feel that they are paying close attention, not just to what you say, but to the energy, intentions, and essence behind it. Their observations can help you feel witnessed in a meaningful way, as though they are looking past the obvious and connecting with something more fundamental about who you are.\n\nBeing understood by them can feel like exhaling. You may feel less guarded, less alone in your experience, and more able to be yourself without explanation. At times, they may find the words for something you have always felt but never fully named.\n\nRemember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.\n\nKeep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other.","tension":"Remember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.","advice":"Keep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"sun","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry-mercury-opposition-sun', 'relationship-mercury-opposition-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-sun_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-sun_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Opposition Sun', null, 'This person may reflect back a version of you that you do not immediately recognize.

They can notice qualities, patterns, and motivations that sit just outside your usual field of vision. Sometimes their observations feel illuminating, like they have found language for something you have always sensed but never fully understood. Other times, their perspective can feel unsettling, exposing a truth you were not ready to face or describing you in a way that misses the heart of who you are.

This connection often asks you to meet yourself through contrast. Their way of thinking may challenge your self-image, not because they are trying to change you, but because they naturally stand across from your point of view. What they see and what you know about yourself may not always match.

At its best, this dynamic expands your awareness. It invites you to consider that there may be more than one truth in the room. Their insight can help you understand how you impact others, while your perspective can remind them that no one is fully defined by an outside interpretation.

At its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal.

Stay open. You do not have to agree with everything they see, but you can stay curious. Keep your own perspective while making room for theirs.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may reflect back a version of you that you do not immediately recognize.\n\nThey can notice qualities, patterns, and motivations that sit just outside your usual field of vision. Sometimes their observations feel illuminating, like they have found language for something you have always sensed but never fully understood. Other times, their perspective can feel unsettling, exposing a truth you were not ready to face or describing you in a way that misses the heart of who you are.\n\nThis connection often asks you to meet yourself through contrast. Their way of thinking may challenge your self-image, not because they are trying to change you, but because they naturally stand across from your point of view. What they see and what you know about yourself may not always match.\n\nAt its best, this dynamic expands your awareness. It invites you to consider that there may be more than one truth in the room. Their insight can help you understand how you impact others, while your perspective can remind them that no one is fully defined by an outside interpretation.\n\nAt its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal.\n\nStay open. You do not have to agree with everything they see, but you can stay curious. Keep your own perspective while making room for theirs."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Stay open. You do not have to agree with everything they see, but you can stay curious. Keep your own perspective while making room for theirs."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-sun_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s identity. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person may reflect back a version of you that you do not immediately recognize.\n\nThey can notice qualities, patterns, and motivations that sit just outside your usual field of vision. Sometimes their observations feel illuminating, like they have found language for something you have always sensed but never fully understood. Other times, their perspective can feel unsettling, exposing a truth you were not ready to face or describing you in a way that misses the heart of who you are.\n\nThis connection often asks you to meet yourself through contrast. Their way of thinking may challenge your self-image, not because they are trying to change you, but because they naturally stand across from your point of view. What they see and what you know about yourself may not always match.\n\nAt its best, this dynamic expands your awareness. It invites you to consider that there may be more than one truth in the room. Their insight can help you understand how you impact others, while your perspective can remind them that no one is fully defined by an outside interpretation.\n\nAt its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal.\n\nStay open. You do not have to agree with everything they see, but you can stay curious. Keep your own perspective while making room for theirs.","tension":"At its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may