  ('A-mercury_B-sun_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"sun","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-sun_sextile', 'synastry-mercury-sextile-sun', 'relationship-mercury-sextile-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-sun_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-sun_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Sextile Sun', null, 'This person may help you feel understood in a way that stays with you. They have a way of asking the question that gets to the heart of something, or noticing the detail that everyone else missed. Conversations with them can leave you feeling clearer about yourself. Not because they tell you who you are, but because they create space for you to hear your own thoughts more honestly.

There is often a quiet sense of safety here. You may find yourself sharing things you did not plan to say, simply because it feels natural to keep opening up. Their curiosity can feel genuine, and that makes it easier to let them see more of the real you.

The connection often grows through small moments that matter more than they seem. They remember something important to you. They ask about it later. They listen closely enough that you can feel the difference. Those moments can create a powerful feeling of being seen, valued, and understood.

At its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is.

The more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may help you feel understood in a way that stays with you. They have a way of asking the question that gets to the heart of something, or noticing the detail that everyone else missed. Conversations with them can leave you feeling clearer about yourself. Not because they tell you who you are, but because they create space for you to hear your own thoughts more honestly.\n\nThere is often a quiet sense of safety here. You may find yourself sharing things you did not plan to say, simply because it feels natural to keep opening up. Their curiosity can feel genuine, and that makes it easier to let them see more of the real you.\n\nThe connection often grows through small moments that matter more than they seem. They remember something important to you. They ask about it later. They listen closely enough that you can feel the difference. Those moments can create a powerful feeling of being seen, valued, and understood.\n\nAt its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is.\n\nThe more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-sun_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s identity. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This person may help you feel understood in a way that stays with you. They have a way of asking the question that gets to the heart of something, or noticing the detail that everyone else missed. Conversations with them can leave you feeling clearer about yourself. Not because they tell you who you are, but because they create space for you to hear your own thoughts more honestly.\n\nThere is often a quiet sense of safety here. You may find yourself sharing things you did not plan to say, simply because it feels natural to keep opening up. Their curiosity can feel genuine, and that makes it easier to let them see more of the real you.\n\nThe connection often grows through small moments that matter more than they seem. They remember something important to you. They ask about it later. They listen closely enough that you can feel the difference. Those moments can create a powerful feeling of being seen, valued, and understood.\n\nAt its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is.\n\nThe more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more.","tension":"At its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is.","advice":"The more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-sun_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"sun","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-sun_square', 'synastry-mercury-square-sun', 'relationship-mercury-square-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-sun_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-sun_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Square Sun', null, 'This person may misunderstand you in a way that gets under your skin. The tension isn''t necessarily about what is being said. It''s about the gap between what is meant and what is received. This person may reflect something back to you that feels slightly off. They may think they understand your intentions while missing an important piece of your experience. You may find yourself repeating, clarifying, or trying to find new language for something that feels obvious from your side.

That can be exhausting. It can also be revealing.

Squares ask us to work. They shine a light on patterns that may be holding you back from deeper connection. In this relationship, misunderstandings can become opportunities for growth. You may be encouraged to communicate more clearly and express what you truly mean, rather than assuming the other person already knows. They may be encouraged to slow down, stay curious, and listen with an open mind before jumping to conclusions.

When the tension builds, conversations can turn into arguments about who understands the situation better. One person feels unseen. The other feels like their efforts are being dismissed. Instead of getting curious, both people may become defensive.

The growth here comes from slowing down. Not by accepting being misunderstood, but by staying in the conversation long enough to understand each other more clearly. This connection isn''t really about proving who''s right. It''s about both of you getting better at seeing each other for who you actually are, instead of getting stuck in your own assumptions about each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may misunderstand you in a way that gets under your skin. The tension isn''t necessarily about what is being said. It''s about the gap between what is meant and what is received. This person may reflect something back to you that feels slightly off. They may think they understand your intentions while missing an important piece of your experience. You may find yourself repeating, clarifying, or trying to find new language for something that feels obvious from your side.\n\nThat can be exhausting. It can also be revealing.\n\nSquares ask us to work. They shine a light on patterns that may be holding you back from deeper connection. In this relationship, misunderstandings can become opportunities for growth. You may be encouraged to communicate more clearly and express what you truly mean, rather than assuming the other person already knows. They may be encouraged to slow down, stay curious, and listen with an open mind before jumping to conclusions.\n\nWhen the tension builds, conversations can turn into arguments about who understands the situation better. One person feels unseen. The other feels like their efforts are being dismissed. Instead of getting curious, both people may become defensive.\n\nThe growth here comes from slowing down. Not by accepting being misunderstood, but by staying in the conversation long enough to understand each other more clearly. This connection isn''t really about proving who''s right. It''s about both of you getting better at seeing each other for who you actually are, instead of getting stuck in your o