  ('A-mercury_B-uranus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"uranus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-uranus_trine', 'synastry-mercury-trine-uranus', 'relationship-mercury-trine-uranus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-uranus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-uranus_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Trine Uranus', null, 'A''s mind meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Translation","body":"A''s mind meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-uranus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":null,"tension":null,"advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":null,"weight":null}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-venus_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"venus","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-venus_conjunction', 'synastry-mercury-conjunction-venus', 'relationship-mercury-conjunction-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-venus_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-venus_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Conjunction Venus', null, 'This connection often feels good from the start. There may be something about the way this person speaks that puts you at ease. Their words can make you feel seen, appreciated, and understood. After spending time with them, you may walk away feeling a little lighter, a little more confident, or simply more like yourself.

When this aspect flows well, conversation becomes a source of connection. You encourage each other naturally. You may spend hours sharing ideas, talking about your hopes, or reflecting on life together. There is often a feeling that this person understands where you''re coming from, and that feeling can be deeply attractive.

You may also find that your values align in meaningful ways. What matters to you matters to them.

The downside is that comfort can become a habit. When things are easy between you, it''s tempting to stick to what feels good and avoid the conversations that are messier, riskier, or harder to navigate.

One of the gifts of this connection is that you naturally help each other feel seen and valued. That creates a strong foundation. The opportunity is to build on it.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection often feels good from the start. There may be something about the way this person speaks that puts you at ease. Their words can make you feel seen, appreciated, and understood. After spending time with them, you may walk away feeling a little lighter, a little more confident, or simply more like yourself.\n\nWhen this aspect flows well, conversation becomes a source of connection. You encourage each other naturally. You may spend hours sharing ideas, talking about your hopes, or reflecting on life together. There is often a feeling that this person understands where you''re coming from, and that feeling can be deeply attractive.\n\nYou may also find that your values align in meaningful ways. What matters to you matters to them.\n\nThe downside is that comfort can become a habit. When things are easy between you, it''s tempting to stick to what feels good and avoid the conversations that are messier, riskier, or harder to navigate.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is that you naturally help each other feel seen and valued. That creates a strong foundation. The opportunity is to build on it."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The downside is that comfort can become a habit. When things are easy between you, it''s tempting to stick to what feels good and avoid the conversations that are messier, riskier, or harder to navigate."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"One of the gifts of this connection is that you naturally help each other feel seen and valued. That creates a strong foundation. The opportunity is to build on it."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-venus_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s love and values. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This connection often feels good from the start. There may be something about the way this person speaks that puts you at ease. Their words can make you feel seen, appreciated, and understood. After spending time with them, you may walk away feeling a little lighter, a little more confident, or simply more like yourself.\n\nWhen this aspect flows well, conversation becomes a source of connection. You encourage each other naturally. You may spend hours sharing ideas, talking about your hopes, or reflecting on life together. There is often a feeling that this person understands where you''re coming from, and that feeling can be deeply attractive.\n\nYou may also find that your values align in meaningful ways. What matters to you matters to them.\n\nThe downside is that comfort can become a habit. When things are easy between you, it''s tempting to stick to what feels good and avoid the conversations that are messier, riskier, or harder to navigate.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is that you naturally help each other feel seen and valued. That creates a strong foundation. The opportunity is to build on it.","tension":"The downside is that comfort can become a habit. When things are easy between you, it''s tempting to stick to what feels good and avoid the conversations that are messier, riskier, or harder to navigate.","advice":"One of the gifts of this connection is that you naturally help each other feel seen and valued. That creates a strong foundation. The opportunity is to build on it.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-venus_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"venus","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-venus_opposition', 'synastry-mercury-opposition-venus', 'relationship-mercury-opposition-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-venus_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-venus_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Opposition Venus', null, 'This connection asks you to stretch beyond your usual understanding of affection.

This person may communicate care in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. The way they flirt, compliment, joke, or express appreciation may not be what you instinctively recognize as warmth. Still, there may be something magnetic about the contrast. Their way of expressing affection can challenge your assumptions and open you to forms of care you might not have noticed before.

Oppositions often bring us face-to-face with another perspective. In this case, the contrast can be compelling. This person may express warmth, affection, or appreciation in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. Their approach can stretch your understanding of connection, showing you that care does not always arrive in the form you expect. Over time, you may discover new ways of giving and receiving affection through the differences between you.

The challenge is that affection does not always arrive in a recognizable form. One person may think they are showing care, while the other does not feel cared for at all. What one person sees as thoughtful may feel distant to the other. What feels sincere may feel awkward. What seems obvious may not register at all.

Both people can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood.

The more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection asks you to stretch beyond your usual understanding of affection.\n\nThis person may communicate care in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. The way they flirt, compliment, joke, or express appreciation may not be what you instinctively recognize as warmth. Still, there may be something magnetic about the contrast. Their way of expressing affection can challenge your assumptions and open you to forms of care you might not have noticed before.\n\nOppositions often bring us face-to-face with another perspective. In this case, the contrast can be compelling. This person may express warmth, affection, or appreciation in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. Their approach can stretch your understanding of connection, showing you that care does not always arrive in the form you expect. Over time, you may discover new ways of giving and receiving affection through the differences between you.\n\nThe challenge is that affection does not always arrive in a recognizable form. One person may think they are showing care, while the other does not feel cared for at all. What one person sees as thoughtful may feel distant to the other. What feels sincere may feel awkward. What seems obvious may not register at all.\n\nBoth people can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood.\n\nThe more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that affection does not always arrive in a recognizable form. One person may think they are showing care, while the other does not feel cared for at all. What one person sees as thoughtful may feel distant to the other. What feels sincere may feel awkward. What seems obvious may not register at all.\n\nBoth people can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-venus_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s love and values. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This connection asks you to stretch beyond your usual understanding of affection.\n\nThis person may communicate care in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. The way they flirt, compliment, joke, or express appreciation may not be what you instinctively recognize as warmth. Still, there may be something magnetic about the contrast. Their way of expressing affection can challenge your assumptions and open you to forms of care you might not have noticed before.\n\nOppositions often bring us face-to-face with another perspective. In this case, the contrast can be compelling. This person may express warmth, affection, or appreciation in ways that feel unfamiliar to you. Their approach can stretch your understanding of connection, showing you that care does not always arrive in the form you expect. Over time, you may discover new ways of giving and receiving affection through the differences between you.\n\nThe challenge is that affection does not always arrive in a recognizable form. One person may think they are showing care, while the other does not feel cared for at all. What one person sees as thoughtful may feel distant to the other. What feels sincere may feel awkward. What seems obvious may not register at all.\n\nBoth people can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood.\n\nThe more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there.","tension":"The challenge is that affection does not always arrive in a recognizable form. One person may think they are showing care, while the other does not feel cared for at all. What one person sees as thoughtful may feel distant to the other. What feels sincere may feel awkward. What seems obvious may not register at all.\n\nBoth people can end up feeling unseen. Each may be trying to connect in a genuine way, but what they offer is not what the other person needs. Even when there is care between you, it can be difficult to feel fully reached or understood.","advice":"The more clearly you learn how each of you gives and receives affection, the easier it becomes to recognize the care that is already there.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"venus","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry-mercury-sextile-venus', 'relationship-mercury-sextile-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-venus_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-venus_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Sextile Venus', null, 'There is a natural opening for warmth here, but it grows when it is expressed. This person may be easy to talk to not only because of what they say, but because of how their mind meets yours. You may enjoy the way they think, the details they notice, the questions they ask, or the way they help a conversation unfold. There is often appreciation present from the beginning. The invitation is to share it.

This connection deepens when appreciation is spoken aloud. Let this person know what you value about them. Reflect back something they shared that stayed with you. Acknowledge the impact their words or actions have had. These small moments of recognition build trust over time. The more you practice naming what matters, the more supported, understood, and connected both of you are likely to feel.

Two people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.

You strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is a natural opening for warmth here, but it grows when it is expressed. This person may be easy to talk to not only because of what they say, but because of how their mind meets yours. You may enjoy the way they think, the details they notice, the questions they ask, or the way they help a conversation unfold. There is often appreciation present from the beginning. The invitation is to share it.\n\nThis connection deepens when appreciation is spoken aloud. Let this person know what you value about them. Reflect back something they shared that stayed with you. Acknowledge the impact their words or actions have had. These small moments of recognition build trust over time. The more you practice naming what matters, the more supported, understood, and connected both of you are likely to feel.\n\nTwo people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.\n\nYou strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Two people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"You strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-venus_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s love and values. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"There is a natural opening for warmth here, but it grows when it is expressed. This person may be easy to talk to not only because of what they say, but because of how their mind meets yours. You may enjoy the way they think, the details they notice, the questions they ask, or the way they help a conversation unfold. There is often appreciation present from the beginning. The invitation is to share it.\n\nThis connection deepens when appreciation is spoken aloud. Let this person know what you value about them. Reflect back something they shared that stayed with you. Acknowledge the impact their words or actions have had. These small moments of recognition build trust over time. The more you practice naming what matters, the more supported, understood, and connected both of you are likely to feel.\n\nTwo people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.\n\nYou strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference.","tension":"Two people can care deeply for each other and still leave the most important things unsaid. The affection is there, but without expression, it can be missed, doubted, or forgotten in the noise of everyday life.","advice":"You strengthen this connection by saying what you appreciate. Thank them when it matters. Encourage them when they need it. Let them know when their presence, ideas, or efforts make a difference.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-venus_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"venus","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-venus_square', 'synastry-mercury-square-venus', 'relationship-mercury-square-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-venus_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-venus_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Square Venus', null, 'This is the quiet distance between what one person says and what the other person needs to feel loved. It lives in a tender, specific place: the gap between being drawn to someone and actually feeling understood by them.

You may find yourself attracted and irritated in nearly the same breath. Something about this person''s mind, their humor, the particular way they put things, pulls you in. And then the same mouth that charmed you says something that lands wrong, and you feel the pull and the friction at once, unsure which one to trust.

Sometimes the mismatch is loud. One of you is too blunt, the other too careful. One wants the truth laid bare, the other wants it handled gently. But more often it is subtle, almost too small to name. A compliment that arrives slightly off. A joke that grazes a nerve. A conversation that was supposed to bring you closer and instead leaves one of you a little lonelier than before it started.

Because this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm.

The work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own version of it. We tend to offer love in the language we would want to receive it, and then feel hurt when it does not translate. What lands as tender to you may read as flat to them. What feels honest to them may feel sharp to you.

This is the slow practice the square asks for. Not better chemistry, you already have that. The harder thing: learning how this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This is the quiet distance between what one person says and what the other person needs to feel loved. It lives in a tender, specific place: the gap between being drawn to someone and actually feeling understood by them.\n\nYou may find yourself attracted and irritated in nearly the same breath. Something about this person''s mind, their humor, the particular way they put things, pulls you in. And then the same mouth that charmed you says something that lands wrong, and you feel the pull and the friction at once, unsure which one to trust.\n\nSometimes the mismatch is loud. One of you is too blunt, the other too careful. One wants the truth laid bare, the other wants it handled gently. But more often it is subtle, almost too small to name. A compliment that arrives slightly off. A joke that grazes a nerve. A conversation that was supposed to bring you closer and instead leaves one of you a little lonelier than before it started.\n\nBecause this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm.\n\nThe work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own version of it. We tend to offer love in the language we would want to receive it, and then feel hurt when it does not translate. What lands as tender to you may read as flat to them. What feels honest to them may feel sharp to you.\n\nThis is the slow practice the square asks for. Not better chemistry, you already have that. The harder thing: learning how this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Because this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own version of it. We tend to offer love in the language we would want to receive it, and then feel hurt when it does not translate. What lands as tender to you may read as flat to them. What feels honest to them may feel sharp to you.\n\nThis is the slow practice the square asks for. Not better chemistry, you already have that. The harder thing: learning how this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-venus_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation"