this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed.","tension":"Because this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm.","advice":"The work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own version of it. We tend to offer love in the language we would want to receive it, and then feel hurt when it does not translate. What lands as tender to you may read as flat to them. What feels honest to them may feel sharp to you.\n\nThis is the slow practice the square asks for. Not better chemistry, you already have that. The harder thing: learning how this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-mercury_B-venus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"mercury","planetB":"venus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-mercury_B-venus_trine', 'synastry-mercury-trine-venus', 'relationship-mercury-trine-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-mercury_B-venus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-mercury_B-venus_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Mercury Trine Venus', null, 'With this person, a lot of the attraction is in the conversation.

You may just enjoy talking to them. You like hearing what they have to say. Maybe they make you laugh, tell good stories, or notice things other people miss. Conversation can feel easy because you genuinely enjoy being around them.

When this works, affection tends to show up through everyday conversation. The text that makes you laugh when you''re having a bad day. The little check-in. The running joke that somehow never gets old. Whatever the relationship is, there is often a feeling of being understood through words. You don''t always have to spell out that you care about each other. It''s already already present in how you talk.

One of the nicest things about this connection is feeling seen. This person may put something into words that you''ve been trying to explain for months. They may understand what you''re getting at before you''ve fully figured it out yourself. There can be a real sense of, "Oh, that''s exactly what I meant."

The thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.

The connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"With this person, a lot of the attraction is in the conversation.\n\nYou may just enjoy talking to them. You like hearing what they have to say. Maybe they make you laugh, tell good stories, or notice things other people miss. Conversation can feel easy because you genuinely enjoy being around them.\n\nWhen this works, affection tends to show up through everyday conversation. The text that makes you laugh when you''re having a bad day. The little check-in. The running joke that somehow never gets old. Whatever the relationship is, there is often a feeling of being understood through words. You don''t always have to spell out that you care about each other. It''s already already present in how you talk.\n\nOne of the nicest things about this connection is feeling seen. This person may put something into words that you''ve been trying to explain for months. They may understand what you''re getting at before you''ve fully figured it out yourself. There can be a real sense of, \"Oh, that''s exactly what I meant.\"\n\nThe thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.\n\nThe connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-mercury_B-venus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s mind meets B''s love and values. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"With this person, a lot of the attraction is in the conversation.\n\nYou may just enjoy talking to them. You like hearing what they have to say. Maybe they make you laugh, tell good stories, or notice things other people miss. Conversation can feel easy because you genuinely enjoy being around them.\n\nWhen this works, affection tends to show up through everyday conversation. The text that makes you laugh when you''re having a bad day. The little check-in. The running joke that somehow never gets old. Whatever the relationship is, there is often a feeling of being understood through words. You don''t always have to spell out that you care about each other. It''s already already present in how you talk.\n\nOne of the nicest things about this connection is feeling seen. This person may put something into words that you''ve been trying to explain for months. They may understand what you''re getting at before you''ve fully figured it out yourself. There can be a real sense of, \"Oh, that''s exactly what I meant.\"\n\nThe thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.\n\nThe connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it.","tension":"The thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.","advice":"The connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-jupiter_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-jupiter_conjunction', 'synastry-moon-conjunction-jupiter', 'relationship-moon-conjunction-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-jupiter_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-jupiter_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Conjunction Jupiter', null, 'This person has a way of reminding you that your feelings deserve room to exist.

Their care can feel abundant. Their instinct is often to meet your emotions with generosity rather than judgment, encouragement rather than criticism. Around them it may feel easier to believe that what you are carrying does not have to be carried alone.

This person makes it easier to be yourself. Their response to your feelings is usually support, not judgment, so opening up feels safer than it does with most people. When life is hard, they remind you that you do not have to carry it alone. When life is good, they are genuinely happy for you. Around them, it is easier to trust your own feelings, ask for what you need, and believe that things can get better.

One thing to watch for is using comfort to avoid the truth. You may rush to make each other feel better instead of staying with what the feeling is trying to tell you.

Take the support. Face the problem anyway. This connection is strongest when the encouragement helps you deal with hard things instead of avoiding them.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a way of reminding you that your feelings deserve room to exist.\n\nTheir care can feel abundant. Their instinct is often to meet your emotions with generosity rather than judgment, encouragement rather than criticism. Around them it may feel easier to believe that what you are carrying does not have to be carried alone.\n\nThis person makes it easier to be yourself. Their response to your feelings is usually support, not judgment, so opening up feels safer than it does with most people. When life is hard, they remind you that you do not have to carry it alone. When life is good, they are genuinely happy for you. Around them, it is easier to trust your own feelings, ask for what you need, and believe that things can get better.\n\nOne thing to watch for is using comfort to avoid the truth. You may rush to make each other feel better instead of staying with what the feeling is trying to tell you.\n\nTake the support. Face the problem anyway. This connection is strongest when the encouragement helps you deal with hard things instead of avoiding them."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"One thing to watch for is using comfort to avoid the truth. You may rush to make each other feel better instead of staying with what the feeling is trying to tell you."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Take the support. Face the problem anyway. This connection is strongest when the encouragement helps you deal with hard things instead of avoiding them."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-jupiter_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s growth. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person has a way of reminding you that your feelings deserve room to exist.\n\nTheir care can feel abundant. Their instinct is often to meet your emotions with generosity rather than judgment, encouragement rather than criticism. Around them it may feel easier to believe that what you are carrying does not have to be carried alone.\n\nThis person makes it easier to be yourself. Their response to your feelings is usually support, not judgment, so opening up feels safer than it does with most people. When life is hard, they remind you that you do not have to carry it alone. When life is good, they are genuinely happy for you. Around them, it is easier to trust your own feelings, ask for what you need, and believe that things can get better.\n\nOne thing to watch for is using comfort to avoid the truth. You may rush to make each other feel better instead of staying with what the feeling is trying to tell you.\n\nTake the support. Face the problem anyway. This connection is strongest when the encouragement helps you deal with hard things instead of avoiding them.","tension":"One thing to watch for is using comfort to avoid the truth. You may rush to make each other feel better instead of staying with what the feeling is trying to tell you.","advice":"Take the support. Face the problem anyway. This connection is strongest when the encouragement helps you deal with hard things instead of avoiding them.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-jupiter_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-jupiter_opposition', 'synastry-moon-opposition-jupiter', 'relationship-moon-opposition-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-jupiter_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-jupiter_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Opposition Jupiter', null, 'This person gives emotional warmth freely, and sometimes it feels like more than you want.

They often respond to your feelings with encouragement, reassurance, or a desire to help. While their intentions are genuine, there may be moments when you feel like they are trying to move you past an emotion before you have had the chance to fully experience it. What feels supportive to them can sometimes leave you feeling unseen.

At its best, this connection teaches both of you something important. They remind you that you do not have to carry everything alone, and that support can be offered freely. You remind them that some feelings need to be witnessed before they can be healed. Not every difficult moment needs a solution right away.

They offer comfort when you want understanding, and they feel rejected when their care does not land. Neither of you is wrong. You are speaking different emotional languages.

Say what you need. Let their warmth in without letting it override your experience.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person gives emotional warmth freely, and sometimes it feels like more than you want.\n\nThey often respond to your feelings with encouragement, reassurance, or a desire to help. While their intentions are genuine, there may be moments when you feel like they are trying to move you past an emotion before you have had the chance to fully experience it. What feels supportive to them can sometimes leave you feeling unseen.\n\nAt its best, this connection teaches both of you something important. They remind you that you do not have to carry everything alone, and that support can be offered freely. You remind them that some feelings need to be witnessed before they can be healed. Not every difficult moment needs a solution right away.\n\nThey offer comfort when you want understanding, and they feel rejected when their care does not land. Neither of you is wrong. You are speaking different emotional languages.\n\nSay what you need. Let their warmth in without letting it override your experience."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"They offer comfort when you want understanding, and they feel rejected when their care does not land. Neither of you is wrong. You are speaking different emotional languages."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Say what you need. Let their warmth in without letting it override your experience."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-jupiter_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s growth. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person gives emotional warmth freely, and sometimes it feels like more than you want.\n\nThey often respond to your feelings with encouragement, reassurance, or a desire to help. While their intentions are genuine, there may be moments when you feel like they are trying to move you past an emotion before you have had the chance to fully experience it. What feels supportive to them can sometimes leave you feeling unseen.\n\nAt its best, this connection teaches both of you something important. They remind you that you do not have to carry everything alone, and that support can be offered freely. You remind them that some feelings need to be witnessed before they can be healed. Not every difficult moment needs a solution right away.\n\nThey offer comfort when you want understanding, and they feel rejected when their care does not land. Neither of you is wrong. You are speaking different emotional languages.\n\nSay what you need. Let their warmth in without letting it override your experience.","tension":"They offer comfort when you want understanding, and they feel rejected when their care does not land. Neither of you is wrong. You are speaking different emotional languages.","advice":"Say what you need. Let their warmth in without letting it override your experience.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry-moon-sextile-jupiter', 'relationship-moon-sextile-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-jupiter_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-jupiter_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Sextile Jupiter', null, 'Support in this connection grows when you actually let each other in.

There''s a natural sense of goodwill here. This person wants good things for you, and you probably want the same for them. But the closeness doesn''t happen automatically. It builds little by little, every time you share something real and find that it''s met with care instead of judgment.

What makes this connection special isn''t some huge emotional breakthrough. It''s the small stuff. Feeling listened to. Feeling remembered. Knowing someone notices when you''re having a hard time. Realizing you don''t have to handle everything on your own.

Because the support is gentle rather than overwhelming, it''s easy to miss. You might assume they know what''s going on without ever saying it. You might keep things to yourself until you''re already struggling, then wonder why the connection doesn''t feel as supportive as it could.

The more you let this person be part of your emotional world, the stronger the bond becomes. The more honest you are about what''s going on, the more room there is for real support. What starts as simple kindness can grow into something deeply comforting and reliable over time.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Support in this connection grows when you actually let each other in.\n\nThere''s a natural sense of goodwill here. This person wants good things for you, and you probably want the same for them. But the closeness doesn''t happen automatically. It builds little by little, every time you share something real and find that it''s met with care instead of judgment.\n\nWhat makes this connection special isn''t some huge emotional breakthrough. It''s the small stuff. Feeling listened to. Feeling remembered. Knowing someone notices when you''re having a hard time. Realizing you don''t have to handle everything on your own.\n\nBecause the support is gentle rather than overwhelming, it''s easy to miss. You might assume they know what''s going on without ever saying it. You might keep things to yourself until you''re already struggling, then wonder why the connection doesn''t feel as supportive as it could.\n\nThe more you let this person be part of your emotional world, the stronger the bond becomes. The more honest you are about what''s going on, the more room there is for real support. What starts as simple kindness can grow into something deeply comforting and reliable over time."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Because the support is gentle rather than overwhelming, it''s easy to miss. You might assume they know what''s going on without ever saying it. You might keep things to yourself until you''re already struggling, then wonder why the connection doesn''t feel as supportive as it could."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The more you let this person be part of your emotional world, the stronger the bond becomes. The more honest you are about what''s going on, the more room there is for real support. What starts as simple kindness can grow into something deeply comforting and reliable over time."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-jupiter_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s growth. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"Support in this connection grows when you actually let each other in.\n\nThere''s a natural sense of goodwill here. This person wants good things for you, and you probably want the same for them. But the closeness doesn''t happen automatically. It builds little by little, every time you share something real and find that it''s met with care instead of judgment.\n\nWhat makes this connection special isn''t some huge emotional breakthrough. It''s the small stuff. Feeling listened to. Feeling remembered. Knowing someone notices when you''re having a hard time. Realizing you don''t have to handle everything on your own.\n\nBecause the support is gentle rather than overwhelming, it''s easy to miss. You might assume they know what''s going on without ever saying it. You might keep things to yourself until you''re already struggling, then wonder why the connection doesn''t feel as supportive as it could.\n\nThe more you let this person be part of your emotional world, the stronger the bond becomes. The more honest you are about what''s going on, the more room there is for real support. What starts as simple kindness can grow into something deeply comforting and reliable over time.","tension":"Because the support is gentle rather than overwhelming, it''s easy to miss. You might assume they know what''s going on without ever saying it. You might keep things to yourself until you''re already struggling, then wonder why the connection doesn''t feel as supportive as it could.","advice":"The more you let this person be part of your emotional world, the stronger the bond becomes. The more honest you are about what''s going on, the more room there is for real support. What starts as simple kindness can grow into something deeply comforting and reliable over time.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-jupiter_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-jupiter_square', 'synastry-moon-square-jupiter', 'relationship-moon-square-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-jupiter_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-jupiter_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Square Jupiter', null, 'This person cares about how you feel, but they do not always know how to be with your feelings.

When you are hurting, they often respond by trying to make the pain feel lighter. Their care comes through reassurance, perspective, and a belief that things can improve. Even when their intentions are good, you may sometimes feel rushed past what you are actually experiencing. What you need in those moments is not a brighter outlook but the feeling that someone truly understands where you are before trying to fix it.

That can be a lonely feeling. You may know they care about you and still feel like something important got missed. You leave the interaction feeling comforted on the surface, but the deeper part of your experience remains untouched. Their optimism can feel reassuring when you need hope and frustrating when you need understanding.

At its best, this connection helps you carry your feelings without getting lost in them. They remind you that what hurts right now is not the whole story. When you feel overwhelmed, they bring perspective, helping you step back from the emotion without dismissing it and remember that there is still room for hope.

The challenge is making room for both truth and comfort. If every difficult feeling gets softened too quickly, important emotions get skipped over. If every attempt at reassurance is rejected, genuine care goes unnoticed.

The more you can meet in the middle, the more supported and understood you both feel.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person cares about how you feel, but they do not always know how to be with your feelings.\n\nWhen you are hurting, they often respond by trying to make the pain feel lighter. Their care comes through reassurance, perspective, and a belief that things can improve. Even when their intentions are good, you may sometimes feel rushed past what you are actually experiencing. What you need in those moments is not a brighter outlook but the feeling that someone truly understands where you are before trying to fix it.\n\nThat can be a lonely feeling. You may know they care about you and still feel like something important got missed. You leave the interaction feeling comforted on the surface, but the deeper part of your experience remains untouched. Their optimism can feel reassuring when you need hope and frustrating when you need understanding.\n\nAt its best, this connection helps you carry your feelings without getting lost in them. They remind you that what hurts right now is not the whole story. When you feel overwhelmed, they bring perspective, helping you step back from the emotion without dismissing it and remember that there is still room for hope.\n\nThe challenge is making room for both truth and comfort. If every difficult feeling gets softened too quickly, important emotions get skipped over. If every attempt at reassurance is rejected, genuine care goes unnoticed.\n\nThe more you can meet in the middle, the more supported and understood you both feel."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is making room for both truth and comfort. If every difficult feeling gets softened too quickly, important emotions get skipped over. If every attempt at reassurance is rejected, genuine care goes unnoticed."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The more you can meet in the middle, the more supported and understood you both feel."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-jupiter_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s growth. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This person cares about how you feel, but they do not always know how to be with your feelings.\n\nWhen you are hurting, they often respond by trying to make the pain feel lighter. Their care comes through reassurance, perspective, and a belief that things can improve. Even when their intentions are good, you may sometimes feel rushed past what you are actually experiencing. What you need in those moments is not a brighter outlook but the feeling that someone truly understands where you are before trying to fix it.\n\nThat can be a lonely feeling. You may know they care about you and still feel like something important got missed. You leave the interaction feeling comforted on the surface, but the deeper part of your experience remains untouched. Their optimism can feel reassuring when you need hope and frustrating when you need understanding.\n\nAt its best, this connection helps you carry your feelings without getting lost in them. They remind you that what hurts right now is not the whole story. When you feel overwhelmed, they bring perspective, helping you step back from the emotion without dismissing it and remember that there is still room for hope.\n\nThe challenge is making room for both truth and comfort. If every difficult feeling gets softened too quickly, important emotions get skipped over. If every attempt at reassurance is rejected, genuine care goes unnoticed.\n\nThe more you can meet in the middle, the more supported and understood you both feel.","tension":"The challenge is making room for both truth and comfort. If every difficult feeling gets softened too quickly, important emotions get skipped over. If every attempt at reassurance is rejected, genuine care goes unnoticed.","advice":"The more you can meet in the middle, the more supported and understood you both feel.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry-moon-trine-jupiter', 'relationship-moon-trine-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-jupiter_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-jupiter_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Trine Jupiter', null, 'This person has a way of making you feel emotionally supported without drawing attention to it.

Around them, your feelings seem to have somewhere soft to land. Instead of feeling examined or questioned, you often feel received. There is a sense that your inner world makes sense to them, even when you are struggling to make sense of it yourself.

One of the gifts of this connection is the feeling that someone is beside you when life gets heavy. They have a way of helping you remember that a difficult moment is not the whole story, while still respecting the reality of what you are going through. Their support can make it easier to breathe, easier to trust that things will move forward, and easier to feel less alone with whatever you are carrying.

Being cared for this consistently can change something in you. When someone meets your feelings with warmth instead of judgment, you stop bracing for rejection. It becomes easier to trust what you feel, ask for support when you need it, and believe your needs matter.

The challenge is not conflict but complacency. Because the support is so reliable, it can fade into the background. You may forget how much this connection contributes to your well-being, or stop actively nurturing something that feels like it will always be there.

Notice what this person brings into your life. Let yourself receive it fully, and make sure you give it value in return.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a way of making you feel emotionally supported without drawing attention to it.\n\nAround them, your feelings seem to have somewhere soft to land. Instead of feeling examined or questioned, you often feel received. There is a sense that your inner world makes sense to them, even when you are struggling to make sense of it yourself.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is the feeling that someone is beside you when life gets heavy. They have a way of helping you remember that a difficult moment is not the whole story, while still respecting the reality of what you are going through. Their support can make it easier to breathe, easier to trust that things will move forward, and easier to feel less alone with whatever you are carrying.\n\nBeing cared for this consistently can change something in you. When someone meets your feelings with warmth instead of judgment, you stop bracing for rejection. It becomes easier to trust what you feel, ask for support when you need it, and believe your needs matter.\n\nThe challenge is not conflict but complacency. Because the support is so reliable, it can fade into the background. You may forget how much this connection contributes to your well-being, or stop actively nurturing something that feels like it will always be there.\n\nNotice what this person brings into your life. Let yourself receive it fully, and make sure you give it value in return."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is not conflict but complacency. Because the support is so reliable, it can fade into the background. You may forget how much this connection contributes to your well-being, or stop actively nurturing something that feels like it will always be there."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Notice what this person brings into your life. Let yourself receive it fully, and make sure you give it value in return."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-jupiter_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s growth. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This person has a way of making you feel emotionally supported without drawing attention to it.\n\nAround them, your feelings seem to have somewhere soft to land. Instead of feeling examined or questioned, you often feel received. There is a sense that your inner world makes sense to them, even when you are struggling to make sense of it yourself.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is the feeling that someone is beside you when life gets heavy. They have a way of helping you remember that a difficult moment is not the whole story, while still respecting the reality of what you are going through. Their support can make it easier to breathe, easier to trust that things will move forward, and easier to feel less alone with whatever you are carrying.\n\nBeing cared for this consistently can change something in you. When someone meets your feelings with warmth instead of judgment, you stop bracing for rejection. It becomes easier to trust what you feel, ask for support when you need it, and believe your needs matter.\n\nThe challenge is not conflict but complacency. Because the support is so reliable, it can fade into the background. You may forget how much this connection contributes to your well-being, or stop actively nurturing something that feels like it will always be there.\n\nNotice what this person brings into your life. Let yourself receive it fully, and make sure you give it value in return.","tension":"The challenge is not conflict but complacency. Because the support is so reliable, it can fade into the background. You may forget how much this connection contributes to your well-being, or stop actively nurturing something that feels like it will always be there.","advice":"Notice what this person brings into your life. Let yourself receive it fully, and make sure you give it value in return.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mars","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry-moon-conjunction-mars', 'relationship-moon-conjunction-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mars_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mars_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Conjunction Mars', null, 'This person can get right under your skin, sometimes in a good way and sometimes not. Around them, your feelings may come up faster than usual. You may feel drawn in, stirred up, irritated, comforted, or more honest than you expected to be. It is hard to stay detached when someone touches this part of you.

There can be something very immediate about the bond. This person may make you feel wanted in a way that is hard to miss. They may not always say the softest thing, but you can feel that they are present. They respond. They engage. They do not treat your emotions like an inconvenience. If you are used to people going vague or quiet when things get intense, that can feel like a relief.

When this works, it can feel protective. You may feel like they would show up for you if something went wrong, or that they care enough to react when you are hurt. There is a kind of warmth here that is not always gentle, but still feels real.

The problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.

Notice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can get right under your skin, sometimes in a good way and sometimes not. Around them, your feelings may come up faster than usual. You may feel drawn in, stirred up, irritated, comforted, or more honest than you expected to be. It is hard to stay detached when someone touches this part of you.\n\nThere can be something very immediate about the bond. This person may make you feel wanted in a way that is hard to miss. They may not always say the softest thing, but you can feel that they are present. They respond. They engage. They do not treat your emotions like an inconvenience. If you are used to people going vague or quiet when things get intense, that can feel like a relief.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel protective. You may feel like they would show up for you if something went wrong, or that they care enough to react when you are hurt. There is a kind of warmth here that is not always gentle, but still feels real.\n\nThe problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.\n\nNotice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Notice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mars_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s drive. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person can get right under your skin, sometimes in a good way and sometimes not. Around them, your feelings may come up faster than usual. You may feel drawn in, stirred up, irritated, comforted, or more honest than you expected to be. It is hard to stay detached when someone touches this part of you.\n\nThere can be something very immediate about the bond. This person may make you feel wanted in a way that is hard to miss. They may not always say the softest thing, but you can feel that they are present. They respond. They engage. They do not treat your emotions like an inconvenience. If you are used to people going vague or quiet when things get intense, that can feel like a relief.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel protective. You may feel like they would show up for you if something went wrong, or that they care enough to react when you are hurt. There is a kind of warmth here that is not always gentle, but still feels real.\n\nThe problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.\n\nNotice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship.","tension":"The problem is that the same closeness can make everything louder. A small comment can feel personal. A mood can turn into an argument. One of you may react first and understand later. If you are not careful, the relationship can start to run on the rush of fighting, making up, and calling the whole thing passion.","advice":"Notice the moment your body starts to heat up. That is where you still have a choice. The intensity can be beautiful, but it should not be in charge of the relationship.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mars","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry-moon-opposition-mars', 'relationship-moon-opposition-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mars_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mars_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Opposition Mars', null, 'This person can pull a strong reaction out of you, but relaxing into it may not always be easy. You may want closeness from them and still feel like you have to brace yourself. They may come toward you with energy when what you really wanted was patience. Or they may think they are helping, while you feel rushed, handled, or pushed past your own pace.

A lot of the tension here comes from timing. One person is ready to act, while the other is still trying to feel their way through the moment. One person wants to fix it, while the other wants to be understood first. Nobody has to be wrong for both people to end up frustrated.

When this works, it can make the relationship more honest. This person may get you to say the thing you were trying not to say. They may make it harder for you to hide behind "I''m fine" when you are clearly not fine. That can be uncomfortable, but it can also be exactly what brings the truth into the room.

The hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.

Slow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can pull a strong reaction out of you, but relaxing into it may not always be easy. You may want closeness from them and still feel like you have to brace yourself. They may come toward you with energy when what you really wanted was patience. Or they may think they are helping, while you feel rushed, handled, or pushed past your own pace.\n\nA lot of the tension here comes from timing. One person is ready to act, while the other is still trying to feel their way through the moment. One person wants to fix it, while the other wants to be understood first. Nobody has to be wrong for both people to end up frustrated.\n\nWhen this works, it can make the relationship more honest. This person may get you to say the thing you were trying not to say. They may make it harder for you to hide behind \"I''m fine\" when you are clearly not fine. That can be uncomfortable, but it can also be exactly what brings the truth into the room.\n\nThe hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.\n\nSlow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Slow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mars_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s drive. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person can pull a strong reaction out of you, but relaxing into it may not always be easy. You may want closeness from them and still feel like you have to brace yourself. They may come toward you with energy when what you really wanted was patience. Or they may think they are helping, while you feel rushed, handled, or pushed past your own pace.\n\nA lot of the tension here comes from timing. One person is ready to act, while the other is still trying to feel their way through the moment. One person wants to fix it, while the other wants to be understood first. Nobody has to be wrong for both people to end up frustrated.\n\nWhen this works, it can make the relationship more honest. This person may get you to say the thing you were trying not to say. They may make it harder for you to hide behind \"I''m fine\" when you are clearly not fine. That can be uncomfortable, but it can also be exactly what brings the truth into the room.\n\nThe hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.\n\nSlow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you.","tension":"The hard part is when the two of you start treating each other like the problem. One person reacts, the other pushes back, and suddenly you are both defending yourselves instead of trying to understand what just got touched. You may not even remember where the fight started. You just know you feel misunderstood.","advice":"Slow it down before it becomes a standoff. You are not enemies just because the feeling is strong. Say what you need while there is still room for the other person to hear you.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mars","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry-moon-sextile-mars', 'relationship-moon-sextile-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mars_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mars_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Sextile Mars', null, 'This connection may not announce itself as loudly as the conjunction or square, but there is something here that responds when one of you reaches for it. The warmth grows when someone checks in, speaks honestly, follows through, or shows care in a way the other person can actually feel.

This is a contact where action matters. Not dramatic action, necessarily. More like showing up when you said you would. Asking the question instead of guessing. Helping with the thing that has been sitting there too long. Making it clear, through behavior, that the other person is not dealing with everything alone.

When this works, both people feel a little more willing to engage. One person says what they want, and the other has something to respond to. One person makes a move, and the connection gets warmer. The care becomes easier to trust because it is not only talked about. It is shown.

The hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to.

Do not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection may not announce itself as loudly as the conjunction or square, but there is something here that responds when one of you reaches for it. The warmth grows when someone checks in, speaks honestly, follows through, or shows care in a way the other person can actually feel.\n\nThis is a contact where action matters. Not dramatic action, necessarily. More like showing up when you said you would. Asking the question instead of guessing. Helping with the thing that has been sitting there too long. Making it clear, through behavior, that the other person is not dealing with everything alone.\n\nWhen this works, both people feel a little more willing to engage. One person says what they want, and the other has something to respond to. One person makes a move, and the connection gets warmer. The care becomes easier to trust because it is not only talked about. It is shown.\n\nThe hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to.\n\nDo not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Do not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mars_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s drive. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This connection may not announce itself as loudly as the conjunction or square, but there is something here that responds when one of you reaches for it. The warmth grows when someone checks in, speaks honestly, follows through, or shows care in a way the other person can actually feel.\n\nThis is a contact where action matters. Not dramatic action, necessarily. More like showing up when you said you would. Asking the question instead of guessing. Helping with the thing that has been sitting there too long. Making it clear, through behavior, that the other person is not dealing with everything alone.\n\nWhen this works, both people feel a little more willing to engage. One person says what they want, and the other has something to respond to. One person makes a move, and the connection gets warmer. The care becomes easier to trust because it is not only talked about. It is shown.\n\nThe hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to.\n\nDo not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do.","tension":"The hard part is letting it stay too quiet. You may both feel the pull, but wait for the other person to make it obvious. You may care, but not say much. You may want closeness, but keep acting casual. Then the connection stays smaller than it has to.","advice":"Do not just sit on the feeling. Say it, show it, reach for it. This one gets stronger when someone gives the warmth something real to do.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mars_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mars","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mars_square', 'synastry-moon-square-mars', 'relationship-moon-square-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mars_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mars_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Square Mars', null, 'This person may hit a nerve before either of you knows where the nerve is. It could be their tone, their timing, the way they push, the way they do not back off, or the way they seem to move on before you are ready. Something about them can make your feelings rise quickly.

There may also be real chemistry here, which makes the whole thing more confusing. You can feel pulled toward someone and still feel irritated by them. You can want them close and also want them to stop doing exactly what they are doing. That does not mean the connection is fake. It means the same person who wakes up your desire can also wake up your defenses.

When this works, it can bring things to the surface that needed to be said. You may stop pretending something does not bother you. They may stop letting things slide. The relationship may have a way of forcing honesty, even when neither person planned on being that honest.

The problem is when the friction becomes the main way you stay connected. If things only feel alive when someone is upset, the relationship can start to confuse tension with intimacy. You poke, they react. They push, you defend. After a while, both people are tired, but neither one knows how to get close without lighting something up first.

Catch the small thing while it is still small. Not every feeling needs to become a fight. This connection works better when both people learn how to pause before trying to win the moment.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may hit a nerve before either of you knows where the nerve is. It could be their tone, their timing, the way they push, the way they do not back off, or the way they seem to move on before you are ready. Something about them can make your feelings rise quickly.\n\nThere may also be real chemistry here, which makes the whole thing more confusing. You can feel pulled toward someone and still feel irritated by them. You can want them close and also want them to stop doing exactly what they are doing. That does not mean the connection is fake. It means the same person who wakes up your desire can also wake up your defenses.\n\nWhen this works, it can bring things to the surface that needed to be said. You may stop pretending something does not bother you. They may stop letting things slide. The relationship may have a way of forcing honesty, even when neither person planned on being that honest.\n\nThe problem is when the friction becomes the main way you stay connected. If things only feel alive when someone is upset, the relationship can start to confuse tension with intimacy. You poke, they react. They push, you defend. After a while, both people are tired, but neither one knows how to get close without lighting something up first.\n\nCatch the small thing while it is still small. Not every feeling needs to become a fight. This connection works better when both people learn how to pause before trying to win the moment."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is when the friction becomes the main way you stay connected. If things only feel alive when someone is upset, the relationship can start to confuse tension with intimacy. You poke, they react. They push, you defend. After a while, both people are tired, but neither one knows how to get close without lighting something up first."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Catch the small thing while it is still small. Not every feeling needs to become a fight. This connection works better when both people learn how to pause before trying to win the moment."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mars_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"This aspect can make feelings move fast. One person''s emotional reactions may trigger the other person''s defensiveness, desire, impatience, or anger before either of them has time to think.","summaryDeep":"This person may hit a nerve before either of you knows where the nerve is. It could be their tone, their timing, the way they push, the way they do not back off, or the way they seem to move on before you are ready. Something about them can make your feelings rise quickly.\n\nThere may also be real chemistry here, which makes the whole thing more confusing. You can feel pulled toward someone and still feel irritated by them. You can want them close and also want them to stop doing exactly what they are doing. That does not mean the connection is fake. It means the same person who wakes up your desire can also wake up your defenses.\n\nWhen this works, it can bring things to the surface that needed to be said. You may stop pretending something does not bother you. They may stop letting things slide. The relationship may have a way of forcing honesty, even when neither person planned on being that honest.\n\nThe problem is when the friction becomes the main way you stay connected. If things only feel alive when someone is upset, the relationship can start to confuse tension with intimacy. You poke, they react. They push, you defend. After a while, both people are tired, but neither one knows how to get close without lighting something up first.\n\nCatch the small thing while it is still small. Not every feeling needs to become a fight. This connection works better when both people learn how to pause before trying to win the moment.","tension":"The problem is when the friction becomes the main way you stay connected. If things only feel alive when someone is upset, the relationship can start to confuse tension with intimacy. You poke, they react. They push, you defend. After a while, both people are tired, but neither one knows how to get close without lighting something up first.","advice":"Catch the small thing while it is still small. Not every feeling needs to become a fight. This connection works better when both people learn how to pause before trying to win the moment.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mars_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mars","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mars_trine', 'synastry-moon-trine-mars', 'relationship-moon-trine-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mars_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mars_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Trine Mars', null, 'This person may stir something in you without making you feel unsafe. They can bring out a more honest, alive version of you, but it does not have to feel like a battle. Around them, you may find it easier to say what you feel, act on what matters, or stop sitting on something that needs your attention.

There is a good kind of responsiveness here. If you are upset, they may not freeze or disappear. If something matters to you, they may take it seriously. You can feel supported by their presence because they do not just listen from a distance. They seem willing to meet the feeling and do something with it.

When this works, comfort and heat can sit together. You may feel wanted without feeling pressured. You may feel protected without feeling controlled. The connection can make both people a little braver with their feelings, not because anyone is forcing it, but because the energy between you makes honesty feel possible.

The only real risk is letting this good rhythm go unused. Because it is easier than the harder Moon-Mars contacts, you may not notice how much it helps. The support is there, but it still needs somewhere to go.

Use it. Say what you feel. Act on the care. Let the trust between you become something you actually build with.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may stir something in you without making you feel unsafe. They can bring out a more honest, alive version of you, but it does not have to feel like a battle. Around them, you may find it easier to say what you feel, act on what matters, or stop sitting on something that needs your attention.\n\nThere is a good kind of responsiveness here. If you are upset, they may not freeze or disappear. If something matters to you, they may take it seriously. You can feel supported by their presence because they do not just listen from a distance. They seem willing to meet the feeling and do something with it.\n\nWhen this works, comfort and heat can sit together. You may feel wanted without feeling pressured. You may feel protected without feeling controlled. The connection can make both people a little braver with their feelings, not because anyone is forcing it, but because the energy between you makes honesty feel possible.\n\nThe only real risk is letting this good rhythm go unused. Because it is easier than the harder Moon-Mars contacts, you may not notice how much it helps. The support is there, but it still needs somewhere to go.\n\nUse it. Say what you feel. Act on the care. Let the trust between you become something you actually build with."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The only real risk is letting this good rhythm go unused. Because it is easier than the harder Moon-Mars contacts, you may not notice how much it helps. The support is there, but it still needs somewhere to go."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Use it. Say what you feel. Act on the care. Let the trust between you become something you actually build with."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mars_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s drive. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This person may stir something in you without making you feel unsafe. They can bring out a more honest, alive version of you, but it does not have to feel like a battle. Around them, you may find it easier to say what you feel, act on what matters, or stop sitting on something that needs your attention.\n\nThere is a good kind of responsiveness here. If you are upset, they may not freeze or disappear. If something matters to you, they may take it seriously. You can feel supported by their presence because they do not just listen from a distance. They seem willing to meet the feeling and do something with it.\n\nWhen this works, comfort and heat can sit together. You may feel wanted without feeling pressured. You may feel protected without feeling controlled. The connection can make both people a little braver with their feelings, not because anyone is forcing it, but because the energy between you makes honesty feel possible.\n\nThe only real risk is letting this good rhythm go unused. Because it is easier than the harder Moon-Mars contacts, you may not notice how much it helps. The support is there, but it still needs somewhere to go.\n\nUse it. Say what you feel. Act on the care. Let the trust between you become something you actually build with.","tension":"The only real risk is letting this good rhythm go unused. Because it is easier than the harder Moon-Mars contacts, you may not notice how much it helps. The support is there, but it still needs somewhere to go.","advice":"Use it. Say what you feel. Act on the care. Let the trust between you become something you actually build with.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry-moon-conjunction-mercury', 'relationship-moon-conjunction-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mercury_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mercury_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Conjunction Mercury', null, 'This person may help you find words for feelings you usually keep inside. Something about the way they listen, ask, or respond can make your inner world feel easier to name.

When this works, it can feel incredibly validating. You may start talking and realize they are following the emotional thread, not just the facts. They can help you understand why something affected you, why a small thing felt bigger than it looked, or why you could not simply "move on" when part of you was still holding the feeling.

There is a quiet intimacy in this. You may feel less alone with your moods because someone can meet them with language. They may help you hear yourself more clearly. Not by telling you who you are, but by giving shape to something you were already feeling.

The challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.

Let the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may help you find words for feelings you usually keep inside. Something about the way they listen, ask, or respond can make your inner world feel easier to name.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel incredibly validating. You may start talking and realize they are following the emotional thread, not just the facts. They can help you understand why something affected you, why a small thing felt bigger than it looked, or why you could not simply \"move on\" when part of you was still holding the feeling.\n\nThere is a quiet intimacy in this. You may feel less alone with your moods because someone can meet them with language. They may help you hear yourself more clearly. Not by telling you who you are, but by giving shape to something you were already feeling.\n\nThe challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.\n\nLet the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mercury_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s mind. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person may help you find words for feelings you usually keep inside. Something about the way they listen, ask, or respond can make your inner world feel easier to name.\n\nWhen this works, it can feel incredibly validating. You may start talking and realize they are following the emotional thread, not just the facts. They can help you understand why something affected you, why a small thing felt bigger than it looked, or why you could not simply \"move on\" when part of you was still holding the feeling.\n\nThere is a quiet intimacy in this. You may feel less alone with your moods because someone can meet them with language. They may help you hear yourself more clearly. Not by telling you who you are, but by giving shape to something you were already feeling.\n\nThe challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.\n\nLet the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace.","tension":"The challenge is that words can move faster than the body. This person may name the feeling before you are ready to process it. They may explain what is happening inside you when what you really need is time to feel it for yourself.","advice":"Let the conversation help you, but do not let it rush you. The point is not to turn every feeling into a sentence right away. The point is to feel understood without losing touch with your own pace.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry-moon-opposition-mercury', 'relationship-moon-opposition-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mercury_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mercury_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Opposition Mercury', null, 'You and this person may process things in very different ways. One of you may need to talk in order to understand what is happening. The other may need quiet before the words come. One person reaches for language. The other is still trying to feel their way through.

This can create a real mismatch in emotional timing. They may ask questions when you need comfort. You may go quiet when they need a conversation. They may think they are helping by making sense of the feeling, while you feel like they are standing outside of it and explaining it back to you.

At its best, this connection teaches both people range. The person with words learns that not everything needs to be solved out loud. The person with feeling learns that language can become a bridge, not a threat. You both get better at translating inner experience into something the other person can actually meet.

The harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other.

The practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, "I need comfort right now," or "I need help making sense of this." Clear language can soften the whole pattern.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You and this person may process things in very different ways. One of you may need to talk in order to understand what is happening. The other may need quiet before the words come. One person reaches for language. The other is still trying to feel their way through.\n\nThis can create a real mismatch in emotional timing. They may ask questions when you need comfort. You may go quiet when they need a conversation. They may think they are helping by making sense of the feeling, while you feel like they are standing outside of it and explaining it back to you.\n\nAt its best, this connection teaches both people range. The person with words learns that not everything needs to be solved out loud. The person with feeling learns that language can become a bridge, not a threat. You both get better at translating inner experience into something the other person can actually meet.\n\nThe harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other.\n\nThe practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration takes over. Say, \"I need comfort right now,\" or \"I need help making sense of this.\" Clear language can soften the whole pattern."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part comes when both people start feeling alone in the same conversation. One person feels unheard. The other feels shut out. One wants a response. The other wants space. Both may be trying to connect, but the methods keep missing each other."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The practice is to ask for the kind of support you need before frustration take