  ('A-moon_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry-moon-sextile-mercury', 'relationship-moon-sextile-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-mercury_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-mercury_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Sextile Mercury', null, 'There is a natural opening here, but it grows when someone uses it.

This person may be easy to talk to about emotional things. They may not always pull everything out of you, but when you choose to share, the conversation can become grounding. You may leave the exchange feeling clearer, softer, or more connected to what you actually feel.

When this works, the connection builds through small moments of emotional honesty. A check-in that becomes real. A question that helps you name the thing underneath the thing. A conversation that starts casually and ends with both people feeling a little more understood.

The strength here is gentle consistency. This person may help you trust that your feelings have a place to go. Not every emotion needs to become a crisis. Not every conversation needs to go deep. But over time, the willingness to listen, ask, and respond with care creates safety.

The challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.

Open the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is a natural opening here, but it grows when someone uses it.\n\nThis person may be easy to talk to about emotional things. They may not always pull everything out of you, but when you choose to share, the conversation can become grounding. You may leave the exchange feeling clearer, softer, or more connected to what you actually feel.\n\nWhen this works, the connection builds through small moments of emotional honesty. A check-in that becomes real. A question that helps you name the thing underneath the thing. A conversation that starts casually and ends with both people feeling a little more understood.\n\nThe strength here is gentle consistency. This person may help you trust that your feelings have a place to go. Not every emotion needs to become a crisis. Not every conversation needs to go deep. But over time, the willingness to listen, ask, and respond with care creates safety.\n\nThe challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.\n\nOpen the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Open the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-mercury_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s mind. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"There is a natural opening here, but it grows when someone uses it.\n\nThis person may be easy to talk to about emotional things. They may not always pull everything out of you, but when you choose to share, the conversation can become grounding. You may leave the exchange feeling clearer, softer, or more connected to what you actually feel.\n\nWhen this works, the connection builds through small moments of emotional honesty. A check-in that becomes real. A question that helps you name the thing underneath the thing. A conversation that starts casually and ends with both people feeling a little more understood.\n\nThe strength here is gentle consistency. This person may help you trust that your feelings have a place to go. Not every emotion needs to become a crisis. Not every conversation needs to go deep. But over time, the willingness to listen, ask, and respond with care creates safety.\n\nThe challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.\n\nOpen the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly.","tension":"The challenge is keeping it too light. You may talk easily and still avoid the things that matter most. The connection can stay pleasant without becoming truly intimate if nobody brings the real feeling into the room.","advice":"Open the door on purpose. Say what is actually going on. Ask the question that matters. This connection becomes comforting when both people stop circling the feeling and begin to meet it directly.","policy"