  ('A-moon_B-neptune_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"neptune","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-neptune_opposition', 'synastry-moon-opposition-neptune', 'relationship-moon-opposition-neptune']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-neptune_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-neptune_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Opposition Neptune', null, 'This person can feel like the answer to a loneliness you had stopped expecting anyone to notice.

There is often a strong emotional pull here, but it can be difficult to understand clearly. The Moon person may feel that the Neptune person sees something in them that others miss. The Neptune person may seem to offer a kind of emotional refuge, a place where old defenses can finally lower.

At its best, this aspect can teach both people how to receive care without armor. The Moon person brings emotional honesty to the surface. The Neptune person brings imagination, compassion, and a willingness to meet feelings that do not fit neatly into words. Together, they can create a bond that feels deeply accepting.

But oppositions invite projection. One person may begin filling in the blanks with what they hope is true. The Moon person may assume the Neptune person feels the same depth, needs the same closeness, or understands the relationship in the same way. The Neptune person may drift in and out of emotional availability, not always realizing how much meaning the Moon person has placed on the connection. When reality arrives, the disappointment can be painful. You may realize you were not only relating to the person in front of you, but also to the feeling they awakened in you. The longing was real. The care may have been real. But the story built around it may not have been.

The invitation here is to keep returning to what is actually happening. Notice where you are hoping, assuming, rescuing, or waiting for the other person to become clearer than they are willing to be. This connection can be beautiful when care and clarity are allowed to exist together. It hurts most when the dream of being understood becomes more important than the truth of who is actually there.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can feel like the answer to a loneliness you had stopped expecting anyone to notice.\n\nThere is often a strong emotional pull here, but it can be difficult to understand clearly. The Moon person may feel that the Neptune person sees something in them that others miss. The Neptune person may seem to offer a kind of emotional refuge, a place where old defenses can finally lower.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can teach both people how to receive care without armor. The Moon person brings emotional honesty to the surface. The Neptune person brings imagination, compassion, and a willingness to meet feelings that do not fit neatly into words. Together, they can create a bond that feels deeply accepting.\n\nBut oppositions invite projection. One person may begin filling in the blanks with what they hope is true. The Moon person may assume the Neptune person feels the same depth, needs the same closeness, or understands the relationship in the same way. The Neptune person may drift in and out of emotional availability, not always realizing how much meaning the Moon person has placed on the connection. When reality arrives, the disappointment can be painful. You may realize you were not only relating to the person in front of you, but also to the feeling they awakened in you. The longing was real. The care may have been real. But the story built around it may not have been.\n\nThe invitation here is to keep returning to what is actually happening. Notice where you are hoping, assuming, rescuing, or waiting for the other person to become clearer than they are willing to be. This connection can be beautiful when care and clarity are allowed to exist together. It hurts most when the dream of being understood becomes more important than the truth of who is actually there."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But oppositions invite projection. One person may begin filling in the blanks with what they hope is true. The Moon person may assume the Neptune person feels the same depth, needs the same closeness, or understands the relationship in the same way. The Neptune person may drift in and out of emotional availability, not always realizing how much meaning the Moon person has placed on the connection. When reality arrives, the disappointment can be painful. You may realize you were not only relating to the person in front of you, but also to the feeling they awakened in you. The longing was real. The care may have been real. But the story built around it may not have been."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The invitation here is to keep returning to what is actually happening. Notice where you are hoping, assuming, rescuing, or waiting for the other person to become clearer than they are willing to be. This connection can be beautiful when care and clarity are allowed to exist together. It hurts most when the dream of being understood becomes more important than the truth of who is actually there."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-neptune_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s dreams. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person can feel like the answer to a loneliness you had stopped expecting anyone to notice.\n\nThere is often a strong emotional pull here, but it can be difficult to understand clearly. The Moon person may feel that the Neptune person sees something in them that others miss. The Neptune person may seem to offer a kind of emotional refuge, a place where old defenses can finally lower.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can