y have been real. But the story built around it may not have been.","advice":"The invitation here is to keep returning to what is actually happening. Notice where you are hoping, assuming, rescuing, or waiting for the other person to become clearer than they are willing to be. This connection can be beautiful when care and clarity are allowed to exist together. It hurts most when the dream of being understood becomes more important than the truth of who is actually there.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-neptune_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"neptune","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-neptune_sextile', 'synastry-moon-sextile-neptune', 'relationship-moon-sextile-neptune']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-neptune_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-neptune_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Sextile Neptune', null, 'Some connections feel emotionally safe long before they become emotionally deep. This is often one of them.

The Neptune person may pick up on the Moon person''s moods and feelings in subtle ways, noticing what is going on beneath the surface without demanding an explanation. The Moon person, in turn, may find themselves opening up more naturally than they expected. There is often a sense of being listened to without being analyzed, understood without being pushed.

What makes this aspect special is that it allows trust to grow at its own pace. Neither person has to force intimacy or manufacture emotional closeness. Instead, it develops through small moments of understanding, thoughtful gestures, and the feeling that there is space for both people to be human. Over time, the relationship can become a source of genuine comfort and support.

There is a softness here that can bring out the best in both people. The Moon person may feel safer expressing vulnerability, while the Neptune person may discover that caring for someone does not require sacrificing themselves. Together, they can create an atmosphere of patience, empathy, and emotional generosity.

The difficulty is that this connection can sometimes stay in the realm of potential. Both people may sense what the other is feeling without ever talking about it directly. Important needs can remain implied rather than expressed. The relationship may feel warm and supportive, yet avoid the conversations that would allow it to deepen further.

This aspect works best when intuition is paired with honesty. Trust what you sense, but also say what you mean. The compassion between you is real, but it becomes much more meaningful when it is supported by clear communication. The gift here is not saving each other. It is creating a relationship where both people feel understood, cared for, and free to remain themselves.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Some connections feel emotionally safe long before they become emotionally deep. This is often one of them.\n\nThe Neptune person may pick up on the Moon person''s moods and feelings in subtle ways, noticing what is going on beneath the surface without demanding an explanation. The Moon person, in turn, may find themselves opening up more naturally than they expected. There is often a sense of being listened to without being analyzed, understood without being pushed.\n\nWhat makes this aspect special is that it allows trust to grow at its own pace. Neither person has to force intimacy or manufacture emotional closeness. Instead, it develops through small moments of understanding, thoughtful gestures, and the feeling that there is space for both people to be human. Over time, the relationship can become a source of genuine comfort and support.\n\nThere is a softness here that can bring out the best in both people. The Moon person may feel safer expressing vulnerability, while the Neptune person may discover that caring for someone does not require sacrificing themselves. Together, they can create an atmosphere of patience, empathy, and emotional generosity.\n\nThe difficulty is that this connection can sometimes stay in the realm of potential. Both people may sense what the other is feeling without ever talking about it directly. Important needs can remain implied rather than expressed. The relationship may feel warm and supportive, yet avoid the conversations that would allow it to deepen further.\n\nThis aspect works best when intuition is paired with honesty. Trust what you sense, but also say what you mean. The compassion between you is real, but it becomes much more meaningful when it is supported by clear communication. The gift here is not saving each other. It is creating a relationship where both people feel understood, cared for, and free to remain themselves."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The difficulty is that this connection can sometimes stay in the realm of potential. Both people may sense what the other is feeling without ever talking about it directly. Important needs can remain implied rather than expressed. The relationship may feel warm and supportive, yet avoid the conversations that would allow it to deepen further."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This aspect works best when intuition is paired with honesty. Trust what you sense, but also say what you mean. The compassion between you is real, but it becomes much more meaningful when it is supported by clear communication. The gift here is not saving each other. It is creating a relationship where both people feel understood, cared for, and free to remain themselves."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-neptune_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s dreams. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"Some connections feel emotionally safe long before they become emotionally deep. This is often one of them.\n\nThe Neptune person may pick up on the Moon person''s moods and feelings in subtle ways, noticing what is going on beneath the surface without demanding an explanation. The Moon person, in turn, may find themselves opening up more naturally than they expected. There is often a sense of being listened to without being analyzed, understood without being pushed.\n\nWhat makes this aspect special is that it allows trust to grow at its own pace. Neither person has to force intimacy or manufacture emotional closeness. Instead, it develops through small moments of understanding, thoughtful gestures, and the feeling that there is space for both people to be human. Over time, the relationship can become a source of genuine comfort and support.\n\nThere is a softness here that can bring out the best in both people. The Moon person may feel safer expressing vulnerability, while the Neptune person may discover that caring for someone does not require sacrificing themselves. Together, they can create an atmosphere of patience, empathy, and emotional generosity.\n\nThe difficulty is that this connection can sometimes stay in the realm of potential. Both people may sense what the other is feeling without ever talking about it directly. Important needs can remain implied rather than expressed. The relationship may feel warm and supportive, yet avoid the conversations that would allow it to deepen further.\n\nThis aspect works best when intuition is paired with honesty. Trust what you sense, but also say what you mean. The compassion between you is real, but it becomes much more meaningful when it is supported by clear communication. The gift here is not saving each other. It is creating a relationship where both people feel understood, cared for, and free to remain themselves.","tension":"The difficulty is that this connection can sometimes stay in the realm of potential. Both people may sense what the other is feeling without ever talking about it directly. Important needs can remain implied rather than expressed. The relationship may feel warm and supportive, yet avoid the conversations that would allow it to deepen further.","advice":"This aspect works best when intuition is paired with honesty. Trust what you sense, but also say what you mean. The compassion between you is real, but it becomes much more meaningful when it is supported by clear communication. The gift here is not saving each other. It is creating a relationship where both people feel understood, cared for, and free to remain themselves.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-neptune_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"neptune","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-neptune_square', 'synastry-moon-square-neptune', 'relationship-moon-square-neptune']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-neptune_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-neptune_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Square Neptune', null, 'There can be a strange pull between you that is hard to define. The connection feels emotionally significant, yet neither person may be able to explain exactly why.

The Moon person is often the first to feel it. They may become unusually preoccupied with the Neptune person, sensing that something important is happening beneath the surface. The Neptune person, meanwhile, may seem deeply attuned to the Moon person''s emotional world, picking up on moods and vulnerabilities without needing much explanation. Yet that sensitivity does not always translate into clarity. What feels understood emotionally can remain difficult to define in practical terms.

When this aspect is expressed well, it can soften emotional defenses. The Moon person may feel more comfortable revealing feelings they normally protect. The Neptune person may discover that empathy becomes more meaningful when it is paired with honesty, consistency, and action. There is real potential for both people to become more emotionally aware through the relationship.

The challenge is that understanding can be assumed rather than communicated. Feelings are sensed, guessed at, or absorbed instead of discussed. Over time, each person may begin playing a role without consciously choosing it. One becomes the emotional caretaker. The other leans on that support. Neither fully notices how the pattern developed. Eventually, the relationship can start to feel heavier than it did at the beginning. Not because the affection is gone, but because so much remains unspoken. The Moon person may find themselves carrying worries, responsibilities, or emotional burdens that do not belong to them. The Neptune person may avoid difficult conversations, hoping compassion will smooth over problems that actually need to be addressed. The result is often a bond that feels deeply connected on the surface while important truths remain untouched underneath.

A useful question is whether this relationship helps you feel more grounded in yourself or whether you lose sight of your own needs inside it. One of the lessons of this aspect is learning that compassion does not require self-sacrifice. Caring for someone is not the same as saving them.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There can be a strange pull between you that is hard to define. The connection feels emotionally significant, yet neither person may be able to explain exactly why.\n\nThe Moon person is often the first to feel it. They may become unusually preoccupied with the Neptune person, sensing that something important is happening beneath the surface. The Neptune person, meanwhile, may seem deeply attuned to the Moon person''s emotional world, picking up on moods and vulnerabilities without needing much explanation. Yet that sensitivity does not always translate into clarity. What feels understood emotionally can remain difficult to define in practical terms.\n\nWhen this aspect is expressed well, it can soften emotional defenses. The Moon person may feel more comfortable revealing feelings they normally protect. The Neptune person may discover that empathy becomes more meaningful when it is paired with honesty, consistency, and action. There is real potential for both people to become more emotionally aware through the relationship.\n\nThe challenge is that understanding can be assumed rather than communicated. Feelings are sensed, guessed at, or absorbed instead of discussed. Over time, each person may begin playing a role without consciously choosing it. One becomes the emotional caretaker. The other leans on that support. Neither fully notices how the pattern developed. Eventually, the relationship can start to feel heavier than it did at the beginning. Not because the affection is gone, but because so much remains unspoken. The Moon person may find themselves carrying worries, responsibilities, or emotional burdens that do not belong to them. The Neptune person may avoid difficult conversations, hoping compassion will smooth over problems that actually need to be addressed. The result is often a bond that feels deeply connected on the surface while important truths remain untouched underneath.\n\nA useful question is whether this relationship helps you feel more grounded in yourself or whether you lose sight of your own needs inside it. One of the lessons of this aspect is learning that compassion does not require self-sacrifice. Caring for someone is not the same as saving them."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that understanding can be assumed rather than communicated. Feelings are sensed, guessed at, or absorbed instead of discussed. Over time, each person may begin playing a role without consciously choosing it. One becomes the emotional caretaker. The other leans on that support. Neither fully notices how the pattern developed. Eventually, the relationship can start to feel heavier than it did at the beginning. Not because the affection is gone, but because so much remains unspoken. The Moon person may find themselves carrying worries, responsibilities, or emotional burdens that do not belong to them. The Neptune person may avoid difficult conversations, hoping compassion will smooth over problems that actually need to be addressed. The result is often a bond that feels deeply connected on the surface while important truths remain untouched underneath."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"A useful question is whether this relationship helps you feel more grounded in yourself or whether you lose sight of your own needs inside it. One of the lessons of this aspect is learning that compassion does not require self-sacrifice. Caring for someone is not the same as saving them."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-neptune_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s dreams. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"There can be a strange pull between you that 