ur own needs inside it. One of the lessons of this aspect is learning that compassion does not require self-sacrifice. Caring for someone is not the same as saving them.","tension":"The challenge is that understanding can be assumed rather than communicated. Feelings are sensed, guessed at, or absorbed instead of discussed. Over time, each person may begin playing a role without consciously choosing it. One becomes the emotional caretaker. The other leans on that support. Neither fully notices how the pattern developed. Eventually, the relationship can start to feel heavier than it did at the beginning. Not because the affection is gone, but because so much remains unspoken. The Moon person may find themselves carrying worries, responsibilities, or emotional burdens that do not belong to them. The Neptune person may avoid difficult conversations, hoping compassion will smooth over problems that actually need to be addressed. The result is often a bond that feels deeply connected on the surface while important truths remain untouched underneath.","advice":"A useful question is whether this relationship helps you feel more grounded in yourself or whether you lose sight of your own needs inside it. One of the lessons of this aspect is learning that compassion does not require self-sacrifice. Caring for someone is not the same as saving them.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-neptune_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"neptune","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-neptune_trine', 'synastry-moon-trine-neptune', 'relationship-moon-trine-neptune']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-neptune_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-neptune_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Trine Neptune', null, 'There is something quietly soothing about this connection.

The Moon person often feels emotionally understood without having to explain every feeling in detail. The Neptune person seems to sense what is happening beneath the surface, responding to emotions that have not yet been fully expressed. This can create a feeling of being deeply seen and emotionally received, even when very little has been said aloud.

Because of that, being together can feel easy. The Moon person may feel less guarded, less worried about being judged for what they feel. The Neptune person may feel free to express their sensitivity without having to defend it or make it seem more practical than it is. There is often a natural gentleness between the two people, as though each instinctively knows how to handle the other''s softer edges.

This can also be a deeply imaginative connection. Shared music, films, memories, dreams, spiritual interests, or simply sitting together in comfortable silence can create a sense of closeness. The relationship may feel meaningful in ways that are difficult to explain. Sometimes the moments that stay with you are not the dramatic ones, but the small, almost invisible exchanges that make you feel understood.

The difficulty is that what feels healing can slowly become necessary. Because emotional support flows so naturally, neither person may notice when the relationship starts carrying more weight than it should. The Moon person may begin looking to the Neptune person for reassurance they need to learn to give themselves. The Neptune person may absorb the Moon person''s emotions so completely that they lose track of where their own begin. This rarely happens overnight. It is usually the result of many small moments of comfort accumulating over time.

The gift of this aspect is emotional trust. The lesson is remembering that closeness works best when it connects two whole people, not when it becomes the place where either person disappears.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is something quietly soothing about this connection.\n\nThe Moon person often feels emotionally understood without having to explain every feeling in detail. The Neptune person seems to sense what is happening beneath the surface, responding to emotions that have not yet been fully expressed. This can create a feeling of being deeply seen and emotionally received, even when very little has been said aloud.\n\nBecause of that, being together can feel easy. The Moon person may feel less guarded, less worried about being judged for what they feel. The Neptune person may feel free to express their sensitivity without having to defend it or make it seem more practical than it is. There is often a natural gentleness between the two people, as though each instinctively knows how to handle the other''s softer edges.\n\nThis can also be a deeply imaginative connection. Shared music, films, memories, dreams, spiritual interests, or simply sitting together in comfortable silence can create a sense of closeness. The relationship may feel meaningful in ways that are difficult to explain. Sometimes the moments that stay with you are not the dramatic ones, but the small, almost invisible exchanges that make you feel understood.\n\nThe difficulty is that what feels healing can slowly become necessary. Because emotional support flows so naturally, neither person may notice when the relationship starts carrying more weight than it should. The Moon person may begin looking to the Neptune person for reassurance they need to learn to give themselves. The Neptune person may absorb the Moon person''s emotions so completely that they lose track of where their own begin. This rarely happens overnight. It is usually the result of many small moments of comfort accumulating over time.\n\nThe gift of this aspect is emotional trust. The lesson is remembering that closeness works best when it connects two whole people, not when it becomes the place where either person disappears."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The difficulty is that what feels healing can slowly become necessary. Because emotional support flows so naturally, neither person may notice when the relationship starts carrying more weight than it should. The Moon person may begin looking to the Neptune person for reassurance they need to learn to give themselves. The Neptune person may absorb the Moon person''s emotions so completely that they lose track of where their own begin. This rarely happens overnight. It is usually the result of many small moments of comfort accumulating over time."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The gift of this aspect is emotional trust. The lesson is remembering that closeness works best when it connects two whole people, not when it becomes the place where either person disappears."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-neptune_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s dreams. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"There is something quietly soothing about this connection.\n\nThe Moon person often feels emotionally understood without having to explain every feeling in detail. The Neptune person seems to sense what is happening beneath the surface, responding to emotions that have not yet been fully expressed. This can create a feeling of being deeply seen and emotionally received, even when very little has been said aloud.\n\nBecause of that, being together can feel easy. The Moon person may feel less guarded, less worried about being judged for what they feel. The Neptune person may feel free to express their sensitivity without having to defend it or make it seem more practical than it is. There is often a natural gentleness between the two people, as though each instinctively knows how to handle the other''s softer edges.\n\nThis can also be a deeply imaginative connection. Shared music, films, memories, dreams, spiritual interests, or simply sitting together in comfortable silence can create a sense of closeness. The relationship may feel meaningful in ways that are difficult to explain. Sometimes the moments that stay with you are not the dramatic ones, but the small, almost invisible exchanges that make you feel understood.\n\nThe difficulty is that what feels healing can slowly become necessary. Because emotional support flows so naturally, neither person may notice when the relationship starts carrying more weight than it should. The Moon person may begin looking to the Neptune person for reassurance they need to learn to give themselves. The Neptune person may absorb the Moon person''s emotions so completely that they lose track of where their own begin. This rarely happens overnight. It is usually the result of many small moments of comfort accumulating over time.\n\nThe gift of this aspect is emotional trust. The lesson is remembering that closeness works best when it connects two whole people, not when it becomes the place where either person disappears.","tension":"The difficulty is that what feels healing can slowly become necessary. Because emotional support flows so naturally, neither person may notice when the relationship starts carrying more weight than it should. The Moon person may begin looking to the Neptune person for reassurance they need to learn to give themselves. The Neptune person may absorb the Moon person''s emotions so completely that they lose track of where their own begin. This rarely happens overnight. It is usually the result of many small moments of comfort accumulating over time.","advice":"The gift of this aspect is emotional trust. The lesson is remembering that closeness works best when it connects two whole people, not when it becomes the place where either person disappears.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-pluto_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-pluto_conjunction', 'synastry-moon-conjunction-pluto', 'relationship-moon-conjunction-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-pluto_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-pluto_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Conjunction Pluto', null, 'This person gets under your skin fast. Moon-Pluto conjunctions are some of the hardest connections to stay objective about because the Pluto person plugs directly into the Moon person''s emotional world. The connection can feel immediate, intense, and impossible to ignore. The Pluto person often seems to know what the Moon person is feeling before it is spoken, and the Moon person may feel more emotionally exposed around them than around anyone else.

At first, this can feel incredible. The Moon person feels deeply seen, understood, and emotionally recognized. The Pluto person feels drawn to the Moon person''s vulnerability and wants access to everything beneath the surface. The intimacy can feel stronger than what either person is used to.

But this aspect can become consuming very quickly. Feelings get intense. Attachment gets intense. The need for reassurance, closeness, and emotional access can become overwhelming. The Moon person may start revolving around the Pluto person emotionally. The Pluto person may become possessive, controlling, or obsessed with maintaining the bond. Healthy distance can start to feel like rejection. This is one of the clearest indicators of emotional enmeshment in synastry when it is handled poorly. Boundaries blur. Dependency grows. Both people can become so wrapped up in each other that they lose perspective and stop functioning from a grounded place.

At its best, this aspect creates deep emotional healing and intimacy. At its worst, it creates an attachment that is incredibly difficult to leave because it hooks directly into the emotional and attachment system. The lesson is simple: depth is not the same thing as health. If this connection is costing you your emotional stability, the intensity is not a sign that it is meant to be.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person gets under your skin fast. Moon-Pluto conjunctions are some of the hardest connections to stay objective about because the Pluto person plugs directly into the Moon person''s emotional world. The connection can feel immediate, intense, and impossible to ignore. The Pluto person often seems to know what the Moon person is feeling before it is spoken, and the Moon person may feel more emotionally exposed around them than around anyone else.\n\nAt first, this can feel incredible. The Moon person feels deeply seen, understood, and emotionally recognized. The Pluto person feels drawn to the Moon person''s vulnerability and wants access to everything beneath the surface. The intimacy can feel stronger than what either person is used to.\n\nBut this aspect can become consuming very quickly. Feelings get intense. Attachment gets intense. The need for reassurance, closeness, and emotional access can become overwhelming. The Moon person may start revolving around the Pluto person emotionally. The Pluto person may become possessive, controlling, or obsessed with maintaining the bond. Healthy distance can start to feel like rejection. This is one of the clearest indicators of emotional enmeshment in synastry when it is handled poorly. Boundaries blur. Dependency grows. Both people can become so wrapped up in each other that they lose perspective and stop functioning from a grounded place.\n\nAt its best, this aspect creates deep emotional healing and intimacy. At its worst, it creates an attachment that is incredibly difficult to leave because it hooks directly into the emotional and attachment system. The lesson is simple: depth is not the same thing as health. If this connection is costing you your emotional stability, the intensity is not a sign that it is meant to be."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But this aspect can become consuming very quickly. Feelings get intense. Attachment gets intense. The need for reassurance, closeness, and emotional access can become overwhelming. The Moon person may start revolving around the Pluto person emotionally. The Pluto person may become possessive, controlling, or obsessed with maintaining the bond. Healthy distance can start to feel like rejection. This is one of the clearest indicators of emotional enmeshment in synastry when it is handled poorly. Boundaries blur. Dependency grows. Both people can become so wrapped up in each other that they lose perspective and stop functioning from a grounded place."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"At its best, this aspect creates deep emotional healing and intimacy. At its worst, it creates an attachment that is incredibly difficult to leave because it hooks directly into the emotional and attachment system. The lesson is simple: depth is not the same thing as health. If this connection is costing you your emotional stability, the intensity is not a sign that it is meant to be."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-pluto_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"This can feel emotionally consuming. The Pluto person may reach places in the Moon person that are usually hidden, while the Moon person can awaken deep attachment, fear, protectiveness, or control in the Pluto person.","summaryDeep":"This person gets under your skin fast. Moon-Pluto conjunctions are some of the hardest connections to stay objective about because the Pluto person plugs directly into the Moon person''s emotional world. The connection can feel immediate, intense, and impossible to ignore. The Pluto person often seems to know what the Moon pe