ur. Dependency grows. Both people can become so wrapped up in each other that they lose perspective and stop functioning from a grounded place.","advice":"At its best, this aspect creates deep emotional healing and intimacy. At its worst, it creates an attachment that is incredibly difficult to leave because it hooks directly into the emotional and attachment system. The lesson is simple: depth is not the same thing as health. If this connection is costing you your emotional stability, the intensity is not a sign that it is meant to be.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-pluto_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-pluto_opposition', 'synastry-moon-opposition-pluto', 'relationship-moon-opposition-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-pluto_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-pluto_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Opposition Pluto', null, 'This person has a way of reaching feelings you thought were buried, forgotten, or long resolved. Being around them can awaken emotions that have been sitting quietly beneath the surface for years, waiting for the right catalyst to bring them into the light.

There is a strong emotional pull between you, but it often comes with a sense of tension or imbalance. The Pluto person seems able to access the Moon person''s deepest emotional terrain while remaining somewhat mysterious themselves. As a result, the Moon person may feel deeply affected by the connection, seen, exposed, changed, or unsettled, while the Pluto person appears to hold more of the emotional power or influence within the dynamic.

At its healthiest, this aspect encourages both people to be honest about what they are really feeling beneath the surface. The Pluto person may help the Moon person recognize emotions they have pushed aside, fears they have been avoiding, or relationship patterns they keep repeating without realizing it. When approached with care and self-awareness, the connection can shine a light on where each person wants deeper intimacy, where they struggle to trust, and where old emotional habits are getting in the way of the closeness they truly want.

But this aspect can also become an emotional power struggle. One person may reach while the other withdraws. One person may need reassurance while the other resists being needed. Jealousy, possessiveness, emotional testing, and manipulation can emerge when fear takes over. The bond can become difficult to step away from, not because it is always nourishing, but because it touches the attachment system so deeply.

The work is mutual care. Both people need to be honest about what they feel without using those feelings as weapons. This connection can deepen intimacy when vulnerability is respected. Without that respect, closeness can become destabilizing.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a way of reaching feelings you thought were buried, forgotten, or long resolved. Being around them can awaken emotions that have been sitting quietly beneath the surface for years, waiting for the right catalyst to bring them into the light.\n\nThere is a strong emotional pull between you, but it often comes with a sense of tension or imbalance. The Pluto person seems able to access the Moon person''s deepest emotional terrain while remaining somewhat mysterious themselves. As a result, the Moon person may feel deeply affected by the connection, seen, exposed, changed, or unsettled, while the Pluto person appears to hold more of the emotional power or influence within the dynamic.\n\nAt its healthiest, this aspect encourages both people to be honest about what they are really feeling beneath the surface. The Pluto person may help the Moon person recognize emotions they have pushed aside, fears they have been avoiding, or relationship patterns they keep repeating without realizing it. When approached with care and self-awareness, the connection can shine a light on where each person wants deeper intimacy, where they struggle to trust, and where old emotional habits are getting in the way of the closeness they truly want.\n\nBut this aspect can also become an emotional power struggle. One person may reach while the other withdraws. One person may need reassurance while the other resists being needed. Jealousy, possessiveness, emotional testing, and manipulation can emerge when fear takes over. The bond can become difficult to step away from, not because it is always nourishing, but because it touches the attachment system so deeply.\n\nThe work is mutual care. Both people need to be honest about what they feel without using those feelings as weapons. This connection can deepen intimacy when vulnerability is respected. Without that respect, closeness can become destabilizing."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But this aspect can also become an emotional power struggle. One person may reach while the other withdraws. One person may need reassurance while the other resists being needed. Jealousy, possessiveness, emotional testing, and manipulation can emerge when fear takes over. The bond can become difficult to step away from, not because it is always nourishing, but because it touches the attachment system so deeply."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The work is mutual care. Both people need to be honest about what they feel without using those feelings as weapons. This connection can deepen intimacy when vulnerability is respected. Without that respect, closeness can become destabilizing."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-pluto_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s depth and power. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person has a way of reaching feelings you thought were buried, forgotten, or long resolved. Being around them can awaken emotions that have been sitting quietly beneath the surface for years, waiting for the right catalyst to bring them into the light.\n\nThere is a strong emotional pull between you, but it often comes with a sense of tension or imbalance. The Pluto person seems able to access the Moon person''s deepest emotional terrain while remaining somewhat mysterious themselves. As a result, the Moon person may feel deeply affected by the connection, seen, exposed, changed, or unsettled, while the Pluto person appears to hold more of the emotional power or influence within the dynamic.\n\nAt its healthiest, this aspect encourages both people to be honest about what they are really feeling beneath the surface. The Pluto person may help the Moon person recognize emotions they have pushed aside, fears they have been avoiding, or relationship patterns they keep repeating without realizing it. When approached with care and self-awareness, the connection can shine a light on where each person wants deeper intimacy, where they struggle to trust, and where old emotional habits are getting in the way of the closeness they truly want.\n\nBut this aspect can also become an emotional power struggle. One person may reach while the other withdraws. One person may need reassurance while the other resists being needed. Jealousy, possessiveness, emotional testing, and manipulation can emerge when fear takes over. The bond can become difficult to step away from, not because it is always nourishing, but because it touches the attachment system so deeply.\n\nThe work is mutual care. Both people need to be honest about what they feel without using those feelings as weapons. This connection can deepen intimacy when vulnerability is respected. Without that respect, closeness can become destabilizing.","tension":"But this aspect can also become an emotional power struggle. One person may reach while the other withdraws. One person may need reassurance while the other resists being needed. Jealousy, possessiveness, emotional testing, and manipulation can emerge when fear takes over. The bond can become difficult to step away from, not because it is always nourishing, but because it touches the attachment system so deeply.","advice":"The work is mutual care. Both people need to be honest about what they feel without using those feelings as weapons. This connection can deepen intimacy when vulnerability is respected. Without that respect, closeness can become destabilizing.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus