  ('A-moon_B-pluto_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-pluto_sextile', 'synastry-moon-sextile-pluto', 'relationship-moon-sextile-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-pluto_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-pluto_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Sextile Pluto', null, 'This connection has the potential to create a deep sense of emotional trust over time. The Pluto person may pick up on feelings the Moon person struggles to put into words, helping them feel understood without pressure or judgment. Rather than forcing vulnerability, the relationship gently encourages it, creating a space where deeper conversations and emotional honesty can develop naturally.

When approached intentionally, this aspect can create a strong foundation for emotional growth. The Pluto person may encourage the Moon person to put words to feelings they have kept inside, recognize recurring emotional patterns, and develop greater trust in their own emotional experience. In turn, the Moon person''s openness and sensitivity can help the Pluto person relate with more compassion, patience, and emotional awareness.

One of the strengths of this aspect is that it does not rush intimacy. The opportunity for deeper connection is there, but it develops through choice rather than pressure. The relationship tends to thrive when both people are willing to be honest, stay curious about each other, and have conversations that go beyond the surface.

The challenge is that it can be easy to settle into comfort without fully engaging the deeper potential of the connection. If both people avoid vulnerability or keep important feelings unspoken, the relationship may remain supportive but never reach the level of closeness it is capable of creating.

Allow trust to build naturally. Share your feelings a little more openly than you normally would. Pay attention to what this relationship teaches you about your needs, your patterns, and your capacity for intimacy. The real gift of this aspect is not intensity. It is the chance to create a deeper, more authentic connection while staying grounded in yourself.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection has the potential to create a deep sense of emotional trust over time. The Pluto person may pick up on feelings the Moon person struggles to put into words, helping them feel understood without pressure or judgment. Rather than forcing vulnerability, the relationship gently encourages it, creating a space where deeper conversations and emotional honesty can develop naturally.\n\nWhen approached intentionally, this aspect can create a strong foundation for emotional growth. The Pluto person may encourage the Moon person to put words to feelings they have kept inside, recognize recurring emotional patterns, and develop greater trust in their own emotional experience. In turn, the Moon person''s openness and sensitivity can help the Pluto person relate with more compassion, patience, and emotional awareness.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is that it does not rush intimacy. The opportunity for deeper connection is there, but it develops through choice rather than pressure. The relationship tends to thrive when both people are willing to be honest, stay curious about each other, and have conversations that go beyond the surface.\n\nThe challenge is that it can be easy to settle into comfort without fully engaging the deeper potential of the connection. If both people avoid vulnerability or keep important feelings unspoken, the relationship may remain supportive but never reach the level of closeness it is capable of creating.\n\nAllow trust to build naturally. Share your feelings a little more openly than you normally would. Pay attention to what this relationship teaches you about your needs, your patterns, and your capacity for intimacy. The real gift of this aspect is not intensity. It is the chance to create a deeper, more authentic connection while staying grounded in yourself."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that it can be easy to settle into comfort without fully engaging the deeper potential of the connection. If both people avoid vulnerability or keep important feelings unspoken, the relationship may remain supportive but never reach the level of closeness it is capable of creating."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Allow trust to build naturally. Share your feelings a little more openly than you normally would. Pay attention to what this relationship teaches you about your needs, your patterns, and your capacity for intimacy. The real gift of this aspect is not intensity. It is the chance to create a deeper, more authentic connection while staying grounded in yourself."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-pluto_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s depth and power. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This connection has the potential to create a deep sense of emotional trust over time. The Pluto person may pick up on feelings the Moon person struggles to put into words, helping them feel understood without pressure or judgment. Rather than forcing vulnerability, the relationship gently encourages it, creating a space where deeper conversations and emotional honesty can develop naturally.\n\nWhen approached intentionally, this aspect can create a strong foundation for emotional growth. The Pluto person may encourage the Moon person to put words to feelings they have kept inside, recognize recurring emotional patterns, and develop greater trust in their own emotional experience. In turn, the Moon person''s openness and sensitivity can help the Pluto person relate with more compassion, patience, and emotional awareness.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is that it does not rush intimacy. The opportunity for deeper connection is there, but it develops through choice rather than pressure. The relationship tends to thrive when both people are willing to be honest, stay curious about each other, and have conversations that go beyond the surface.\n\nThe challenge is that it can be easy to settle into comfort without fully engaging the deeper potential of the connection. If both people avoid vulnerability or keep important feelings unspoken, the relationship may remain supportive but never reach the level of closeness it is capable of creating.\n\nAllow trust to build naturally. Share your feelings a little more openly than you normally would. Pay attention to what this relationship teaches you about your needs, your patterns, and your capacity for intimacy. The real gift of this aspect is not intensity. It is the chance to create a deeper, more authentic connection while staying grounded in yourself.","tension":"The challenge is that it can be easy to settle into comfort without fully engaging the deeper potential of the connection. If both people avoid vulnerability or keep important feelings unspoken, the relationship may remain supportive but never reach the level of closeness it is capable of creating.","advice":"Allow trust to build naturally. Share your feelings a little more openly than you normally would. Pay attention to what this relationship teaches you about your needs, your patterns, and your capacity for intimacy. The real gift of this aspect is not intensity. It is the chance to create a deeper, more authentic connection while staying grounded in yourself.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-pluto_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-pluto_square', 'synastry-moon-square-pluto', 'relationship-moon-square-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-pluto_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-pluto_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Square Pluto', null, 'This connection has a way of reaching beneath your usual emotional defenses and touching something raw, tender, and deeply rooted.

Moon-Pluto squares often arrive with intensity. Not because either person is trying to create drama, but because the relationship activates emotional material that has been waiting for attention. Old fears, unmet needs, attachment wounds, and protective patterns can rise to the surface quickly. What happens between you may feel bigger than the moment itself because it is connected to something much older.

There is often a strong pull toward one another, even when the connection feels uncomfortable. The Moon person may feel emotionally exposed or unusually reactive. The Pluto person may feel compelled to go deeper, ask harder questions, or hold on more tightly when vulnerability appears. Both people can find themselves caught in dynamics that feel difficult to explain but impossible to ignore.

This aspect has the potential to be deeply transformative. It can reveal where intimacy feels threatening, where control has been mistaken for safety, and where emotional intensity has become confused with love. It asks both people to become more conscious of the stories, fears, and survival strategies they bring into relationship.

But depth alone does not make a relationship healthy. A strong connection should help you feel more grounded in yourself, not less. Pay attention to what happens to your emotional stability over time. Do you feel more secure, more honest, and more connected to yourself because of this bond? Or do you find yourself constantly worrying about where you stand, losing sight of your own needs, or feeling as though your peace depends on the other person''s presence and reassurance? When difficult feelings arise, notice how the relationship handles them. Healthy intimacy creates space for vulnerability, accountability, and repair. Unhealthy dynamics tend to circle the same pain without resolving it. Fear can slowly reshape the connection, turning closeness into control, insecurity into suspicion, or attachment into something that feels increasingly consuming.

The invitation here is to pay attention. Notice what this relationship awakens in you. Notice what it teaches you about your emotional needs, your boundaries, and your capacity for intimacy. Growth is possible when both people are willing to meet what arises with honesty and compassion. You do not have to earn love through emotional struggle. You do not have to stay in chaos to prove your commitment. The wisdom of this aspect comes from listening to what your feelings are trying to show you and allowing that knowledge to change the way you relate.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection has a way of reaching beneath your usual emotional defenses and touching something raw, tender, and deeply rooted.\n\nMoon-Pluto squares often arrive with intensity. Not because either person is trying to create drama, but because the relationship activates emotional material that has been waiting for attention. Old fears, unmet needs, attachment wounds, and protective patterns can rise to the surface quickly. What happens between you may feel bigger than the moment itself because it is connected to something much older.\n\nThere is often a strong pull toward one another, even when the connection feels uncomfortable. The Moon person may feel emotionally exposed or unusually reactive. The Pluto person may feel compelled to go deeper, ask harder questions, or hold on more tightly when vulnerability appears. Both people can find themselves caught in dynamics that feel difficult to explain but impossible to ignore.\n\nThis aspect has the potential to be deeply transformative. It can reveal where intimacy feels threatening, where control has been mistaken for safety, and where emotional intensity has become confused with love. It asks both people to become more conscious of the stories, fears, and survival strategies they bring into relationship.\n\nBut depth alone does not make a relationship healthy. A strong connection should help you feel more grounded in yourself, not less. Pay attention to what happens to your emotional stability over time. Do you feel more secure, more honest, and more connected to yourself because of this bond? Or do you find yourself constantly worrying about where you stand, losing sight of your own needs, or feeling as though your peace depends on the other person''s presence and reassurance? When difficult feelings arise, notice how the relationship handles them. Healthy intimacy creates space for vulnerability, accountability, and repair. Unhealthy dynamics tend to circle the same pain without resolving it. Fear can slowly reshape the connection, turning closeness into control, insecurity into suspicion, or attachment into something that feels increasingly consuming.\n\nThe invitation here is to pay attention. Notice what this relationship awakens in you. Notice what it teaches you about your emotional needs, your boundaries, and your capacity for intimacy. Growth is possible when both people are willing to meet what arises with honesty and compassion. You do not have to earn love through emotional struggle. You do not have to stay in chaos to prove your commitment. The wisdom of this aspect comes from listening to what your feelings are trying to show you and allowing that knowledge to change the way you relate."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But depth alone does not make a relationship healthy. A strong connection should help you feel more grounded in yourself, not less. Pay attention to what happens to your emotional stability over time. Do you feel more secure, more honest, and more connected to yourself because of this bond? Or do you find yourself constantly worrying about where you stand, losing sight of your own needs, or feeling as though your peace depends on the other person''s presence and reassurance? When difficult feelings arise, notice how the relationship handles them. Healthy intimacy creates space for vulnerability, accountability, and repair. Unhealthy dynamics tend to circle the same pain without resolving it. Fear can slowly reshape the connection, turning closeness into control, insecurity into suspicion, or attachment into something that feels increasingly consuming."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The invitation here is to pay attention. Notice what this relationship awakens in you. Notice what it teaches you about your emotional needs, your boundaries, and your capacity for intimacy. Growth is possible when both people are willing to meet what arises with honesty and compassion. You do not have to earn love through emotional struggle. You do not have to stay in chaos to prove your commitment. The wisdom of this aspect comes from listening to what your feelings are trying to show you and allowing that knowledge to change the way you relate."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-pluto_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Moon person''s emotional body meets Pluto''s intensity. This can pull hidden feelings into the open, but it can also create fear, jealousy, or emotional surveillance. Depth needs gentleness to become safe.","summaryDeep":"This connection has a way of reaching beneath your usual emotional defenses and touching something raw, tender, and deeply rooted.\n\nMoon-Pluto squares often arrive with intensity. Not because either person is trying to create drama, but because the relationship activates emotional material that has been waiting for attention. Old fears, unmet needs, attachment wounds, and protective patterns can rise to the surface quickly. What happens between you may feel bigger than the moment itself because it is connected to something much older.\n\nThere is often a strong pull toward one another, even when the connection feels uncomfortable. The Moon person may feel emotionally exposed or unusually reactive. The Pluto person may feel compelled to go deeper, ask harder questions, or hold on more tightly when vulnerability appears. Both people can find themselves caught in dynamics that feel difficul