y over time. Do you feel more secure, more honest, and more connected to yourself because of this bond? Or do you find yourself constantly worrying about where you stand, losing sight of your own needs, or feeling as though your peace depends on the other person''s presence and reassurance? When difficult feelings arise, notice how the relationship handles them. Healthy intimacy creates space for vulnerability, accountability, and repair. Unhealthy dynamics tend to circle the same pain without resolving it. Fear can slowly reshape the connection, turning closeness into control, insecurity into suspicion, or attachment into something that feels increasingly consuming.","advice":"The invitation here is to pay attention. Notice what this relationship awakens in you. Notice what it teaches you about your emotional needs, your boundaries, and your capacity for intimacy. Growth is possible when both people are willing to meet what arises with honesty and compassion. You do not have to earn love through emotional struggle. You do not have to stay in chaos to prove your commitment. The wisdom of this aspect comes from listening to what your feelings are trying to show you and allowing that knowledge to change the way you relate.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-pluto_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-pluto_trine', 'synastry-moon-trine-pluto', 'relationship-moon-trine-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-pluto_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-pluto_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Trine Pluto', null, 'This connection carries emotional depth without the same level of friction.

The Pluto person may understand the Moon person''s feelings with unusual sensitivity and care. There is often a natural trust here, as though vulnerability can emerge without being forced. The Moon person may feel safe revealing hidden fears, tender memories, or private emotional needs, while the Pluto person offers presence, depth, and steadiness.

At its best, this aspect can be deeply healing. The Pluto person may help the Moon person feel emotionally understood in places that have felt difficult to share. Their presence can support honesty, intimacy, and the slow softening of old defenses. The Moon person may feel held rather than exposed, strengthened rather than consumed.

There is still intensity here. Pluto never becomes shallow. But the trine often allows the depth to move with more trust and less crisis. Instead of forcing emotional transformation through conflict, this aspect can support it through acceptance, loyalty, and care.

The shadow is that you can get attached without noticing it. Because the connection feels easy and supportive, the Moon person may slowly start leaning on the Pluto person for emotional stability, guidance, or reassurance. Over time, more and more of their emotional world can end up revolving around the relationship, making it harder to stay grounded in themselves.

Let the depth heal you, and keep your own emotional ground as you do. The closeness here nourishes when you stay a whole person inside it.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection carries emotional depth without the same level of friction.\n\nThe Pluto person may understand the Moon person''s feelings with unusual sensitivity and care. There is often a natural trust here, as though vulnerability can emerge without being forced. The Moon person may feel safe revealing hidden fears, tender memories, or private emotional needs, while the Pluto person offers presence, depth, and steadiness.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can be deeply healing. The Pluto person may help the Moon person feel emotionally understood in places that have felt difficult to share. Their presence can support honesty, intimacy, and the slow softening of old defenses. The Moon person may feel held rather than exposed, strengthened rather than consumed.\n\nThere is still intensity here. Pluto never becomes shallow. But the trine often allows the depth to move with more trust and less crisis. Instead of forcing emotional transformation through conflict, this aspect can support it through acceptance, loyalty, and care.\n\nThe shadow is that you can get attached without noticing it. Because the connection feels easy and supportive, the Moon person may slowly start leaning on the Pluto person for emotional stability, guidance, or reassurance. Over time, more and more of their emotional world can end up revolving around the relationship, making it harder to stay grounded in themselves.\n\nLet the depth heal you, and keep your own emotional ground as you do. The closeness here nourishes when you stay a whole person inside it."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The shadow is that you can get attached without noticing it. Because the connection feels easy and supportive, the Moon person may slowly start leaning on the Pluto person for emotional stability, guidance, or reassurance. Over time, more and more of their emotional world can end up revolving around the relationship, making it harder to stay grounded in themselves."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the depth heal you, and keep your own emotional ground as you do. The closeness here nourishes when you stay a whole person inside it."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-pluto_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s feelings meets B''s depth and power. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This connection carries emotional depth without the same level of friction.\n\nThe Pluto person may understand the Moon person''s feelings with unusual sensitivity and care. There is often a natural trust here, as though vulnerability can emerge without being forced. The Moon person may feel safe revealing hidden fears, tender memories, or private emotional needs, while the Pluto person offers presence, depth, and steadiness.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can be deeply healing. The Pluto person may help the Moon person feel emotionally understood in places that have felt difficult to share. Their presence can support honesty, intimacy, and the slow softening of old defenses. The Moon person may feel held rather than exposed, strengthened rather than consumed.\n\nThere is still intensity here. Pluto never becomes shallow. But the trine often allows the depth to move with more trust and less crisis. Instead of forcing emotional transformation through conflict, this aspect can support it through acceptance, loyalty, and care.\n\nThe shadow is that you can get attached without noticing it. Because the connection feels easy and supportive, the Moon person may slowly start leaning on the Pluto person for emotional stability, guidance, or reassurance. Over time, more and more of their emotional world can end up revolving around the relationship, making it harder to stay grounded in themselves.\n\nLet the depth heal you, and keep your own emotional ground as you do. The closeness here nourishes when you stay a whole person inside it.","tension":"The shadow is that you can get attached without noticing it. Because the connection feels easy and supportive, the Moon person may slowly start leaning on the Pluto person for emotional stability, guidance, or reassurance. Over time, more and more of their emotional world can end up revolving around the relationship, making it harder to stay grounded in themselves.","advice":"Let the depth heal you, and keep your own emotional ground as you do. The closeness here nourishes when you stay a whole person inside it.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-saturn_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-saturn_conjunction', 'synastry-moon-conjunction-saturn', 'relationship-moon-conjunction-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-saturn_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-saturn_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Conjunction Saturn', null, 'This person does not take your feelings lightly. Being around them can make you feel emotionally exposed. They have a way of bringing your inner world into sharper focus, making it harder to look away from the parts of yourself you usually keep tucked out of sight. You may become more aware of your vulnerabilities and more cautious about how much of them you reveal. It can feel as though your emotions need to be managed or contained before they can be shared, leading you to present the version of yourself that seems most composed while keeping the more complicated parts hidden.

When this works, the heaviness turns into something dependable. This person may not always know how to soothe you in the moment, but they can offer a steady presence that does not disappear when things get difficult. Their care often shows itself through reliability, patience, and a willingness to stay engaged over time. The sense of security here is usually built gradually rather than given all at once.

The challenge comes when responsibility starts to feel more like judgment than support. Saturn often responds to emotion by trying to steady it, structure it, or bring it under control. Even when the intention is helpful, the Moon person can experience this as a signal that their feelings are excessive, inconvenient, or somehow wrong. The hurt builds when vulnerability is consistently met with correction, restraint, emotional distance, or pressure to handle things better than they realistically can. Over time, you may start expecting criticism before it happens, filtering your emotions through self-doubt and treating your feelings as something to manage instead of something that deserves understanding.

Do not start policing your own emotions just to keep the peace. Let this connection help you develop emotional resilience, but do not let it convince you that your feelings are something to be embarrassed by. Healthy structure gives your emotions a place to land.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person does not take your feelings lightly. Being around them can make you feel emotionally exposed. They have a way of bringing your inner world into sharper focus, making it harder to look away from the parts of yourself you usually keep tucked out of sight. You may become more aware of your vulnerabilities and more cautious about how much of them you reveal. It can feel as though your emotions need to be managed or contained before they can be shared, leading you to present the version of yourself that seems most composed while keeping the more complicated parts hidden.\n\nWhen this works, the heaviness turns into something dependable. This person may not always know how to soothe you in the moment, but they can offer a steady presence that does not disappear when things get difficult. Their care often shows itself through reliability, patience, and a willingness to stay engaged over time. The sense of security here is usually built gradually rather than given all at once.\n\nThe challenge comes when responsibility starts to feel more like judgment than support. Saturn often responds to emotion by trying to steady it, structure it, or bring it under control. Even when the intention is helpful, the Moon person can experience this as a signal that their feelings are excessive, inconvenient, or somehow wrong. The hurt builds when vulnerability is consistently met with correction, restraint, emotional distance, or pressure to handle things better than they realistically can. Over time, you may start expecting criticism before it happens, filtering your emotions through self-doubt and treating your feelings as something to manage instead of something that deserves understanding.\n\nDo not start policing your own emotions just to keep the peace. Let this connection help you develop emotional resilience, but do not let it convince you that your feelings are something to be embarrassed by. Healthy structure gives your emotions a place to land."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge comes when responsibility starts to feel more like judgment than support. Saturn often responds to emotion by trying to steady it, structure it, or bring it under control. Even when the intention is helpful, the Moon person can experience this as a signal that their feelings are excessive, inconvenient, or somehow wrong. The hurt builds when vulnerability is consistently met with correction, restraint, emotional distance, or pressure to handle things better than they realistically can. Over time, you may start expecting criticism before it happens, filtering your emotions through self-doubt and treating your feelings as something to manage instead of something that deserves understanding."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Do not start policing your own emotions just to keep the peace. Let this connection help you develop emotional resilience, but do not let it convince you that your feelings are something to be embarrassed by. Healthy structure gives your emotions a place to land."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-saturn_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Deep loyalty fused with real weight. The Saturn person grounds and steadies the Moon person; the Moon person can feel held at arm''s length, judged, or quietly unmet. One of the strongest stay-together contacts, and one that can calcify into duty without warmth. Failure mode: the structure outlasts the affection and committed becomes cold. Say the warmth out loud and often; if it''s obligation with no tenderness left, name that instead of calling it depth.","summaryDeep":"This person does not take your feelings lightly. Being around them can make you feel emotionally exposed. They have a way of bringing your inner world into sharper focus, making it harder to look away from the parts of yourself you usually keep tucked out of sight. You may become more aware of your vulnerabilities and more cautious about how much of them you reveal. It can feel as though your emotions need to be managed or contained before they can be shared, leading you to present the version of yourself that seems most composed while keeping the more complicated parts hidden.\n\nWhen this works, the heaviness turns into something dependable. This person may not always know how to soothe you in the moment, but they can offer a steady presence that does not disappear when things get difficult. Their care often shows itself through reliability, patience, and a willingness to stay engaged over time. The sense of security here is usually built gradually rather than given all at once.\n\nThe challenge comes when responsibility starts to feel more like judgment than support. Saturn often responds to emotion by trying to steady it, structure it, or bring it under control. Even when the intention is helpful, the Moon person can experience this as a signal that their feelings are excessive, inconvenient, or somehow wrong. The hurt builds when vulnerability is consistently met with correction, restraint, emotional distance, or pressure to handle things better than they realistically can. Over time, you may start expecting criticism before it happens, filtering your emotions through self-doubt and treating your feelings as something to manage instead of something that deserves understanding.\n\nDo not start policing your own emotions just to keep the peace. Let this connection help you develop emotional resilience, but do not let it convince you that your feelings are something to be embarrassed by. Healthy structure gives your emotions a place to land.","tension":"The challenge comes when responsibility starts to feel more like judgment than support. Saturn often responds to emotion by trying to steady it, structure it, or bring it under control. Even when the intention is helpful, the Moon person can experience this as a signal that their feelings are excessive, inconvenient, or somehow wrong. The hurt builds when vulnerability is consistently met with correction, restraint, emotional distance, or pressure to handle things better than they realistically can. Over time, you may start expecting criticism before it happens, filtering your emotions through self-doubt and treating your feelings as something to manage instead of something that deserves understanding.","advice":"Do not start policing your own emotions just to keep the peace. Let this connection help you develop emotional resilience, but do not let it convince you that your feelings are something to be embarrassed by. Healthy structure gives your emotions a place to land.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-saturn_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-saturn_opposition', 'synastry-moon-opposition-saturn', 'relationship-moon-opposition-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-saturn_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-saturn_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Opposition Saturn', null, 'This person may seem emotionally distant, even when they care.

You might look for comfort, reassurance, or a sense of emotional closeness, while they respond with caution, restraint, or practical advice. What feels supportive to them may feel cold to you. What feels like a reasonable emotional need to you may feel overwhelming to them. It is easy for both people to misunderstand each other''s intentions.

At its best, this connection creates balance. They can help you step back from emotional overwhelm and see situations more clearly. Their steadiness can offer perspective when feelings become consuming. In return, you can help them stay connected to emotions they might otherwise avoid or suppress.

The challenge comes when the relationship falls into a cycle that neither person intends. One person reaches for reassurance, and the other responds by creating more distance. That distance then increases the need for reassurance, which can keep the pattern going. The goal is not to decide who is right, but to recognize the pattern together and create space for both emotional needs and healthy boundaries.

This aspect works best when both people resist turning differences into proof that they are unloved. Be clear about what you need, and stay open to what the other person is actually able to offer.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may seem emotionally distant, even when they care.\n\nYou might look for comfort, reassurance, or a sense of emotional closeness, while they respond with caution, restraint, or practical advice. What feels supportive to them may feel cold to you. What feels like a reasonable emotional need to you may feel overwhelming to them. It is easy for both people to misunderstand each other''s intentions.\n\nAt its best, this connection creates balance. They can help you step back from emotional overwhelm and see situations more clearly. Their steadiness can offer perspective when feelings become consuming. In return, you can help them stay connected to emotions they might otherwise avoid or suppress.\n\nThe challenge comes when the relationship falls into a cycle that neither person intends. One person reaches for reassurance, and the other responds by creating more distance. That distance then increases the need for reassurance, which can keep the pattern going. The goal is not to decide who is right, but to recognize the pattern together and create space for both emotional needs and healthy boundaries.\n\nThis aspect works best when both people resist turning differences into proof that they are unloved. Be clear about what you need, and stay open to what the other person is actually able to offer."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge comes when the relationship falls into a cycle that neither person intends. One person reaches for reassurance, and the other responds by creating more distance. That distance then increases the need for reassurance, which can keep the pattern going. The goal is not to decide who is right, but to recognize the pattern together and create space for both emotional needs and healthy boundaries."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This aspect works best when both people resist turning differences into proof that they are unloved. Be clear about what you need, and stay open to what the other person is actually able to offer."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-saturn_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Need versus distance, across the table. One wants more closeness; the other guards the gate, often from fear rather than malice. Failure mode: a pursue-withdraw loop where both feel wronged. Set terms you both say out loud, and don''t mistake someone''s walls for emotional depth.","summaryDeep":"This person may seem emotionally distant, even when they care.\n\nYou might look for comfort, reassurance, or a sense of emotional closeness, while they respond with caution, restraint, or practical advice. What feels supportive to them may feel cold to you. What feels like a reasonable emotional need to you may feel overwhelming to them. It is easy for both people to misunderstand each other''s intentions.\n\nAt its best, this connection creates balance. They can help you step back from emotional overwhelm and see situations more clearly. Their steadiness can offer perspective when feelings become consuming. In return, you can help them stay connected to emotions they might otherwise avoid or suppress.\n\nThe challenge comes when the relationship falls into a cycle that neither person intends. One person reaches for reassurance, and the other responds by creating more distance. That distance then increases the need for reassurance, which can keep the pattern going. The goal is not to decide who is right, but to recognize the pattern together and create space for both emotional needs and healthy boundaries.\n\nThis aspect works best when both people resist turning differences into proof that they are unloved. Be clear about what you need, and stay open to what the other person is actually able to offer.","tension":"The challenge comes when the relationship falls into a cycle that neither person intends. One person reaches for reassurance, and the other responds by creating more distance. That distance then increases the need for reassurance, which can keep the pattern going. The goal is not to decide who is right, but to recognize the pattern together and create space for both emotional needs and healthy boundaries.","advice":"This aspect works best when both people resist turning differences into proof that they are unloved. Be clear about what you need, and stay open to what the other person is actually able to offer.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-saturn_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-saturn_sextile', 'synastry-moon-sextile-saturn', 'relationship-moon-sextile-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-saturn_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-saturn_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Sextile Saturn', null, 'This aspect offers the possibility of trust that is built slowly, intentionally, and over time. Moon-Saturn sextiles are not usually dramatic. They tend to reveal themselves through small acts of care that accumulate. Someone remembers. Someone checks in. Someone follows through on what they said they would do. The relationship gains strength through consistency rather than intensity.

When this aspect is working well, it creates a sense of emotional stability. This person may help you approach your feelings with maturity and care rather than getting lost in them. They can encourage you to give your emotions the attention they need without treating them as a problem to fix. Their steady presence may make it easier to carry life''s responsibilities while still honoring what you feel.

The growth edge is learning how to receive what is being offered. Old experiences may have taught you to handle everything alone or to hide your needs before anyone can dismiss them. Meanwhile, this person may express care through reliability and practical support rather than overt displays of emotion. Both people benefit from learning each other''s language of care.

The gift is commitment. It is the willingness to keep showing up, to keep listening, and to keep tending to what matters. Emotional safety is built through practice. This aspect can create something steady, grounding, and lasting when both people are willing to help build it.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This aspect offers the possibility of trust that is built slowly, intentionally, and over time. Moon-Saturn sextiles are not usually dramatic. They tend to reveal themselves through small acts of care that accumulate. Someone remembers. Someone checks in. Someone follows through on what they said they would do. The relationship gains strength through consistency rather than intensity.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it creates a sense of emotional stability. This person may help you approach your feelings with maturity and care rather than getting lost in them. They can encourage you to give your emotions the attention they need without treating them as a problem to fix. Their steady presence may make it easier to carry life''s responsibilities while still honoring what you feel.\n\nThe growth edge is learning how to receive what is being offered. Old experiences may have taught you to handle everything alone or to hide your needs before anyone can dismiss them. Meanwhile, this person may express care through reliability and practical support rather than overt displays of emotion. Both people benefit from learning each other''s language of care.\n\nThe gift is commitment. It is the willingness to keep showing up, to keep listening, and to keep tending to what matters. Emotional safety is built through practice. This aspect can create something steady, grounding, and lasting when both people are willing to help build it."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The growth edge is learning how to receive what is being offered. Old experiences may have taught you to handle everything alone or to hide your needs before anyone can dismiss them. Meanwhile, this person may express care through reliability and practical support rather than overt displays of emotion. Both people benefit from learning each other''s language of care."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The gift is commitment. It is the willingness to keep showing up, to keep listening, and to keep tending to what matters. Emotional safety is built through practice. This aspect can create something steady, grounding, and lasting when both people are willing to help build it."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-saturn_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A supportive blend of feeling and stability. The Saturn person offers reliability; the Moon person softens the Saturn person''s edges, and it''s there without strain. Failure mode: under-using it - the steadiness exists but you don''t lean on it. Build the routines and commitments that make the emotional safety concrete.","summaryDeep":"This aspect offers the possibility of trust that is built slowly, intentionally, and over time. Moon-Saturn sextiles are not usually dramatic. They tend to reveal themselves through small acts of care that accumulate. Someone remembers. Someone checks in. Someone follows through on what they said they would do. The relationship gains strength through consistency rather than intensity.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it creates a sense of emotional stability. This person may help you approach your feelings with maturity and care rather than getting lost in them. They can encourage you to give your emotions the attention they need without treating them as a problem to fix. Their steady presence may make it easier to carry life''s responsibilities while still honoring what you feel.\n\nThe growth edge is learning how to receive what is being offered. Old experiences may have taught you to handle everything alone or to hide your needs before anyone can dismiss them. Meanwhile, this person may express care through reliability and practical support rather than overt displays of emotion. Both people benefit from learning each other''s language of care.\n\nThe gift is commitment. It is the willingness to keep showing up, to keep listening, and to keep tending to what matters. Emotional safety is built through practice. This aspect can create something steady, grounding, and lasting when both people are willing to help build it.","tension":"The growth edge is learning how to receive what is being offered. Old experiences may have taught you to handle everything alone or to hide your needs before anyone can dismiss them. Meanwhile, this person may express care through reliability and practical support rather than overt displays of emotion. Both people benefit from learning each other''s language of care.","advice":"The gift is commitment. It is the willingness to keep showing up, to keep listening, and to keep tending to what matters. Emotional safety is built through practice. This aspect can create something steady, grounding, and lasting when both people are willing to help build it.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-saturn_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-saturn_square', 'synastry-moon-square-saturn', 'relationship-moon-square-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-saturn_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-saturn_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Square Saturn', null, 'This person can make you feel like your feelings are wrong.

They may not say it directly. It may come through as criticism, correction, silence, or a response that feels colder than the moment needs. You share something vulnerable, and suddenly you feel exposed. You ask for comfort, and somehow you end up defending why you needed it.

This can get under your skin quickly. Over time, you may stop questioning their reaction and start questioning yourself. You wonder if you are too sensitive, too needy, too emotional, too much. That is where this aspect becomes painful. The judgment does not stay between you. It starts living inside you.

At its best, this friction pushes you toward stronger self-respect. You learn to stand by your feelings instead of apologizing for them. You learn that emotional maturity is not about having fewer needs. It is about being honest about them without letting shame take over.

At its worst, you can end up chasing approval that never quite arrives. You explain yourself. You try harder. You adjust your approach. You make yourself smaller. Yet it still feels like the understanding you want remains out of reach. The lesson here is not to stop feeling. It is to learn how to hold your feelings without turning against yourself. You can reflect on your patterns. You can take responsibility for your actions. You can grow. None of that requires you to believe that your needs are the problem.

Do not let someone else''s discomfort with emotions become the measure of your worth.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can make you feel like your feelings are wrong.\n\nThey may not say it directly. It may come through as criticism, correction, silence, or a response that feels colder than the moment needs. You share something vulnerable, and suddenly you feel exposed. You ask for comfort, and somehow you end up defending why you needed it.\n\nThis can get under your skin quickly. Over time, you may stop questioning their reaction and start questioning yourself. You wonder if you are too sensitive, too needy, too emotional, too much. That is where this aspect becomes painful. The judgment does not stay between you. It starts living inside you.\n\nAt its best, this friction pushes you toward stronger self-respect. You learn to stand by your feelings instead of apologizing for them. You learn that emotional maturity is not about having fewer needs. It is about being honest about them without letting shame take over.\n\nAt its worst, you can end up chasing approval that never quite arrives. You explain yourself. You try harder. You adjust your approach. You make yourself smaller. Yet it still feels like the understanding you want remains out of reach. The lesson here is not to stop feeling. It is to learn how to hold your feelings without turning against yourself. You can reflect on your patterns. You can take responsibility for your actions. You can grow. None of that requires you to believe that your needs are the problem.\n\nDo not let someone else''s discomfort with emotions become the measure of your worth."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its worst, you can end up chasing approval that never quite arrives. You explain yourself. You try harder. You adjust your approach. You make yourself smaller. Yet it still feels like the understanding you want remains out of reach. The lesson here is not to stop feeling. It is to learn how to hold your feelings without turning against yourself. You can reflect on your patterns. You can take responsibility for your actions. You can grow. None of that requires you to believe that your needs are the problem."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Do not let someone else''s discomfort with emotions become the measure of your worth."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-saturn_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"This aspect can make emotional needs feel heavy. The Moon person may want warmth or reassurance, while the Saturn person may respond with caution, distance, duty, or restraint.","summaryDeep":"This person can make you feel like your feelings are wrong.\n\nThey may not say it directly. It may come through as criticism, correction, silence, or a response that feels colder than the moment needs. You share something vulnerable, and suddenly you feel exposed. You ask for comfort, and somehow you end up defending why you needed it.\n\nThis can get under your skin quickly. Over time, you may stop questioning their reaction and start questioning yourself. You wonder if you are too sensitive, too needy, too emotional, too much. That is where this aspect becomes painful. The judgment does not stay between you. It starts living inside you.\n\nAt its best, this friction pushes you toward stronger self-respect. You learn to stand by your feelings instead of apologizing for them. You learn that emotional maturity is not about having fewer needs. It is about being honest about them without letting shame take over.\n\nAt its worst, you can end up chasing approval that never quite arrives. You explain yourself. You try harder. You adjust your approach. You make yourself smaller. Yet it still feels like the understanding you want remains out of reach. The lesson here is not to stop feeling. It is to learn how to hold your feelings without turning against yourself. You can reflect on your patterns. You can take responsibility for your actions. You can grow. None of that requires you to believe that your needs are the problem.\n\nDo not let someone else''s discomfort with emotions become the measure of your worth.","tension":"At its worst, you can end up chasing approval that never quite arrives. You explain yourself. You try harder. You adjust your approach. You make yourself smaller. Yet it still feels like the understanding you want remains out of reach. The lesson here is not to stop feeling. It is to learn how to hold your feelings without turning against yourself. You can reflect on your patterns. You can take responsibility for your actions. You can grow. None of that requires you to believe that your needs are the problem.","advice":"Do not let someone else''s discomfort with emotions become the measure of your worth.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry-moon-trine-saturn', 'relationship-moon-trine-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-saturn_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-saturn_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Trine Saturn', null, 'This connection can remind you that care is something you can count on. There is a quiet steadiness here, a sense that someone is paying attention even when they are not making a show of it. Their presence can be grounding. They follow through. They make room for what is real. And when life gets heavy, they are often still standing beside you. If you have known inconsistency or disappointment, that kind of reliability can feel deeply restorative.

At its best, this is emotional stability. Their presence helps you calm down instead of spiral. They remind you that feelings do not have to control your life to be valid. Over time, you may trust yourself more because someone consistently treats your emotions like they matter.

The downside is that their practicality can sometimes feel a little too practical. They may focus on solving the problem instead of sitting with the feeling. Their realism can sometimes come across as emotionally detached, even when they are trying to help. Because they tend to approach things logically, it can be easy to miss the moment when useful perspective starts feeling like your feelings are being brushed aside.

The lesson here is simple: stability is good, but feelings still need room to exist.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection can remind you that care is something you can count on. There is a quiet steadiness here, a sense that someone is paying attention even when they are not making a show of it. Their presence can be grounding. They follow through. They make room for what is real. And when life gets heavy, they are often still standing beside you. If you have known inconsistency or disappointment, that kind of reliability can feel deeply restorative.\n\nAt its best, this is emotional stability. Their presence helps you calm down instead of spiral. They remind you that feelings do not have to control your life to be valid. Over time, you may trust yourself more because someone consistently treats your emotions like they matter.\n\nThe downside is that their practicality can sometimes feel a little too practical. They may focus on solving the problem instead of sitting with the feeling. Their realism can sometimes come across as emotionally detached, even when they are trying to help. Because they tend to approach things logically, it can be easy to miss the moment when useful perspective starts feeling like your feelings are being brushed aside.\n\nThe lesson here is simple: stability is good, but feelings still need room to exist."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The downside is that their practicality can sometimes feel a little too practical. They may focus on solving the problem instead of sitting with the feeling. Their realism can sometimes come across as emotionally detached, even when they are trying to help. Because they tend to approach things logically, it can be easy to miss the moment when useful perspective starts feeling like your feelings are being brushed aside."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The lesson here is simple: stability is good, but feelings still need room to exist."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-saturn_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Emotional security that comes easily. Quiet commitment, dependable warmth, the sense of being safely held. Failure mode: steady drifts toward flat if no one adds heat. Use the stability to commit to something lasting, and keep warmth deliberate so it doesn''t go quiet.","summaryDeep":"This connection can remind you that care is something you can count on. There is a quiet steadiness here, a sense that someone is paying attention even when they are not making a show of it. Their presence can be grounding. They follow through. They make room for what is real. And when life gets heavy, they are often still standing beside you. If you have known inconsistency or disappointment, that kind of reliability can feel deeply restorative.\n\nAt its best, this is emotional stability. Their presence helps you calm down instead of spiral. They remind you that feelings do not have to control your life to be valid. Over time, you may trust yourself more because someone consistently treats your emotions like they matter.\n\nThe downside is that their practicality can sometimes feel a little too practical. They may focus on solving the problem instead of sitting with the feeling. Their realism can sometimes come across as emotionally detached, even when they are trying to help. Because they tend to approach things logically, it can be easy to miss the moment when useful perspective starts feeling like your feelings are being brushed aside.\n\nThe lesson here is simple: stability is good, but feelings still need room to exist.","tension":"The downside is that their practicality can sometimes feel a little too practical. They may focus on solving the problem instead of sitting with the feeling. Their realism can sometimes come across as emotionally detached, even when they are trying to help. Because they tend to approach things logically, it can be easy to miss the moment when useful perspective starts feeling like your feelings are being brushed aside.","advice":"The lesson here is simple: stability is good, but feelings still need room to exist.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"sun","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry-moon-conjunction-sun', 'relationship-moon-conjunction-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-sun_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-sun_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Conjunction Sun', 'This can feel familiar right away. One person''s personality fits easily with the other person''s emotional needs, so being around each other may feel natural without either of you doing much.', 'This can feel familiar right away. One person''s personality fits easily with the other person''s emotional needs, so being around each other may feel natural without either of you doing much.

There''s a real comfort here. One person may feel seen, and the other may feel needed in a way that actually feels good. It''s not always dramatic or flashy. It''s more like, "Oh, I can relax around you."

The problem is that comfort can turn into dependence. One person may start expecting the other to always be their soft place to land, and the relationship can get a little too comfortable without anyone noticing.

Enjoy the closeness, but don''t disappear into it. This works best when both people still have their own life.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This can feel familiar right away. One person''s personality fits easily with the other person''s emotional needs, so being around each other may feel natural without either of you doing much.\n\nThere''s a real comfort here. One person may feel seen, and the other may feel needed in a way that actually feels good. It''s not always dramatic or flashy. It''s more like, \"Oh, I can relax around you.\"\n\nThe problem is that comfort can turn into dependence. One person may start expecting the other to always be their soft place to land, and the relationship can get a little too comfortable without anyone noticing.\n\nEnjoy the closeness, but don''t disappear into it. This works best when both people still have their own life."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is that comfort can turn into dependence. One person may start expecting the other to always be their soft place to land, and the relationship can get a little too comfortable without anyone noticing."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Enjoy the closeness, but don''t disappear into it. This works best when both people still have their own life."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-sun_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Moon person''s feelings meet the Sun person''s identity with very little translation needed. The Moon person often feels recognized at an instinctive level, while the Sun person feels emotionally received. Strong glue, but still not proof of fit; build behavior around the ease.","summaryDeep":"This can feel familiar right away. One person''s personality fits easily with the other person''s emotional needs, so being around each other may feel natural without either of you doing much.\n\nThere''s a real comfort here. One person may feel seen, and the other may feel needed in a way that actually feels good. It''s not always dramatic or flashy. It''s more like, \"Oh, I can relax around you.\"\n\nThe problem is that comfort can turn into dependence. One person may start expecting the other to always be their soft place to land, and the relationship can get a little too comfortable without anyone noticing.\n\nEnjoy the closeness, but don''t disappear into it. This works best when both people still have their own life.","tension":"The problem is that comfort can turn into dependence. One person may start expecting the other to always be their soft place to land, and the relationship can get a little too comfortable without anyone noticing.","advice":"Enjoy the closeness, but don''t disappear into it. This works best when both people still have their own life.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"sun","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry-moon-opposition-sun', 'relationship-moon-opposition-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-sun_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-sun_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Opposition Sun', 'There''s a strong pull here, but you may not always feel like you''re coming from the same place. One person''s way of being can bring up a lot of feelings in the other person, sometimes in a good way, sometimes in a "why am I reacting like this?" way.', 'There''s a strong pull here, but you may not always feel like you''re coming from the same place. One person''s way of being can bring up a lot of feelings in the other person, sometimes in a good way, sometimes in a "why am I reacting like this?" way.

At its best, you balance each other out. One person brings direction, confidence, or clarity. The other brings care, sensitivity, and emotional reality. You may feel like this person has something you need, even when they also get on your nerves.

The problem is that it can turn into a standoff. One person feels unseen. The other feels like nothing they do is enough.

Don''t make it a competition over whose needs matter more. Say what you need, listen to what they need, and meet somewhere in the middle.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There''s a strong pull here, but you may not always feel like you''re coming from the same place. One person''s way of being can bring up a lot of feelings in the other person, sometimes in a good way, sometimes in a \"why am I reacting like this?\" way.\n\nAt its best, you balance each other out. One person brings direction, confidence, or clarity. The other brings care, sensitivity, and emotional reality. You may feel like this person has something you need, even when they also get on your nerves.\n\nThe problem is that it can turn into a standoff. One person feels unseen. The other feels like nothing they do is enough.\n\nDon''t make it a competition over whose needs matter more. Say what you need, listen to what they need, and meet somewhere in the middle."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is that it can turn into a standoff. One person feels unseen. The other feels like nothing they do is enough."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Don''t make it a competition over whose needs matter more. Say what you need, listen to what they need, and meet somewhere in the middle."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-sun_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Moon person and Sun person often stand on opposite sides of the same room: one leading from feeling, one from identity. The attraction can be strong because each carries what the other notices. The work is trading perspective instead of casting one person as too needy or too self-focused.","summaryDeep":"There''s a strong pull here, but you may not always feel like you''re coming from the same place. One person''s way of being can bring up a lot of feelings in the other person, sometimes in a good way, sometimes in a \"why am I reacting like this?\" way.\n\nAt its best, you balance each other out. One person brings direction, confidence, or clarity. The other brings care, sensitivity, and emotional reality. You may feel like this person has something you need, even when they also get on your nerves.\n\nThe problem is that it can turn into a standoff. One person feels unseen. The other feels like nothing they do is enough.\n\nDon''t make it a competition over whose needs matter more. Say what you need, listen to what they need, and meet somewhere in the middle.","tension":"The problem is that it can turn into a standoff. One person feels unseen. The other feels like nothing they do is enough.","advice":"Don''t make it a competition over whose needs matter more. Say what you need, listen to what they need, and meet somewhere in the middle.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-sun_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"sun","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-sun_sextile', 'synastry-moon-sextile-sun', 'relationship-moon-sextile-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-sun_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-sun_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Sextile Sun', 'There''s a good fit here, but it gets better when both people actually put something into it. One person''s way of being can support the other person''s emotional needs, especially when there''s effort, attention, and basic follow-through.', 'There''s a good fit here, but it gets better when both people actually put something into it. One person''s way of being can support the other person''s emotional needs, especially when there''s effort, attention, and basic follow-through.

This is the kind of connection where small things count. Checking in. Remembering what matters. Being a little more present than you technically have to be. The more you invest, the safer and warmer it feels.

The problem is leaving it half-open. The compatibility is there, but it may stay kind of mild if both people wait for the other one to make it more real.

Make the effort. Not a grand gesture, just enough to show the connection matters.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There''s a good fit here, but it gets better when both people actually put something into it. One person''s way of being can support the other person''s emotional needs, especially when there''s effort, attention, and basic follow-through.\n\nThis is the kind of connection where small things count. Checking in. Remembering what matters. Being a little more present than you technically have to be. The more you invest, the safer and warmer it feels.\n\nThe problem is leaving it half-open. The compatibility is there, but it may stay kind of mild if both people wait for the other one to make it more real.\n\nMake the effort. Not a grand gesture, just enough to show the connection matters."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is leaving it half-open. The compatibility is there, but it may stay kind of mild if both people wait for the other one to make it more real."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Make the effort. Not a grand gesture, just enough to show the connection matters."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-sun_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Moon person can support the Sun person''s direction, and the Sun person can give the Moon person a clear place to respond from. The warmth is available, but it wants small choices: checking in, noticing moods, and making room for both identity and need.","summaryDeep":"There''s a good fit here, but it gets better when both people actually put something into it. One person''s way of being can support the other person''s emotional needs, especially when there''s effort, attention, and basic follow-through.\n\nThis is the kind of connection where small things count. Checking in. Remembering what matters. Being a little more present than you technically have to be. The more you invest, the safer and warmer it feels.\n\nThe problem is leaving it half-open. The compatibility is there, but it may stay kind of mild if both people wait for the other one to make it more real.\n\nMake the effort. Not a grand gesture, just enough to show the connection matters.","tension":"The problem is leaving it half-open. The compatibility is there, but it may stay kind of mild if both people wait for the other one to make it more real.","advice":"Make the effort. Not a grand gesture, just enough to show the connection matters.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-moon_B-sun_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"moon","planetB":"sun","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-moon_B-sun_square', 'synastry-moon-square-sun', 'relationship-moon-square-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-moon_B-sun_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-moon_B-sun_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Moon Square Sun', 'There''s a connection here, but it can rub the wrong way. One person''s natural style may clash with what the other person needs to feel safe, cared for, or understood.', 'There''s a connection here, but it can rub the wrong way. One person''s natural style may clash with what the other person needs to feel safe, cared for, or understood.

It can show up in ordinary little moments. One person wants to move on, the other wants to talk it through. One person needs space, the other needs reassurance. Nobody has to be doing anything terrible for it to still feel frustrating.

The problem is taking the mismatch personally. You can start thinking, "Why are they like this?" when really, the two of you may just have different settings.

Don''t let every small rub become a larger story about the relationship. Name the pattern, adjust, and stop expecting the other person to magically know what would make you feel better.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There''s a connection here, but it can rub the wrong way. One person''s natural style may clash with what the other person needs to feel safe, cared for, or understood.\n\nIt can show up in ordinary little moments. One person wants to move on, the other wants to talk it through. One person needs space, the other needs reassurance. Nobody has to be doing anything terrible for it to still feel frustrating.\n\nThe problem is taking the mismatch personally. You can start thinking, \"Why are they like this?\" when really, the two of you may just have different settings.\n\nDon''t let every small rub become a larger story about the relationship. Name the pattern, adjust, and stop expecting the other person to magically know what would make you feel better."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is taking the mismatch personally. You can start thinking, \"Why are they like this?\" when really, the two of you may just have different settings."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Don''t let every small rub become a larger story about the relationship. Name the pattern, adjust, and stop expecting the other person to magically know what would make you feel better."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-moon_B-sun_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Moon person''s needs and the Sun person''s way of being can rub in a place both people feel quickly. One person''s normal self-expression may land as emotional disruption to the other. This can work, but only when both people stop treating their own rhythm as the only reasonable one.","summaryDeep":"There''s a connection here, but it can rub the wrong way. One person''s natural style may clash with what the other person needs to feel safe, cared for, or understood.\n\nIt can show up in ordinary little