s one of the easiest places you have to think and create. Left alone, it stays a nice feeling and nothing more.","tension":"The catch is that it sits in the background unless you use it. This kind of connection invites but does not push. It opens a door and waits. If you both keep waiting for the other to go deeper, neither of you will, and all that potential stays a pleasant background hum instead of becoming anything real. It can also fake depth if you let it. Conversations can feel meaningful while going nowhere, a warm atmosphere of shared sensitivity that never turns into an actual insight or decision. And because the mood between you is so easy, it is tempting to protect it. When something difficult needs to be said, you avoid saying it directly. Instead, you soften it, hint at it, or talk around it. Over time, keeping the peace can become more important than being honest.","advice":"Reach for it on purpose. Make something with the sensitivity you share, a project, a creative habit, a real conversation that goes somewhere. And keep checking that you actually know what the other one means, not just what they feel but what they specifically think and want. Used deliberately, this becomes one of the easiest places you have to think and create. Left alone, it stays a nice feeling and nothing more.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-neptune_B-mercury_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-mercury_square', 'synastry-neptune-square-mercury', 'relationship-neptune-square-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-mercury_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-mercury_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Square Mercury', null, 'This connection brings confusion into how you talk to each other. What one of you says and what the other hears can be very different things, and the gap between what was meant and what landed is wider here than almost anywhere else.

You are both communicating in good faith. You try to be clear, and they take it as harsh. They try to be honest, and you take it as evasive. The signal between you gets distorted, like static on a line, and accurate reception takes real effort that neither of you should have to make for a simple exchange.

It is rarely actual lying, though it can feel that way. More often it is perception. You hear something confusing, decide they must be hiding something, and only realize later that they were clear the first time and you understood it in a completely different light. The tell is that they communicate with everyone else fine. The problem lives between the two of you, and the closer the aspect, the worse it gets. The distrust is often baseless, and it tends to come from the Neptune person. Left alone, the Mercury person gets tired of being doubted and walks away. This does not break in a single dramatic moment. Trust erodes gradually, through a slow build-up of misunderstandings, half-truths, and well-meant vagueness, until the pattern is entrenched before either of you sees it. What makes it hard is that the square makes honest communication feel uncomfortable and dishonest communication feel natural. Clarity feels harsh. Vagueness feels kind. Specificity feels aggressive. These associations are backwards, and recognizing that they are backwards is the first step toward fixing the dynamic.

It can be worked through. Say what you mean in plain language, even when it feels unromantic. When something does not make sense, ask about it directly instead of filling in the blanks. Be transparent with each other. The trust problem can be repaired when both of you do your part.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection brings confusion into how you talk to each other. What one of you says and what the other hears can be very different things, and the gap between what was meant and what landed is wider here than almost anywhere else.\n\nYou are both communicating in good faith. You try to be clear, and they take it as harsh. They try to be honest, and you take it as evasive. The signal between you gets distorted, like static on a line, and accurate reception takes real effort that neither of you should have to make for a simple exchange.\n\nIt is rarely actual lying, though it can feel that way. More often it is perception. You hear something confusing, decide they must be hiding something, and only realize later that they were clear the first time and you understood it in a completely different light. The tell is that they communicate with everyone else fine. The problem lives between the two of you, and the closer the aspect, the worse it gets. The distrust is often baseless, and it tends to come from the Neptune person. Left alone, the Mercury person gets tired of being doubted and walks away. This does not break in a single dramatic moment. Trust erodes gradually, through a slow build-up of misunderstandings, half-truths, and well-meant vagueness, until the pattern is entrenched before either of you sees it. What makes it hard is that the square makes honest communication feel uncomfortable and dishonest communication feel natural. Clarity feels harsh. Vagueness feels kind. Specificity feels aggressive. These associations are backwards, and recognizing that they are backwards is the first step toward fixing the dynamic.\n\nIt can be wo