ft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-neptune_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"moon","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry-neptune-conjunction-moon', 'relationship-neptune-conjunction-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-moon_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-moon_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Conjunction Moon', null, 'This person can feel familiar in a way that is difficult to explain.

You may find yourself relaxing around them before you''ve decided whether they deserve your trust. The emotional connection often arrives first, with understanding following later. The Moon person can feel unusually exposed in the Neptune person''s presence, not because they''re being questioned, but because the Neptune person seems to pick up on feelings that haven''t been put into words yet.

There is often a softness to the connection. The Neptune person may respond to the Moon person''s emotions with patience and acceptance, making it easier for the Moon person to reveal parts of themselves they usually keep hidden. Conversations can drift into vulnerable territory without either person intending them to. What begins as simple understanding can feel surprisingly intimate.

When this aspect is working well, both people feel emotionally accepted. The Moon person feels safe enough to be honest about what they''re feeling, while the Neptune person feels appreciated for their sensitivity and compassion. There can be a sense that neither person has to perform, explain, or defend their emotions. The relationship becomes a place where feelings are allowed to exist without immediately needing solutions.

The difficulty is that this level of emotional openness can make separation harder to maintain. The Moon person may start carrying the Neptune person''s moods without realizing it. The Neptune person may become so focused on caring for the Moon person that they lose sight of their own emotional reality. Because the empathy feels natural, neither person may notice when healthy boundaries begin to fade. The problem is rarely obvious at first. It often develops quietly. One person becomes the source of comfort. The other becomes the source of care. Gradually, emotional support turns into emotional responsibility. Instead of sharing feelings, both people begin managing them together, sometimes at the expense of their own individual needs.

This aspect works best when emotional closeness is balanced with emotional clarity. Care about each other. Be open with each other. The comfort here is real. The challenge is remembering that love and empathy do not require becoming responsible for another person''s inner world.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can feel familiar in a way that is difficult to explain.\n\nYou may find yourself relaxing around them before you''ve decided whether they deserve your trust. The emotional connection often arrives first, with understanding following later. The Moon person can feel unusually exposed in the Neptune person''s presence, not because they''re being questioned, but because the Neptune person seems to pick up on feelings that haven''t been put into words yet.\n\nThere is often a softness to the connection. The Neptune person may respond to the Moon person''s emotions with patience and acceptance, making it easier for the Moon person to reveal parts of themselves they usually keep hidden. Conversations can drift into vulnerable territory without either person intending them to. What begins as simple understanding can feel surprisingly intimate.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, both people feel emotionally accepted. The Moon person feels safe enough to be honest about what they''re feeling, while the Neptune person feels appreciated for their sensitivity and compassion. There can be a sense that neither person has to perform, explain, or defend their emotions. The relationship becomes a place where feelings are allowed to exist without immediately needing solutions.\n\nThe difficulty is that this level of emotional openness can make separation harder to maintain. The Moon person may start carrying the Neptune person''s moods without realizing it. The Neptune person may become so focused on caring for the Moon person that they lose sight of their own emotional reality. Because the empathy feels natural, neither person may notice when healthy boundaries begin to fade. The problem is rarely obvious at first. It often develops quietly. One person becomes the source of comfort. The other becomes the source of care. Gradually, emotional support turns into emotional responsibility. Instead of sharing feelings, both people begin managing them together, sometimes at the expense of their own individual needs.\n\nThis aspect works best when emotional closeness is balanced with emotional clarity. Care about each other. Be open with each other. The comfort here is real. The challenge is remembering that love and empathy do not require becoming responsible for another person''s inner world."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The difficulty is that this level of emotional openness can make separation harder to maintain. The Moon person may start carrying the Neptune person''s moods without realizing it. The Neptune person may become so focused on caring for the Moon person that they lose sight of their own emotional reality. Because the empathy feels natural, neither person may notice when healthy boundaries begin to fade. The problem is rarely obvious at first. It often develops quietly. One person becomes the source of comfort. The other becomes the source of care. Gradually, emotional support turns into emotional responsibility. Instead of sharing feelings, both people begin managing them together, sometimes at the expense of their own individual needs."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This aspect works best when emotional closeness is balanced with emotional clarity. Care about each other. Be open with each other. The comfort here is real. The challenge is remembering that love and empathy do not require becoming responsible for another person''s inner world."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-neptune_B-moon_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Neptune person dissolves the edge around the Moon person''s feelings. Empathy can be deep, almost wordless, but so can confusion and rescuing. The Moon person needs reality checks, not just emotional merging.","summaryDeep":"This person can feel familiar in a way that is difficult to explain.\n\nYou may find yourself relaxing around them before you''ve decided whether they deserve your trust. The emotional connection often arrives first, with understanding following later. The Moon person can feel unusually exposed in the Neptune person''s presence, not because they''re being questioned, but because the Neptune person seems to pick up on feelings that haven''t been put into words yet.\n\nThere is often a softness to the connection. The Neptune person may respond to the Moon person''s emotions with patience and acceptance, making it easier for the Moon person to reveal parts of themselves they usually keep hidden. Conversations can drift into vulnerable territory without either person intending them to. What begins as simple understanding can feel surprisingly intimate.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, both people feel emotionally accepted. The Moon person feels safe enough to be honest about what they''re feeling, while the Neptune person feels appreciated for their sensitivity and compassion. There can be a sense that neither person has to perform, explain, or defend their emotions. The relationship becomes a place where feelings are allowed to exist without immediately needing solutions.\n\nThe difficulty is that this level of emotional openness can make separation harder to maintain. The Moon person may start carrying the Neptune person''s moods without realizing it. The Neptune person may become so focused on caring for the Moon person that they lose sight of their own emotional reality. Because the empathy feels natural, neither person may notice when healthy boundaries begin to fade. The problem is rarely obvious at first. It often develops quietly. One person becomes the source of comfort. The other becomes the source of care. Gradually, emotional support turns into emotional responsibility. Instead of sharing feelings, both people begin managing them together, sometimes at the expense of their own individual needs.\n\nThis aspect works best when emotional closeness is balanced with emotional clarity. Care about each other. Be open with each other. The comfort here is real. The challenge is remembering that love and empathy do not require becoming responsible for another person''s inner world.","tension":"The difficulty is that this level of emotional openness can make separation harder to maintain. The Moon person may start carrying the Neptune person''s moods without realizing it. The Neptune person may become so focused on caring for the Moon person that they lose sight of their own emotional reality. Because the empathy feels natural, neither person may notice when healthy boundaries begin to fade. The problem is rarely obvious at first. It often develops quietly. One person becomes the source of comfort. The other becomes the source of care. Gradually, emotional support turns into emotional responsibility. Instead of sharing feelings, both people begin managing them together, sometimes at the expense of their own individual needs.","advice":"This aspect works best when emotional closeness is balanced with emotional clarity. Care about each other. Be open with each other. The comfort here is real. The challenge is remembering that love and empathy do not require becoming responsible for another person''s inner world.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-neptune_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"moon","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry-neptune-opposition-moon', 'relationship-neptune-opposition-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-moon_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-moon_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Opposition Moon', null, 'This person can feel like the answer to a loneliness you had stopped expecting anyone to notice.

There is often a strong emotional pull here, but it can be difficult to understand clearly. The Moon person may feel that the Neptune person sees something in them that others miss. The Neptune person may seem to offer a kind of emotional refuge, a place where old defenses can finally lower.

At its best, this aspect can teach both people how to receive care without armor. The Moon person brings emotional honesty to the surface. The Neptune person brings imagination, compassion, and a willingness to meet feelings that do not fit neatly into words. Together, they can create a bond that feels deeply accepting.

But oppositions invite projection. One person may begin filling in the blanks with what they hope is true. The Moon person may assume the Neptune person feels the same depth, needs the same closeness, or understands the relationship in the same way. The Neptune person may drift in and out of emotional availability, not always realizing how much meaning the Moon person has placed on the connection. When reality arrives, the disappointment can be painful. You may realize you were not only relating to the person in front of you, but also to the feeling they awakened in you. The longing was real. The care may have been real. But the story built around it may not have been.

The invitation here is to keep returning to what is actually happening. Notice where you are hoping, assuming, rescuing, or waiting for the other person to become clearer than they are willing to be. This connection can be beautiful when care and clarity are allowed to exist together. It hurts most when the dream of being understood becomes more important than the truth of who is actually there.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can feel like the answer to a loneliness you had stopped expecting anyone to notice.\n\nThere is often a strong emotional pull here, but it can be difficult to understand clearly. The Moon person may feel that the Neptune person sees something in them that others miss. The Neptune person may seem to offer a kind of emotional refuge, a place where old defenses can finally lower.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can teach both people how to receive care without armor. The Moon person brings emotional honesty to the surface. The Neptune person brings imagination, compassion, and a willingness to meet feelings that do not fit neatly into words. Together, they can create a bond that feels deeply accepting.\n\nBut oppositions invite projection. One person may begin filling in the blanks with what they hope is true. The Moon person may assume the Neptune person feels the same depth, needs the same closeness, or understands the relationship in the same way. The Neptune person may drift in and out of emotional availability, not always realizing how much meaning the Moon person has placed on the connection. When reality arrives, the disappointment can be painful. You may realize you were not only relating to the person in front of you, but also to the feeling they awakened in you. The longing was real. The care may have been real. But the story built around it may not have been.\n\nThe invitation here is to keep returning to what is actually happening. Notice where you are hoping, assuming, rescuing, or waiting for the other person to become clearer than they are willing to be. This connection can be beautiful when care and clarity are allowed to exist together. It hurts most when the dream of being understood becomes more important than the truth of who is actually there."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But oppositions invite projection. One person may begin filling in the blanks with what they hope is true. The Moon person may assume the Neptune person feels the same depth, needs the same closeness, or understands the relationship in the same way. The Neptune person may drift in and out of emotional availability, not always realizing how much meaning the Moon person has placed on the connection. When reality arrives, the disappointment can be painful. You may realize you were not only relating to the person in front of you, but also to the feeling they awakened in you. The longing was real. The care may have been real. But the story built around it may not have been."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The invitation here is to keep returning to what is actually happening. Notice where you are hoping, assuming, rescuing, or waiting for the other person to become clearer than they are willing to be. This connection can be beautiful when care and clarity are allowed to exist together. It hurts most when the dream of being understood becomes more important than the truth of who is actually there."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-neptune_B-moon_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s dreams meets B''s feelings. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person can feel like the answer to a loneliness you had stopped expecting anyone to notice.\n\nThere is often a strong emotional pull here, but it can be difficult to understand clearly. The Moon person may feel that the Neptune person sees something in them that others miss. The Neptune person may seem to offer a kind of emotional refuge, a place where old defenses can finally lower.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can