erministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-neptune_B-moon_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"moon","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-moon_square', 'synastry-neptune-square-moon', 'relationship-neptune-square-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-moon_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-moon_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Square Moon', null, 'There can be a strange pull between you that is hard to define. The connection feels emotionally significant, yet neither person may be able to explain exactly why.

The Moon person is often the first to feel it. They may become unusually preoccupied with the Neptune person, sensing that something important is happening beneath the surface. The Neptune person, meanwhile, may seem deeply attuned to the Moon person''s emotional world, picking up on moods and vulnerabilities without needing much explanation. Yet that sensitivity does not always translate into clarity. What feels understood emotionally can remain difficult to define in practical terms.

When this aspect is expressed well, it can soften emotional defenses. The Moon person may feel more comfortable revealing feelings they normally protect. The Neptune person may discover that empathy becomes more meaningful when it is paired with honesty, consistency, and action. There is real potential for both people to become more emotionally aware through the relationship.

The challenge is that understanding can be assumed rather than communicated. Feelings are sensed, guessed at, or absorbed instead of discussed. Over time, each person may begin playing a role without consciously choosing it. One becomes the emotional caretaker. The other leans on that support. Neither fully notices how the pattern developed. Eventually, the relationship can start to feel heavier than it did at the beginning. Not because the affection is gone, but because so much remains unspoken. The Moon person may find themselves carrying worries, responsibilities, or emotional burdens that do not belong to them. The Neptune person may avoid difficult conversations, hoping compassion will smooth over problems that actually need to be addressed. The result is often a bond that feels deeply connected on the surface while important truths remain untouched underneath.

A useful question is whether this relationship helps you feel more grounded in yourself or whether you lose sight of your own needs inside it. One of the lessons of this aspect is learning that compassion does not require self-sacrifice. Caring for someone is not the same as saving them.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There can be a strange pull between you that is hard to define. The connection feels emotionally significant, yet neither person may be able to explain exactly why.\n\nThe Moon person is often the first to feel it. They may become unusually preoccupied with the Neptune person, sensing that something important is happening beneath the surface. The Neptune person, meanwhile, may seem deeply attuned to the Moon person''s emotional world, picking up on moods and vulnerabilities without needing much explanation. Yet that sensitivity does not always translate into clarity. What feels understood emotionally can remain difficult to define in practical terms.\n\nWhen this aspect is expressed well, it can soften emotional defenses. The Moon person may feel more comfortable revealing feelings they normally protect. The Neptune person may discover that empathy becomes more meaningful when it is paired with honesty, consistency, and action. There is real potential for both people to become more emotionally aware through the relationship.\n\nThe challenge is that understanding can be assumed rather than communicated. Feelings are sensed, guessed at, or absorbed instead of discussed. Over time, each person may begin playing a role without consciously choosing it. One becomes the emotional caretaker. The other leans on that support. Neither fully notices how the pattern developed. Eventually, the relationship can start to feel heavier than it did at the beginning. Not because the affection is gone, but because so much remains unspoken. The Moon person may find themselves carrying worries, responsibilities, or emotional burdens that do not belong to them. The Neptune person may avoid difficult conversations, hoping compassion will smooth over problems that actually need to be addressed. The result is often a bond that feels deeply connected on the surface while important truths remain untouched underneath.\n\nA useful question is whether this relationship helps you feel more grounded in yourself or whether you lose sight of your own needs inside it. One of the lessons of this aspect is learning that compassion does not require self-sacrifice. Caring for someone is not the same as saving them."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that understanding can be assumed rather than communicated. Feelings are sensed, guessed at, or absorbed instead of discussed. Over time, each person may begin playing a role without consciously choosing it. One becomes the emotional caretaker. The other leans on that support. Neither fully notices how the pattern developed. Eventually, the relationship can start to feel heavier than it did at the beginning. Not because the affection is gone, but because so much remains unspoken. The Moon person may find themselves carrying worries, responsibilities, or emotional burdens that do not belong to them. The Neptune person may avoid difficult conversations, hoping compassion will smooth over problems that actually need to be addressed. The result is often a bond that feels deeply connected on the surface while important truths remain untouched underneath."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"A useful question is whether this relationship helps you feel more grounded in yourself or whether you lose sight of your own needs inside it. One of the lessons of this aspect is learning that compassion does not require self-sacrifice. Caring for someone is not the same as saving them."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-neptune_B-moon_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Neptune person can stir compassion in the Moon person while also confusing emotional reality. The Moon person may feel everything and still not know what is true. Boundaries are care here, not a lack of love.","summaryDeep":"There can be a strange pull between you that is hard to define. The connection feels emotionally significant, yet neither person may be able to explain exactly why.\n\nThe Moon person is often the first to feel it. They may become unusually preoccupied with the Neptune person, sensing that something important is happening beneath the surface. The Neptune person, meanwhile, may seem deeply attuned to the Moon person''s emotional world, picking up on moods and vulnerabilities without needing much explanation. Yet that sensitivity does not always translate into clarity. What feels understood emotionally can remain difficult to define in practical terms.\n\nWhen this aspect is expressed well, it can soften emotional defenses. The Moon person may feel more comfortable revealing feelings they normally protect. The Neptune person may discover that empathy becomes more meaningful when it is paired with honesty, consistency, and action. There is real potential for both people to become more emotionally aware through the relationship.\n\nThe challenge is that understanding can be assumed rather than communicated. Feelings are sensed, guessed at, or absorbed instead of discussed. Over time, each person may begin playing a role without consciously choosing it. One becomes the emotional caretaker. The other leans on that support. Neither fully notices how the pattern developed. Eventually, the relationship can start to feel heavier than it did at the beginning. Not because the affection is gone, but because so much remains unspoken. The Moon person may find themselves carrying worries, responsibilities, or emotional burdens that do not belong to them. The Neptune person may avoid difficult conversations, hoping compassion will smooth over problems that actually need to be addressed. The result is often a bond that feels deeply connected on the surface while important truths remain untouched underneath.\n\nA useful question is whether this relationship helps you feel more grounded in yourself or whether you lose sight of your own needs inside it. One of the lessons of this aspect is learning that compassion does not require self-sacrifice. Caring for someone is not the same as saving them.","tension":"The challenge is that understanding can be assumed rather than communicated. Feelings are sensed, guessed at, or absorbed instead of discussed. Over time, each person may begin playing a role without consciously choosing it. One becomes the emotional caretaker. The other leans on that support. Neither fully notices how the pattern developed. Eventually, the relationship can start to feel heavier than it did at the beginning. Not because the affection is gone, but because so much remains unspoken. The Moon person may find themselves carrying worries, responsibilities, or emotional burdens that do not belong to them. The Neptune person may avoid difficult conversations, hoping compassion will smooth over problems that actually need to be addressed. The result is often a bond that feels deeply connected on the surface while important truths remain untouched underneath.","advice":"A useful question is whether this relationship helps you feel more grounded in yourself or whether you lose sight of your own needs inside it. One of the lessons of this aspect is learning that compassion does not require self-sacrifice. Caring for someone is not the same as saving them.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-neptune_B-moon_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"moon","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-moon_trine', 'synastry-neptune-trine-moon', 'relationship-neptune-trine-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-moon_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-moon_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Trine Moon', null, 'There is something quietly soothing about this connection.

The Moon person often feels emotionally understood without having to explain every feeling in detail. The Neptune person seems to sense what is happening beneath the surface, responding to emotions that have not yet been fully expressed. This can create a feeling of being deeply seen and emotionally received, even when very little has been said aloud.

Because of that, being together can feel easy. The Moon person may feel less guarded, less worried about being judged for what they feel. The Neptune person may feel free to express their sensitivity without having to defend it or make it seem more practical than it is. There is often a natural gentleness between the two people, as though each instinctively knows how to handle the other''s softer edges.

This can also be a deeply imaginative connection. Shared music, films, memories, dreams, spiritual interests, or simply sitting together in comfortable silence can create a sense of closeness. The relationship may feel meaningful in ways that are difficult to explain. Sometimes the moments that stay with you are not the dramatic ones, but the small, almost invisible exchanges that make you feel understood.

The difficulty is that what feels healing can slowly become necessary. Because emotional support flows so naturally, neither person may notice when the relationship starts carrying more weight than it should. The Moon person may begin looking to the Neptune person for reassurance they need to learn to give themselves. The Neptune person may absorb the Moon person''s emotions so completely that they lose track of where their own begin. This rarely happens overnight. It is usually the result of many small moments of comfort accumulating over time.

The gift of this aspect is emotional trust. The lesson is remembering that closeness works best when it connects two whole people, not when it becomes the place where either person disappears.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is something quietly soothing about this connection.\n\nThe Moon person often feels emotionally understood without having to explain every feeling in detail. The Neptune person seems to sense what is happening beneath the surface, responding to emotions that have not yet been fully expressed. This can create a feeling of being deeply seen and emotionally received, even when very little has been said aloud.\n\nBecause of that, being together can feel easy. The Moon person may feel less guarded, less worried about being judged for what they feel. The Neptune person may feel free to express their sensitivity without having to defend it or make it seem more practical than it is. There is often a natural gentleness between the two people, as though each instinctively knows how to handle the other''s softer edges.\n\nThis can also be a deeply imaginative connection. Shared music, films, memories, dreams, spiritual interests, or simply sitting together in comfortable silence can create a sense of closeness. The relationship may feel meaningful in ways that are difficult to explain. Sometimes the moments that stay with you are not the dramatic ones, but the small, almost invisible exchanges that make you feel understood.\n\nThe difficulty is that what feels healing can slowly become necessary. Because emotional support flows so naturally, neither person may notice when the relationship starts carrying more weight than it should. The Moon person may begin looking to the Neptune person for reassurance they need to learn to give themselves. The Neptune person may absorb the Moon person''s emotions so completely that they lose track of where their own begin. This rarely happens overnight. It is usually the result of many small moments of comfort accumulating over time.\n\nThe gift of this aspect is emotional trust. The lesson is remembering that closeness works best when it connects two whole people, not when it becomes the place where either person disappears."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The difficulty is that what feels healing can slowly become necessary. Because emotional support flows so naturally, neither person may notice when the relationship starts carrying more weight than it should. The Moon person may begin looking to the Neptune person for reassurance they need to learn to give themselves. The Neptune person may absorb the Moon person''s emotions so completely that they lose track of where their own begin. This rarely happens overnight. It is usually the result of many small moments of comfort accumulating over time."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The gift of this aspect is emotional trust. The lesson is remembering that closeness works best when it connects two whole people, not when it becomes the place where either person disappears."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-neptune_B-moon_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s dreams meets B''s feelings. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"There is something quietly soothing about this connection.\n\nThe Moon person often feels emotionally understood without having to explain every feeling in detail. The Neptune person seems to sense what is happening beneath the surface, responding to emotions that have not yet been fully expressed. This can create a feeling of being deeply seen and emotionally received, even when very little has been said aloud.\n\nBecause of that, being together can feel easy. The Moon person may feel less guarded, less worried about being judged for what they feel. The Neptune person may feel free to express their sensitivity without having to defend it or make it seem more practical than it is. There is often a natural gentleness between the two people, as though each instinctively knows how to handle the other''s softer edges.\n\nThis can also be a deeply imaginative connection. Shared music, films, memories, dreams, spiritual interests, or simply sitting together in comfortable silence can create a sense of closeness. The relationship may feel meaningful in ways that are difficult to explain. Sometimes the moments that stay with you are not the dramatic ones, but the small, almost invisible exchanges that make you feel understood.\n\nThe difficulty is that what feels healing can slowly become necessary. Because emotional support flows so naturally, neither person may notice when the relationship starts carrying more weight than it should. The Moon person may begin looking to the Neptune person for reassurance they need to learn to give themselves. The Neptune person may absorb the Moon person''s emotions so completely that they lose track of where their own begin. This rarely happens overnight. It is usually the result of many small moments of comfort accumulating over time.\n\nThe gift of this aspect is emotional trust. The lesson is remembering that closeness works best when it connects two whole people, not when it becomes the place where either person disappears.","tension":"The difficulty is that what feels healing can slowly become necessary. Because emotional support flows so naturally, neither person may notice when the relationship starts carrying more weight than it should. The Moon person may begin looking to the Neptune person for reassurance they need to learn to give themselves. The Neptune person may absorb the Moon person''s emotions so completely that they lose track of where their own begin. This rarely happens overnight. It is usually the result of many small moments of comfort accumulating over time.","advice":"The gift of this aspect is emotional trust. The lesson is remembering that closeness works best when it connects two whole people, not when it becomes the place where either person disappears.","policy":"Governed by s