  ('A-neptune_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry-neptune-trine-saturn', 'relationship-neptune-trine-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-saturn_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-saturn_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Trine Saturn', null, 'A''s dreams meets B''s structure. The trine lets them flow together easily.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Translation","body":"A''s dreams meets B''s structure. The trine lets them flow together easily."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-neptune_B-saturn_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s dreams meets B''s structure. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":null,"tension":null,"advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":null,"weight":null}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-neptune_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"sun","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry-neptune-conjunction-sun', 'relationship-neptune-conjunction-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-sun_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-sun_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Conjunction Sun', null, 'This person may see something in you before you see it in yourself.

The Neptune person often comes to the Sun person not with knowledge, but with trust. Not the trust that is based on evidence, but the trust of the heart. They look and see a flower where others see only a seed. Long before there is any proof, they feel what may become.

For the Sun person, this can be a strange and beautiful experience. It can feel as though someone has looked beyond the personality, beyond the masks and accumulated history, and recognized something essential. They may feel valued not for what they have accomplished, but for who they are at their core. In that recognition, parts of themselves that have long been dormant may begin to awaken.

At its best, this aspect can feel like a blessing. The Neptune person reflects back possibilities the Sun person may have forgotten, neglected, or never believed were theirs to begin with. Around them, the Sun person may feel more connected to their imagination, their compassion, their creativity, or their sense of purpose. There can be a feeling that something meaningful is moving through the relationship, something that cannot be measured but can be felt.

And yet Neptune''s gifts are rarely uncomplicated. The same vision that inspires can also distort. The Neptune person may be relating to a dream, a longing, or an ideal as much as they are relating to the actual person in front of them. The Sun person may find themselves stepping into that role, consciously or not, because it feels good to be adored for what someone believes you could be. But no one can live inside a projection forever. Eventually the human being beneath the image asks to be seen. When reality arrives, it can feel like a loss, not because the connection was false, but because the fantasy was so powerful.

The invitation here is to let wonder and truth exist together, without asking either one to disappear. This aspect works best when both people make room for reality from the beginning. Being admired is not the same as being truly seen.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may see something in you before you see it in yourself.\n\nThe Neptune person often comes to the Sun person not with knowledge, but with trust. Not the trust that is based on evidence, but the trust of the heart. They look and see a flower where others see only a seed. Long before there is any proof, they feel what may become.\n\nFor the Sun person, this can be a strange and beautiful experience. It can feel as though someone has looked beyond the personality, beyond the masks and accumulated history, and recognized something essential. They may feel valued not for what they have accomplished, but for who they are at their core. In that recognition, parts of themselves that have long been dormant may begin to awaken.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can feel like a blessing. The Neptune person reflects back possibilities the Sun person may have forgotten, neglected, or never believed were theirs to begin with. Around them, the Sun person may feel more connected to their imagination, their compassion, their creativity, or their sense of purpose. There can be a feeling that something meaningful is moving through the relationship, something that cannot be measured but can be felt.\n\nAnd yet Neptune''s gifts are rarely uncomplicated. The same vision that inspires can also distort. The Neptune person may be relating to a dream, a longing, or an ideal as much as they are relating to the actual person in front of them. The Sun person may find themselves stepping into that role, consciously or not, because it feels good to be adored for what someone believes you could be. But no one can live inside a projection forever. Eventually the human being beneath the image asks to be seen. When