  ('A-neptune_B-sun_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"sun","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-sun_square', 'synastry-neptune-square-sun', 'relationship-neptune-square-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-sun_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-sun_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Square Sun', null, 'This connection can make it difficult to know where inspiration ends and illusion begins.

In the beginning, there is often a feeling of being seen through enchanted eyes. The Neptune person may look at the Sun person and immediately sense something beautiful, meaningful, or full of possibility. The Sun person can feel deeply moved by this attention, as though someone has recognized a hidden part of them that others have missed.

But there is a subtle tension underneath it. Being admired in this way can feel intoxicating, yet it can also create an unspoken expectation. The Sun person may begin to feel the weight of the image being reflected back to them, even before they fully realize it exists.

The square creates friction between what is real and what is imagined. The Sun person may find themselves slowly adapting to the Neptune person''s vision of who they are, often without realizing it. The Neptune person may cling to an idealized image, turning away from anything that complicates the story they want to believe. Both can feel that something is off, yet the connection itself seems to blur the edges, making honest conversations harder than they should be.

At its best, this aspect can gently dissolve the walls the Sun person has built around their identity. Around the Neptune person, they may feel more connected to their imagination, their compassion, and the parts of themselves that cannot be explained by logic alone. The relationship can reveal possibilities the Sun person had not considered, inviting them to grow beyond old definitions of who they think they are. But when clarity is sacrificed for the sake of the dream, the relationship can start to feel heavy. One person may feel responsible for keeping the other happy, inspired, or emotionally afloat. Important conversations get postponed because neither person wants to risk disappointing the other or changing the feeling of the connection. Sometimes there is deception, but more often there is projection. No one is trying to mislead anyone. Instead, both people may be responding to who they hope the other person is rather than taking the time to understand who they actually are.

Ask yourself a simple question: can you be yourself in this relationship, or do you feel pressured to live up to someone else''s image of you? The lesson of this aspect is to be yourself, even when it feels good to be put on a pedestal.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection can make it difficult to know where inspiration ends and illusion begins.\n\nIn the beginning, there is often a feeling of being seen through enchanted eyes. The Neptune person may look at the Sun person and immediately sense something beautiful, meaningful, or full of possibility. The Sun person can feel deeply moved by this attention, as though someone has recognized a hidden part of them that others have missed.\n\nBut there is a subtle tension underneath it. Being admired in this way can feel intoxicating, yet it can also create an unspoken expectation. The Sun person may begin to feel the weight of the image being reflected back to them, even before they fully realize it exists.\n\nThe square creates friction between what is real and what is imagined. The Sun person may find themselves slowly adapting to the Neptune person''s vision of who they are, often without realizing it. The Neptune person may cling to an idealized image, turning away from anything that complicates the story they want to believe. Both can feel that something is off, yet the connection itself seems to blur the edges, making honest conversations harder than they should be.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can gently dissolve the walls the Sun person has built around their identity. Around the Neptune person, they may feel more connected to their imagination, their compassion, and the parts of themselves that cannot be explained by logic alone. The relationship can reveal possibilities the Sun person had not considered, inviting them to grow beyond old definitions of who they think they are. But when clarity is sacrificed for the sake of the dream, the relationship can start to feel heavy. One perso