o be put on a pedestal.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-neptune_B-sun_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"sun","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-sun_trine', 'synastry-neptune-trine-sun', 'relationship-neptune-trine-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-sun_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-sun_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Trine Sun', null, 'This relationship often feels quietly inspiring from the start.

The Neptune person tends to pick up on something in the Sun person that other people might miss. They see potential, talent, or a side of the Sun person that hasn''t fully come out yet. Being around the Neptune person can make the Sun person feel more creative, more connected to their instincts, and more comfortable showing parts of themselves they don''t usually put on display.

What''s powerful about it is that the Neptune person doesn''t have to make a big deal out of anything. Their belief alone can have an effect. The Sun person may start trusting themselves more simply because someone sees what they''re capable of. At the same time, the Sun person helps the Neptune person get out of their head and turn ideas into something real, giving structure to dreams that might otherwise stay in the realm of "maybe someday."

There''s often a feeling that the connection means more than what''s happening on the surface. A random conversation can stick with them long after it''s over. Small moments can feel surprisingly meaningful. Together, they tend to bring out each other''s imagination, compassion, and willingness to believe in possibilities that don''t always make perfect sense.

Even in a harmonious aspect like this, Neptune can make things a little blurry around the edges. Because being together feels so natural, it''s easy to gloss over the small moments when you''re not seeing each other quite clearly. The Sun person may enjoy being admired and believed in. The Neptune person may prefer the version of the relationship that feels beautiful rather than asking harder questions about what''s actually there. Nothing dramatic has to happen for this to become a problem. Sometimes it''s just a tendency to let things slide, to avoid uncomfortable conversations, or to assume everything is fine because the connection feels good. Over time, those unspoken realities can quietly build up in the background.

The key is to enjoy the magic without losing touch with what''s real. Let the relationship inspire you, but stay honest about who you are and who the other person is. The more clearly you see each other, the more this aspect can deliver on its promise.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This relationship often feels quietly inspiring from the start.\n\nThe Neptune person tends to pick up on something in the Sun person that other people might miss. They see potential, talent, or a side of the Sun person that hasn''t fully come out yet. Being around the Neptune person can make the Sun person feel more creative, more connected to their instincts, and more comfortable showing parts of themselves they don''t usually put on display.\n\nWhat''s powerful about it is that the Neptune person doesn''t have to make a big deal out of anything. Their belief alone can have an effect. The Sun person may start trusting themselves more simply because someone sees what they''re capable of. At the same time, the Sun person helps the Neptune person get out of their head and turn ideas into something real, giving structure to dreams that might otherwise stay in the realm of \"maybe someday.\"\n\nThere''s often a feeling that the connection means more than what''s happening on the surface. A random conversation can stick with them long after it''s over. Small moments can feel surprisingly meaningful. Together, they tend to bring out each other''s imagination, compassion, and willingness to believe in possibilities that don''t always make perfect sense.\n\nEven in a harmonious aspect like this, Neptune can make things a little blurry around the edges. Because being together feels so natural, it''s easy to gloss over the small moments when you''re not seeing each other quite clearly. The Sun person may enjoy being admired and believed in. The Neptune person may prefer the version of the relationship that feels beautiful rather than asking harder questions about what''s actual