  ('A-neptune_B-uranus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"uranus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-uranus_trine', 'synastry-neptune-trine-uranus', 'relationship-neptune-trine-uranus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-uranus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-uranus_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Trine Uranus', null, 'A''s dreams meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Translation","body":"A''s dreams meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-neptune_B-uranus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s dreams meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":null,"tension":null,"advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":null,"weight":null}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-neptune_B-venus_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"venus","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-venus_conjunction', 'synastry-neptune-conjunction-venus', 'relationship-neptune-conjunction-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-venus_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-venus_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Conjunction Venus', null, 'This person can awaken a kind of love that feels both familiar and longed for, as though something in you has been waiting for their arrival.

The attraction can feel immediate, as though something in you recognizes each other before there is enough history to explain why. The Neptune person may be captivated by the Venus person''s beauty, charm, or perceived goodness, seeing them through a lens that turns ordinary details into something meaningful. The Venus person may feel cherished, admired, and deeply appreciated, sometimes to a degree that feels almost magical.

There can be a visible charge around this connection. Other people may notice the way you look at each other, the way the room seems to narrow when you are together, the way both of you seem caught inside something that does not include anyone else yet. Sometimes the spell is not private. Sometimes the people around you can see it before you know what to call it.

At its best, this aspect reaches the places that expect disappointment and offers something different. The Venus person may feel more willing to offer affection without guarding every feeling. The Neptune person may feel less alone in their longing, as though something they have been searching for has finally taken shape. Together, you may create a kind of intimacy that feels imaginative, romantic, and deeply moving. Even the smallest exchanges can seem touched by something larger than themselves.

But the conjunction can make the dream too powerful.

The Neptune person may begin loving the image as much as the person. The Venus person may begin performing the image because being adored this way feels good. Over time, the pedestal becomes heavy. You cannot have an ordinary mood. You cannot need too much. You cannot be inconvenient without the dream flickering.

Reality always arrives. And when it does, there can be a moment of grief. Not because the love was false, but because no human being can fully embody a dream. The challenge is letting the relationship become real without treating reality as a loss.

The work is to choose the real person again and again. Let the romance stay alive, but do not ask anyone to become a symbol.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can awaken a kind of love that feels both familiar and longed for, as though something in you has been waiting for their arrival.\n\nThe attraction can feel immediate, as though something in you recognizes each other before there is enough history to explain why. The Neptune person may be captivated by the Venus person''s beauty, charm, or perceived goodness, seeing them through a lens that turns ordinary details into something meaningful. The Venus person may feel cherished, admired, and deeply appreciated, sometimes to a degree that feels almost magical.\n\nThere can be a visible charge around this connection. Other people may notice the way you look at each other, the way the room seems to narrow when you are together, the way both of you seem caught inside something that does not include anyone else yet. Sometimes the spell is not private. Sometimes the people around you can see it before you know what to call it.\n\nAt its best, this aspect reaches the places that expect disappointment and offers something different. The Venus person may feel more willing to offer affection without guarding every feeling. The Neptune person may feel less alone in their longing, as though something they have been searching for has finally taken shape. Together, you may create a kind of intimacy that feels imaginative, romantic, and deeply moving. Even the smallest exchanges can seem touched by something larger than themselves.\n\nBut the conjunction can make the dream too powerful.\n\nThe Neptune person may begin loving the image as much as the person. The Venus person may begin performing the image because being adored this way feels good. Over time, the pedestal becomes heavy. You cannot have an ordinary mood. You cannot need too much. You cannot be inconvenient without the dream flickering.\n\nReality always arrives. And when it does, there can be a moment of grief. Not because the love was false, but because no human being can fully embody a dream. The challenge is letting the relationship become real without treating reality as a loss.\n\nThe work is to choose the real person again and again. Let the romance stay alive, but do not ask anyone to become a symbol."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The Neptune person may begin loving the image as much as the person. The Venus person may begin performing the image because being adored this way feels good. Over time, the pedestal becomes heavy. You cannot have an ordinary mood. You cannot need too much. You cannot be inconvenient without the dream flickering.\n\nReality always arrives. And when it does, there can be a moment of grief. Not because the love was false, but because no human being can fully embody a dream. The challenge is letting the relationship become real without treating reality as a loss."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The work is to choose the real person again and again. Let the romance stay alive, but do not ask anyone to become a symbol."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-neptune_B-venus_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Neptune person can make Venus feel romantic, spiritual, and unusually tender. It is beautiful, and it can blur truth. Love the person in front of you, not the story your longing built around them.","summaryDeep":"This person can awaken a kind of love that feels both familiar and longed for, as though something in you has been waiting for their arrival.\n\nThe attraction can feel immediate, as though something in you recognizes each other before there is enough history to explain why. The Neptune person may be captivated by the Venus person''s beauty, charm, or perceived goodness, seeing them through a lens that turns ordinary details into something meaningful. The Venus person may feel cherished, admired, and deeply appreciated, sometimes to a degree that feels almost magical.\n\nThere can be a visible charge around this connection. Other people may notice the way you look at each other, the way the room seems to narrow when you are together, the way both of you seem caught inside something that does not include anyone else yet. Sometimes the spell is not private. Sometimes the people around you can see it before you know what to call it.\n\nAt its best, this aspect reaches the places that expect disappointment and offers something different. The Venus person may feel more willing to offer affection without guarding every feeling. The Neptune person may feel less alone in their longing, as though something they have been searching for has finally taken shape. Together, you may create a kind of intimacy that feels imaginative, romantic, and deeply moving. Even the smallest exchanges can seem touched by something larger than themselves.\n\nBut the conjunction can make the dream too powerful.\n\nThe Neptune person may begin loving the image as much as the person. The Venus person may begin performing the image because being adored this way feels good. Over time, the pedestal becomes heavy. You cannot have an ordinary mood. You cannot need too much. You cannot be inconvenient without the dream flickering.\n\nReality always arrives. And when it does, there can be a moment of grief. Not because the love was false, but because no human being can fully embody a dream. The challenge is letting the relationship become real without treating reality as a loss.\n\nThe work is to choose the real person again and again. Let the romance stay alive, but do not ask anyone to become a symbol.","tension":"The Neptune person may begin loving the image as much as the person. The Venus person may begin performing the image because being adored this way feels good. Over time, the pedestal becomes heavy. You cannot have an ordinary mood. You cannot need too much. You cannot be inconvenient without the dream flickering.\n\nReality always arrives. And when it does, there can be a moment of grief. Not because the love was false, but because no human being can fully embody a dream. The challenge is letting the relationship become real without treating reality as a loss.","advice":"The work is to choose the real person again and again. Let the romance stay alive, but do not ask anyone to become a symbol.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-neptune_B-venus_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"venus","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-venus_opposition', 'synastry-neptune-opposition-venus', 'relationship-neptune-opposition-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-venus_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-venus_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Opposition Venus', null, 'This person may feel just out of reach, even when they are close.

There is often a strong pull here. You may feel drawn to their beauty, mystery, kindness, imagination, or the feeling they awaken in you. The relationship may seem meaningful before it has had time to become clear. You may feel that something important is happening, even if you cannot name what it is.

At its best, this aspect gives both people something they need. One brings love into the room in a real way, through affection, presence, and attention. The other brings a sense of wonder, meaning, and possibility. Together, love can feel both human and larger than human.

But the opposition can keep you reaching.

One person may want the dream to become concrete. The other may want ordinary affection to become something endless, spiritual, or ideal. Both may be drawn to a version of the relationship that exists partly in the space between what is known and what is imagined.

That space can be intoxicating. It can also be confusing.

This is where the fog can go both ways. You may believe the other person is offering more than they have actually offered. They may believe you understood something they never clearly said. One person may become evasive because they do not want to disappoint. The other may become self-protective because the uncertainty starts to hurt. Before long, both people are responding to the story around the relationship, not the relationship itself.

In its shadow, Neptune can show up as unavailability, broken promises, vague intentions, not responding, avoidance, lying, or gaslighting. That does not mean this aspect predicts those behaviors. It means that when the bond begins with bliss and then becomes unclear, you have to name what is happening instead of explaining it away as romance.

Come back to what is actually happening between you. Not the story you have built around them. Not the future version of the relationship you hope will arrive. The person in front of you.

Longing can be powerful, but it is not the same thing as intimacy. The relationships that endure are not sustained by fantasy alone. They are built through the choices two people make to show up.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may feel just out of reach, even when they are close.\n\nThere is often a strong pull here. You may feel drawn to their beauty, mystery, kindness, imagination, or the feeling they awaken in you. The relationship may seem meaningful before it has had time to become clear. You may feel that something important is happening, even if you cannot name what it is.\n\nAt its best, this aspect gives both people something they need. One brings love into the room in a real way, through affection, presence, and attention. The other brings a sense of wonder, meaning, and possibility. Together, love can feel both human and larger than human.\n\nBut the opposition can keep you reaching.\n\nOne person may want the dream to become concrete. The other may want ordinary affection to become something endless, spiritual, or ideal. Both may be drawn to a version of the relationship that exists partly in the space between what is known and what is imagined.\n\nThat space can be intoxicating. It can also be confusing.\n\nThis is where the fog can go both ways. You may believe the other person is offering more than they have actually offered. They may believe you understood something they never clearly said. One person may become evasive because they do not want to disappoint. The other may become self-protective because the uncertainty starts to hurt. Before long, both people are responding to the story around the relationship, not the relationship itself.\n\nIn its shadow, Neptune can show up as unavailability, broken promises, vague intentions, not responding, avoidance, lying, or gaslighting. That does not mean this aspect predicts those behaviors. It means that when the bond begins with bliss and then becomes unclear, you have to name what is happening instead of explaining it away as romance.\n\nCome back to what is actually happening between you. Not the story you have built around them. Not the future version of the relationship you hope will arrive. The person in front of you.\n\nLonging can be powerful, but it is not the same thing as intimacy. The relationships that endure are not sustained by fantasy alone. They are built through the choices two people make to show up."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"This is where the fog can go both ways. You may believe the other person is offering more than they have actually offered. They may believe you understood something they never clearly said. One person may become evasive because they do not want to disappoint. The other may become self-protective because the uncertainty starts to hurt. Before long, both people are responding to the story around the relationship, not the relationship itself.\n\nIn its shadow, Neptune can show up as unavailability, broken promises, vague intentions, not responding, avoidance, lying, or gaslighting. That does not mean this aspect predicts those behaviors. It means that when the bond begins with bliss and then becomes unclear, you have to name what is happening instead of explaining it away as romance."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Come back to what is actually happening between you. Not the story you have built around them. Not the future version of the relationship you hope will arrive. The person in front of you.\n\nLonging can be powerful, but it is not the same thing as intimacy. The relationships that endure are not sustained by fantasy alone. They are built through the choices two people make to show up."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-neptune_B-venus_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s dreams meets B''s love and values. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person may feel just out of reach, even when they are close.\n\nThere is often a strong pull here. You may