  ('A-neptune_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"venus","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry-neptune-sextile-venus', 'relationship-neptune-sextile-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-venus_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-venus_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Sextile Venus', null, 'Sometimes this connection starts as a subtle pull rather than an obvious attraction. You enjoy each other. You feel understood. There is a sweetness between you that is easy to overlook at first because it does not demand attention.

The Neptune person often picks up on something delicate and beautiful in the Venus person, something that goes beyond appearance. They may be drawn to the way Venus loves, creates, cares, or moves through the world. In turn, the Venus person may feel more open around Neptune, more willing to trust their feelings and follow their heart instead of second-guessing it.

There is a natural kindness here, but it tends to unfold through choice rather than fate. The opportunities for closeness are present, yet neither person is likely to force the relationship into a particular shape. Instead, it grows through small moments of honesty, affection, and mutual curiosity.

One of the gifts of this aspect is the way it can make love feel meaningful without becoming overwhelming. You may inspire each other creatively or emotionally. You may help each other believe in possibilities that once felt out of reach. There can be a sense that the relationship adds beauty to your life simply by existing.

The difficulty is that both people can become comfortable living in potential. Feelings are sensed rather than spoken. Hopes are assumed rather than discussed. You may believe you are on the same page without ever checking whether that is actually true.

Over time, what remains unsaid matters.

This aspect works best when you allow the magic to coexist with clarity.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Sometimes this connection starts as a subtle pull rather than an obvious attraction. You enjoy each other. You feel understood. There is a sweetness between you that is easy to overlook at first because it does not demand attention.\n\nThe Neptune person often picks up on something delicate and beautiful in the Venus person, something that goes beyond appearance. They may be drawn to the way Venus loves, creates, cares, or moves through the world. In turn, the Venus person may feel more open around Neptune, more willing to trust their feelings and follow their heart instead of second-guessing it.\n\nThere is a natural kindness here, but it tends to unfold through choice rather than fate. The opportunities for closeness are present, yet neither person is likely to force the relationship into a particular shape. Instead, it grows through small moments of honesty, affection, and mutual curiosity.\n\nOne of the gifts of this aspect is the way it can make love feel meaningful without becoming overwhelming. You may inspire each other creatively or emotionally. You may help each other believe in possibilities that once felt out of reach. There can be a sense that the relationship adds beauty to your life simply by existing.\n\nThe difficulty is that both people can become comfortable living in potential. Feelings are sensed rather than spoken. Hopes are assumed rather than discussed. You may believe you are on the same page without ever checking whether that is actually true.\n\nOver time, what remains unsaid matters.\n\nThis aspect works best when you allow the magic to coexist with clarity."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The difficulty is that both people can become comfortable living in potential. Feelings are sensed rather than spoken. Hopes are assumed rather than discussed. You may believe you are on the same page without ever checking whether that is actually true."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Over time, what remains unsaid matters.\n\nThis aspect works best when you allow the magic to coexist with clarity."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-neptune_B-venus_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s dreams meets B''s love and values. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"Sometimes this connection starts as a subtle pull rather than an obvious attraction. You enjoy each other. You feel understood. There is a sweetness between you that is easy to overlook at first because it does not demand attention.\n\nThe Neptune person often picks up on something delicate and beautiful in the Venus person, something that goes beyond appearance. They may be drawn to the way Venus loves, creates, cares, or moves through the world. In turn, the Venus person may feel more open around Neptune, more willing to trust their feelings and follow their heart instead of second-guessing it.\n\nThere is a natural kindness here, but it tends to unfold through choice rather than fate. The opportunities for closeness are present, yet neither person is likely to force the relationship into a particular shape. Instead, it grows through small moments of honesty, affection, and mutual curiosity.\n\nOne of the gifts of this aspect is the way it can make love feel meaningful without becoming overwhelming. You may inspire each other creatively or emotionally. You may help each other believe in possibilities that once felt out of reach. There can be a sense that the relationship adds beauty to your life simply by existing.\n\nThe difficulty is that both people can become comfortable living in potential. Feelings are sensed rather than spoken. Hopes are assumed rather than discussed. You may believe you are on the same page without ever checking whether that is actually true.\n\nOver time, what remains unsaid matters.\n\nThis aspect works best when you allow the magic to coexist with clarity.","tension":"The difficulty is that both people can become comfortable living in potential. Feelings are sensed rather than spoken. Hopes are assumed rather than discussed. You may believe you are on the same page without ever checking whether that is actually true.","advice":"Over time, what remains unsaid matters.\n\nThis aspect works best when you allow the magic to coexist with clarity.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-neptune_B-venus_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"venus","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-venus_square', 'synastry-neptune-square-venus', 'relationship-neptune-square-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-venus_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-venus_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Square Venus', null, 'This connection can make it hard to tell love from longing.

At first, being seen by this person may feel beautiful. The Neptune person may look at the Venus person and sense something lovely, rare, or full of promise. The Venus person may feel deeply moved by that gaze, as though someone has finally noticed the most beautiful part of them.

But the square makes the image unstable.

The Venus person may begin shaping themselves around what the Neptune person wants to see. The Neptune person may avoid anything that complicates the fantasy. Both people may sense that something is unclear, but the feeling between them can make honesty strangely difficult. No one wants to break the spell.

This is where the relationship can become heavy.

One person may take on the job of staying lovely, forgiving, inspiring, or easy to adore. The other may settle into the dream and resist seeing what is real. It can feel romantic at first. Eventually it can become exhausting. You may realize that the relationship has been protecting an image instead of getting to know the people inside it.

There may not be any intentional deception here. More often, both of you are relating to an idea of each other instead of the actual person. You see what you want to see. They do the same. The feelings are real, but feelings alone are not enough to tell you how a relationship will unfold over time.

In its harder expression, this aspect can move from bliss into confusion. Someone becomes unavailable. Someone stops answering clearly. Promises are made and not kept. The truth gets slippery. Avoidance starts to replace honesty. If gaslighting enters the dynamic, name it as gaslighting, not as chemistry, not as fate, and not as Neptune being romantic.

The lesson is to stop protecting the dream at the expense of your reality.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection can make it hard to tell love from longing.\n\nAt first, being seen by this person may feel beautiful. The Neptune person may look at the Venus person and sense something lovely, rare, or full of promise. The Venus person may feel deeply moved by that gaze, as though someone has finally noticed the most beautiful part of them.\n\nBut the square makes the image unstable.\n\nThe Venus person may begin shaping themselves around what the Neptune person wants to see. The Neptune person may avoid anything that complicates the fantasy. Both people may sense that something is unclear, but the feeling between them can make honesty strangely difficult. No one wants to break the spell.\n\nThis is where the relationship can become heavy.\n\nOne person may take on the job of staying lovely, forgiving, inspiring, or easy to adore. The other may settle into the dream and resist seeing what is real. It can feel romantic at first. Eventually it can become exhausting. You may realize that the relationship has been protecting an image instead of getting to know the people inside it.\n\nThere may not be any intentional deception here. More often, both of you are relating to an idea of each other instead of the actual person. You see what you want to see. They do the same. The feelings are real, but feelings alone are not enough to tell you how a relationship will unfold over time.\n\nIn its harder expression, this aspect can move from bliss into confusion. Someone becomes unavailable. Someone stops answering clearly. Promises are made and not kept. The truth gets slippery. Avoidance starts to replace honesty. If gaslighting enters the dynamic, name it as gaslighting, not as chemistry, not as fate, and not as Neptune being romantic.\n\nThe lesson is to stop protecting the dream at the expense of your reality."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"One person may take on the job of staying lovely, forgiving, inspiring, or easy to adore. The other may settle into the dream and resist seeing what is real. It can feel romantic at first. Eventually it can become exhausting. You may realize that the relationship has been protecting an image instead of getting to know the people inside it.\n\nThere may not be any intentional deception here. More often, both of you are relating to an idea of each other instead of the actual person. You see what you want to see. They do the same. The feelings are real, but feelings alone are not enough to tell you how a relationship will unfold over time.\n\nIn its harder expression, this aspect can move from bliss into confusion. Someone becomes unavailable. Someone stops answering clearly. Promises are made and not kept. The truth gets slippery. Avoidance starts to replace honesty. If gaslighting enters the dynamic, name it as gaslighting, not as chemistry, not as fate, and not as Neptune being romantic."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The lesson is to stop protecting the dream at the expense of your reality."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-neptune_B-venus_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Neptune person can turn Venus into longing, fantasy, and romantic fog. The beauty is real, but it may not be reliable. Watch secrecy, saving, and loving potential more than behavior.","summaryDeep":"This connection can make it hard to tell love from longing.\n\nAt first, being seen by this person may feel beautiful. The Neptune person may look at the Venus person and sense something lovely, rare, or full of promise. The Venus person may feel deeply moved by that gaze, as though someone has finally noticed the most beautiful part of them.\n\nBut the square makes the image unstable.\n\nThe Venus person may begin shaping themselves around what the Neptune person wants to see. The Neptune person may avoid anything that complicates the fantasy. Both people may sense that something is unclear, but the feeling between them can make honesty strangely difficult. No one wants to break the spell.\n\nThis is where the relationship can become heavy.\n\nOne person may take on the job of staying lovely, forgiving, inspiring, or easy to adore. The other may settle into the dream and resist seeing what is real. It can feel romantic at first. Eventually it can become exhausting. You may realize that the relationship has been protecting an image instead of getting to know the people inside it.\n\nThere may not be any intentional deception here. More often, both of you are relating to an idea of each other instead of the actual person. You see what you want to see. They do the same. The feelings are real, but feelings alone are not enough to tell you how a relationship will unfold over time.\n\nIn its harder expression, this aspect can move from bliss into confusion. Someone becomes unavailable. Someone stops answering clearly. Promises are made and not kept. The truth gets slippery. Avoidance starts to replace honesty. If gaslighting enters the dynamic, name it as gaslighting, not as chemistry, not as fate, and not as Neptune being romantic.\n\nThe lesson is to stop protecting the dream at the expense of your reality.","tension":"One person may take on the job of staying lovely, forgiving, inspiring, or easy to adore. The other may settle into the dream and resist seeing what is real. It can feel romantic at first. Eventually it can become exhausting. You may realize that the relationship has been protecting an image instead of getting to know the people inside it.\n\nThere may not be any intentional deception here. More often, both of you are relating to an idea of each other instead of the actual person. You see what you want to see. They do the same. The feelings are real, but feelings alone are not enough to tell you how a relationship will unfold over time.\n\nIn its harder expression, this aspect can move from bliss into confusion. Someone becomes unavailable. Someone stops answering clearly. Promises are made and not kept. The truth gets slippery. Avoidance starts to replace honesty. If gaslighting enters the dynamic, name it as gaslighting, not as chemistry, not as fate, and not as Neptune being romantic.","advice":"The lesson is to stop protecting the dream at the expense of your reality.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-neptune_B-venus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"neptune","planetB":"venus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-neptune_B-venus_trine', 'synastry-neptune-trine-venus', 'relationship-neptune-trine-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-neptune_B-venus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-neptune_B-venus_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Neptune Trine Venus', null, 'This relationship often carries an easy kind of magic, as though affection and understanding flow naturally between you.

There can be a real sense of peace in each other''s presence. Warmth, kindness, comfort, and the feeling that everything will be okay may come more easily here than they do with most people. Even irritation may pass quickly. You can be annoyed for a moment, then somehow the edge dissolves and you remember why you care.

This connection often feels easy from the start. The Neptune person may notice something beautiful or special about the Venus person that others miss, while the Venus person may feel more relaxed, loving, and open in return. Simply being together can feel comforting, inspiring, and emotionally nourishing.

At its best, this aspect encourages kindness and compassion. The Neptune person brings imagination, sensitivity, and faith in the relationship, while the Venus person helps turn those feelings into something tangible through affection and care. Together, you may find it easier to appreciate beauty, extend forgiveness, and enjoy the simple moments that make life feel meaningful.

Still, Neptune can blur boundaries, even in a flowing aspect like this one.

Because things feel so natural between you, it can be tempting to avoid difficult conversations or overlook issues that need attention. The Venus person may enjoy feeling appreciated and choose not to question certain things. The Neptune person may focus on what is lovely about the relationship and avoid dealing with its more complicated realities. Over time, what goes unsaid can quietly build up.

The challenge is not to lose the magic of the connection, but to stay grounded in what is real.

Let yourself enjoy the romance, the peace, the kindness, and the sense of possibility. Just make sure there is room for the messy conversations too.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This relationship often carries an easy kind of magic, as though affection and understanding flow naturally between you.\n\nThere can be a real sense of peace in each other''s presence. Warmth, kindness, comfort, and the feeling that everything will be okay may come more easily here than they do with most people. Even irritation may pass quickly. You can be annoyed for a moment, then somehow the edge dissolves and you remember why you care.\n\nThis connection often feels easy from the start. The Neptune person may notice something beautiful or special about the Venus person that others miss, while the Venus person may feel more relaxed, loving, and open in return. Simply being together can feel comforting, inspiring, and emotionally nourishing.\n\nAt its best, this aspect encourages kindness and compassion. The Neptune person brings imagination, sensitivity, and faith in the relationship, while the Venus person helps turn those feelings into something tangible through affection and care. Together, you may find it easier to appreciate beauty, extend forgiveness, and enjoy the simple moments that make life feel meaningful.\n\nStill, Neptune can blur boundaries, even in a flowing aspect like this one.\n\nBecause things feel so natural between you, it can be tempting to avoid difficult conversations or overlook issues that need attention. The Venus person may enjoy feeling appreciated and choose not to question certain things. The Neptune person may focus on what is lovely about the relationship and avoid dealing with its more complicated realities. Over time, what goes unsaid can quietly build up.\n\nThe challenge is not to lose the magic of the connection, but to stay grounded in what is real.\n\nLet yourself enjoy the romance, the peace, the kindness, and the sense of pos