rned by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry-pluto-opposition-mercury', 'relationship-pluto-opposition-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-mercury_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-mercury_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Opposition Mercury', null, 'This person has a way of getting under your skin and into your thoughts. Their presence can challenge how you make sense of the world, how you communicate, and even how you trust your own perceptions. There is a magnetic mental connection here, but it rarely feels neutral. The Pluto person may pick up on what is left unsaid, sensing the deeper story beneath the Mercury person''s words. The Mercury person may be drawn to the Pluto person''s insight while also feeling unsettled by how easily they seem to see through the surface.

At its best, this aspect asks both people to grow beyond the stories they''ve been telling themselves. The Pluto person can encourage the Mercury person to question inherited beliefs, speak more honestly, and explore ideas that feel uncomfortable but necessary. The Mercury person can help the Pluto person give language to what has been sensed, feared, or understood beneath the surface. Together, they can uncover truths that neither would likely find on their own.

But oppositions rarely let us stay comfortable. This connection can become a struggle over whose version of reality gets to take up the most space. One person may push for answers while the other feels the need to defend themselves. Conversations can go in circles about what was said, what was meant, and who is right. When fear, insecurity, or control takes over, communication can become more about winning than understanding each other.

The invitation here is to practice curiosity instead of certainty. Both people need enough room to think, question, change their minds, and disagree without feeling diminished. The wisdom of this aspect comes from recognizing that truth is often larger than any one person''s perspective.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a way of getting under your skin and into your thoughts. Their presence can challenge how you make sense of the world, how you communicate, and even how you trust your own perceptions. There is a magnetic mental connection here, but it rarely feels neutral. The Pluto person may pick up on what is left unsaid, sensing the deeper story beneath the Mercury person''s words. The Mercury person may be drawn to the Pluto person''s insight while also feeling unsettled by how easily they seem to see through the surface.\n\nAt its best, this aspect asks both people to grow beyond the stories they''ve been telling themselves. The Pluto person can encourage the Mercury person to question inherited beliefs, speak more honestly, and explore ideas that feel uncomfortable but necessary. The Mercury person can help the Pluto person give language to what has been sensed, feared, or understood beneath the surface. Together, they can uncover truths that neither would likely find on their own.\n\nBut oppositions rarely let us stay comfortable. This connection can become a struggle over whose version of reality gets to take up the most space. One person may push for answers while the other feels the need to defend themselves. Conversations can go in circles about what was said, what was meant, and who is right. When fear, insecurity, or control takes over, communication can become more about winning than understanding each other.\n\nThe invitation here is to practice curiosity instead of certainty. Both people need enough room to think, question, change their minds, and disagree without feeling diminished. The wisdom of this aspect comes from recognizing that truth is often larger than any one person''s perspective."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But oppositions rarely let us stay comfortable. This connection can become a struggle over whose version of reality gets to take up the most space. One person may push for answers while the other feels the need to defend themselves. Conversations can go in circles about what was said, what was meant, and who is right. When fear, insecurity, or control takes over, communication can become more about winning than understanding each other."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The invitation here is to practice curiosity instead of certainty. Both people need enough room to think, question, change their minds, and disagree without feeling diminished. The wisdom of this aspect comes from recognizing that truth is often larger than any one person''s perspective."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-mercury_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s depth and power meets B''s mind. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person has a way of getting under your skin and into your thoughts. Their presence can challenge how you make sense of the world, how you communicate, and even how you trust your own perceptions. There is a magnetic mental connection here, but it rarely feels neutral. The Pluto person may pick up on what is left unsaid, sensing the deeper story beneath the Mercury person''s words. The Mercury person may be drawn to the Pluto person''s insight while also feeling unsettled by how easily they seem to see through the surface.\n\nAt its best, this aspect asks both people to grow beyond the stories they''ve been telling themselves. The Pluto person can encourage the Mercury person to question inherited beliefs, speak more honestly, and explore ideas that feel uncomfortable but necessary. The Mercury person can help the Pluto person give language to what has been sensed, feared, or understood beneath the surface. Together, they can uncover truths that neither would likely find on their own.\n\nBut oppositions rarely let us stay comfortable. This connection can become a struggle over whose version of reality gets to take up the most space. One person may push for answers while the other feels the need to defend themselves. Conversations can go in circles about what was said, what was meant, and who is right. When fear, insecurity, or control takes over, communication can become more about winning than understanding each other.\n\nThe invitation here is to practice curiosity instead of certainty. Both people need enough room to think, question, change their minds, and disagree without feeling diminished. The wisdom of this aspect comes from recognizing that truth is often larger than any one person''s perspective.","tension":"But oppositions rarely let us stay comfortable. This connection can become a struggle over whose version of reality gets to take up the most space. One person may push for answers while the other feels the need to defend themselves. Conversations can go in circles about what was said, what was meant, and who is right. When fear, insecurity, or control takes over, communication can become more about winning than understanding each other.","advice":"The invitation here is to practice curiosity instead of certainty. Both people need enough room to think, question, change their minds, and disagree without feeling diminished. The wisdom of this aspect comes from recognizing that truth is often larger than any one person''s perspective.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry-pluto-sextile-mercury', 'relationship-pluto-sextile-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-mercury_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-mercury_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Sextile Mercury', null, 'This aspect creates an opportunity for deeper, more honest communication. The Pluto person often senses what lies beneath the Mercury person''s words. They may notice the hesitation, hear what has been left unsaid, or ask the question that brings the real conversation into focus.

There is depth here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured, it can build a strong sense of trust. The Mercury person may feel encouraged to speak more openly, explore thoughts they have not fully formed, or find language for experiences that have been difficult to express. The Pluto person may discover that their deeper perceptions, instincts, and private insights are met with curiosity rather than discomfort.

One of the strengths of this aspect is its patience. It does not require immediate vulnerability. Instead, it allows intimacy to develop gradually through honest conversation. The more willing both people are to stay curious and engaged, the more meaningful the connection becomes.

The challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to appreciate the possibility of depth without fully stepping into it. If difficult conversations are continually avoided, the relationship may remain supportive and interesting, but some of its greatest opportunities for understanding and growth may never be realized.

Let the deeper conversations happen instead of always steering around them. This one rewards the choice to go there.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This aspect creates an opportunity for deeper, more honest communication. The Pluto person often senses what lies beneath the Mercury person''s words. They may notice the hesitation, hear what has been left unsaid, or ask the question that brings the real conversation into focus.\n\nThere is depth here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured, it can build a strong sense of trust. The Mercury person may feel encouraged to speak more openly, explore thoughts they have not fully formed, or find language for experiences that have been difficult to express. The Pluto person may discover that their deeper perceptions, instincts, and private insights are met with curiosity rather than discomfort.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is its patience. It does not require immediate vulnerability. Instead, it allows intimacy to develop gradually through honest conversation. The more willing both people are to stay curious and engaged, the more meaningful the connection becomes.\n\nThe challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to appreciate the possibility of depth without fully stepping into it. If difficult conversations are continually avoided, the relationship may remain supportive and interesting, but some of its greatest opportunities for understanding and growth may never be realized.\n\nLet the deeper conversations happen instead of always steering around them. This one rewards the choice to go there."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to appreciate the possibility of depth without fully stepping into it. If difficult conversations are continually avoided, the relationship may remain supportive and interesting, but some of its greatest opportunities for understanding and growth may never be realized."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the deeper conversations happen instead of always steering around them. This one rewards the choice to go there."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-mercury_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s depth and power meets B''s mind. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This aspect creates an opportunity for deeper, more honest communication. The Pluto person often senses what lies beneath the Mercury person''s words. They may notice the hesitation, hear what has been left unsaid, or ask the question that brings the real conversation into focus.\n\nThere is depth here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured, it can build a strong sense of trust. The Mercury person may feel encouraged to speak more openly, explore thoughts they have not fully formed, or find language for experiences that have been difficult to express. The Pluto person may discover that their deeper perceptions, instincts, and private insights are met with curiosity rather than discomfort.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is its patience. It does not require immediate vulnerability. Instead, it allows intimacy to develop gradually through honest conversation. The more willing both people are to stay curious and engaged, the more meaningful the connection becomes.\n\nThe challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to appreciate the possibility of depth without fully stepping into it. If difficult conversations are continually avoided, the relationship may remain supportive and interesting, but some of its greatest opportunities for understanding and growth may never be realized.\n\nLet the deeper conversations happen instead of always steering around them. This one rewards the choice to go there.","tension":"The challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to appreciate the possibility of depth without fully stepping into it. If difficult conversations are continually avoided, the relationship may remain supportive and interesting, but some of its greatest opportunities for understanding and growth may never be realized.","advice":"Let the deeper conversations happen instead of always steering around them. This one rewards the choice to go there.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-mercury_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-mercury_square', 'synastry-pluto-square-mercury', 'relationship-pluto-square-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-mercury_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-mercury_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Square Mercury', null, 'Mercury-Pluto squares have a way of getting under the skin of a conversation. This is not the kind of connection that stays on the surface for long. The Pluto person often pushes for what is underneath the words, while the Mercury person may feel challenged to explain, clarify, or reveal more than they intended.

There can be a powerful fascination between you. The conversations may feel compelling, consuming, and difficult to walk away from. Even when an exchange becomes uncomfortable, there can be a sense that something important is trying to emerge. Hidden fears, old assumptions, and unspoken truths have a way of making themselves known here.

At its best, this aspect can transform the way both people communicate. It can expose patterns that no longer serve, reveal where honesty has been avoided, and encourage a deeper relationship with the truth. The tension itself can become a catalyst for growth.

But not every difficult conversation is a meaningful one. When this dynamic becomes unconscious, communication can turn into a struggle for control. The Pluto person may push too hard for answers, certainty, or disclosure. The Mercury person may respond by becoming defensive, guarded, or determined to prove their point. Conversations can become less about understanding and more about protecting territory. The question this aspect asks is simple: what happens when the stakes feel high? Do you move closer to honesty, or closer to strategy? Do you feel invited into deeper truth, or pressured into revealing more than feels safe?

This connection has the potential to teach both people something important about communication. Not every truth needs to be extracted. Not every disagreement needs to be won. The real work is learning how to stay present with intensity without turning every conversation into a battleground.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"Mercury-Pluto squares have a way of getting under the skin of a conversation. This is not the kind of connection that stays on the surface for long. The Pluto person often pushes for what is underneath the words, while the Mercury person may feel challenged to explain, clarify, or reveal more than they intended.\n\nThere can be a powerful fascination between you. The conversations may feel compelling, consuming, and difficult to walk away from. Even when an exchange becomes uncomfortable, there can be a sense that something important is trying to emerge. Hidden fears, old assumptions, and unspoken truths have a way of making themselves known here.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can transform the way both people communicate. It can expose patterns that no longer serve, reveal where honesty has been avoided, and encourage a deeper relationship with the truth. The tension itself can become a catalyst for growth.\n\nBut not every difficult conversation is a meaningful one. When this dynamic becomes unconscious, communication can turn into a struggle for control. The Pluto person may push too hard for answers, certainty, or disclosure. The Mercury person may respond by becoming defensive, guarded, or determined to prove their point. Conversations can become less about understanding and more about protecting territory. The question this aspect asks is simple: what happens when the stakes feel high? Do you move closer to honesty, or closer to strategy? Do you feel invited into deeper truth, or pressured into revealing more than feels safe?\n\nThis connection has the potential to teach both people something important about communication. Not