  ('A-pluto_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry-pluto-trine-saturn', 'relationship-pluto-trine-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-saturn_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-saturn_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Trine Saturn', null, 'A''s depth and power meets B''s structure. The trine lets them flow together easily.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Translation","body":"A''s depth and power meets B''s structure. The trine lets them flow together easily."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-saturn_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s depth and power meets B''s structure. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":null,"tension":null,"advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":null,"weight":null}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"sun","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry-pluto-conjunction-sun', 'relationship-pluto-conjunction-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-sun_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-sun_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Conjunction Sun', null, 'This person can feel like an obsession before you have words for why.

The charge is immediate. Electric. Unsettling. It can feel as though the Pluto person recognizes something in you that even you have not fully claimed. You may feel exposed, chosen, pulled into a current so powerful that ordinary attraction suddenly feels insignificant.

There is a raw magnetism here that is difficult to resist. The Pluto person often awakens something dormant in the Sun person. Buried desires, hidden strengths, long-forgotten hungers, and truths that have been waiting beneath the surface. Their fascination can feel intoxicating. Their presence can make the Sun person feel more alive, more visible, more powerful than they have in a very long time.

But Pluto does not touch anything lightly. The conjunction amplifies everything. Desire becomes consuming. Curiosity becomes fixation. Intimacy becomes a force that can alter the landscape of both people''s lives. What feels like deep recognition can slowly become entanglement. What feels like devotion can become possession. The main challenge is that strong emotions can sometimes be mistaken for genuine understanding or connection. The Pluto person may have a clear sense of the Sun person''s vulnerabilities, desires, and emotional needs, which can create a powerful bond. If this dynamic is handled poorly, however, it can become overwhelming. The Sun person may find it difficult to maintain perspective or create healthy distance when needed.

This aspect can be deeply transformative, but it''s important to stay connected to your own center as it unfolds. Keep your boundaries clear and trust your own perspective, even when the connection feels powerful. Let the relationship teach you what it has to teach, but remember that growth doesn''t require giving away your agency.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can feel like an obsession before you have words for why.\n\nThe charge is immediate. Electric. Unsettling. It can feel as though the Pluto person recognizes something in you that even you have not fully claimed. You may feel exposed, chosen, pulled into a current so powerful that ordinary attraction suddenly feels insignificant.\n\nThere is a raw magnetism here that is difficult to resist. The Pluto person often awakens something dormant in the Sun person. Buried desires, hidden strengths, long-forgotten hungers, and truths that have been waiting beneath the surface. Their fascination can feel intoxicating. Their presence can make the Sun person feel more alive, more visible, more powerful than they have in a very long time.\n\nBut Pluto does not touch anything lightly. The conjunction amplifies everything. Desire becomes consuming. Curiosity becomes fixation. Intimacy becomes a force that can alter the landscape of both people''s lives. What feels like deep recognition can slowly become entanglement. What feels like devotion can become possession. The main challenge is that strong emotions can sometimes be mistaken for genuine understanding or connection. The Pluto person may have a clear sense of the Sun person''s vulnerabilities, desires, and emotional needs, which can create a powerful bond. If this dynamic is handled poorly, however, it can become overwhelming. The Sun person may find it difficult to maintain perspective or create healthy distance when needed.\n\nThis aspect can be deeply transformative, but it''s important to stay connected to your own center as it unfolds. Keep your boundaries clear and trust your own perspective, even when the connection feels powerful. Let the relationship teach you what it has to teach, but remember that growth doesn''t require giving away your agency."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But Pluto does not touch anything lightly. The conjunction amplifies everything. Desire becomes consuming. Curiosity becomes fixation. Intimacy becomes a force that can alter the landscape of both people''s lives. What feels like deep recognition can slowly become entanglement. What feels like devotion can become possession. The main challenge is that strong emotions can sometimes be mistaken for genuine understanding or connection. The Pluto person may have a clear sense of the Sun person''s vulnerabilities, desires, and emotional needs, which can create a powerful bond. If this dynamic is handled poorly, however, it can become overwhelming. The Sun person may find it difficult to maintain perspective or create healthy distance when needed."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This aspect can be deeply transformative, but it''s important to stay connected to your own center as it unfolds. Keep your boundaries clear and trust your own perspective, even when the connection feels powerful. Let the relationship teach you what it has to teach, but remember that growth doesn''t require giving away your agency."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-sun_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A total transformation of the Sun person''s sense of self, driven by the Pluto person. Magnetic, intense, sometimes a crisis, ultimately a rebuild. Failure mode: power struggles over who the Sun person gets to be - control dressed as devotion. Let the old self go where it needs to, watch for domination, and remember intensity isn''t the same as a good fit.","summaryDeep":"This person can feel like an obsession before you have words for why.\n\nThe charge is immediate. Electric. Unsettling. It can feel as though the Pluto person recognizes something in you that even you have not fully claimed. You may feel exposed, chosen, pulled into a current so powerful that ordinary attraction suddenly feels insignificant.\n\nThere is a raw magnetism here that is difficult to resist. The Pluto person often awakens something dormant in the Sun person. Buried desires, hidden strengths, long-forgotten hungers, and truths that have been waiting beneath the surface. Their fascination can feel intoxicating. Their presence can make the Sun person feel more alive, more visible, more powerful than they have in a very long time.\n\nBut Pluto does not touch anything lightly. The conjunction amplifies everything. Desire becomes consuming. Curiosity becomes fixation. Intimacy becomes a force that can alter the landscape of both people''s lives. What feels like deep recognition can slowly become entanglement. What feels like devotion can become possession. The main challenge is that strong emotions can sometimes be mistaken for genuine understanding or connection. The Pluto person may have a clear sense of the Sun person''s vulnerabilities, desires, and emotional needs, which can create a powerful bond. If this dynamic is handled poorly, however, it can become overwhelming. The Sun person may find it difficult to maintain perspective or create healthy distance when needed.\n\nThis aspect can be deeply transformative, but it''s important to stay connected to your own center as it unfolds. Keep your boundaries clear and trust your own perspective, even when the connection feels powerful. Let the relationship teach you what it has to teach, but remember that growth doesn''t require giving away your agency.","tension":"But Pluto does not touch anything lightly. The conjunction amplifies everything. Desire becomes consuming. Curiosity becomes fixation. Intimacy becomes a force that can alter the landscape of both people''s lives. What feels like deep recognition can slowly become entanglement. What feels like devotion can become possession. The main challenge is that strong emotions can sometimes be mistaken for genuine understanding or connection. The Pluto person may have a clear sense of the Sun person''s vulnerabilities, desires, and emotional needs, which can create a powerful bond. If this dynamic is handled poorly, however, it can become overwhelming. The Sun person may find it difficult to maintain perspective or create healthy distance when needed.","advice":"This aspect can be deeply transformative, but it''s important to stay connected to your own center as it unfolds. Keep your boundaries clear and trust your own perspective, even when the connection feels powerful. Let the relationship teach you what it has to teach, but remember that growth doesn''t require giving away your agency.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"sun","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry-pluto-opposition-sun', 'relationship-pluto-opposition-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-sun_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-sun_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Opposition Sun', null, 'This person may arrive as a mirror you didn''t ask for but cannot look away from. There is a powerful pull here, but it rarely comes without tension. The Pluto person often reflects back what the Sun person has not yet fully claimed, acknowledged, or understood about themselves. The attraction can feel undeniable, carrying the weight of recognition, as though something ancient has been awakened. At the same time, it can feel deeply uncomfortable. Being seen this clearly is not always easy.

At its best, this aspect invites self-awareness. The Pluto person challenges the Sun person to move beyond old identities, inherited stories, and carefully maintained appearances. Through the friction of difference, both people are asked to grow. The relationship can become a catalyst for honesty, helping each person encounter truths that might otherwise remain hidden.

But Pluto''s gifts are rarely offered without shadow work. This connection can activate questions of power, trust, and vulnerability. The Pluto person may instinctively sense where the Sun person feels most exposed, carrying an uncanny awareness of their fears, desires, and unspoken wounds. When that insight is used with care, it can deepen intimacy and understanding. When it is not, the dynamic can become imbalanced. One person may feel picked apart while the other gains the upper hand. The attraction can be intense, but so can the discomfort. This is the kind of bond that can become obsessive, controlling, and difficult to walk away from.

The key here is mutual respect. Without it, strong feelings can turn into control, and honesty can be used to hurt instead of help. This aspect asks both people to take responsibility for their own actions while being mindful of each other''s vulnerability.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may arrive as a mirror you didn''t ask for but cannot look away from. There is a powerful pull here, but it rarely comes without tension. The Pluto person often reflects back what the Sun person has not yet fully claimed, acknowledged, or understood about themselves. The attraction can feel undeniable, carrying the weight of recognition, as though something ancient has been awakened. At the same time, it can feel deeply uncomfortable. Being seen this clearly is not always easy.\n\nAt its best, this aspect invites self-awareness. The Pluto person challenges the Sun person to move beyond old identities, inherited stories, and carefully maintained appearances. Through the friction of difference, both people are asked to grow. The relationship can become a catalyst for honesty, helping each person encounter truths that might otherwise remain hidden.\n\nBut Pluto''s gifts are rarely offered without shadow work. This connection can activate questions of power, trust, and vulnerability. The Pluto person may instinctively sense where the Sun person feels most exposed, carrying an uncanny awareness of their fears, desires, and unspoken wounds. When that insight is used with care, it can deepen intimacy and understanding. When it is not, the dynamic can become imbalanced. One person may feel picked apart while the other gains the upper hand. The attraction can be intense, but so can the discomfort. This is the kind of bond that can become obsessive, controlling, and difficult to walk away from.\n\nThe key here is mutual respect. Without it, strong feelings can turn into control, and honesty can be used to hurt instead of help. This aspect asks both people to take responsibility for their own actions while being mindful of each other''s vulnerability."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But Pluto''s gifts are rarely offered without shadow work. This connection can activate questions of power, trust, and vulnerability. The Pluto person may instinctively sense where the Sun person feels most exposed, carrying an uncanny awareness of their fears, desires, and unspoken wounds. When that insight is used with care, it can deepen intimacy and understanding. When it is not, the dynamic can become imbalanced. One person may feel picked apart while the other gains the upper hand. The attraction can be intense, but so can the discomfort. This is the kind of bond that can become obsessive, controlling, and difficult to walk away from."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The key here is mutual respect. Without it, strong feelings can turn into control, and honesty can be used to hurt instead of help. This aspect asks both people to take responsibility for their own actions while being mindful of each other''s vulnerability."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-sun_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Power and control surfacing through the other person. Your autonomy gets tested - someone wants to steer who you are. Failure mode: a battle of wills over identity. Name the game, hold your ground without becoming controlling yourself, and don''t confuse the intensity for closeness.","summaryDeep":"This person may arrive as a mirror you didn''t ask for but cannot look away from. There is a powerful pull here, but it rarely comes without tension. The Pluto person often reflects back what the Sun person has not yet fully claimed, acknowledged, or understood about themselves. The attraction can feel undeniable, carrying the weight of recognition, as though something ancient has been awakened. At the same time, it can feel deeply uncomfortable. Being seen this clearly is not always easy.\n\nAt its best, this aspect invites self-awareness. The Pluto person challenges the Sun person to move beyond old identities, inherited stories, and carefully maintained appearances. Through the friction of difference, both people are asked to grow. The relationship can become a catalyst for honesty, helping each person encounter truths that might otherwise remain hidden.\n\nBut Pluto''s gifts are rarely offered without shadow work. This connection can activate questions of power, trust, and vulnerability. The Pluto person may instinctively sense where the Sun person feels most exposed, carrying an uncanny awareness of their fears, desires, and unspoken wounds. When that insight is used with care, it can deepen intimacy and understanding. When it is not, the dynamic can become imbalanced. One person may feel picked apart while the other gains the upper hand. The attraction can be intense, but so can the discomfort. This is the kind of bond that can become obsessive, controlling, and difficult to walk away from.\n\nThe key here is mutual respect. Without it, strong feelings can turn into control, and honesty can be used to hurt instead of help. This aspect asks both people to take responsibility for their own actions while being mindful of each other''s vulnerability.","tension":"But Pluto''s gifts are rarely offered without shadow work. This connection can activate questions of power, trust, and vulnerability. The Pluto person may instinctively sense where the Sun person feels most exposed, carrying an uncanny awareness of their fears, desires, and unspoken wounds. When that insight is used with care, it can deepen intimacy and understanding. When it is not, the dynamic can become imbalanced. One person may feel picked apart while the other gains the upper hand. The attraction can be intense, but so can the discomfort. This is the kind of bond that can become obsessive, controlling, and difficult to walk away from.","advice":"The key here is mutual respect. Without it, strong feelings can turn into control, and honesty can be used to hurt instead of help. This aspect asks both people to take responsibility for their own actions while being mindful of each other''s vulnerability.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-sun_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"sun","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-sun_sextile', 'synastry-pluto-sextile-sun', 'relationship-pluto-sextile-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-sun_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-sun_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Sextile Sun', null, 'This connection carries a quiet kind of magic. Nothing is demanded of you here. Nothing is ripped open before you''re ready. Instead, the Pluto person may recognize gifts, truths, and untapped power within the Sun person long before those qualities have fully emerged. There is depth in this bond, but it moves gently, like an invitation rather than a command.

When nurtured consciously, this aspect can become a beautiful catalyst for growth. The Pluto person may inspire the Sun person to trust their inner authority, pursue what feels deeply meaningful, and step more fully into their own power. In return, the Sun person''s vitality, creativity, and sense of purpose can help the Pluto person direct their intensity toward healing, creation, and transformation.

The beauty of this aspect is that it honors free will. Growth is available, but it is never forced. The doorway is open, yet each person must choose whether to walk through it. The more willing both people are to meet themselves honestly, the more wisdom and empowerment this connection can reveal.

The shadow here is not overwhelm but inertia. Because the energy flows so naturally, it can be easy to enjoy the connection without exploring its deeper potential. The relationship may remain supportive and meaningful while deeper layers of healing, self-discovery, and transformation quietly wait to be claimed.

Stay curious about what this person awakens within you. Notice the parts of yourself that become more visible in their presence. Pay attention to the truths that rise gently to the surface. Let the connection deepen your relationship with yourself while remaining rooted in your own center. Transformation does not always arrive through crisis or upheaval. Sometimes it unfolds through trust.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection carries a quiet kind of magic. Nothing is demanded of you here. Nothing is ripped open before you''re ready. Instead, the Pluto person may recognize gifts, truths, and untapped power within the Sun person long before those qualities have fully emerged. There is depth in this bond, but it moves gently, like an invitation rather than a command.\n\nWhen nurtured consciously, this aspect can become a beautiful catalyst for growth. The Pluto person may inspire the Sun person to trust their inner authority, pursue what feels deeply meaningful, and step more fully into their own power. In return, the Sun person''s vitality, creativity, and sense of purpose can help the Pluto person direct their intensity toward healing, creation, and transformation.\n\nThe beauty of this aspect is that it honors free will. Growth is available, but it is never forced. The doorway is open, yet each person must choose whether to walk through it. The more willing both people are to meet themselves honestly, the more wisdom and empowerment this connection can reveal.\n\nThe shadow here is not overwhelm but inertia. Because the energy flows so naturally, it can be easy to enjoy the connection without exploring its deeper potential. The relationship may remain supportive and meaningful while deeper layers of healing, self-discovery, and transformation quietly wait to be claimed.\n\nStay curious about what this person awakens within you. Notice the parts of yourself that become more visible in their presence. Pay attention to the truths that rise gently to the surface. Let the connection deepen your relationship with yourself while remaining rooted in your own center. Transformation does not always arrive through crisis or upheaval. Sometimes it unfolds through trust."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The shadow here is not overwhelm but inertia. Because the energy flows so naturally, it can be easy to enjoy the connection without exploring its deeper potential. The relationship may remain supportive and meaningful while deeper layers of healing, self-discovery, and transformation quietly wait to be claimed."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Stay curious about what this person awakens within you. Notice the parts of yourself that become more visible in their presence. Pay attention to the truths that rise gently to the surface. Let the connection deepen your relationship with yourself while remaining rooted in your own center. Transformation does not always arrive through crisis or upheaval. Sometimes it unfolds through trust."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-sun_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"An opening for real, chosen growth. You can go deeper and change in a way that empowers rather than overpowers. Failure mode: flinching from the harder step. Take it - this contact rewards depth you choose.","summaryDeep":"This connection carries a quiet kind of magic. Nothing is demanded of you here. Nothing is ripped open before you''re ready. Instead, the Pluto person may recognize gifts, truths, and untapped power within the Sun person long before those qualities have fully emerged. There is depth in this bond, but it moves gently, like an invitation rather than a command.\n\nWhen nurtured consciously, this aspect can become a beautiful catalyst for growth. The Pluto person may inspire the Sun person to trust their inner authority, pursue what feels deeply meaningful, and step more fully into their own power. In return, the Sun person''s vitality, creativity, and sense of purpose can help the Pluto person direct their intensity toward healing, creation, and transformation.\n\nThe beauty of this aspect is that it honors free will. Growth is available, but it is never forced. The doorway is open, yet each person must choose whether to walk through it. The more willing both people are to meet themselves honestly, the more wisdom and empowerment this connection can reveal.\n\nThe shadow here is not overwhelm but inertia. Because the energy flows so naturally, it can be easy to enjoy the connection without exploring its deeper potential. The relationship may remain supportive and meaningful while deeper layers of healing, self-discovery, and transformation quietly wait to be claimed.\n\nStay curious about what this person awakens within you. Notice the parts of yourself that become more visible in their presence. Pay attention to the truths that rise gently to the surface. Let the connection deepen your relationship with yourself while remaining rooted in your own center. Transformation does not always arrive through crisis or upheaval. Sometimes it unfolds through trust.","tension":"The shadow here is not overwhelm but inertia. Because the energy flows so naturally, it can be easy to enjoy the connection without exploring its deeper potential. The relationship may remain supportive and meaningful while deeper layers of healing, self-discovery, and transformation quietly wait to be claimed.","advice":"Stay curious about what this person awakens within you. Notice the parts of yourself that become more visible in their presence. Pay attention to the truths that rise gently to the surface. Let the connection deepen your relationship with yourself while remaining rooted in your own center. Transformation does not always arrive through crisis or upheaval. Sometimes it unfolds through trust.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-sun_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"sun","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-sun_square', 'synastry-pluto-square-sun', 'relationship-pluto-square-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-sun_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-sun_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Square Sun', null, 'This person gets under your skin. The square brings friction, pressure, and a kind of psychological heat that is hard to ignore. The Pluto person may stir something in the Sun person that has been buried for a long time. Old defenses rise. Hidden fears surface. Reactions may feel bigger than the moment itself.

There is magnetism here, but it is rarely simple. You may find yourself drawn back to this person again and again, even when the connection feels uncomfortable or exposes tender places within you. Interactions can stir powerful emotional reactions that seem larger than the circumstances at hand, bringing buried fears, insecurities, and unmet needs to the surface. In trying to protect what feels vulnerable, both people may be tempted to grasp for certainty, influence outcomes, or hold each other too tightly.

When handled in a healthy way, this aspect can help both people grow. The Pluto person may point out areas where the Sun person has given away their power, avoided facing the truth, or stayed in situations that feel comfortable but are no longer good for them. Even though this can be uncomfortable, the challenges between them can bring old habits to the surface and create an opportunity for real change.

But pressure is not always growth.

If this relationship consistently brings up strong emotions or challenges, it''s worth paying attention to how those experiences are affecting both of you. Intense connections can be deeply meaningful and transformative, but they can also highlight areas where growth, communication, or clearer boundaries are needed.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person gets under your skin. The square brings friction, pressure, and a kind of psychological heat that is hard to ignore. The Pluto person may stir something in the Sun person that has been buried for a long time. Old defenses rise. Hidden fears surface. Reactions may feel bigger than the moment itself.\n\nThere is magnetism here, but it is rarely simple. You may find yourself drawn back to this person again and again, even when the connection feels uncomfortable or exposes tender places within you. Interactions can stir powerful emotional reactions that seem larger than the circumstances at hand, bringing buried fears, insecurities, and unmet needs to the surface. In trying to protect what feels vulnerable, both people may be tempted to grasp for certainty, influence outcomes, or hold each other too tightly.\n\nWhen handled in a healthy way, this aspect can help both people grow. The Pluto person may point out areas where the Sun person has given away their power, avoided facing the truth, or stayed in situations that feel comfortable but are no longer good for them. Even though this can be uncomfortable, the challenges between them can bring old habits to the surface and create an opportunity for real change.\n\nBut pressure is not always growth.\n\nIf this relationship consistently brings up strong emotions or challenges, it''s worth paying attention to how those experiences are affecting both of you. Intense connections can be deeply meaningful and transformative, but they can also highlight areas where growth, communication, or clearer boundaries are needed."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But pressure is not always growth."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"If this relationship consistently brings up strong emotions or challenges, it''s worth paying attention to how those experiences are affecting both of you. Intense connections can be deeply meaningful and transformative, but they can also highlight areas where growth, communication, or clearer boundaries are needed."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-sun_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Pressure to change, hard, with power struggles built in. Control, intimidation, a forced accounting over identity and autonomy. Failure mode: gripping for control, or being remade against your will. Drop what''s genuinely ending in you but hold your autonomy; if someone''s trying to dominate who you are, that''s the signal to step back.","summaryDeep":"This person gets under your skin. The square brings friction, pressure, and a kind of psychological heat that is hard to ignore. The Pluto person may stir something in the Sun person that has been buried for a long time. Old defenses rise. Hidden fears surface. Reactions may feel bigger than the moment itself.\n\nThere is magnetism here, but it is rarely simple. You may find yourself drawn back to this person again and again, even when the connection feels uncomfortable or exposes tender places within you. Interactions can stir powerful emotional reactions that seem larger than the circumstances at hand, bringing buried fears, insecurities, and unmet needs to the surface. In trying to protect what feels vulnerable, both people may be tempted to grasp for certainty, influence outcomes, or hold each other too tightly.\n\nWhen handled in a healthy way, this aspect can help both people grow. The Pluto person may point out areas where the Sun person has given away their power, avoided facing the truth, or stayed in situations that feel comfortable but are no longer good for them. Even though this can be uncomfortable, the challenges between them can bring old habits to the surface and create an opportunity for real change.\n\nBut pressure is not always growth.\n\nIf this relationship consistently brings up strong emotions or challenges, it''s worth paying attention to how those experiences are affecting both of you. Intense connections can be deeply meaningful and transformative, but they can also highlight areas where growth, communication, or clearer boundaries are needed.","tension":"But pressure is not always growth.","advice":"If this relationship consistently brings up strong emotions or challenges, it''s worth paying attention to how those experiences are affecting both of you. Intense connections can be deeply meaningful and transformative, but they can also highlight areas where growth, communication, or clearer boundaries are needed.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-sun_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"sun","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-sun_trine', 'synastry-pluto-trine-sun', 'relationship-pluto-trine-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-sun_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-sun_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Trine Sun', null, 'This connection carries depth without demanding crisis. When one person''s Pluto forms a trine to another person''s Sun, there is often a natural sense of trust between them, as though vulnerability can emerge without force. The Pluto person tends to recognize the Sun person''s strengths, fears, and untapped potential with remarkable clarity, yet their insight feels supportive rather than invasive. In response, the Sun person may feel deeply seen and accepted, making it easier to show up authentically, speak honestly, and grow into more of who they are.

There is still intensity here. Pluto never loses its capacity to transform. But the energy tends to flow with less resistance than it does in the conjunction, square, or opposition. Instead of forcing change through crisis, this aspect often supports growth through encouragement, insight, and mutual respect.

At its best, the Pluto person helps the Sun person recognize their own power. They may inspire greater confidence, emotional honesty, and a willingness to step more fully into life. The Sun person often feels strengthened by the connection, as though someone is quietly reminding them of who they are beneath old fears and limiting stories.

One of the gifts of this aspect is the way it can make growth feel safe. The relationship often creates enough trust for both people to be honest about who they are and what they are moving through. Instead of forcing change through crisis or conflict, it can support a more natural process of self-discovery. That said, it is still a Pluto aspect, and Pluto''s influence is rarely insignificant. Because the connection flows so easily, it can be easy to miss just how much impact the relationship is having. The Pluto person may carry more influence than either person realizes, and the Sun person may not always notice how deeply they are being shaped by the bond.

