  ('A-pluto_B-uranus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"uranus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-uranus_trine', 'synastry-pluto-trine-uranus', 'relationship-pluto-trine-uranus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-uranus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-uranus_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Trine Uranus', null, 'A''s depth and power meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Translation","body":"A''s depth and power meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-uranus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s depth and power meets B''s need for freedom. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":null,"tension":null,"advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":null,"weight":null}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-venus_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"venus","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-venus_conjunction', 'synastry-pluto-conjunction-venus', 'relationship-pluto-conjunction-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-venus_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-venus_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Conjunction Venus', null, 'The attraction here can feel immediate, consuming, and hard to explain.

Venus-Pluto conjunctions often create a powerful magnetic pull. The Pluto person may feel intensely drawn to the Venus person''s beauty, softness, affection, or desirability. The Venus person may feel wanted in a way that feels rare, almost overwhelming, as though the Pluto person sees something in them that others only skim past.

At first, this can feel incredible. The chemistry can be strong, the emotional charge difficult to ignore, and the sense of recognition deeply intoxicating. The Pluto person often wants access to more than surface affection. They want the deeper layer, the hidden desire, the part of the Venus person that is not offered casually.

At its best, this aspect can create deep intimacy. It can help both people become more honest about what they want, what they fear, and how vulnerable it feels to be desired deeply. Love can become transformative here, not because it is easy, but because it asks both people to show up with less pretense.

But this aspect can become consuming quickly. The desire to be close can become the need to possess. Attraction can become obsession. The Pluto person may become controlling, jealous, or fixated on maintaining access to the Venus person. The Venus person may begin to feel dependent on the Pluto person''s attention, approval, or desire. This is one of the clearest Venus-Pluto indicators of a bond that can be hard to leave when it is handled poorly. The intensity can feel like proof that the connection matters, even when the relationship is costing one or both people their peace.

The lesson is simple: being wanted deeply is not the same as being loved well.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"The attraction here can feel immediate, consuming, and hard to explain.\n\nVenus-Pluto conjunctions often create a powerful magnetic pull. The Pluto person may feel intensely drawn to the Venus person''s beauty, softness, affection, or desirability. The Venus person may feel wanted in a way that feels rare, almost overwhelming, as though the Pluto person sees something in them that others only skim past.\n\nAt first, this can feel incredible. The chemistry can be strong, the emotional charge difficult to ignore, and the sense of recognition deeply intoxicating. The Pluto person often wants access to more than surface affection. They want the deeper layer, the hidden desire, the part of the Venus person that is not offered casually.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can create deep intimacy. It can help both people become more honest about what they want, what they fear, and how vulnerable it feels to be desired deeply. Love can become transformative here, not because it is easy, but because it asks both people to show up with less pretense.\n\nBut this aspect can become consuming quickly. The desire to be close can become the need to possess. Attraction can become obsession. The Pluto person may become controlling, jealous, or fixated on maintaining access to the Venus person. The Venus person may begin to feel dependent on the Pluto person''s attention, approval, or desire. This is one of the clearest Venus-Pluto indicators of a bond that can be hard to leave when it is handled poorly. The intensity can feel like proof that the connection matters, even when the relationship is costing one or both people their peace.\n\nThe lesson is simple: being wanted deeply is not the same as being loved well."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But this aspect can become consuming quickly. The desire to be close can become the need to possess. Attraction can become obsession. The Pluto person may become controlling, jealous, or fixated on maintaining access to the Venus person. The Venus person may begin to feel dependent on the Pluto person''s attention, approval, or desire. This is one of the clearest Venus-Pluto indicators of a bond that can be hard to leave when it is handled poorly. The intensity can feel like proof that the connection matters, even when the relationship is costing one or both people their peace."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The lesson is simple: being wanted deeply is not the same as being loved well."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-venus_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Obsessive, magnetic, all-consuming attraction. You bond at the root and the pull is enormous - and so is the possessiveness. It transforms how the Venus person loves, sometimes beautifully, sometimes through loss. Failure mode: jealousy, control, and the inability to let go when it''s over. Magnetic and bad-for-you can be the same bond - name which one this is, and if it runs on control, that''s not love.","summaryDeep":"The attraction here can feel immediate, consuming, and hard to explain.\n\nVenus-Pluto conjunctions often create a powerful magnetic pull. The Pluto person may feel intensely drawn to the Venus person''s beauty, softness, affection, or desirability. The Venus person may feel wanted in a way that feels rare, almost overwhelming, as though the Pluto person sees something in them that others only skim past.\n\nAt first, this can feel incredible. The chemistry can be strong, the emotional charge difficult to ignore, and the sense of recognition deeply intoxicating. The Pluto person often wants access to more than surface affection. They want the deeper layer, the hidden desire, the part of the Venus person that is not offered casually.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can create deep intimacy. It can help both people become more honest about what they want, what they fear, and how vulnerable it feels to be desired deeply. Love can become transformative here, not because it is easy, but because it asks both people to show up with less pretense.\n\nBut this aspect can become consuming quickly. The desire to be close can become the need to possess. Attraction can become obsession. The Pluto person may become controlling, jealous, or fixated on maintaining access to the Venus person. The Venus person may begin to feel dependent on the Pluto person''s attention, approval, or desire. This is one of the clearest Venus-Pluto indicators of a bond that can be hard to leave when it is handled poorly. The intensity can feel like proof that the connection matters, even when the relationship is costing one or both people their peace.\n\nThe lesson is simple: being wanted deeply is not the same as being loved well.","tension":"But this aspect can become consuming quickly. The desire to be close can become the need to possess. Attraction can become obsession. The Pluto person may become controlling, jealous, or fixated on maintaining access to the Venus person. The Venus person may begin to feel dependent on the Pluto person''s attention, approval, or desire. This is one of the clearest Venus-Pluto indicators of a bond that can be hard to leave when it is handled poorly. The intensity can feel like proof that the connection matters, even when the relationship is costing one or both people their peace.","advice":"The lesson is simple: being wanted deeply is not the same as being loved well.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-venus_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"venus","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-venus_opposition', 'synastry-pluto-opposition-venus', 'relationship-pluto-opposition-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-venus_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-venus_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Opposition Venus', null, 'This person may pull at your desire in a way that feels magnetic and unsettling at the same time. There is often a strong attraction here, but it can come with a sense of imbalance. The Pluto person may seem to reach the Venus person''s deeper wants, insecurities, and need for validation while remaining somewhat harder to read themselves. The Venus person may feel deeply desired, but also exposed, vulnerable, or unsure of where they stand.

At its healthiest, this aspect can bring honesty to the surface. The Pluto person may help the Venus person recognize what they truly want in love, where they seek approval, and where they have confused being desired with being secure. The Venus person can soften the Pluto person''s intensity, helping them experience love with more openness and less control.

But this aspect can also become a power struggle around love and desire. One person may reach while the other withdraws. One person may need reassurance while the other protects their power by staying mysterious, unavailable, or hard to pin down. Jealousy, possessiveness, testing, and withdrawal games can emerge when fear takes over. The bond can become difficult to step away from, because it activates desire so strongly. Wanting someone can begin to feel like needing them. Being wanted can begin to feel like proof of worth.

The work is staying anchored in your own value. Both people need to be honest about what they want without using affection, distance, jealousy, or desire as tools for control. This connection can deepen love when vulnerability is respected. Without that respect, attraction can become destabilizing.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may pull at your desire in a way that feels magnetic and unsettling at the same time. There is often a strong attraction here, but it can come with a sense of imbalance. The Pluto person may seem to reach the Venus person''s deeper wants, insecurities, and need for validation while remaining somewhat harder to read themselves. The Venus person may feel deeply desired, but also exposed, vulnerable, or unsure of where they stand.\n\nAt its healthiest, this aspect can bring honesty to the surface. The Pluto person may help the Venus person recognize what they truly want in love, where they seek approval, and where they have confused being desired with being secure. The Venus person can soften the Pluto person''s intensity, helping them experience love with more openness and less control.\n\nBut this aspect can also become a power struggle around love and desire. One person may reach while the other withdraws. One person may need reassurance while the other protects their power by staying mysterious, unavailable, or hard to pin down. Jealousy, possessiveness, testing, and withdrawal games can emerge when fear takes over. The bond can become difficult to step away from, because it activates desire so strongly. Wanting someone can begin to feel like needing them. Being wanted can begin to feel like proof of worth.\n\nThe work is staying anchored in your own value. Both people need to be honest about what they want without using affection, distance, jealousy, or desire as tools for control. This connection can deepen love when vulnerability is respected. Without that respect, attraction can become destabilizing."},{"h