try-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"venus","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry-pluto-sextile-venus', 'relationship-pluto-sextile-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-venus_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-venus_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Sextile Venus', null, 'This connection has the potential to create deep attraction, trust, and emotional honesty over time. The Pluto person may sense something beneath the Venus person''s surface: a hidden desire, a guarded softness, a deeper need to be loved and chosen. The Venus person may feel drawn to the Pluto person''s depth, intensity, and emotional presence without feeling immediately overwhelmed by it.

There is magnetism here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured consciously, it can become a strong foundation for intimacy. The Pluto person may help the Venus person become more honest about what they want and what they value. The Venus person may help the Pluto person soften their intensity and trust love without needing to control it.

One of the strengths of this aspect is that it does not rush transformation. The opportunity for depth is there, but both people have to engage it. The relationship tends to grow through trust, honest affection, and a willingness to explore what lives beneath attraction.

The challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to enjoy the chemistry without fully exploring the deeper emotional work available between you. If both people avoid vulnerability, the relationship may remain pleasant, magnetic, and supportive, but some of its most transformative gifts may stay unopened.

Let the connection deepen at a pace that feels safe. Be honest about desire without turning it into control. The gift of this aspect is not intensity for its own sake. It is the chance to experience love as something that transforms without consuming.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection has the potential to create deep attraction, trust, and emotional honesty over time. The Pluto person may sense something beneath the Venus person''s surface: a hidden desire, a guarded softness, a deeper need to be loved and chosen. The Venus person may feel drawn to the Pluto person''s depth, intensity, and emotional presence without feeling immediately overwhelmed by it.\n\nThere is magnetism here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured consciously, it can become a strong foundation for intimacy. The Pluto person may help the Venus person become more honest about what they want and what they value. The Venus person may help the Pluto person soften their intensity and trust love without needing to control it.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is that it does not rush transformation. The opportunity for depth is there, but both people have to engage it. The relationship tends to grow through trust, honest affection, and a willingness to explore what lives beneath attraction.\n\nThe challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to enjoy the chemistry without fully exploring the deeper emotional work available between you. If both people avoid vulnerability, the relationship may remain pleasant, magnetic, and supportive, but some of its most transformative gifts may stay unopened.\n\nLet the connection deepen at a pace that feels safe. Be honest about desire without turning it into control. The gift of this aspect is not intensity for its own sake. It is the chance to experience love as something that transforms without consuming."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to enjoy the chemistry without fully exploring the deeper emotional work available between you. If both people avoid vulnerability, the relationship may remain pleasant, magnetic, and supportive, but some of its most transformative gifts may stay unopened."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the connection deepen at a pace that feels safe. Be honest about desire without turning it into control. The gift of this aspect is not intensity for its own sake. It is the chance to experience love as something that transforms without consuming."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-venus_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"An opening for deeper intimacy and honest bonding. The intensity is available without the war - you can go deep by choice. Failure mode: staying on the surface out of fear of the depth. Take the vulnerable step; this one rewards courage.","summaryDeep":"This connection has the potential to create deep attraction, trust, and emotional honesty over time. The Pluto person may sense something beneath the Venus person''s surface: a hidden desire, a guarded softness, a deeper need to be loved and chosen. The Venus person may feel drawn to the Pluto person''s depth, intensity, and emotional presence without feeling immediately overwhelmed by it.\n\nThere is magnetism here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured consciously, it can become a strong foundation for intimacy. The Pluto person may help the Venus person become more honest about what they want and what they value. The Venus person may help the Pluto person soften their intensity and trust love without needing to control it.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is that it does not rush transformation. The opportunity for depth is there, but both people have to engage it. The relationship tends to grow through trust, honest affection, and a willingness to explore what lives beneath attraction.\n\nThe challenge