  ('A-pluto_B-venus_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"venus","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-venus_square', 'synastry-pluto-square-venus', 'relationship-pluto-square-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-venus_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-venus_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Square Venus', null, 'This connection can stir desire in a way that feels powerful, uncomfortable, and difficult to ignore. Venus-Pluto squares often arrive with chemistry. Not light chemistry, but the kind that exposes what people want, fear, envy, crave, or feel ashamed of wanting. The Pluto person may activate the Venus person''s deeper insecurities around beauty, desirability, worth, and love. The Venus person may awaken the Pluto person''s hunger for closeness, control, or emotional certainty.

There is often a strong pull toward one another, even when the connection feels complicated. The attraction may feel intense, but not necessarily peaceful. Both people can find themselves drawn into dynamics that feel larger than the moment itself, as though the relationship has tapped into deeper patterns around love, rejection, longing, or power.

At its best, this aspect can be transformative. It can reveal where love has become tangled with control, where desire has become confused with validation, and where old relationship patterns are ready to be seen more clearly. The tension can force honesty about what each person truly wants and what they are afraid of losing.

But pressure is not the same as love. When this aspect becomes unconscious, the relationship can start running on jealousy, testing, withdrawal, rupture, reunion, and emotional intensity. One person may try to regain power by pulling away. The other may chase harder. The connection can become addictive, not because it is healthy, but because the highs and lows keep activating the desire to be chosen. Pay attention to what this bond brings out in you. Do you feel more confident, more honest, and more connected to your own worth? Or do you feel consumed by the need to be wanted, reassured, or chosen?

You do not have to call possession love. You do not have to stay in a painful cycle because the chemistry is strong. The wisdom of this aspect comes from learning the difference between desire that transforms you and desire that destabilizes you.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection can stir desire in a way that feels powerful, uncomfortable, and difficult to ignore. Venus-Pluto squares often arrive with chemistry. Not light chemistry, but the kind that exposes what people want, fear, envy, crave, or feel ashamed of wanting. The Pluto person may activate the Venus person''s deeper insecurities around beauty, desirability, worth, and love. The Venus person may awaken the Pluto person''s hunger for closeness, control, or emotional certainty.\n\nThere is often a strong pull toward one another, even when the connection feels complicated. The attraction may feel intense, but not necessarily peaceful. Both people can find themselves drawn into dynamics that feel larger than the moment itself, as though the relationship has tapped into deeper patterns around love, rejection, longing, or power.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can be transformative. It can reveal where love has become tangled with control, where desire has become confused with validation, and where old relationship patterns are ready to be seen more clearly. The tension can force honesty about what each person truly wants and what they are afraid of losing.\n\nBut pressure is not the same as love. When this aspect becomes unconscious, the relationship can start running on jealousy, testing, withdrawal, rupture, reunion, and emotional intensity. One person may try to regain power by pulling away. The other may chase harder. The connection can become addictive, not because it is healthy, but because the highs and lows keep activating the desire to be chosen. Pay attention to what this bond brings out in you. Do you feel more confident, more honest, and more connected to your own worth? Or do you feel consumed by the need to be wanted, reassured, or chosen?\n\nYou do not have to call possession love. You do not have to stay in a painful cycle because the chemistry is strong. The wisdom of this aspect comes from learning the difference between desire that transforms you and desire that destabilizes you."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But pressure is not the same as love. When this aspect becomes unconscious, the relationship can start running on jealousy, testing, withdrawal, rupture, reunion, and emotional intensity. One person may try to regain power by pulling away. The other may chase harder. The connection can become addictive, not because it is healthy, but because the highs and lows keep activating the desire to be chosen. Pay attention to what this bond brings out in you. Do you feel more confident, more honest, and more connected to your own worth? Or do you feel consumed by the need to be wanted, reassured, or chosen?"},{"heading":"Advice","body":"You do not have to call possession love. You do not have to stay in a painful cycle because the chemistry is strong. The wisdom of this aspect comes from learning the difference between desire that transforms you and desire that destabilizes you."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-venus_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Love turned into a power struggle. Possessiveness, jealousy, control, the urge to remake the other person. Failure mode: mistaking obsession for passion and tightening your grip. Drop the control - trust it or release it. Intensity is not compatibility, and a bond that runs on fear isn''t a deep one.","summaryDeep":"This connection can stir desire in a way that feels powerful, uncomfortable, and difficult to ignore. Venus-Pluto squares often arrive with chemistry. Not light chemistry, but the kind that exposes what people want, fear, envy, crave, or feel ashamed of wanting. The Pluto person may activate the Venus person''s deeper insecurities around beauty, desirability, worth, and love. The Venus person may awaken the Pluto person''s hunger for closeness, control, or emotional certainty.\n\nThere is often a strong pull toward one another, even when the connection feels complicated. The attraction may feel intense, but not necessarily peaceful. Both people can find themselves drawn into dynamics that feel larger than the moment itself, as though the relationship has tapped into deeper patterns around love, rejection, longing, or power.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can be transformative. It can reveal where love has become tangled with control, where desire has become confused with validation, and where old relationship patterns are ready to be seen more clearly. The tension can force honesty about what each person truly wants and what they are afraid of losing.\n\nBut pressure is not the same as love. When this aspect becomes unconscious, the relationship can start running on jealousy, testing, withdrawal, rupture, reunion, and emotional intensity. One person may try to regain power by pulling away. The other may chase harder. The connection can become addictive, not because it is healthy, but because the highs and lows keep activating the desire to be chosen. Pay attention to what this bond brings out in you. Do you feel more confident, more honest, and more connected to your own worth? Or do you feel consumed by the need to be wanted, reassured, or chosen?\n\nYou do not have to call possession love. You do not have to stay in a painful cycle because the chemistry is strong. The wisdom of this aspect comes from learning the difference between desire that transforms you and desire that destabilizes you.","tension":"But pressure is not the same as love. When this aspect becomes unconscious, the relationship can start running on jealousy, testing, withdrawal, rupture, reunion, and emotional intensity. One person may try to regain power by pulling away. The other may chase harder. The connection can become addictive, not because it is healthy, but because the highs and lows keep activating the desire to be chosen. Pay attention to what this bond brings out in you. Do you feel more confident, more honest, and more connected to your own worth? Or do you feel consumed by the need to be wanted, reassured, or chosen?","advice":"You do not have to call possession love. You do not have to stay in a painful cycle because the chemistry is strong. The wisdom of this aspect comes from learning the difference between desire that transforms you and desire that destabilizes you.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-pluto_B-venus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"pluto","planetB":"venus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-pluto_B-venus_trine', 'synastry-pluto-trine-venus', 'relationship-pluto-trine-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-pluto_B-venus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-pluto_B-venus_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Pluto Trine Venus', null, 'This connection carries deep attraction without the same level of friction. The Pluto person may be drawn to the Venus person with unusual depth and focus, while the Venus person may feel genuinely desired, valued, and emotionally recognized. There is often a natural trust here, as though affection can deepen without being forced and desire can be expressed without immediately becoming a power struggle.

At its best, this aspect can be deeply healing. The Pluto person may help the Venus person feel more confident in their desirability, more honest about what they want, and more willing to receive love at a deeper level. The Venus person can soften the Pluto person''s intensity, helping them experience closeness with more trust, tenderness, and care.

There is still intensity here. Pluto never keeps love entirely light. But the trine often allows that intensity to move with more ease and less fear. Instead of forcing transformation through jealousy, crisis, or control, this aspect can support it through loyalty, trust, emotional honesty, and deep affection.

The shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to underestimate how much influence it carries. The Venus person may slowly begin organizing their sense of beauty, worth, or desire around the Pluto person''s attention. The Pluto person may not realize how much power their approval or withdrawal has.

Let the love deepen you, but keep your own sense of worth intact. This aspect can offer rare intimacy, but it still asks both people to stay aware of where devotion ends and dependency begins.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection carries deep attraction without the same level of friction. The Pluto person may be drawn to the Venus person with unusual depth and focus, while the Venus person may feel genuinely desired, valued, and emotionally recognized. There is often a natural trust here, as though affection can deepen without being forced and desire can be expressed without immediately becoming a power struggle.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can be deeply healing. The Pluto person may help the Venus person feel more confident in their desirability, more honest about what they want, and more willing to receive love at a deeper level. The Venus person can soften the Pluto person''s intensity, helping them experience closeness with more trust, tenderness, and care.\n\nThere is still intensity here. Pluto never keeps love entirely light. But the trine often allows that intensity to move with more ease and less fear. Instead of forcing transformation through jealousy, crisis, or control, this aspect can support it through loyalty, trust, emotional honesty, and deep affection.\n\nThe shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to underestimate how much influence it carries. The Venus person may slowly begin organizing their sense of beauty, worth, or desire around the Pluto person''s attention. The Pluto person may not realize how much power their approval or withdrawal has.\n\nLet the love deepen you, but keep your own sense of worth intact. This aspect can offer rare intimacy, but it still asks both people to stay aware of where devotion ends and dependency begins."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to underestimate how much influence it carries. The Venus person may slowly begin organizing their sense of beauty, worth, or desire around the Pluto person''s attention. The Pluto person may not realize how much power their approval or withdrawal has."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the love deepen you, but keep your own sense of worth intact. This aspect can offer rare intimacy, but it still asks both people to stay aware of where devotion ends and dependency begins."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-pluto_B-venus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Deep, transformative love that flows without the power struggle. Intimacy, honesty, and real change come more easily. Failure mode: underestimating how strong the bond is and being careless with it. Use the depth well; it''s powerful even when it''s smooth.","summaryDeep":"This connection carries deep attraction without the same level of friction. The Pluto person may be drawn to the Venus person with unusual depth and focus, while the Venus person may feel genuinely desired, valued, and emotionally recognized. There is often a natural trust here, as though affection can deepen without being forced and desire can be expressed without immediately becoming a power struggle.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can be deeply healing. The Pluto person may help the Venus person feel more confident in their desirability, more honest about what they want, and more willing to receive love at a deeper level. The Venus person can soften the Pluto person''s intensity, helping them experience closeness with more trust, tenderness, and care.\n\nThere is still intensity here. Pluto never keeps love entirely light. But the trine often allows that intensity to move with more ease and less fear. Instead of forcing transformation through jealousy, crisis, or control, this aspect can support it through loyalty, trust, emotional honesty, and deep affection.\n\nThe shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to underestimate how much influence it carries. The Venus person may slowly begin organizing their sense of beauty, worth, or desire around the Pluto person''s attention. The Pluto person may not realize how much power their approval or withdrawal has.\n\nLet the love deepen you, but keep your own sense of worth intact. This aspect can offer rare intimacy, but it still asks both people to stay aware of where devotion ends and dependency begins.","tension":"The shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to underestimate how much influence it carries. The Venus person may slowly begin organizing their sense of beauty, worth, or desire around the Pluto person''s attention. The Pluto person may not realize how much power their approval or withdrawal has.","advice":"Let the love deepen you, but keep your own sense of worth intact. This aspect can offer rare intimacy, but it still asks both people to stay aware of where devotion ends and dependency begins.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
