  ('A-saturn_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-jupiter_trine', 'synastry-saturn-trine-jupiter', 'relationship-saturn-trine-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-jupiter_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-jupiter_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Trine Jupiter', null, 'A''s structure meets B''s growth. The trine lets them flow together easily.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Translation","body":"A''s structure meets B''s growth. The trine lets them flow together easily."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-jupiter_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s structure meets B''s growth. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":null,"tension":null,"advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":null,"weight":null}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"mars","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry-saturn-conjunction-mars', 'relationship-saturn-conjunction-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-mars_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-mars_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Conjunction Mars', null, 'This person brings you face to face with the reality of your actions. Around them, you become more aware of timing, responsibility, consequences, and the effort required to make something last. If you tend to move quickly, their presence can help you slow down enough to see what you''re building. If you''re eager to act, however, it may feel as though every impulse is being asked to prove itself before it can move forward. What you want to do meets the question of what it will take to sustain it.

When this works, they help your energy find direction. Instead of acting on every impulse, you learn how to focus your effort, choose your timing more carefully, and stay with a goal after the excitement of beginning has passed. Their influence may not always feel encouraging, but it can help you develop greater self-control.

There is real value in what they offer. Desire can get something started, but it is discipline that carries it through. This person may help you develop the patience to stay with the process, the resilience to keep going when things get difficult, and the commitment needed to create results that last.

The difficulty comes when their restraint feels less like guidance and more like a barrier. You may begin to feel stopped before you have a chance to act, questioned before you have a chance to try, or made to doubt instincts that once felt clear. When every step feels subject to their judgment, resentment can grow.

Let this connection teach you how to move with more strength, but do not let it train you to stop moving.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person brings you face to face with the reality of your actions. Around them, you become more aware of timing, responsibility, consequences, and the effort required to make something last. If you tend to move quickly, their presence can help you slow down enough to see what you''re building. If you''re eager to act, however, it may feel as though every impulse is being asked to prove itself before it can move forward. What you want to do meets the question of what it will take to sustain it.\n\nWhen this works, they help your energy find direction. Instead of acting on every impulse, you learn how to focus your effort, choose your timing more carefully, and stay with a goal after the excitement of beginning has passed. Their influence may not always feel encouraging, but it can help you develop greater self-control.\n\nThere is real value in what they offer. Desire can get something started, but it is discipline that carries it through. This person may help you develop the patience to stay with the process, the resilience to keep going when things get difficult, and the commitment needed to create results that last.\n\nThe difficulty comes when their restraint feels less like guidance and more like a barrier. You may begin to feel stopped before you have a chance to act, questioned before you have a chance to try, or made to doubt instincts that once felt clear. When every step feels subject to their judgment, resentment can grow.\n\nLet this connection teach you how to move with more strength, but do not let it train you to stop moving."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The difficulty comes when their restraint feels less like guidance and more like a barrier. You may begin to feel stopped before you have a chance to act, questioned before you have a chance to try, or made to doubt instincts that once felt clear. When every step feels subject to their judgment, resentment can grow."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let this connection teach you how to move with more strength, but do not let it train you to stop moving."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-mars_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s structure meets B''s drive. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person brings you face to face with the reality of your actions. Around them, you become more aware of timing, responsibility, consequences, and the effort required to make something last. If you tend to move quickly, their presence can help you slow down enough to see what you''re building. If you''re eager to act, however, it may feel as though every impulse is being asked to prove itself before it can move forward. What you want to do meets the question of what it will take to sustain it.\n\nWhen this works, they help your energy find direction. Instead of acting on every impulse, you learn how to focus your effort, choose your timing more carefully, and stay with a goal after the excitement of beginning has passed. Their influence may not always feel encouraging, but it can help you develop greater self-control.\n\nThere is real value in what they offer. Desire can get something started, but it is discipline that carries it through. This person may help you develop the patience to stay with the process, the resilience to keep going when things get difficult, and the commitment needed to create results that last.\n\nThe difficulty comes when their restraint feels less like guidance and more like a barrier. You may begin to feel stopped before you have a chance to act, questioned before you have a chance to try, or made to doubt instincts that once felt clear. When every step feels subject to their judgment, resentment can grow.\n\nLet this connection teach you how to move with more strength, but do not let it train you to stop moving.","tension":"The difficulty comes when their restraint feels less like guidance and more like a barrier. You may begin to feel stopped before you have a chance to act, questioned before you have a chance to try, or made to doubt instincts that once felt clear. When every step feels subject to their judgment, resentment can grow.","advice":"Let this connection teach you how to move with more strength, but do not let it train you to stop moving.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"mars","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-mars_opposition', 'synastry-saturn-opposition-mars', 'relationship-saturn-opposition-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-mars_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-mars_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Opposition Mars', null, 'This aspect is about what happens when desire meets resistance. You may feel a strong urge to pursue what you want, while this person seems focused on limits, responsibilities, or potential consequences. Your instincts may tell you to move forward, while they question whether the timing is right. This can create tension because what feels like healthy caution to them may feel like discouragement to you.

When this works, the relationship teaches balance. They can help you direct your passion more effectively instead of scattering it, and you can help them trust action instead of remaining stuck in hesitation. One person brings movement. The other brings patience and perspective. Together, you can learn how to take meaningful action without losing sight of what it will require.

The challenge is that you want to move and they keep hitting the brakes. You get frustrated because everything feels harder than it needs to be. They get frustrated because you seem reckless or impatient. If neither of you adjusts, the relationship turns into a constant fight between action and resistance. At that point, the issue is no longer the goal itself but the struggle over how it should be pursued.

This connection works best when both people recognize that passion and discipline serve different purposes. Desire provides the motivation to move forward. Wisdom helps determine how and when to act. When those forces work together, the relationship can accomplish far more than either could alone.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This aspect is about what happens when desire meets resistance. You may feel a strong urge to pursue what you want, while this person seems focused on limits, responsibilities, or potential consequences. Your instincts may tell you to move forward, while they question whether the timing is right. This can create tension because what feels like healthy caution to them may feel like discouragement to you.\n\nWhen this works, the relationship teaches balance. They can help you direct your passion more effectively instead of scattering it, and you can help them trust action instead of remaining stuck in hesitation. One person brings movement. The other brings patience and perspective. Together, you can learn how to take meaningful action without losing sight of what it will require.\n\nThe challenge is that you want to move and they keep hitting the brakes. You get frustrated because everything feels harder than it needs to be. They get frustrated because you seem reckless or impatient. If neither of you adjusts, the relationship turns into a constant fight between action and resistance. At that point, the issue is no longer the goal itself but the struggle over how it should be pursued.\n\nThis connection works best when both people recognize that passion and discipline serve different purposes. Desire provides the motivation to move forward. Wisdom helps determine how and when to act. When those forces work together, the relationship can accomplish far more than either could alone."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that you want to move and they keep hitting the brakes. You get frustrated because everything feels harder than it needs to be. They get frustrated because you seem reckless or impatient. If neither of you adjusts, the relationship turns into a constant fight between action and resistance. At that point, the issue is no longer the goal itself but the struggle over how it should be pursued."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This connection works best when both people recognize that passion and discipline serve different purposes. Desire provides the motivation to move forward. Wisdom helps determine how and when to act. When those forces work together, the relationship can accomplish far more than either could alone."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-mars_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s structure meets B''s drive. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This aspect is about what happens when desire meets resistance. You may feel a strong urge to pursue what you want, while this person seems focused on limits, responsibilities, or potential consequences. Your instincts may tell you to move forward, while they question whether the timing is right. This can create tension because what feels like healthy caution to them may feel like discouragement to you.\n\nWhen this works, the relationship teaches balance. They can help you direct your passion more effectively instead of scattering it, and you can help them trust action instead of remaining stuck in hesitation. One person brings movement. The other brings patience and perspective. Together, you can learn how to take meaningful action without losing sight of what it will require.\n\nThe challenge is that you want to move and they keep hitting the brakes. You get frustrated because everything feels harder than it needs to be. They get frustrated because you seem reckless or impatient. If neither of you adjusts, the relationship turns into a constant fight between action and resistance. At that point, the issue is no longer the goal itself but the struggle over how it should be pursued.\n\nThis connection works best when both people recognize that passion and discipline serve different purposes. Desire provides the motivation to move forward. Wisdom helps determine how and when to act. When those forces work together, the relationship can accomplish far more than either could alone.","tension":"The challenge is that you want to move and they keep hitting the brakes. You get frustrated because everything feels harder than it needs to be. They get frustrated because you seem reckless or impatient. If neither of you adjusts, the relationship turns into a constant fight between action and resistance. At that point, the issue is no longer the goal itself but the struggle over how it should be pursued.","advice":"This connection works best when both people recognize that passion and discipline serve different purposes. Desire provides the motivation to move forward. Wisdom helps determine how and when to act. When those forces work together, the relationship can accomplish far more than either could alone.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"mars","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-mars_sextile', 'synastry-saturn-sextile-mars', 'relationship-saturn-sextile-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-mars_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-mars_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Sextile Mars', null, 'This connection works because it helps action find a path forward. The support here is often subtle. Instead of creating pressure or resistance, it creates momentum that can actually be sustained. One person may provide the spark that gets things moving, while the other naturally helps shape that energy into something workable. Plans feel easier to follow through on, obstacles seem more manageable, and effort is less likely to be wasted. Together, there is a sense that progress is possible because inspiration and discipline are working in the same direction.

When this works, this person helps you trust the process. They may encourage you to take the next step instead of worrying about the entire journey. They may help you stay committed when the excitement fades, or remind you that meaningful progress is often built through small, consistent acts of devotion. Your drive remains your own, but their presence helps it find direction.

The challenge is that caution can quietly turn into avoidance. You may find yourself endlessly preparing, analyzing, or addressing one concern after another until you lose touch with the original goal. On the other side, you may dismiss their input before fully considering it because receiving guidance feels uncomfortable or limiting.

Discipline is useful when it helps you move forward. It is a problem when it becomes an excuse to do nothing.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection works because it helps action find a path forward. The support here is often subtle. Instead of creating pressure or resistance, it creates momentum that can actually be sustained. One person may provide the spark that gets things moving, while the other naturally helps shape that energy into something workable. Plans feel easier to follow through on, obstacles seem more manageable, and effort is less likely to be wasted. Together, there is a sense that progress is possible because inspiration and discipline are working in the same direction.\n\nWhen this works, this person helps you trust the process. They may encourage you to take the next step instead of worrying about the entire journey. They may help you stay committed when the excitement fades, or remind you that meaningful progress is often built through small, consistent acts of devotion. Your drive remains your own, but their presence helps it find direction.\n\nThe challenge is that caution can quietly turn into avoidance. You may find yourself endlessly preparing, analyzing, or addressing one concern after another until you lose touch with the original goal. On the other side, you may dismiss their input before fully considering it because receiving guidance feels uncomfortable or limiting.\n\nDiscipline is useful when it helps you move forward. It is a problem when it becomes an excuse to do nothing."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that caution can quietly turn into avoidance. You may find yourself endlessly preparing, analyzing, or addressing one concern after another until you lose touch with the original goal. On the other side, you may dismiss their input before fully considering it because receiving guidance feels uncomfortable or limiting."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Discipline is useful when it helps you move forward. It is a problem when it becomes an excuse to do nothing."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-mars_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s structure meets B''s drive. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This connection works because it helps action find a path forward. The support here is often subtle. Instead of creating pressure or resistance, it creates momentum that can actually be sustained. One person may provide the spark that gets things moving, while the other naturally helps shape that energy into something workable. Plans feel easier to follow through on, obstacles seem more manageable, and effort is less likely to be wasted. Together, there is a sense that progress is possible because inspiration and discipline are working in the same direction.\n\nWhen this works, this person helps you trust the process. They may encourage you to take the next step instead of worrying about the entire journey. They may help you stay committed when the excitement fades, or remind you that meaningful progress is often built through small, consistent acts of devotion. Your drive remains your own, but their presence helps it find direction.\n\nThe challenge is that caution can quietly turn into avoidance. You may find yourself endlessly preparing, analyzing, or addressing one concern after another until you lose touch with the original goal. On the other side, you may dismiss their input before fully considering it because receiving guidance feels uncomfortable or limiting.\n\nDiscipline is useful when it helps you move forward. It is a problem when it becomes an excuse to do nothing.","tension":"The challenge is that caution can quietly turn into avoidance. You may find yourself endlessly preparing, analyzing, or addressing one concern after another until you lose touch with the original goal. On the other side, you may dismiss their input before fully considering it because receiving guidance feels uncomfortable or limiting.","advice":"Discipline is useful when it helps you move forward. It is a problem when it becomes an excuse to do nothing.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-mars_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"mars","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-mars_square', 'synastry-saturn-square-mars', 'relationship-saturn-square-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-mars_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-mars_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Square Mars', null, 'This person has a way of bringing you face to face with your limits. Their timing may not match yours. Their caution may feel like resistance. Their questions may arrive right when you are ready to act. You reach for movement, and suddenly you are being asked to slow down, consider the consequences, or work within a set of constraints you did not choose. This can be deeply frustrating. It can also become a teacher.

This is about frustration. You want to act, and something gets in the way.

At its best, the conflict forces you to get your act together. This person points out where you''re wasting energy, acting too fast, or chasing something without a real plan. If you want results, you have to be more disciplined.

At its worst, it''s just a power struggle. They block. You push. They dig in. You get angry. Eventually, the relationship stops being about the original issue and becomes a fight over control. This is where the aspect can become exhausting. What could have been used to build something meaningful ends up consumed by the struggle itself.

The lesson is discernment. Some limits are real. Some come from caution, uncertainty, or a desire to protect what matters. Some feedback helps you act with more strength. Some feedback reflects a different relationship to risk and timing. Learn the difference. Turn the no into a conversation when you can. Ask what the concern is protecting and what the action is trying to accomplish.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a way of bringing you face to face with your limits. Their timing may not match yours. Their caution may feel like resistance. Their questions may arrive right when you are ready to act. You reach for movement, and suddenly you are being asked to slow down, consider the consequences, or work within a set of constraints you did not choose. This can be deeply frustrating. It can also become a teacher.\n\nThis is about frustration. You want to act, and something gets in the way.\n\nAt its best, the conflict forces you to get your act together. This person points out where you''re wasting energy, acting too fast, or chasing something without a real plan. If you want results, you have to be more disciplined.\n\nAt its worst, it''s just a power struggle. They block. You push. They dig in. You get angry. Eventually, the relationship stops being about the original issue and becomes a fight over control. This is where the aspect can become exhausting. What could have been used to build something meaningful ends up consumed by the struggle itself.\n\nThe lesson is discernment. Some limits are real. Some come from caution, uncertainty, or a desire to protect what matters. Some feedback helps you act with more strength. Some feedback reflects a different relationship to risk and timing. Learn the difference. Turn the no into a conversation when you can. Ask what the concern is protecting and what the action is trying to accomplish."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its worst, it''s just a power struggle. They block. You push. They dig in. You get angry. Eventually, the relationship stops being about the original issue and becomes a fight over control. This is where the aspect can become exhausting. What could have been used to build something meaningful ends up consumed by the struggle itself."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The lesson is discernment. Some limits are real. Some come from caution, uncertainty, or a desire to protect what matters. Some feedback helps you act with more strength. Some feedback reflects a different relationship to risk and timing. Learn the difference. Turn the no into a conversation when you can. Ask what the concern is protecting and what the action is trying to accomplish."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-mars_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s structure meets B''s drive. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This person has a way of bringing you face to face with your limits. Their timing may not match yours. Their caution may feel like resistance. Their questions may arrive right when you are ready to act. You reach for movement, and suddenly you are being asked to slow down, consider the consequences, or work within a set of constraints you did not choose. This can be deeply frustrating. It can also become a teacher.\n\nThis is about frustration. You want to act, and something gets in the way.\n\nAt its best, the conflict forces you to get your act together. This person points out where you''re wasting energy, acting too fast, or chasing something without a real plan. If you want results, you have to be more disciplined.\n\nAt its worst, it''s just a power struggle. They block. You push. They dig in. You get angry. Eventually, the relationship stops being about the original issue and becomes a fight over control. This is where the aspect can become exhausting. What could have been used to build something meaningful ends up consumed by the struggle itself.\n\nThe lesson is discernment. Some limits are real. Some come from caution, 