  ('A-saturn_B-mars_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"mars","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-mars_trine', 'synastry-saturn-trine-mars', 'relationship-saturn-trine-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-mars_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-mars_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Trine Mars', null, 'This person has a steadying effect on your actions. Instead of feeling restricted, you may feel supported by a sense of structure that helps you use your energy more wisely. Around them, it can become easier to focus on what truly matters, work at a sustainable pace, and remain committed to your goals. Their influence encourages patience, helping your efforts gain strength through consistency rather than urgency.

When this works, the two of you create a steady rhythm between effort and patience. You are less likely to rush into things that cannot be sustained or scatter your energy across too many directions at once. What you begin has a better chance of growing roots. What you commit to has a better chance of lasting.

There is a quiet strength in this connection. It supports follow-through. It helps you stay with the work after the excitement fades, and it reminds you that meaningful results often come from consistency more than intensity.

The challenge is remembering that caution and fear can wear similar clothes. Because the pace feels measured, it can be easy to believe that more time, more preparation, or one more adjustment will bring certainty. But certainty is rarely what gets us moving. If you''re not careful, the desire that once felt alive can get buried beneath endless refinement. What began as thoughtful timing can quietly become avoidance, and the moment you''re waiting for never quite arrives.

This connection works best when discipline gives your drive endurance, not another reason to stay still.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a steadying effect on your actions. Instead of feeling restricted, you may feel supported by a sense of structure that helps you use your energy more wisely. Around them, it can become easier to focus on what truly matters, work at a sustainable pace, and remain committed to your goals. Their influence encourages patience, helping your efforts gain strength through consistency rather than urgency.\n\nWhen this works, the two of you create a steady rhythm between effort and patience. You are less likely to rush into things that cannot be sustained or scatter your energy across too many directions at once. What you begin has a better chance of growing roots. What you commit to has a better chance of lasting.\n\nThere is a quiet strength in this connection. It supports follow-through. It helps you stay with the work after the excitement fades, and it reminds you that meaningful results often come from consistency more than intensity.\n\nThe challenge is remembering that caution and fear can wear similar clothes. Because the pace feels measured, it can be easy to believe that more time, more preparation, or one more adjustment will bring certainty. But certainty is rarely what gets us moving. If you''re not careful, the desire that once felt alive can get buried beneath endless refinement. What began as thoughtful timing can quietly become avoidance, and the moment you''re waiting for never quite arrives.\n\nThis connection works best when discipline gives your drive endurance, not another reason to stay still."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is remembering that caution and fear can wear similar clothes. Because the pace feels measured, it can be easy to believe that more time, more preparation, or one more adjustment will bring certainty. But certainty is rarely what gets us moving. If you''re not careful, the desire that once felt alive can get buried beneath endless refinement. What began as thoughtful timing can quietly become avoidance, and the moment you''re waiting for never quite arrives."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This connection works best when discipline gives your drive endurance, not another reason to stay still."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-mars_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s structure meets B''s drive. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This person has a steadying effect on your actions. Instead of feeling restricted, you may feel supported by a sense of structure that helps you use your energy more wisely. Around them, it can become easier to focus on what truly matters, work at a sustainable pace, and remain committed to your goals. Their influence encourages patience, helping your efforts gain strength through consistency rather than urgency.\n\nWhen this works, the two of you create a steady rhythm between effort and patience. You are less likely to rush into things that cannot be sustained or scatter your energy across too many directions at once. What you begin has a better chance of growing roots. What you commit to has a better chance of lasting.\n\nThere is a quiet strength in this connection. It supports follow-through. It helps you stay with the work after the excitement fades, and it reminds you that meaningful results often come from consistency more than intensity.\n\nThe challenge is remembering that caution and fear can wear similar clothes. Because the pace feels measured, it can be easy to believe that more time, more preparation, or one more adjustment will bring certainty. But certainty is rarely what gets us moving. If you''re not careful, the desire that once felt alive can get buried beneath endless refinement. What began as thoughtful timing can quietly become avoidance, and the moment you''re waiting for never quite arrives.\n\nThis connection works best when discipline gives your drive endurance, not another reason to stay still.","tension":"The challenge is remembering that caution and fear can wear similar clothes. Because the pace feels measured, it can be easy to believe that more time, more preparation, or one more adjustment will bring certainty. But certainty is rarely what gets us moving. If you''re not careful, the desire that once felt alive can get buried beneath endless refinement. What began as thoughtful timing can quietly become avoidance, and the moment you''re waiting for never quite arrives.","advice":"This connection works best when discipline gives your drive endurance, not another reason to stay still.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry-saturn-conjunction-mercury', 'relationship-saturn-conjunction-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-mercury_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-mercury_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Conjunction Mercury', null, 'This person has a strong influence on how you express yourself. Around them, you may become more aware of what you know, what you can defend, and where your thinking still feels uncertain. Conversations can feel weightier than usual. Instead of speaking on impulse, you may find yourself choosing your words carefully and thinking several steps ahead before saying anything.

At its best, this creates real mental growth. They can help you develop stronger judgment, spot weaknesses in your reasoning, and bring more discipline to your ideas. What starts as a rough concept can become something thoughtful, practical, and well-constructed through their influence.

There is a maturity to this connection. They are often less interested in quick opinions and more interested in whether something holds up over time. Because of that, they may encourage you to think more deeply, prepare more thoroughly, and communicate with greater clarity.

The difficulty comes when that pressure becomes self-doubt. You may begin second-guessing yourself before you''ve even finished a sentence. Instead of using their feedback to strengthen your ideas, you may start assuming your ideas are not good enough to share in the first place.

The strongest expression of this aspect combines accountability with self-trust. Let this person help you strengthen your thinking, refine your communication, and raise your standards, but do not become so focused on getting it right that you stop sharing ideas before they are fully developed. Growth often comes from testing, learning, and improving along the way.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person has a strong influence on how you express yourself. Around them, you may become more aware of what you know, what you can defend, and where your thinking still feels uncertain. Conversations can feel weightier than usual. Instead of speaking on impulse, you may find yourself choosing your words carefully and thinking several steps ahead before saying anything.\n\nAt its best, this creates real mental growth. They can help you develop stronger judgment, spot weaknesses in your reasoning, and bring more discipline to your ideas. What starts as a rough concept can become something thoughtful, practical, and well-constructed through their influence.\n\nThere is a maturity to this connection. They are often less interested in quick opinions and more interested in whether something holds up over time. Because of that, they may encourage you to think more deeply, prepare more thoroughly, and communicate with greater clarity.\n\nThe difficulty comes when that pressure becomes self-doubt. You may begin second-guessing yourself before you''ve even finished a sentence. Instead of using their feedback to strengthen your ideas, you may start assuming your ideas are not good enough to share in the first place.\n\nThe strongest expression of this aspect combines accountability with self-trust. Let this person help you strengthen your thinking, refine your communication, and raise your standards, but do not become so focused on getting it right that you stop sharing ideas before they are fully developed. Growth often comes from testing, learning, and improving along the way."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The difficulty comes when that pressure becomes self-doubt. You may begin second-guessing yourself before you''ve even finished a sentence. Instead of using their feedback to strengthen your ideas, you may start assuming your ideas are not good enough to share in the first place."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The strongest expression of this aspect combines accountability with self-trust. Let this person help you strengthen your thinking, refine your communication, and raise your standards, but do not become so focused on getting it right that you stop sharing ideas before they are fully developed. Growth often comes from testing, learning, and improving along the way."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-mercury_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s structure meets B''s mind. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person has a strong influence on how you express yourself. Around them, you may become more aware of what you know, what you can defend, and where your thinking still feels uncertain. Conversations can feel weightier than usual. Instead of speaking on impulse, you may find yourself choosing your words carefully and thinking several steps ahead before saying anything.\n\nAt its best, this creates real mental growth. They can help you develop stronger judgment, spot weaknesses in your reasoning, and bring more discipline to your ideas. What starts as a rough concept can become something thoughtful, practical, and well-constructed through their influence.\n\nThere is a maturity to this connection. They are often less interested in quick opinions and more interested in whether something holds up over time. Because of that, they may encourage you to think more deeply, prepare more thoroughly, and communicate with greater clarity.\n\nThe difficulty comes when that pressure becomes self-doubt. You may begin second-guessing yourself before you''ve even finished a sentence. Instead of using their feedback to strengthen your ideas, you may start assuming your ideas are not good enough to share in the first place.\n\nThe strongest expression of this aspect combines accountability with self-trust. Let this person help you strengthen your thinking, refine your communication, and raise your standards, but do not become so focused on getting it right that you stop sharing ideas before they are fully developed. Growth often comes from testing, learning, and improving along the way.","tension":"The difficulty comes when that pressure becomes self-doubt. You may begin second-guessing yourself before you''ve even finished a sentence. Instead of using their feedback to strengthen your ideas, you may start assuming your ideas are not good enough to share in the first place.","advice":"The strongest expression of this aspect combines accountability with self-trust. Let this person help you strengthen your thinking, refine your communication, and raise your standards, but do not become so focused on getting it right that you stop sharing ideas before they are fully developed. Growth often comes from testing, learning, and improving along the way.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry-saturn-opposition-mercury', 'relationship-saturn-opposition-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-mercury_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-mercury_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Opposition Mercury', null, 'This connection can feel like a conversation between possibility and caution. You may need space to think out loud, to wander through an idea before you know exactly where it is going. They may want clarity from the beginning. A plan. A purpose. A reason to follow the thread. What feels exploratory to you may feel unfocused to them. What feels responsible to them may feel limiting to you.

Oppositions ask us to learn from what stands across from us. This person may help you strengthen your thinking, question your assumptions, and give shape to ideas that would otherwise drift. You may help them stay curious, flexible, and open to possibilities they would dismiss too quickly.

They may think your ideas are unrealistic. You may think they are rigid and overly controlling. Conversations can turn into arguments where both people are trying to prove the other one wrong. The opportunity here is learning to value different ways of solving problems. Some insights come from asking questions and exploring possibilities. Others come from hands-on experience, pattern recognition, or careful analysis. The strongest results often come from combining these approaches rather than treating them as competing strengths.

Let this connection teach you how to evaluate feedback without losing confidence in your own perspective. Let go of criticism that undermines your confidence or discourages you from contributing your ideas.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection can feel like a conversation between possibility and caution. You may need space to think out loud, to wander through an idea before you know exactly where it is going. They may want clarity from the beginning. A plan. A purpose. A reason to follow the thread. What feels exploratory to you may feel unfocused to them. What feels responsible to them may feel limiting to you.\n\nOppositions ask us to learn from what stands across from us. This person may help you strengthen your thinking, question your assumptions, and give shape to ideas that would otherwise drift. You may help them stay curious, flexible, and open to possibilities they would dismiss too quickly.\n\nThey may think your ideas are unrealistic. You may think they are rigid and overly controlling. Conversations can turn into arguments where both people are trying to prove the other one wrong. The opportunity here is learning to value different ways of solving problems. Some insights come from asking questions and exploring possibilities. Others come from hands-on experience, pattern recognition, or careful analysis. The strongest results often come from combining these approaches rather than treating them as competing strengths.\n\nLet this connection teach you how to evaluate feedback without losing confidence in your own perspective. Let go of criticism that undermines your confidence or discourages you from contributing your ideas."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"They may think your ideas are unrealistic. You may think they are rigid and overly controlling. Conversations can turn into arguments where both people are trying to prove the other one wrong. The opportunity here is learning to value different ways of solving problems. Some insights come from asking questions and exploring possibilities. Others come from hands-on experience, pattern recognition, or careful analysis. The strongest results often come from combining these approaches rather than treating them as competing strengths."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let this connection teach you how to evaluate feedback without losing confidence in your own perspective. Let go of criticism that undermines your confidence or discourages you from contributing your ideas."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-mercury_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s structure meets B''s mind. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This connection can feel like a conversation between possibility and caution. You may need space to think out loud, to wander through an idea before you know exactly where it is going. They may want clarity from the beginning. A plan. A purpose. A reason to follow the thread. What feels exploratory to you may feel unfocused to them. What feels responsible to them may feel limiting to you.\n\nOppositions ask us to learn from what stands across from us. This person may help you strengthen your thinking, question your assumptions, and give shape to ideas that would otherwise drift. You may help them stay curious, flexible, and open to possibilities they would dismiss too quickly.\n\nThey may think your ideas are unrealistic. You may think they are rigid and overly controlling. Conversations can turn into arguments where both people are trying to prove the other one wrong. The opportunity here is learning to value different ways of solving problems. Some insights come from asking questions and exploring possibilities. Others come from hands-on experience, pattern recognition, or careful analysis. The strongest results often come from combining these approaches rather than treating them as competing strengths.\n\nLet this connection teach you how to evaluate feedback without losing confidence in your own perspective. Let go of criticism that undermines your confidence or discourages you from contributing your ideas.","tension":"They may think your ideas are unrealistic. You may think they are rigid and overly controlling. Conversations can turn into arguments where both people are trying to prove the other one wrong. The opportunity here is learning to value different ways of solving problems. Some insights come from asking questions and exploring possibilities. Others come from hands-on experience, pattern recognition, or careful analysis. The strongest results often come from combining these approaches rather than treating them as competing strengths.","advice":"Let this connection teach you how to evaluate feedback without losing confidence in your own perspective. Let go of criticism that undermines your confidence or discourages you from contributing your ideas.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry-saturn-sextile-mercury', 'relationship-saturn-sextile-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-mercury_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-mercury_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Sextile Mercury', null, 'This connection offers your mind a steady place to land. There is something supportive about the way this person thinks with you. They may help you slow down enough to hear your own wisdom. They may ask the question that brings clarity, offer the perspective that helps things click into place, or remind you that good ideas often need time, patience, and care to take shape.

When this aspect is working well, it helps you trust your thoughts. Not because every idea is perfect, but because you learn that your mind can hold both curiosity and responsibility. Conversations can feel grounding. Plans can feel achievable. What once felt overwhelming may become easier to organize and understand.

The challenge is knowing when to balance discipline with exploration. Strong planning and practical thinking are valuable, but they should not prevent you from pursuing promising opportunities. Sometimes an idea needs time, testing, and development before its value becomes clear.

The most successful growth comes from combining good judgment with a willingness to stay open to possibility.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection offers your mind a steady place to land. There is something supportive about the way this person thinks with you. They may help you slow down enough to hear your own wisdom. They may ask the question that brings clarity, offer the perspective that helps things click into place, or remind you that good ideas often need time, patience, and care to take shape.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it helps you trust your thoughts. Not because every idea is perfect, but because you learn that your mind can hold both curiosity and responsibility. Conversations can feel grounding. Plans can feel achievable. What once felt overwhelming may become easier to organize and understand.\n\nThe challenge is knowing when to balance discipline with exploration. Strong planning and practical thinking are valuable, but they should not prevent you from pursuing promising opportunities. Sometimes an idea needs time, testing, and development before its value becomes clear.\n\nThe most successful growth comes from combining good judgment with a willingness to stay open to possibility."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is knowing when to balance discipline with exploration. Strong planning and practical thinking are valuable, but they should not prevent you from pursuing promising opportunities. Sometimes an idea needs time, testing, and development before its value becomes clear."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The most successful growth comes from combining good judgment with a willingness to stay open to possibility."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-mercury_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s structure meets B''s mind. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This connection offers your mind a steady place to land. There is something supportive about the way this person thinks with you. They may help you slow down enough to hear your own wisdom. They may ask the question that brings clarity, offer the perspective that helps things click into place, or remind you that good ideas often need time, patience, and care to take shape.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it helps you trust your thoughts. Not because every idea is perfect, but because you learn that your mind can hold both curiosity and responsibility. Conversations can feel grounding. Plans can feel achievable. What once felt overwhelming may become easier to organize and understand.\n\nThe challenge is knowing when to balance discipline with exploration. Strong planning and practical thinking are valuable, but they should not prevent you from pursuing promising opportunities. Sometimes an idea needs time, testing, and development before its value becomes clear.\n\nThe most successful growth comes from combining good judgment with a willingness to stay open to possibility.","tension":"The challenge is knowing when to balance discipline with exploration. Strong planning and practical thinking are valuable, but they should not prevent you from pursuing promising opportunities. Sometimes an idea needs time, testing, and development before its value becomes clear.","advice":"The most successful growth comes from combining good judgment with a willingness to stay open to possibility.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-mercury_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-mercury_square', 'synastry-saturn-square-mercury', 'relationship-saturn-square-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-mercury_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-mercury_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Square Mercury', null, 'This person will challenge your thinking, whether you like it or not. They may question your logic, point out weaknesses in your ideas, or push back on things you thought were obvious. Sometimes their feedback is valuable. Sometimes it feels like they are looking for problems instead of solutions.

The risk is that you start second-guessing yourself. You stop speaking up until every detail is perfect. You spend more time defending your ideas than developing them. That is a losing strategy. No one grows by staying silent.

The upside is that this pressure can make you better. If you are willing to do the work, this person can force you to think more clearly, communicate more effectively, and back up your opinions with substance. Weak ideas get exposed. Strong ideas get stronger.

The downside is when the criticism never stops. You bring an idea, they find a flaw. You solve the flaw, they find another one. Over time, the conversation stops being productive and starts becoming draining. You leave feeling less confident instead of more capable.

Treat this like a lesson in discernment. Some critiques arrive carrying wisdom. Others arrive carrying someone else''s fear, frustration, or need for control. Your task is not to absorb every judgment that comes your way. Your task is to know what feedback helps you grow and what feedback you should ignore. You are not here to earn this person''s approval. You are here to deepen your relationship with your own mind.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person will challenge your thinking, whether you like it or not. They may question your logic, point out weaknesses in your ideas, or push back on things you thought were obvious. Sometimes their feedback is valuable. Sometimes it feels like they are looking for problems instead of solutions.\n\nThe risk is that you start second-guessing yourself. You stop speaking up until every detail is perfect. You spend more time defending your ideas than developing them. That is a losing strategy. No one grows by staying silent.\n\nThe upside is that this pressure can make you better. If you are willing to do the work, this person can force you to think more clearly, communicate more effectively, and back up your opinions with substance. Weak ideas get exposed. Strong ideas get stronger.\n\nThe downside is when the criticism never stops. You bring an idea, they find a flaw. You solve the flaw, they find another one. Over time, the conversation stops being productive and starts becoming draining. You leave feeling less confident instead of more capable.\n\nTreat this like a lesson in discernment. Some critiques arrive carrying wisdom. Others arrive carrying someone else''s fear, frustration, or need for control. Your task is not to absorb every judgment that comes your way. Your task is to know what feedback helps you grow and what feedback you should ignore. You are not here to earn this person''s approval. You are here to deepen your relationship with your own mind."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The downside 