  ('A-saturn_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"moon","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry-saturn-conjunction-moon', 'relationship-saturn-conjunction-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-moon_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-moon_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Conjunction Moon', null, 'This person does not take your feelings lightly. Being around them can make you feel emotionally exposed. They have a way of bringing your inner world into sharper focus, making it harder to look away from the parts of yourself you usually keep tucked out of sight. You may become more aware of your vulnerabilities and more cautious about how much of them you reveal. It can feel as though your emotions need to be managed or contained before they can be shared, leading you to present the version of yourself that seems most composed while keeping the more complicated parts hidden.

When this works, the heaviness turns into something dependable. This person may not always know how to soothe you in the moment, but they can offer a steady presence that does not disappear when things get difficult. Their care often shows itself through reliability, patience, and a willingness to stay engaged over time. The sense of security here is usually built gradually rather than given all at once.

The challenge comes when responsibility starts to feel more like judgment than support. Saturn often responds to emotion by trying to steady it, structure it, or bring it under control. Even when the intention is helpful, the Moon person can experience this as a signal that their feelings are excessive, inconvenient, or somehow wrong. The hurt builds when vulnerability is consistently met with correction, restraint, emotional distance, or pressure to handle things better than they realistically can. Over time, you may start expecting criticism before it happens, filtering your emotions through self-doubt and treating your feelings as something to manage instead of something that deserves understanding.

Do not start policing your own emotions just to keep the peace. Let this connection help you develop emotional resilience, but do not let it convince you that your feelings are something to be embarrassed by. Healthy structure gives your emotions a place to land.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person does not take your feelings lightly. Being around them can make you feel emotionally exposed. They have a way of bringing your inner world into sharper focus, making it harder to look away from the parts of yourself you usually keep tucked out of sight. You may become more aware of your vulnerabilities and more cautious about how much of them you reveal. It can feel as though your emotions need to be managed or contained before they can be shared, leading you to present the version of yourself that seems most composed while keeping the more complicated parts hidden.\n\nWhen this works, the heaviness turns into something dependable. This person may not always know how to soothe you in the moment, but they can offer a steady presence that does not disappear when things get difficult. Their care often shows itself through reliability, patience, and a willingness to stay engaged over time. The sense of security here is usually built gradually rather than given all at once.\n\nThe challenge comes when responsibility starts to feel more like judgment than support. Saturn often responds to emotion by trying to steady it, structure it, or bring it under control. Even when the intention is helpful, the Moon person can experience this as a signal that their feelings are excessive, inconvenient, or somehow wrong. The hurt builds when vulnerability is consistently met with correction, restraint, emotional distance, or pressure to handle things better than they realistically can. Over time, you may start expecting criticism before it happens, filtering your emotions through self-doubt and treating your feelings as something to manage instead of something that