more aware of your vulnerabilities and more cautious about how much of them you reveal. It can feel as though your emotions need to be managed or contained before they can be shared, leading you to present the version of yourself that seems most composed while keeping the more complicated parts hidden.\n\nWhen this works, the heaviness turns into something dependable. This person may not always know how to soothe you in the moment, but they can offer a steady presence that does not disappear when things get difficult. Their care often shows itself through reliability, patience, and a willingness to stay engaged over time. The sense of security here is usually built gradually rather than given all at once.\n\nThe challenge comes when responsibility starts to feel more like judgment than support. Saturn often responds to emotion by trying to steady it, structure it, or bring it under control. Even when the intention is helpful, the Moon person can experience this as a signal that their feelings are excessive, inconvenient, or somehow wrong. The hurt builds when vulnerability is consistently met with correction, restraint, emotional distance, or pressure to handle things better than they realistically can. Over time, you may start expecting criticism before it happens, filtering your emotions through self-doubt and treating your feelings as something to manage instead of something that deserves understanding.\n\nDo not start policing your own emotions just to keep the peace. Let this connection help you develop emotional resilience, but do not let it convince you that your feelings are something to be embarrassed by. Healthy structure gives your emotions a place to land.","tension":"The challenge comes when responsibility starts to feel more like judgment than support. Saturn often responds to emotion by trying to steady it, structure it, or bring it under control. Even when the intention is helpful, the Moon person can experience this as a signal that their feelings are excessive, inconvenient, or somehow wrong. The hurt builds when vulnerability is consistently met with correction, restraint, emotional distance, or pressure to handle things better than they realistically can. Over time, you may start expecting criticism before it happens, filtering your emotions through self-doubt and treating your feelings as something to manage instead of something that deserves understanding.","advice":"Do not start policing your own emotions just to keep the peace. Let this connection help you develop emotional resilience, but do not let it convince you that your feelings are something to be embarrassed by. Healthy structure gives your emotions a place to land.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"moon","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry-saturn-opposition-moon', 'relationship-saturn-opposition-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-moon_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-moon_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Opposition Moon', null, 'This person may seem emotionally distant, even when they care.

You might look for comfort, reassurance, or a sense of emotional closeness, while they respond with caution, restraint, or practical advice. What feels supportive to them may feel cold to you. What feels like a reasonable emotional need to you may feel overwhelming to them. It is easy for both people to misunderstand each other''s intentions.

At its best, this connection creates balance. They can help you step back from emotional overwhelm and see situations more clearly. Their steadiness can offer perspective when feelings become consuming. In return, you can help them stay connected to emotions they might otherwise avoid or suppress.

The challenge comes when the relationship falls into a cycle that neither person intends. One person reaches for reassurance, and the other responds by creating more distance. That distance then increases the need for reassurance, which can keep the pattern going. The goal is not to decide who is right, but to recognize the pattern together and create space for both emotional needs and healthy boundaries.

This aspect works best when both people resist turning differences into proof that they are unloved. Be clear about what you need, and stay open to what the other person is actually able to offer.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may seem emotionally distant, even when they care.\n\nYou might look for comfort, reassurance, or a sense of emotional closeness, while they respond with caution, restraint, or practical advice. What feels supportive to them may feel cold to you. What feels like a reasonable emotional need to you may feel overwhelming to them. It is easy for both people to misunderstand each other''s intentions.\n\nAt its best, this connection creates balance. They can help you step back from emotional overwhelm and see situations more clearly. Their steadiness can offer perspective when feelings become consuming. In return, you can help them stay connected to emotions they might otherwise avoid or suppress.\n\nThe challenge comes when the relationship falls into a cycle that neither person intends. One person reaches for reassurance, and the other responds by creating more distance. That distance then increases the need for reassurance, which can keep the pattern going. The goal is not to decide who is right, but to recognize the pattern together and create space for both emotional needs and healthy boundaries.\n\nThis aspect works best when both people resist turning differences into proof that they are unloved. Be clear about what you need, and stay open to what the other person is actually able to offer."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge comes when the relationship falls into a cycle that neither person intends. One person reaches for reassurance, and the other responds by creating more distance. That distance then increases the need for reassurance, which can keep the pattern going. The goal is not to decide who is right, but to recognize the pattern together and create space for both emotional needs and healthy boundaries."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This aspect works best when both people resist turning differences into proof that they are unloved. Be clear about what you need, and stay open to what the other person is actually able to offer."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-moon_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Saturn person may stand at the threshold of closeness while the Moon person reaches for it. This can build commitment if both people name their needs honestly. If one person keeps withholding and the other keeps begging, the pattern is the message.","summaryDeep":"This person may seem emotionally distant, even when they care.\n\nYou might look for comfort, reassurance, or a sense of emotional closeness, while they respond with caution, restraint, or practical advice. What feels supportive to them may feel cold to you. What feels like a reasonable emotional need to you may feel overwhelming to them. It is easy for both people to misunderstand each other''s intentions.\n\nAt its best, this connection creates balance. They can help you step back from emotional overwhelm and see situations more clearly. Their steadiness can offer perspective when feelings become consuming. In return, you can help them stay connected to emotions they might otherwise avoid or suppress.\n\nThe challenge comes when the relationship falls into a cycle that neither person intends. One person reaches for reassurance, and the other responds by creating more distance. That distance then increases the need for reassurance, which can keep the pattern going. The goal is not to decide who is right, but to recognize the pattern together and create space for both emotional needs and healthy boundaries.\n\nThis aspect works best when both people resist turning differences into proof that they are unloved. Be clear about what you need, and stay open to what the other person is actually able to offer.","tension":"The challenge comes when the relationship falls into a cycle that neither person intends. One person reaches for reassurance, and the other responds by creating more distance. That distance then increases the need for reassurance, which can keep the pattern going. The goal is not to decide who is right, but to recognize the pattern together and create space for both emotional needs and healthy boundaries.","advice":"This aspect works best when both people resist turning differences into proof that they are unloved. Be clear about what you need, and stay open to what the other person is actually able to offer.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-moon_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"moon","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-moon_sextile', 'synastry-saturn-sextile-moon', 'relationship-saturn-sextile-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-moon_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-moon_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Sextile Moon', null, 'This aspect offers the possibility of trust that is built slowly, intentionally, and over time. Moon-Saturn sextiles are not usually dramatic. They tend to reveal themselves through small acts of care that accumulate. Someone remembers. Someone checks in. Someone follows through on what they said they would do. The relationship gains strength through consistency rather than intensity.

When this aspect is working well, it creates a sense of emotional stability. This person may help you approach your feelings with maturity and care rather than getting lost in them. They can encourage you to give your emotions the attention they need without treating them as a problem to fix. Their steady presence may make it easier to carry life''s responsibilities while still honoring what you feel.

The growth edge is learning how to receive what is being offered. Old experiences may have taught you to handle everything alone or to hide your needs before anyone can dismiss them. Meanwhile, this person may express care through reliability and practical support rather than overt displays of emotion. Both people benefit from learning each other''s language of care.

The gift is commitment. It is the willingness to keep showing up, to keep listening, and to keep tending to what matters. Emotional safety is built through practice. This aspect can create something steady, grounding, and lasting when both people are willing to help build it.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This aspect offers the possibility of trust that is built slowly, intentionally, and over time. Moon-Saturn sextiles are not usually dramatic. They tend to reveal themselves through small acts of care that accumulate. Someone remembers. Someone checks in. Someone follows through on what they said they would do. The relationship gains strength through consistency rather than intensity.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it creates a sense of emotional stability. This person may help you approach your feelings with maturity and care rather than getting lost in them. They can encourage you to give your emotions the attention they need without treating them as a problem to fix. Their steady presence may make it easier to carry life''s responsibilities while still honoring what you feel.\n\nThe growth edge is learning how to receive what is being offered. Old experiences may have taught you to handle everything alone or to hide your needs before anyone can dismiss them. Meanwhile, this person may express care through reliability and practical support rather than overt displays of emotion. Both people benefit from learning each other''s language of care.\n\nThe gift is commitment. It is the willingness to keep showing up, to keep listening, and to keep tending to what matters. Emotional safety is built through practice. This aspect can create something steady, grounding, and lasting when both people are willing to help build it."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The growth edge is learning how to receive what is being offered. Old experiences may have taught you to handle everything alone or to hide your needs before anyone can dismiss them. Meanwhile, this person may express care through reliability and practical support rather than overt displays of emotion. Both people benefit from learning each other''s language of care."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The gift is commitment. It is the willingness to keep showing up, to keep listening, and to keep tending to what matters. Emotional safety is built through practice. This aspect can create something steady, grounding, and lasting when both people are willing to help build it."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-moon_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Saturn person can help the Moon person feel safer through consistency, practical care, and follow-through. The Moon person softens Saturn''s guardedness. This works best when both people treat emotional needs as real, not inconvenient.","summaryDeep":"This aspect offers the possibility of trust that is built slowly, intentionally, and over time. Moon-Saturn sextiles are not usually dramatic. They tend to reveal themselves through small acts of care that accumulate. Someone remembers. Someone checks in. Someone follows through on what they said they would do. The relationship gains strength through consistency rather than intensity.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it creates a sense of emotional stability. This person may help you approach your feelings with maturity and care rather than getting lost in them. They can encourage you to give your emotions the attention they need without treating them as a problem to fix. Their steady presence may make it easier to carry life''s responsibilities while still honoring what you feel.\n\nThe growth edge is learning how to receive what is being offered. Old experiences may have taught you to handle everything alone or to hide your needs before anyone can dismiss them. Meanwhile, this person may express care through reliability and practical support rather than overt displays of emotion. Both people benefit from learning each other''s language of care.\n\nThe gift is commitment. It is the willingness to keep showing up, to keep listening, and to keep tending to what matters. Emotional safety is built through practice. This aspect can create something steady, grounding, and lasting when both people are willing to help build it.","tension":"The growth edge is learning how to receive what is being offered. Old experiences may have taught you to handle everything alone or to hide your needs before anyone can dismiss them. Meanwhile, this person may express care through reliability and practical support rather than overt displays of emotion. Both people benefit from learning each other''s language of care.","advice":"The gift is commitment. It is the willingness to keep showing up, to keep listening, and to keep tending to what matters. Emotional safety is built through practice. This aspect can create something steady, grounding, and lasting when both people are willing to help build it.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-moon_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"moon","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-moon_square', 'synastry-saturn-square-moon', 'relationship-saturn-square-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-moon_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-moon_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Square Moon', null, 'This person can make you feel like your feelings are wrong.

They may not say it directly. It may come through as criticism, correction, silence, or a response that feels colder than the moment needs. You share something vulnerable, and suddenly you feel exposed. You ask for comfort, and somehow you end up defending why you needed it.

This can get under your skin quickly. Over time, you may stop questioning their reaction and start questioning yourself. You wonder if you are too sensitive, too needy, too emotional, too much. That is where this aspect becomes painful. The judgment does not stay between you. It starts living inside you.

At its best, this friction pushes you toward stronger self-respect. You learn to stand by your feelings instead of apologizing for them. You learn that emotional maturity is not about having fewer needs. It is about being honest about them without letting shame take over.

At its worst, you can end up chasing approval that never quite arrives. You explain yourself. You try harder. You adjust your approach. You make yourself smaller. Yet it still feels like the understanding you want remains out of reach. The lesson here is not to stop feeling. It is to learn how to hold your feelings without turning against yourself. You can reflect on your patterns. You can take responsibility for your actions. You can grow. None of that requires you to believe that your needs are the problem.

Do not let someone else''s discomfort with emotions become the measure of your worth.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can make you feel like your feelings are wrong.\n\nThey may not say it directly. It may come through as criticism, correction, silence, or a response that feels colder than the moment needs. You share something vulnerable, and suddenly you feel exposed. You ask for comfort, and somehow you end up defending why you needed it.\n\nThis can get under your skin quickly. Over time, you may stop questioning their reaction and start questioning yourself. You wonder if you are too sensitive, too needy, too emotional, too much. That is where this aspect becomes painful. The judgment does not stay between you. It starts living inside you.\n\nAt its best, this friction pushes you toward stronger self-respect. You learn to stand by your feelings instead of apologizing for them. You learn that emotional maturity is not about having fewer needs. It is about being honest about them without letting shame take over.\n\nAt its worst, you can end up chasing approval that never quite arrives. You explain yourself. You try harder. You adjust your approach. You make yourself smaller. Yet it still feels like the understanding you want remains out of reach. The lesson here is not to stop feeling. It is to learn how to hold your feelings without turning against yourself. You can reflect on your patterns. You can take responsibility for your actions. You can grow. None of that requires you to believe that your needs are the problem.\n\nDo not let someone else''s discomfort with emotions become the measure of your worth."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its worst, you can end up chasing approval that never quite arrives. You explain yourself. You try harder. You adjust your approach. You make yourself smaller. Yet it still feels like the understanding you want remains out of reach. The lesson here is not to stop feeling. It is to learn how to hold