try_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-saturn_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"saturn","planetB":"venus","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-saturn_B-venus_sextile', 'synastry-saturn-sextile-venus', 'relationship-saturn-sextile-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-saturn_B-venus_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-saturn_B-venus_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Saturn Sextile Venus', null, 'This connection tends to develop through small, steady choices rather than dramatic moments. Trust is built gradually as both people learn they can rely on each other. Over time, the relationship gains strength from simple acts of dependability, such as keeping promises, being honest, showing up when it matters, and proving through actions that the bond is worth investing in.

When this aspect is working well, it teaches both people that love is something you build, not something you stumble into. Care becomes more intentional. Commitment gives affection somewhere to land. This person may encourage you to honor your needs, strengthen your boundaries, and take your own worth seriously. They can remind you that the relationships that endure are often the ones that are nurtured slowly, with consistency and care.

The invitation here is to participate. Saturn asks for effort, presence, and accountability. If one person waits to feel completely safe before opening up, or if vulnerability stays hidden behind too many defenses, the connection can feel more distant than it needs to. The capacity for devotion exists, but it has to be practiced to become tangible.

This aspect asks for patience without abandoning yourself. It asks for discernment without shutting love out. It asks both people to express care in ways that can actually be felt and received. Over time, this connection can grow into something solid and dependable, built through consistent effort and a shared willingness to care for it intentionally.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection tends to develop through small, steady choices rather than dramatic moments. Trust is built gradually as both people learn they can rely on each other. Over time, the relationship gains strength from simple acts of dependability, such as keeping promises, being honest, showing up when it matters, and proving through actions that the bond is worth investing in.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it teaches both people that love is something you build, not something you stumble into. Care becomes more intentional. Commitment gives affection somewhere to land. This person may encourage you to honor your needs, strengthen your boundaries, and take your own worth seriously. They can remind you that the relationships that endure are often the ones that are nurtured slowly, with consistency and care.\n\nThe invitation here is to participate. Saturn asks for effort, presence, and accountability. If one person waits to feel completely safe before opening up, or if vulnerability stays hidden behind too many defenses, the connection can feel more distant than it needs to. The capacity for devotion exists, but it has to be practiced to become tangible.\n\nThis aspect asks for patience without abandoning yourself. It asks for discernment without shutting love out. It asks both people to express care in ways that can actually be felt and received. Over time, this connection can grow into something solid and dependable, built through consistent effort and a shared willingness to care for it intentionally."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The invitation here is to participate. Saturn asks for effort, presence, and accountability. If one person waits to feel completely safe before opening up, or if vulnerability stays hidden behind too many defenses, the connection can feel more distant than it needs to. The capacity for devotion exists, but it has to be practiced to become tangible."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This aspect asks for patience without abandoning yourself. It asks for discernment without shutting love out. It asks both people to express care in ways that can actually be felt and received. Over time, this connection can grow into something solid and dependable, built through consistent effort and a shared willingness to care for it intentionally."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-saturn_B-venus_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Saturn person can help Venus turn affection into commitment, plans, and steady acts of care. Venus helps Saturn soften. This is supportive when responsibility protects love rather than replacing it.","summaryDeep":"This connection tends to develop through small, steady choices rather than dramatic moments. Trust is built gradually as both people learn they can rely on each other. Over time, the relationship gains strength from simple acts of dependability, such as keeping promises, being honest, showing up when it matters, and proving through actions that the bond is worth investing in.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it teaches both people that love is something you build, not something you stumble into. Care becomes more intentional. Commitment gives affection somewhere to land. This person may encourage you to honor your needs, strengthen your boundaries, and take your own worth seriously. They can remind you that the relationships that endure are often the ones that are nurtured slowly, with consistency and care.\n\nThe invitation here is to participate. Saturn asks for effort, presence, and accountability. If one person waits to feel completely safe before opening up, or if