  ('A-sun_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry-sun-sextile-jupiter', 'relationship-sun-sextile-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-jupiter_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-jupiter_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Sextile Jupiter', null, 'There is something quietly encouraging about this connection.

This person may have a way of responding to your ideas that makes them feel more possible. You mention something you have been thinking about, and instead of dismissing it or poking holes in it, they become curious. They ask questions. They want to know more. What begins as a passing thought can start to feel like something worth pursuing simply because someone else is willing to take it seriously.

The support here often grows through conversation. You share a hope, a plan, or a direction you are considering, and they help you see it more clearly. Not by telling you what to do, but by reflecting back possibilities you may not have noticed on your own. Their faith in your potential can help you trust yourself enough to take the next step.

When this works, this person is in your corner. They celebrate your progress, remind you why you started, and help you keep sight of what matters when you get lost in the details. Their encouragement feels supportive, not overwhelming.

The challenge is that you have to let them in. If you keep your hopes to yourself or wait until everything is figured out before sharing it, you may never experience the full support this connection can offer.

Talk about what you want before you have everything figured out. Share the goal while it is still a work in progress. This connection becomes most useful when you let this person support your growth, challenge you to think bigger, and hold you accountable to what you say you want.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is something quietly encouraging about this connection.\n\nThis person may have a way of responding to your ideas that makes them feel more possible. You mention something you have been thinking about, and instead of dismissing it or poking holes in it, they become curious. They ask questions. They want to know more. What begins as a passing thought can start to feel like something worth pursuing simply because someone else is willing to take it seriously.\n\nThe support here often grows through conversation. You share a hope, a plan, or a direction you are considering, and they help you see it more clearly. Not by telling you what to do, but by reflecting back possibilities you may not have noticed on your own. Their faith in your potential can help you trust yourself enough to take the next step.\n\nWhen this works, this person is in your corner. They celebrate your progress, remind you why you started, and help you keep sight of what matters when you get lost in the details. Their encouragement feels supportive, not overwhelming.\n\nThe challenge is that you have to let them in. If you keep your hopes to yourself or wait until everything is figured out before sharing it, you may never experience the full support this connection can offer.\n\nTalk about what you want before you have everything figured out. Share the goal while it is still a work in progress. This connection becomes most useful when you let this person support your growth, challenge you to think bigger, and hold you accountable to what you say you want."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that you have to let them in. If you keep your hopes to yourself or