  ('A-sun_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"mars","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-mars_conjunction', 'synastry-sun-conjunction-mars', 'relationship-sun-conjunction-mars']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-mars_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-mars_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Conjunction Mars', null, 'This person energizes you in a way that is hard to ignore. They can quiet the voice in your head that second-guesses everything and bring out the part of you that trusts its instincts and just goes for it. The attraction here is immediate, and so is the momentum. Things can spark quickly, heat up quickly, and take on a life of their own before either of you has time to slow down and think about where it is all going. This is not the kind of connection that likes to sit still. It wants movement, action, and the thrill of seeing what happens when neither of you holds back.

At its best, this person helps you trust yourself a little more. You may find yourself acting on things you would normally overthink, saying what you really mean, or finally dealing with something you have been putting off. It can feel good to be around someone who gets you out of your head and reminds you that you do not have to second-guess every step.

At its most challenging, the same energy can feel like pressure. What starts out exciting can turn into frustration when one person wants to move faster than the other. You may feel like they''re pushing you, while they may feel like they''re just trying to get things moving. Because there''s so much energy between you, even small disagreements can pick up speed before either of you realizes it.

The good news is that this energy does not have to turn into conflict. It works best when you channel it into something shared. Tackle a project, make plans, get out of the house, or work toward a goal together. The more you have to focus on as a team, the less likely you are to end up pushing against each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person energizes you in a way that is hard to ignore. They can quiet the voice in your head that second-guesses everything and bring out the part of you that trusts its instincts and just goes for it. The attraction here is immediate, and so is the momentum. Things can spark quickly, heat up quickly, and take on a life of their own before either of you has time to slow down and think about where it is all going. This is not the kind of connection that likes to sit still. It wants movement, action, and the thrill of seeing what happens when neither of you holds back.\n\nAt its best, this person helps you trust yourself a little more. You may find yourself acting on things you would normally overthink, saying what you really mean, or finally dealing with something you have been putting off. It can feel good to be around someone who gets you out of your head and reminds you that you do not have to second-guess every step.\n\nAt its most challenging, the same energy can feel like pressure. What starts out exciting can turn into frustration when one person wants to move faster than the other. You may feel like they''re pushing you, while they may feel like they''re just trying to get things moving. Because there''s so much energy between you, even small disagreements can pick up speed before either of you realizes it.\n\nThe good news is that this energy does not have to turn into conflict. It works best when you channel it into something shared. Tackle a project, make plans, get out of the house, or work toward a goal together. The more you have to focus on as a team, the less likely you are to end up pushing against each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its most challenging, the same energy can feel like pressure. What starts out exciting can turn into frustration when one person wants to move faster than the other. You may feel like they''re pushing you, while they may feel like they''re just trying to get things moving. Because there''s so much energy between you, even small disagreements can pick up speed before either of you realizes it."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The good news is that this energy does not have to turn into conflict. It works best when you channel it into something shared. Tackle a project, make plans, get out of the house, or work toward a goal together. The more you have to focus on as a team, the less likely you are to end up pushing against each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-mars_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s drive. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person energizes you in a way that is hard to ignore. They can quiet the voice in your head that second-guesses everything and bring out the part of you that trusts its instincts and just goes for it. The attraction here is immediate, and so is the momentum. Things can spark quickly, heat up quickly, and take on a life of their own before either of you has time to slow down and think about where it is all going. This is not the kind of connection that likes to sit still. It wants movement, action, and the thrill of seeing what happens when neither of you holds back.\n\nAt its best, this person helps you trust yourself a little more. You may find yourself acting on things you would normally overthink, saying what you really mean, or finally dealing with something you have been putting off. It can feel good to be around someone who gets you out of your head and reminds you that you do not have to second-guess every step.\n\nAt its most challenging, the same energy can feel like pressure. What