  ('A-sun_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-mercury_conjunction', 'synastry-sun-conjunction-mercury', 'relationship-sun-conjunction-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-mercury_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-mercury_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Conjunction Mercury', null, 'This person may seem to understand you right away. Conversation often feels easy, as if they naturally follow your train of thought and quickly pick up on what matters to you.

When this works well, it can feel deeply affirming. They may notice parts of you that often go unseen and reflect them back in a way that resonates. You might feel that they are paying close attention, not just to what you say, but to the energy, intentions, and essence behind it. Their observations can help you feel witnessed in a meaningful way, as though they are looking past the obvious and connecting with something more fundamental about who you are.

Being understood by them can feel like exhaling. You may feel less guarded, less alone in your experience, and more able to be yourself without explanation. At times, they may find the words for something you have always felt but never fully named.

Remember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.

Keep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may seem to understand you right away. Conversation often feels easy, as if they naturally follow your train of thought and quickly pick up on what matters to you.\n\nWhen this works well, it can feel deeply affirming. They may notice parts of you that often go unseen and reflect them back in a way that resonates. You might feel that they are paying close attention, not just to what you say, but to the energy, intentions, and essence behind it. Their observations can help you feel witnessed in a meaningful way, as though they are looking past the obvious and connecting with something more fundamental about who you are.\n\nBeing understood by them can feel like exhaling. You may feel less guarded, less alone in your experience, and more able to be yourself without explanation. At times, they may find the words for something you have always felt but never fully named.\n\nRemember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.\n\nKeep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Remember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Keep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-mercury_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s mind. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person may seem to understand you right away. Conversation often feels easy, as if they naturally follow your train of thought and quickly pick up on what matters to you.\n\nWhen this works well, it can feel deeply affirming. They may notice parts of you that often go unseen and reflect them back in a way that resonates. You might feel that they are paying close attention, not just to what you say, but to the energy, intentions, and essence behind it. Their observations can help you feel witnessed in a meaningful way, as though they are looking past the obvious and connecting with something more fundamental about who you are.\n\nBeing understood by them can feel like exhaling. You may feel less guarded, less alone in your experience, and more able to be yourself without explanation. At times, they may find the words for something you have always felt but never fully named.\n\nRemember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.\n\nKeep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other.","tension":"Remember that feeling understood is not the same as someone knowing everything about you. This person may think they know what you mean before you have finished explaining.","advice":"Keep sharing who you are as you grow and change. The real gift here is staying open, curious, and willing to keep learning about each other.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-mercury_opposition', 'synastry-sun-opposition-mercury', 'relationship-sun-opposition-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-mercury_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-mercury_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Opposition Mercury', null, 'This person may reflect back a version of you that you do not immediately recognize.

They can notice qualities, patterns, and motivations that sit just outside your usual field of vision. Sometimes their observations feel illuminating, like they have found language for something you have always sensed but never fully understood. Other times, their perspective can feel unsettling, exposing a truth you were not ready to face or describing you in a way that misses the heart of who you are.

This connection often asks you to meet yourself through contrast. Their way of thinking may challenge your self-image, not because they are trying to change you, but because they naturally stand across from your point of view. What they see and what you know about yourself may not always match.

At its best, this dynamic expands your awareness. It invites you to consider that there may be more than one truth in the room. Their insight can help you understand how you impact others, while your perspective can remind them that no one is fully defined by an outside interpretation.

At its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal.

Stay open. You do not have to agree with everything they see, but you can stay curious. Keep your own perspective while making room for theirs.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may reflect back a version of you that you do not immediately recognize.\n\nThey can notice qualities, patterns, and motivations that sit just outside your usual field of vision. Sometimes their observations feel illuminating, like they have found language for something you have always sensed but never fully understood. Other times, their perspective can feel unsettling, exposing a truth you were not ready to face or describing you in a way that misses the heart of who you are.\n\nThis connection often asks you to meet yourself through contrast. Their way of thinking may challenge your self-image, not because they are trying to change you, but because they naturally stand across from your point of view. What they see and what you know about yourself may not always match.\n\nAt its best, this dynamic expands your awareness. It invites you to consider that there may be more than one truth in the room. Their insight can help you understand how you impact others, while your perspective can remind them that no one is fully defined by an outside interpretation.\n\nAt its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal.\n\nStay open. You do not have to agree with everything they see, but you can stay curious. Keep your own perspective while making room for theirs."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its most difficult, conversations can become a struggle over who gets to name reality. You may feel misunderstood. They may feel unheard. Both people can become attached to proving their perspective instead of remaining open about what the other is trying to reveal."}