  ('A-sun_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-mercury_sextile', 'synastry-sun-sextile-mercury', 'relationship-sun-sextile-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-mercury_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-mercury_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Sextile Mercury', null, 'This person may help you feel understood in a way that stays with you. They have a way of asking the question that gets to the heart of something, or noticing the detail that everyone else missed. Conversations with them can leave you feeling clearer about yourself. Not because they tell you who you are, but because they create space for you to hear your own thoughts more honestly.

There is often a quiet sense of safety here. You may find yourself sharing things you did not plan to say, simply because it feels natural to keep opening up. Their curiosity can feel genuine, and that makes it easier to let them see more of the real you.

The connection often grows through small moments that matter more than they seem. They remember something important to you. They ask about it later. They listen closely enough that you can feel the difference. Those moments can create a powerful feeling of being seen, valued, and understood.

At its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is.

The more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may help you feel understood in a way that stays with you. They have a way of asking the question that gets to the heart of something, or noticing the detail that everyone else missed. Conversations with them can leave you feeling clearer about yourself. Not because they tell you who you are, but because they create space for you to hear your own thoughts more honestly.\n\nThere is often a quiet sense of safety here. You may find yourself sharing things you did not plan to say, simply because it feels natural to keep opening up. Their curiosity can feel genuine, and that makes it easier to let them see more of the real you.\n\nThe connection often grows through small moments that matter more than they seem. They remember something important to you. They ask about it later. They listen closely enough that you can feel the difference. Those moments can create a powerful feeling of being seen, valued, and understood.\n\nAt its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is.\n\nThe more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connection feels. What starts as easy communication can grow into something deeper: the feeling that someone truly sees you and wants to know you more."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its best, this connection reminds you that understanding is not built through grand declarations. It is built through attention. Through showing up. Through caring enough to keep learning who the other person is."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The more honest the conversation becomes, the more meaningful the connectio