  ('A-sun_B-pluto_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-pluto_square', 'synastry-sun-square-pluto', 'relationship-sun-square-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-pluto_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-pluto_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Square Pluto', null, 'This person gets under your skin. The square brings friction, pressure, and a kind of psychological heat that is hard to ignore. The Pluto person may stir something in the Sun person that has been buried for a long time. Old defenses rise. Hidden fears surface. Reactions may feel bigger than the moment itself.

There is magnetism here, but it is rarely simple. You may find yourself drawn back to this person again and again, even when the connection feels uncomfortable or exposes tender places within you. Interactions can stir powerful emotional reactions that seem larger than the circumstances at hand, bringing buried fears, insecurities, and unmet needs to the surface. In trying to protect what feels vulnerable, both people may be tempted to grasp for certainty, influence outcomes, or hold each other too tightly.

When handled in a healthy way, this aspect can help both people grow. The Pluto person may point out areas where the Sun person has given away their power, avoided facing the truth, or stayed in situations that feel comfortable but are no longer good for them. Even though this can be uncomfortable, the challenges between them can bring old habits to the surface and create an opportunity for real change.

But pressure is not always growth.

If this relationship consistently brings up strong emotions or challenges, it''s worth paying attention to how those experiences are affecting both of you. Intense connections can be deeply meaningful and transformative, but they can also highlight areas where growth, communication, or clearer boundaries are needed.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person gets under your skin. The square brings friction, pressure, and a kind of psychological heat that is hard to ignore. The Pluto person may stir something in the Sun person that has been buried for a long time. Old defenses rise. Hidden fears surface. Reactions may feel bigger than the moment itself.\n\nThere is magnetism here, but it is rarely simple. You may find yourself drawn back to this person again and again, even when the connection feels uncomfortable or exposes tender places within you. Interactions can stir powerful emotional reactions that seem larger than the circumstances at hand, bringing buried fears, insecurities, and unmet needs to the surface. In trying to protect what feels vulnerable, both people may be tempted to grasp for certainty, influence outcomes, or hold each other too tightly.\n\nWhen handled in a healthy way, this aspect can help both people grow. The Pluto person may point out areas where the Sun person has given away their power, avoided facing the truth, or stayed in situations that feel comfortable but are no longer good for them. Even though this can be uncomfortable, the challenges between them can bring old habits to the surface and create an opportunity for real change.\n\nBut pressure is not always growth.\n\nIf this relationship consistently brings up strong emotions or challenges, it''s worth paying attention to how those experiences are affecting both of you. Intense connections can be deeply meaningful and transformative, but they can also highlight areas where growth, communication, or clearer boundaries are needed."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But pressure is not always growth."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"If this relationship consistently brings up strong emotions or challenges, it''s worth paying attention to how those experiences are affecting both of you. Intense connections can be deeply meaningful and transformative, but they can also highlight areas where growth, communication, or clearer boundaries are needed."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-pluto_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Sun person''s identity meets Pluto''s pressure, and the relationship can feel consuming. Growth is possible, but only if both people refuse control tactics. The Sun person should not have to disappear to keep the bond alive.","summaryDeep":"This person gets under your skin. The square brings friction, pressure, and a kind of psychological heat that is hard to ignore. The Pluto person may stir something in the Sun person that has been buried for a long time. Old defenses rise. Hidden fears surface. Reactions may feel bigger than the moment itself.\n\nThere is magnetism here, but it is rarely simple. You may find yourself drawn back to this person again and again, even when the connection feels uncomfortable or exposes tender places within you. Interactions can stir powerful emotional reactions that seem larger than the circumstances at hand, bringing buried fears, insecurities, and unmet needs to the surface. In trying to protect what feels vulnerable, both people may be tempted to grasp for certainty, influence outcomes, or hold each other too tightly.\n\nWhen handled in a healthy way, this aspect can help both people grow. The Pluto person may point out areas where the Sun person has given away their power, avoided facing the truth, or stayed in situations that feel comfortable but are no longer good for them. Even though this can be uncomfortable, the challenges between them can bring old habits to the surface and create an opportunity for real change.\n\nBut pressure is not always growth.\n\nIf this relationship consistently brings up strong emotions or challenges, it''s worth paying attention to how those experiences are affecting both of you. Intense connections can be deeply meaningful and transformative, but they can also highlight areas where growth, communication, or clearer boundaries are needed.","tension":"But pressure is not always growth.","advice":"If this relationship consistently brings up strong emotions or challenges, it''s worth paying attention to how those experiences are affecting both of you. Intense connections can be deeply meaningful and transformative, but they can also highlight areas where growth, communication, or clearer boundaries are needed.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-pluto_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-pluto_trine', 'synastry-sun-trine-pluto', 'relationship-sun-trine-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-pluto_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-pluto_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Trine Pluto', null, 'This connection carries depth without demanding crisis. When one person''s Pluto forms a trine to another person''s Sun, there is often a natural sense of trust between them, as though vulnerability can emerge without force. The Pluto person tends to recognize the Sun person''s strengths, fears, and untapped potential with remarkable clarity, yet their insight feels supportive rather than invasive. In response, the Sun person may feel deeply seen and accepted, making it easier to show up authentically, speak honestly, and grow into more of who they are.

There is still intensity here. Pluto never loses its capacity to transform. But the energy tends to flow with less resistance than it does in the conjunction, square, or opposition. Instead of forcing change through crisis, this aspect often supports growth through encouragement, insight, and mutual respect.

At its best, the Pluto person helps the Sun person recognize their own power. They may inspire greater confidence, emotional honesty, and a willingness to step more fully into life. The Sun person often feels strengthened by the connection, as though someone is quietly reminding them of who they are beneath old fears and limiting stories.

One of the gifts of this aspect is the way it can make growth feel safe. The relationship often creates enough trust for both people to be honest about who they are and what they are moving through. Instead of forcing change through crisis or conflict, it can support a more natural process of self-discovery. That said, it is still a Pluto aspect, and Pluto''s influence is rarely insignificant. Because the connection flows so easily, it can be easy to miss just how much impact the relationship is having. The Pluto person may carry more influence than either person realizes, and the Sun person may not always notice how deeply they are being shaped by the bond.

Healthy awareness and strong boundaries help ensure that the connection remains empowering rather than overwhelming.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection carries depth without demanding crisis. When one person''s Pluto forms a trine to another person''s Sun, there is often a natural sense of trust between them, as though vulnerability can emerge without force. The Pluto person tends to recognize the Sun person''s strengths, fears, and untapped potential with remarkable clarity, yet their insight feels supportive rather than invasive. In response, the Sun person may feel deeply seen and accepted, making it easier to show up authentically, speak honestly, and grow into more of who they are.\n\nThere is still intensity here. Pluto never loses its capacity to transform. But the energy tends to flow with less resistance than it does in the conjunction, square, or opposition. Instead of forcing change through crisis, this aspect often supports growth through encouragement, insight, and mutual respect.\n\nAt its best, the Pluto person helps the Sun person recognize their own power. They may inspire greater confidence, emotional honesty, and a willingness to step more fully into life. The Sun person often feels strengthened by the connection, as though someone is quietly reminding them of who they are beneath old fears and limiting stories.\n\nOne of the gifts of this aspect is the way it can make growth feel safe. The relationship often creates enough trust for both people to be honest about who they are and what they are moving through. Instead of forcing change through crisis or conflict, it can support a more natural process of self-discovery. That said, it is still a Pluto aspect, and Pluto''s influence is rarely insignificant. Because the connection flows so easily, it can be easy to miss just how much impact the relationship is having. The Pluto person may carry more influence than either person realizes, and the Sun person may not always notice how deeply they are being shaped by the bond.\n\nHealthy awareness and strong boundaries help ensure that the connection remains empowering rather than overwhelming."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"One of the gifts of this aspect is the way it can make growth feel safe. The relationship often creates enough trust for both people to be honest about who they are and what they are moving through. Instead of forcing change through crisis or conflict, it can support a more natural process of self-discovery. That said, it is still a Pluto aspect, and Pluto''s influence is rarely insignificant. Because the connection flows so easily, it can be easy to miss just how much impact the relationship is having. The Pluto person may carry more influence than either person realizes, and the Sun person may not always notice how deeply they are being shaped by the bond."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Healthy awareness and strong boundaries help ensure that the connection remains empowering rather than overwhelming."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-pluto_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s depth and power. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This connection carries depth without demanding crisis. When one person''s Pluto forms a trine to another person''s Sun, there is often a natural sense of trust between them, as though vulnerability can emerge without force. The Pluto person tends to recognize the Sun person''s strengths, fears, and untapped potential with remarkable clarity, yet their insight feels supportive rather than invasive. In response, the Sun person may feel deeply seen and accepted, making it easier to show up authentically, speak honestly, and grow into more of who they are.\n\nThere is still intensity here. Pluto never loses its capacity to transform. But the energy tends to flow with less resistance than it does in the conjunction, square, or opposition. Instead of forcing change through crisis, this aspect often supports growth through encouragement, insight, and mutual respect.\n\nAt its best, the Pluto person helps the Sun person recognize their own power. They may inspire greater confidence, emotional honesty, and a willingness to step more fully into life. The Sun person often feels strengthened by the connection, as though someone is quietly reminding them of who they are beneath old fears and limiting stories.\n\nOne of the gifts of this aspect is the way it can make growth feel safe. The relationship often creates enough trust for both people to be honest about who they are and what they are moving through. Instead of forcing change through crisis or conflict, it can support a more natural process of self-discovery. That said, it is still a Pluto aspect, and Pluto''s influence is rarely insignificant. Because the connection flows so easily, it can be easy to miss just how much impact the relationship is having. The Pluto person may carry more influence than either person realizes, and the Sun person may not always notice how deeply they are being shaped by the bond.\n\nHealthy awareness and strong boundaries help ensure that the connection remains empowering rather than overwhelming.","tension":"One of the gifts of this aspect is the way it can make growth feel safe. The relationship often creates enough trust for both people to be honest about who they are and what they are moving through. Instead of forcing change through crisis or conflict, it can support a more natural process of self-discovery. That said, it is still a Pluto aspect, and Pluto''s influence is rarely insignificant. Because the connection flows so easily, it can be easy to miss just how much impact the relationship is having. The Pluto person may carry more influence than either person realizes, and the Sun person may not always notice how deeply they are being shaped by the bond.","advice":"Healthy awareness and strong boundaries help ensure that the connection remains empowering rather than overwhelming.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-saturn_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-saturn_conjunction', 'synastry-sun-conjunction-saturn', 'relationship-sun-conjunction-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-saturn_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-saturn_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Conjunction Saturn', null, 'This person may push you to operate at a higher level.

Around them, you may become more aware of your goals, your habits, and the gap between where you are and where you want to be. They tend to pay attention to results, consistency, and follow-through. Because of that, the connection can feel motivating, demanding, and occasionally intimidating.

They encourage you to think long-term, stay focused, and invest in meaningful growth. They may see capabilities in you that are not fully developed yet and challenge you to take them seriously.

That kind of support has its own quiet power. Instead of reflecting back who you already believe yourself to be, this person may ask you to become it. Confidence grows here not from reassurance, but from the slow accumulation of effort, commitment, and the undeniable evidence of what you are capable of building over time.

The challenge is that accountability can turn into pressure. You may begin measuring your worth by their feedback or feel like you are constantly trying to prove yourself. If expectations keep increasing without recognition of your progress, the relationship can start to feel like an endless performance review.

Pay attention to the impact this has on your confidence. Healthy challenge helps you grow and develop new strengths. Unhealthy pressure leaves you feeling inadequate no matter how much you accomplish.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may push you to operate at a higher level.\n\nAround them, you may become more aware of your goals, your habits, and the gap between where you are and where you want to be. They tend to pay attention to results, consistency, and follow-through. Because of that, the connection can feel motivating, demanding, and occasionally intimidating.\n\nThey encourage you to think long-term, stay focused, and invest in meaningful growth. They may see capabilities in you that are not fully developed yet and challenge you to take them seriously.\n\nThat kind of support has its own quiet power. Instead of reflecting back who you already believe yourself to be, this person may ask you to become it. Confidence grows here not from reassurance, but from the slow accumulation of effort, commitment, and the undeniable evidence of what you are capable of building over time.\n\nThe challenge is that accountability can turn into pressure. You may begin measuring your worth by their feedback or feel like you are constantly trying to prove yourself. If expectations keep increasing without recognition of your progress, the relationship can start to feel like an endless performance review.\n\nPay attention to the impact this has on your confidence. Healthy challenge helps you grow and develop new strengths. Unhealthy pressure leaves you feeling inadequate no matter how much you accomplish."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that accountability can turn into pressure. You may begin measuring your worth by their feedback or feel like you are constantly trying to prove yourself. If expectations keep increasing without recognition of your progress, the relationship can start to feel like an endless performance review."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Pay attention to the impact this has on your confidence. Healthy challenge helps you grow and develop new strengths. Unhealthy pressure leaves you feeling inadequate no matter how much you accomplish."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-saturn_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Steadying and heavy at once. The Saturn person grounds the Sun person''s direction - anchor, mentor, ballast - or controls and dampens it. Built to last; can feel restrictive. Failure mode: a parent-child slide where one criticizes and one shrinks. Honesty about the weight keeps this a commitment instead of a cage; if it''s shrinking you, say so.","summaryDeep":"This person may push you to operate at a higher level.\n\nAround them, you may become more aware of your goals, your habits, and the gap between where you are and where you want to be. They tend to pay attention to results, consistency, and follow-through. Because of that, the connection can feel motivating, demanding, and occasionally intimidating.\n\nThey encourage you to think long-term, stay focused, and invest in meaningful growth. They may see capabilities in you that are not fully developed yet and challenge you to take them seriously.\n\nThat kind of support has its own quiet power. Instead of reflecting back who you already believe yourself to be, this person may ask you to become it. Confidence grows here not from reassurance, but from the slow accumulation of effort, commitment, and the undeniable evidence of what you are capable of building over time.\n\nThe challenge is that accountability can turn into pressure. You may begin measuring your worth by their feedback or feel like you are constantly trying to prove yourself. If expectations keep increasing without recognition of your progress, the relationship can start to feel like an endless performance review.\n\nPay attention to the impact this has on your confidence. Healthy challenge helps you grow and develop new strengths. Unhealthy pressure leaves you feeling inadequate no matter how much you accomplish.","tension":"The challenge is that accountability can turn into pressure. You may begin measuring your worth by their feedback or feel like you are constantly trying to prove yourself. If expectations keep increasing without recognition of your progress, the relationship can start to feel like an endless performance review.","advice":"Pay attention to the impact this has on your confidence. Healthy challenge helps you grow and develop new strengths. Unhealthy pressure leaves you feeling inadequate no matter how much you accomplish.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-saturn_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-saturn_opposition', 'synastry-sun-opposition-saturn', 'relationship-sun-opposition-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-saturn_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-saturn_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Opposition Saturn', null, 'This person may feel like a reality check.

They may slow you down, question your choices, or bring attention to responsibilities you would rather not deal with yet. At times, this can feel grounding. At other times, it can feel like they are standing between you and your own light.

When this works, they help you build more discipline. They may bring steadiness where you bring momentum. They may help you think long-term, make better decisions, and stop skipping the steps that matter. Their influence can make you more intentional.

The challenge is that the difference can turn into a standoff. You may feel judged or restricted. They may feel like you are not taking things seriously enough. You want room to be yourself. They want proof that you can handle what you are trying to become. This can create a painful pattern where one person feels controlled and the other feels responsible for holding everything together. Nobody feels fully seen. Nobody feels fully trusted.

This connection works best when seriousness becomes collaboration, not correction. Let them help you ground your life, but do not hand them the authority to define your worth. You can learn from someone without making them the judge of who you are.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may feel like a reality check.\n\nThey may slow you down, question your choices, or bring attention to responsibilities you would rather not deal with yet. At times, this can feel grounding. At other times, it can feel like they are standing between you and your own light.\n\nWhen this works, they help you build more discipline. They may bring steadiness where you bring momentum. They may help you think long-term, make better decisions, and stop skipping the steps that matter. Their influence can make you more intentional.\n\nThe challenge is that the difference can turn into a standoff. You may feel judged or restricted. They may feel like you are not taking things seriously enough. You want room to be yourself. They want proof that you can handle what you are trying to become. This can create a painful pattern where one person feels controlled and the other feels responsible for holding everything together. Nobody feels fully seen. Nobody feels fully trusted.\n\nThis connection works best when seriousness becomes collaboration, not correction. Let them help you ground your life, but do not hand them the authority to define your worth. You can learn from someone without making them the judge of who you are."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that the difference can turn into a standoff. You may feel judged or restricted. They may feel like you are not taking things seriously enough. You want room to be yourself. They want proof that you can handle what you are trying to become. This can create a painful pattern where one person feels controlled and the other feels responsible for holding everything together. Nobody feels fully seen. Nobody feels fully trusted."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This connection works best when seriousness becomes collaboration, not correction. Let them help you ground your life, but do not hand them the authority to define your worth. You can learn from someone without making them the judge of who you are."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-saturn_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Self-expression meets restriction across the relationship. The Saturn person''s caution opposes the Sun person''s drive - useful brakes, or a constant no. Failure mode: one is always the adult, one always the kid. Hold the line that matters, loosen the rest, and check who''s in charge of whom.","summaryDeep":"This person may feel like a reality check.\n\nThey may slow you down, question your choices, or bring attention to responsibilities you would rather not deal with yet. At times, this can feel grounding. At other times, it can feel like they are standing between you and your own light.\n\nWhen this works, they help you build more discipline. They may bring steadiness where you bring momentum. They may help you think long-term, make better decisions, and stop skipping the steps that matter. Their influence can make you more intentional.\n\nThe challenge is that the difference can turn into a standoff. You may feel judged or restricted. They may feel like you are not taking things seriously enough. You want room to be yourself. They want proof that you can handle what you are trying to become. This can create a painful pattern where one person feels controlled and the other feels responsible for holding everything together. Nobody feels fully seen. Nobody feels fully trusted.\n\nThis connection works best when seriousness becomes collaboration, not correction. Let them help you ground your life, but do not hand them the authority to define your worth. You can learn from someone without making them the judge of who you are.","tension":"The challenge is that the difference can turn into a standoff. You may feel judged or restricted. They may feel like you are not taking things seriously enough. You want room to be yourself. They want proof that you can handle what you are trying to become. This can create a painful pattern where one person feels controlled and the other feels responsible for holding everything together. Nobody feels fully seen. Nobody feels fully trusted.","advice":"This connection works best when seriousness becomes collaboration, not correction. Let them help you ground your life, but do not hand them the authority to define your worth. You can learn from someone without making them the judge of who you are.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-saturn_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-saturn_sextile', 'synastry-sun-sextile-saturn', 'relationship-sun-sextile-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-saturn_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-saturn_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Sextile Saturn', null, 'This connection offers the chance to build something solid, but it grows through effort rather than happening automatically. This person may take you seriously in a way that encourages you to take yourself seriously too. They may help you focus, follow through, and turn good intentions into something tangible. The support is there, but it becomes stronger the more you engage with it.

When this works, both of you become more dependable with each other. You show up. You keep your word. You make plans and follow through on them. Trust develops because, over time, both people demonstrate that they are willing to do what the relationship requires.

This is not the flashiest kind of support, but it can be one of the most valuable. It helps you mature. It asks you to stop treating potential as enough on its own. It reminds you that love, respect, and trust are built through consistent action.

The challenge is leaving that potential unused. You may recognize that this person could help you grow, yet avoid the commitment, honesty, or effort needed to deepen the connection.

Meet the seriousness with your own. Show up consistently. Say what you mean. Follow through. This connection becomes truly grounding when both people choose to build something real instead of simply hoping it will happen.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection offers the chance to build something solid, but it grows through effort rather than happening automatically. This person may take you seriously in a way that encourages you to take yourself seriously too. They may help you focus, follow through, and turn good intentions into something tangible. The support is there, but it becomes stronger the more you engage with it.\n\nWhen this works, both of you become more dependable with each other. You show up. You keep your word. You make plans and follow through on them. Trust develops because, over time, both people demonstrate that they are willing to do what the relationship requires.\n\nThis is not the flashiest kind of support, but it can be one of the most valuable. It helps you mature. It asks you to stop treating potential as enough on its own. It reminds you that love, respect, and trust are built through consistent action.\n\nThe challenge is leaving that potential unused. You may recognize that this person could help you grow, yet avoid the commitment, honesty, or effort needed to deepen the connection.\n\nMeet the seriousness with your own. Show up consistently. Say what you mean. Follow through. This connection becomes truly grounding when both people choose to build something real instead of simply hoping it will happen."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is leaving that potential unused. You may recognize that this person could help you grow, yet avoid the commitment, honesty, or effort needed to deepen the connection."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Meet the seriousness with your own. Show up consistently. Say what you mean. Follow through. This connection becomes truly grounding when both people choose to build something real instead of simply hoping it will happen."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-saturn_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Structure that supports identity. The Saturn person helps the Sun person build something real, available without strain. Failure mode: leaving the support on the table. Do the steady work together - good for long-term plans.","summaryDeep":"This connection offers the chance to build something solid, but it grows through effort rather than happening automatically. This person may take you seriously in a way that encourages you to take yourself seriously too. They may help you focus, follow through, and turn good intentions into something tangible. The support is there, but it becomes stronger the more you engage with it.\n\nWhen this works, both of you become more dependable with each other. You show up. You keep your word. You make plans and follow through on them. Trust develops because, over time, both people demonstrate that they are willing to do what the relationship requires.\n\nThis is not the flashiest kind of support, but it can be one of the most valuable. It helps you mature. It asks you to stop treating potential as enough on its own. It reminds you that love, respect, and trust are built through consistent action.\n\nThe challenge is leaving that potential unused. You may recognize that this person could help you grow, yet avoid the commitment, honesty, or effort needed to deepen the connection.\n\nMeet the seriousness with your own. Show up consistently. Say what you mean. Follow through. This connection becomes truly grounding when both people choose to build something real instead of simply hoping it will happen.","tension":"The challenge is leaving that potential unused. You may recognize that this person could help you grow, yet avoid the commitment, honesty, or effort needed to deepen the connection.","advice":"Meet the seriousness with your own. Show up consistently. Say what you mean. Follow through. This connection becomes truly grounding when both people choose to build something real instead of simply hoping it will happen.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-saturn_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-saturn_square', 'synastry-sun-square-saturn', 'relationship-sun-square-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-saturn_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-saturn_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Square Saturn', null, 'This person can make you feel like you are never quite good enough. Around them, you may feel judged, corrected, or held to standards you did not agree to. Sometimes it is explicit. Sometimes it is just the feeling that you are being watched and measured. Either way, it can be hard to relax.

The lesson here is learning the difference between responsibility and shame. This connection often exposes places where you need more discipline, maturity, or follow-through. It can push you to stop avoiding difficult truths, take ownership of your choices, and build a stronger foundation for yourself. Growth comes from accepting what needs work without deciding that your worth depends on being perfect.

At its best, this pushes you to get your act together. They may call out excuses, challenge weak spots, or force you to take responsibility for things you would rather avoid. The experience is not always comfortable, but it can help you build resilience, accountability, and a stronger foundation for success if you are willing to engage with the lessons being offered.

At its worst, the lesson gets distorted. You keep trying to prove yourself. They keep finding flaws. Instead of learning responsibility, you learn self-doubt. Instead of building confidence, you become preoccupied with what is wrong with you. The question is whether the challenge is teaching you to trust yourself more or less.

A healthy Sun-Saturn square helps you develop strength, accountability, and self-respect. An unhealthy one leaves you believing that no matter what you do, you will never be enough.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can make you feel like you are never quite good enough. Around them, you may feel judged, corrected, or held to standards you did not agree to. Sometimes it is explicit. Sometimes it is just the feeling that you are being watched and measured. Either way, it can be hard to relax.\n\nThe lesson here is learning the difference between responsibility and shame. This connection often exposes places where you need more discipline, maturity, or follow-through. It can push you to stop avoiding difficult truths, take ownership of your choices, and build a stronger foundation for yourself. Growth comes from accepting what needs work without deciding that your worth depends on being perfect.\n\nAt its best, this pushes you to get your act together. They may call out excuses, challenge weak spots, or force you to take responsibility for things you would rather avoid. The experience is not always comfortable, but it can help you build resilience, accountability, and a stronger foundation for success if you are willing to engage with the lessons being offered.\n\nAt its worst, the lesson gets distorted. You keep trying to prove yourself. They keep finding flaws. Instead of learning responsibility, you learn self-doubt. Instead of building confidence, you become preoccupied with what is wrong with you. The question is whether the challenge is teaching you to trust yourself more or less.\n\nA healthy Sun-Saturn square helps you develop strength, accountability, and self-respect. An unhealthy one leaves you believing that no matter what you do, you will never be enough."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At its worst, the lesson gets distorted. You keep trying to prove yourself. They keep finding flaws. Instead of learning responsibility, you learn self-doubt. Instead of building confidence, you become preoccupied with what is wrong with you. The question is whether the challenge is teaching you to trust yourself more or less."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"A healthy Sun-Saturn square helps you develop strength, accountability, and self-respect. An unhealthy one leaves you believing that no matter what you do, you will never be enough."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-saturn_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Identity under pressure from the other''s limits or authority. One feels blocked or judged; the other feels responsible for reining them in. Failure mode: resentment dressed as respect, or control dressed as care. Push on what genuinely needs structure and drop the rest; don''t let it become one person managing the other.","summaryDeep":"This person can make you feel like you are never quite good enough. Around them, you may feel judged, corrected, or held to standards you did not agree to. Sometimes it is explicit. Sometimes it is just the feeling that you are being watched and measured. Either way, it can be hard to relax.\n\nThe lesson here is learning the difference between responsibility and shame. This connection often exposes places where you need more discipline, maturity, or follow-through. It can push you to stop avoiding difficult truths, take ownership of your choices, and build a stronger foundation for yourself. Growth comes from accepting what needs work without deciding that your worth depends on being perfect.\n\nAt its best, this pushes you to get your act together. They may call out excuses, challenge weak spots, or force you to take responsibility for things you would rather avoid. The experience is not always comfortable, but it can help you build resilience, accountability, and a stronger foundation for success if you are willing to engage with the lessons being offered.\n\nAt its worst, the lesson gets distorted. You keep trying to prove yourself. They keep finding flaws. Instead of learning responsibility, you learn self-doubt. Instead of building confidence, you become preoccupied with what is wrong with you. The question is whether the challenge is teaching you to trust yourself more or less.\n\nA healthy Sun-Saturn square helps you develop strength, accountability, and self-respect. An unhealthy one leaves you believing that no matter what you do, you will never be enough.","tension":"At its worst, the lesson gets distorted. You keep trying to prove yourself. They keep finding flaws. Instead of learning responsibility, you learn self-doubt. Instead of building confidence, you become preoccupied with what is wrong with you. The question is whether the challenge is teaching you to trust yourself more or less.","advice":"A healthy Sun-Saturn square helps you develop strength, accountability, and self-respect. An unhealthy one leaves you believing that no matter what you do, you will never be enough.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry-sun-trine-saturn', 'relationship-sun-trine-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-saturn_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-saturn_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Trine Saturn', null, 'This person can bring out your strongest, most grounded self. Around them, you may find it easier to stay focused on what matters. They tend to offer support in practical ways: showing up consistently, encouraging your goals, and reminding you of the bigger picture when you lose sight of it. Their presence can help you trust yourself more.

When this works, the relationship becomes a source of steady growth. This person may encourage you to follow through on your commitments, believe in your abilities, and keep moving toward the life you want to create. They do not need to motivate you with constant praise. Instead, they help you build confidence by helping you see what you are capable of accomplishing.

One of the gifts of this connection is that it supports progress over time. You may become more disciplined, more patient with yourself, and more willing to invest energy in what truly matters. Growth feels natural because you are being supported, not pushed.

The main challenge is overlooking the value of something that feels stable and predictable. If you are used to relationships that run on excitement or uncertainty, you may not immediately recognize how powerful consistency can be.

Appreciate the people who help you stay aligned with your goals and values. Lasting growth often comes from steady support, not dramatic moments. This connection reminds you that real strength is built one step at a time.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can bring out your strongest, most grounded self. Around them, you may find it easier to stay focused on what matters. They tend to offer support in practical ways: showing up consistently, encouraging your goals, and reminding you of the bigger picture when you lose sight of it. Their presence can help you trust yourself more.\n\nWhen this works, the relationship becomes a source of steady growth. This person may encourage you to follow through on your commitments, believe in your abilities, and keep moving toward the life you want to create. They do not need to motivate you with constant praise. Instead, they help you build confidence by helping you see what you are capable of accomplishing.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is that it supports progress over time. You may become more disciplined, more patient with yourself, and more willing to invest energy in what truly matters. Growth feels natural because you are being supported, not pushed.\n\nThe main challenge is overlooking the value of something that feels stable and predictable. If you are used to relationships that run on excitement or uncertainty, you may not immediately recognize how powerful consistency can be.\n\nAppreciate the people who help you stay aligned with your goals and values. Lasting growth often comes from steady support, not dramatic moments. This connection reminds you that real strength is built one step at a time."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The main challenge is overlooking the value of something that feels stable and predictable. If you are used to relationships that run on excitement or uncertainty, you may not immediately recognize how powerful consistency can be."},{"heading":"Advice","body":