oking the value of something that feels stable and predictable. If you are used to relationships that run on excitement or uncertainty, you may not immediately recognize how powerful consistency can be.","advice":"Appreciate the people who help you stay aligned with your goals and values. Lasting growth often comes from steady support, not dramatic moments. This connection reminds you that real strength is built one step at a time.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"sun","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry-sun-conjunction-sun', 'relationship-sun-conjunction-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-sun_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-sun_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Conjunction Sun', null, 'You may recognize something familiar in this person right away. Maybe it is how they carry themselves, what they care about, or the way they handle life. Being around them can feel easy because you do not have to explain every little thing.

When this works, there is a relief in not having to explain yourself all the time. This person may understand why certain things matter to you, why you make the choices you do, or why you care as much as you do. You can feel seen in a way that feels simple and natural, like they already speak the language you''re speaking.

The tricky part is that being alike can also bring out competition. You may both want to lead, both want to be seen, or both expect the other person to move out of the way. What felt familiar at first can start to feel crowded if nobody leaves room.

Let the similarity make you feel understood, not threatened.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"You may recognize something familiar in this person right away. Maybe it is how they carry themselves, what they care about, or the way they handle life. Being around them can feel easy because you do not have to explain every little thing.\n\nWhen this works, there is a relief in not having to explain yourself all the time. This person may understand why certain things matter to you, why you make the choices you do, or why you care as much as you do. You can feel seen in a way that feels simple and natural, like they already speak the language you''re speaking.\n\nThe tricky part is that being alike can also bring out competition. You may both want to lead, both want to be seen, or both expect the other person to move out of the way. What felt familiar at first can start to feel crowded if nobody leaves room.\n\nLet the similarity make you feel understood, not threatened."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The tricky part is that being alike can also bring out competition. You may both want to lead, both want to be seen, or both expect the other person to move out of the way. What felt familiar at first can start to feel crowded if nobody leaves room."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the similarity make you feel understood, not threatened."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-sun_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s identity. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"You may recognize something familiar in this person right away. Maybe it is how they carry themselves, what they care about, or the way they handle life. Being around them can feel easy because you do not have to explain every little thing.\n\nWhen this works, there is a relief in not having to explain yourself all the time. This person may understand why certain things matter to you, why you make the choices you do, or why you care as much as you do. You can feel seen in a way that feels simple and natural, like they already speak the language you''re speaking.\n\nThe tricky part is that being alike can also bring out competition. You may both want to lead, both want to be seen, or both expect the other person to move out of the way. What felt familiar at first can start to feel crowded if nobody leaves room.\n\nLet the similarity make you feel understood, not threatened.","tension":"The tricky part is that being alike can also bring out competition. You may both want to lead, both want to be seen, or both expect the other person to move out of the way. What felt familiar at first can start to feel crowded if nobody leaves room.","advice":"Let the similarity make you feel understood, not threatened.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"sun","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry-sun-opposition-sun', 'relationship-sun-opposition-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-sun_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-sun_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Opposition Sun', null, 'This person may have a way of approaching life that feels noticeably different from yours. They may make choices you would not make, focus on things you tend to overlook, or respond to situations from a completely different starting point. Part of what draws you to them may be that difference. Part of what frustrates you may be the same thing.

When this works, the difference can be surprisingly helpful. This person may show you another way of handling things, one that would not have occurred to you on your own. They can make you question old assumptions, consider a different approach, or appreciate strengths you usually overlook. You may not always understand where they are coming from at first, but over time they can broaden your sense of what is possible.

The harder part is when the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling frustrating. You do things one way, they do things another, and before long both of you are explaining, defending, or pushing back. What began as contrast can turn into a pattern where each person feels misunderstood by the other.

You do not have to agree on everything to respect each other. The difference becomes much easier to live with when neither person is trying to prove their way is the right one.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may have a way of approaching life that feels noticeably different from yours. They may make choices you would not make, focus on things you tend to overlook, or respond to situations from a completely different starting point. Part of what draws you to them may be that difference. Part of what frustrates you may be the same thing.\n\nWhen this works, the difference can be surprisingly helpful. This person may show you another way of handling things, one that would not have occurred to you on your own. They can make you question old assumptions, consider a different approach, or appreciate strengths you usually overlook. You may not always understand where they are coming from at first, but over time they can broaden your sense of what is possible.\n\nThe harder part is when the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling frustrating. You do things one way, they do things another, and before long both of you are explaining, defending, or pushing back. What began as contrast can turn into a pattern where each person feels misunderstood by the other.\n\nYou do not have to agree on everything to respect each other. The difference becomes much easier to live with when neither person is trying to prove their way is the right one."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part is when the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling frustrating. You do things one way, they do things another, and before long both of you are explaining, defending, or pushing back. What began as contrast can turn into a pattern where each person feels misunderstood by the other."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"You do not have to agree on everything to respect each other. The difference becomes much easier to live with when neither person is trying to prove their way is the right one."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-sun_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s identity. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person may have a way of approaching life that feels noticeably different from yours. They may make choices you would not make, focus on things you tend to overlook, or respond to situations from a completely different starting point. Part of what draws you to them may be that difference. Part of what frustrates you may be the same thing.\n\nWhen this works, the difference can be surprisingly helpful. This person may show you another way of handling things, one that would not have occurred to you on your own. They can make you question old assumptions, consider a different approach, or appreciate strengths you usually overlook. You may not always understand where they are coming from at first, but over time they can broaden your sense of what is possible.\n\nThe harder part is when the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling frustrating. You do things one way, they do things another, and before long both of you are explaining, defending, or pushing back. What began as contrast can turn into a pattern where each person feels misunderstood by the other.\n\nYou do not have to agree on everything to respect each other. The difference becomes much easier to live with when neither person is trying to prove their way is the right one.","tension":"The harder part is when the difference stops feeling interesting and starts feeling frustrating. You do things one way, they do things another, and before long both of you are explaining, defending, or pushing back. What began as contrast can turn into a pattern where each person feels misunderstood by the other.","advice":"You do not have to agree on everything to respect each other. The difference becomes much easier to live with when neither person is trying to prove their way is the right one.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-sun_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"sun","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-sun_sextile', 'synastry-sun-sextile-sun', 'relationship-sun-sextile-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-sun_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-sun_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Sextile Sun', null, 'There is an easy understanding here, but it tends to grow through participation. You may naturally get each other, yet the connection becomes more meaningful when you stay curious about each other''s lives and take an active interest in what matters to the other person.

When this works, there is a quiet sense of being on each other''s side. You may encourage each other in small ways, remember what matters to the other person, or take an interest in things that might seem insignificant to everyone else. The support is not flashy, but it feels genuine.

The harder part is assuming that getting along is enough. You may enjoy each other''s company and still keep the relationship at arm''s length. The connection stays easy and enjoyable, but never quite grows into something deeper.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is an easy understanding here, but it tends to grow through participation. You may naturally get each other, yet the connection becomes more meaningful when you stay curious about each other''s lives and take an active interest in what matters to the other person.\n\nWhen this works, there is a quiet sense of being on each other''s side. You may encourage each other in small ways, remember what matters to the other person, or take an interest in things that might seem insignificant to everyone else. The support is not flashy, but it feels genuine.\n\nThe harder part is assuming that getting along is enough. You may enjoy each other''s company and still keep the relationship at arm''s length. The connection stays easy and enjoyable, but never quite grows into something deeper."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part is assuming that getting along is enough. You may enjoy each other''s company and still keep the relationship at arm''s length. The connection stays easy and enjoyable, but never quite grows into something deeper."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-sun_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s identity. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"There is an easy understanding here, but it tends to grow through participation. You may naturally get each other, yet the connection becomes more meaningful when you stay curious about each other''s lives and take an active interest in what matters to the other person.\n\nWhen this works, there is a quiet sense of being on each other''s side. You may encourage each other in small ways, remember what matters to the other person, or take an interest in things that might seem insignificant to everyone else. The support is not flashy, but it feels genuine.\n\nThe harder part is assuming that getting along is enough. You may enjoy each other''s company and still keep the relationship at arm''s length. The connection stays easy and enjoyable, but never quite grows into something deeper.","tension":"The harder part is assuming that getting along is enough. You may enjoy each other''s company and still keep the relationship at arm''s length. The connection stays easy and enjoyable, but never quite grows into something deeper.","advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-sun_B-sun_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"sun","planetB":"sun","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-sun_B-sun_square', 'synastry-sun-square-sun', 'relationship-sun-square-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-sun_B-sun_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-sun_B-sun_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Sun Square Sun', null, 'This person can get under your skin without meaning to. It may be something small: the way they jump in with an opinion, the confidence they bring into a room, or the way they seem completely comfortable doing things their own way. Whatever it is, you may find yourself reacting more strongly than the situation seems to call for.

When this works, it can push you to be more honest with yourself. This person may have a way of exposing habits, blind spots, or assumptions you usually do not question. You may not always enjoy being challenged by them, but they can make it harder to keep doing things the same way without noticing why.

The harder part is when everything starts feeling personal. You may read their confidence as arrogance. They may read yours the same way. A normal difference in style can start to feel like disrespect, even when neither person means it that way.

Not every difference is a challenge to answer. Sometimes the other person is just being themselves, not trying to outshine you. The more you can remember that, the easier it is to stop turning friction into a competition.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can get under your skin without meaning to. It may be something small: the way they jump in with an opinion, the confidence they bring into a room, or the way they seem completely comfortable doing things their own way. Whatever it is, you may find yourself reacting more strongly than the situation seems to call for.\n\nWhen this works, it can push you to be more honest with yourself. This person may have a way of exposing habits, blind spots, or assumptions you usually do not question. You may not always enjoy being challenged by them, but they can make it harder to keep doing things the same way without noticing why.\n\nThe harder part is when everything starts feeling personal. You may read their confidence as arrogance. They may read yours the same way. A normal difference in style can start to feel like disrespect, even when neither person means it that way.\n\nNot every difference is a challenge to answer. Sometimes the other person is just being themselves, not trying to outshine you. The more you can remember that, the easier it is to stop turning friction into a competition."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part is when everything starts feeling personal. You may read their confidence as arrogance. They may read yours the same way. A normal difference in style can start to feel like disrespect, even when neither person means it that way."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Not every difference is a challenge to answer. Sometimes the other person is just being themselves, not trying to outshine you. The more you can remember that, the easier it is to stop turning friction into a competition."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-sun_B-sun_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s identity meets B''s identity. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"This person can get under your skin without meaning to. It may be something small: the way they jump in with an opinion, the confidence they bring into a room, or the way they seem completely comfortable doing things their own way. Whatever it is, you may find yourself reacting more strongly than the situation seems to call for.\n\nWhen this works, it can push you to be more honest with yourself. This person may have a way of exposing habits, blind spots, or assumptions you usually do not question. You may not always enjoy being challenged by them, but they can make it harder to keep doing things the same way without noticing why.\n\nThe harder part is when everything starts feeling personal. You may read their confidence as arrogance. They may read yours the same way. A normal difference in style can start to feel like disrespect, even when neither person means it that way.\n\nNot every difference is a challenge to answer. Sometimes the other person is just being themselves, not trying to outshine you. The more you can remember that, the easier it is to stop turning friction into a competition.","tension":"The harder part is when everything starts feeling personal. You may read their confidence as arrogance. They may read yours the same way. A normal difference in style can start to feel like disrespect, even when neither person means it that way.","advice":"Not every difference is a challenge to answer. Sometimes the other person is just being themselves, not trying to outshine you. The more you can remember that, the easier it is to stop turning friction into a competition.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":2}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect',