  ('A-uranus_B-venus_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"uranus","planetB":"venus","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-uranus_B-venus_trine', 'synastry-uranus-trine-venus', 'relationship-uranus-trine-venus']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-uranus_B-venus_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-uranus_B-venus_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Uranus Trine Venus', null, 'A''s need for freedom meets B''s love and values. The trine lets them flow together easily.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Translation","body":"A''s need for freedom meets B''s love and values. The trine lets them flow together easily."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-uranus_B-venus_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s need for freedom meets B''s love and values. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":null,"tension":null,"advice":null,"policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Imported from project-authored synastry matrix material. Source file was not copied into the repository.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":null,"weight":null}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-ascendant_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"ascendant","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-ascendant_sextile', 'synastry-venus-sextile-ascendant', 'relationship-venus-sextile-ascendant']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-ascendant_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-ascendant_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Sextile Ascendant', 'The attraction or affection does not have to be forced. Venus softens the room, the Ascendant feels seen, and the connection can become warmer when both people let it be visible.', 'There is an ease to this one. The attraction or affection does not have to be worked for in an obvious way. It is often just there, soft and available, when the two of you are in the same room.

The Venus person usually notices first. Not only how the Ascendant person looks, though that can be part of it, but how they hold themselves, how they move through space, and how their presence arrives before they say anything. Something about them registers as lovely, charming, or worth lingering on, and Venus tends to let that show.

The Ascendant person feels it land. They may feel more like themselves here, and more attractive too. Being received that warmly can be a kind of relief: the wanting, liking, or sweetness is offered without making them perform for it. Their confidence comes up more naturally, and because Venus responds to that, the warmth can begin to move in both directions.

Affection comes easily. Touch may find a natural rhythm if the relationship allows for that. Flirting can feel less risky. A compliment lands where it is meant to. The two of you may simply like being near each other, standing close, catching each other''s eye, or letting the warmth be visible. There can be a public sweetness to it, a chemistry that does not hide itself particularly well.

Because this is a sextile, it does not take over the room. It offers. It opens a door and waits to see if you will walk through it. But if you both lean in, the physical or affectionate side can deepen naturally. What begins as charm and comfort can become desire, tenderness, or a very real pleasure in being close.

The thing to stay honest about is that ease is not the whole relationship. You can love what you see and love how you feel and still need the slower work: showing up, telling the truth, and staying present when the first glow settles.

The gift here is feeling wanted in a way that does not cost you anything to receive. Let the attraction be what it is. Let it become real. Just do not ask it to be the entire thing on its own.

The ease can become so pleasant that both people treat it as the whole story, even when the relationship needs clearer truth, follow-through, or emotional presence.

Let the warmth be visible, but keep it honest. Enjoy the attraction, offer the compliment, make the invitation, and give the connection enough presence to become real.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is an ease to this one. The attraction or affection does not have to be worked for in an obvious way. It is often just there, soft and available, when the two of you are in the same room.\n\nThe Venus person usually notices first. Not only how the Ascendant person looks, though that can be part of it, but how they hold themselves, how they move through space, and how their presence arrives before they say anything. Something about them registers as lovely, charming, or worth lingering on, and Venus tends to let that show.\n\nThe Ascendant person feels it land. They may feel more like themselves here, and more attractive too. Being received that warmly can be a kind of relief: the wanting, liking, or sweetness is offered without making them perform for it. Their confidence comes up more naturally, and because Venus responds to that, the warmth can begin to move in both directions.\n\nAffection comes easily. Touch may find a natural rhythm if the relationship allows for that. Flirting can feel less risky. A compliment lands where it is meant to. The two of you may simply like being near each other, standing close, catching each other''s eye, or letting the warmth be visible. There can be a public sweetness to it, a chemistry that does not hide itself particularly well.\n\nBecause this is a sextile, it does not take over the room. It offers. It opens a door and waits to see if you will walk through it. But if you both lean in, the physical or affectionate side can deepen naturally. What begins as charm and comfort can become desire, tenderness, or a very real pleasure in being close.\n\nThe thing to stay honest about is that ease is not the whole relationship. You can love what you see and love how you feel and still need the slower work: showing up, telling the truth, and staying present when the first glow settles.\n\nThe gift here is feeling wanted in a way that does not cost you anything to receive. Let the attraction be what it is. Let it become real. Just do not ask it to be the entire thing on its own."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The ease can become so pleasant that both people treat it as the whole story, even when the relationship needs clearer truth, follow-through, or emotional presence."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the warmth be visible, but keep it honest. Enjoy the attraction, offer the compliment, make the invitation, and give the connection enough presence to become real."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-ascendant_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"There is an easy warmth here. The Venus person tends to notice the Ascendant person''s presence, style, body language, or way of moving through the world, and the Ascendant person may feel more attractive and relaxed in response.","summaryDeep":"There is an ease to this one. The attraction or affection does not have to be worked for in an obvious way. It is often just there, soft and available, when the two of you are in the same room.\n\nThe Venus person usually notices first. Not only how the Ascendant person looks, though that can be part of it, but how they hold themselves, how they move through space, and how their presence arrives before they say anything. Something about them registers as lovely, charming, or worth lingering on, and Venus tends to let that show.\n\nThe Ascendant person feels it land. They may feel more like themselves here, and more attractive too. Being received that warmly can be a kind of relief: the wanting, liking, or sweetness is offered without making them perform for it. Their confidence comes up more naturally, and because Venus responds to that, the warmth can begin to move in both directions.\n\nAffection comes easily. Touch may find a natural rhythm if the relationship allows for that. Flirting can feel less risky. A compliment lands where it is meant to. The two of you may simply like being near each other, standing close, catching each other''s eye, or letting the warmth be visible. There can be a public sweetness to it, a chemistry that does not hide itself particularly well.\n\nBecause this is a sextile, it does not take over the room. It offers. It opens a door and waits to see if you will walk through it. But if you both lean in, the physical or affectionate side can deepen naturally. What begins as charm and comfort can become desire, tenderness, or a very real pleasure in being close.\n\nThe thing to stay honest about is that ease is not the whole relationship. You can love what you see and love how you feel and still need the slower work: showing up, telling the truth, and staying present when the first glow settles.\n\nThe gift here is feeling wanted in a way that does not cost you anything to receive. Let the attraction be what it is. Let it become real. Just do not ask it to be the entire thing on its own.","tension":"The ease can become so pleasant that both people treat it as the whole story, even when the relationship needs clearer truth, follow-through, or emotional presence.","advice":"Let the warmth be visible, but keep it honest. Enjoy the attraction, offer the compliment, make the invitation, and give the connection enough presence to become real.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Authored to cover planet-to-angle synastry fallback for the relationship interaspect list.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-jupiter_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-jupiter_conjunction', 'synastry-venus-conjunction-jupiter', 'relationship-venus-conjunction-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-jupiter_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-jupiter_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Conjunction Jupiter', null, 'This person expands your capacity for joy. Being with them can remind you that relationships are not only about solving problems or building security. They are also about feeling appreciated, welcomed, and genuinely enjoyed. Their presence may make it easier for you to relax, open up, and trust that there is enough affection, attention, and goodwill to go around.

When this works, you bring out each other''s confidence in life. You celebrate wins together. You encourage each other''s growth. You create an atmosphere where generosity feels natural and where both people feel seen for what is good and valuable in them. There is a sense of possibility here, as though the relationship helps both of you believe in more.

One of the gifts of this connection is that it can shift your mindset from scarcity to abundance. Instead of focusing on what is missing, you notice what is working. Instead of withholding appreciation, you offer it freely. The relationship can become a source of encouragement, optimism, and emotional nourishment.

The challenge is remembering that growth requires honesty as well as positivity. It is easy to focus on the good and overlook what needs attention. You may avoid difficult conversations, assume things will work themselves out, or mistake comfort for progress.

Enjoy what is good, but do not ignore what needs attention. This connection works best when appreciation and responsibility are both present.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person expands your capacity for joy. Being with them can remind you that relationships are not only about solving problems or building security. They are also about feeling appreciated, welcomed, and genuinely enjoyed. Their presence may make it easier for you to relax, open up, and trust that there is enough affection, attention, and goodwill to go around.\n\nWhen this works, you bring out each other''s confidence in life. You celebrate wins together. You encourage each other''s growth. You create an atmosphere where generosity feels natural and where both people feel seen for what is good and valuable in them. There is a sense of possibility here, as though the relationship helps both of you believe in more.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is that it can shift your mindset from scarcity to abundance. Instead of focusing on what is missing, you notice what is working. Instead of withholding appreciation, you offer it freely. The relationship can become a source of encouragement, optimism, and emotional nourishment.\n\nThe challenge is remembering that growth requires honesty as well as positivity. It is easy to focus on the good and overlook what needs attention. You may avoid difficult conversations, assume things will work themselves out, or mistake comfort for progress.\n\nEnjoy what is good, but do not ignore what needs attention. This connection works best when appreciation and responsibility are both present."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is remembering that growth requires honesty as well as positivity. It is easy to focus on the good and overlook what needs attention. You may avoid difficult conversations, assume things will work themselves out, or mistake comfort for progress."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Enjoy what is good, but do not ignore what needs attention. This connection works best when appreciation and responsibility are both present."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-jupiter_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s growth. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person expands your capacity for joy. Being with them can remind you that relationships are not only about solving problems or building security. They are also about feeling appreciated, welcomed, and genuinely enjoyed. Their presence may make it easier for you to relax, open up, and trust that there is enough affection, attention, and goodwill to go around.\n\nWhen this works, you bring out each other''s confidence in life. You celebrate wins together. You encourage each other''s growth. You create an atmosphere where generosity feels natural and where both people feel seen for what is good and valuable in them. There is a sense of possibility here, as though the relationship helps both of you believe in more.\n\nOne of the gifts of this connection is that it can shift your mindset from scarcity to abundance. Instead of focusing on what is missing, you notice what is working. Instead of withholding appreciation, you offer it freely. The relationship can become a source of encouragement, optimism, and emotional nourishment.\n\nThe challenge is remembering that growth requires honesty as well as positivity. It is easy to focus on the good and overlook what needs attention. You may avoid difficult conversations, assume things will work themselves out, or mistake comfort for progress.\n\nEnjoy what is good, but do not ignore what needs attention. This connection works best when appreciation and responsibility are both present.","tension":"The challenge is remembering that growth requires honesty as well as positivity. It is easy to focus on the good and overlook what needs attention. You may avoid difficult conversations, assume things will work themselves out, or mistake comfort for progress.","advice":"Enjoy what is good, but do not ignore what needs attention. This connection works best when appreciation and responsibility are both present.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-jupiter_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-jupiter_opposition', 'synastry-venus-opposition-jupiter', 'relationship-venus-opposition-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-jupiter_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-jupiter_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Opposition Jupiter', null, 'This person may bring more. More generosity. More enthusiasm. More willingness to say yes to what feels good. Part of you may find that deeply refreshing. Another part may wonder where the limit is. They can encourage you to open up to life''s pleasures while also challenging your sense of balance, moderation, and what feels sustainable.

This connection asks both of you to examine your relationship with receiving. They may encourage you to loosen your grip, trust life a little more, and stop acting as though joy always has to be justified. You may help them recognize when enough is enough and make better choices about where their time, energy, and generosity go.

The tension appears when your differences start to feel like judgments. A difference in perspective can slowly harden into a question of whose truth gets to lead. They may experience your caution as a limit on what is possible, while you may experience their faith in expansion as a refusal to acknowledge reality. Over time, what began as a difference in style can become a story about who has the better way of moving through life.

This connection is not about proving whose approach is right. It is about recognizing that both of your instincts can become excessive in different ways, and finding a balance that serves the relationship better than either extreme. Neither person needs to become the other. The goal is to find a balance where generosity has room to breathe and good judgment still has a voice.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may bring more. More generosity. More enthusiasm. More willingness to say yes to what feels good. Part of you may find that deeply refreshing. Another part may wonder where the limit is. They can encourage you to open up to life''s pleasures while also challenging your sense of balance, moderation, and what feels sustainable.\n\nThis connection asks both of you to examine your relationship with receiving. They may encourage you to loosen your grip, trust life a little more, and stop acting as though joy always has to be justified. You may help them recognize when enough is enough and make better choices about where their time, energy, and generosity go.\n\nThe tension appears when your differences start to feel like judgments. A difference in perspective can slowly harden into a question of whose truth gets to lead. They may experience your caution as a limit on what is possible, while you may experience their faith in expansion as a refusal to acknowledge reality. Over time, what began as a difference in style can become a story about who has the better way of moving through life.\n\nThis connection is not about proving whose approach is right. It is about recognizing that both of your instincts can become excessive in different ways, and finding a balance that serves the relationship better than either extreme. Neither person needs to become the other. The goal is to find a balance where generosity has room to breathe and good judgment still has a voice."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The tension appears when your differences start to feel like judgments. A difference in perspective can slowly harden into a question of whose truth gets to lead. They may experience your caution as a limit on what is possible, while you may experience their faith in expansion as a refusal to acknowledge reality. Over time, what began as a difference in style can become a story about who has the better way of moving through life."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This connection is not about proving whose approach is right. It is about recognizing that both of your instincts can become excessive in different ways, and finding a balance that serves the relationship better than either extreme. Neither person needs to become the other. The goal is to find a balance where generosity has room to breathe and good judgment still has a voice."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-jupiter_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s growth. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"This person may bring more. More generosity. More enthusiasm. More willingness to say yes to what feels good. Part of you may find that deeply refreshing. Another part may wonder where the limit is. They can encourage you to open up to life''s pleasures while also challenging your sense of balance, moderation, and what feels sustainable.\n\nThis connection asks both of you to examine your relationship with receiving. They may encourage you to loosen your grip, trust life a little more, and stop acting as though joy always has to be justified. You may help them recognize when enough is enough and make better choices about where their time, energy, and generosity go.\n\nThe tension appears when your differences start to feel like judgments. A difference in perspective can slowly harden into a question of whose truth gets to lead. They may experience your caution as a limit on what is possible, while you may experience their faith in expansion as a refusal to acknowledge reality. Over time, what began as a difference in style can become a story about who has the better way of moving through life.\n\nThis connection is not about proving whose approach is right. It is about recognizing that both of your instincts can become excessive in different ways, and finding a balance that serves the relationship better than either extreme. Neither person needs to become the other. The goal is to find a balance where generosity has room to breathe and good judgment still has a voice.","tension":"The tension appears when your differences start to feel like judgments. A difference in perspective can slowly harden into a question of whose truth gets to lead. They may experience your caution as a limit on what is possible, while you may experience their faith in expansion as a refusal to acknowledge reality. Over time, what began as a difference in style can become a story about who has the better way of moving through life.","advice":"This connection is not about proving whose approach is right. It is about recognizing that both of your instincts can become excessive in different ways, and finding a balance that serves the relationship better than either extreme. Neither person needs to become the other. The goal is to find a balance where generosity has room to breathe and good judgment still has a voice.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"jupiter","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-jupiter_sextile', 'synastry-venus-sextile-jupiter', 'relationship-venus-sextile-jupiter']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-jupiter_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-jupiter_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Sextile Jupiter', null, 'This person likes you. Roots for you, sees the best in you, makes you feel good without you having to earn it. Right away it''s obvious this could be one of the easy, happy ones, a connection that adds to your life instead of draining it.

The good feeling won''t do the work for you. A little effort goes a long way here, the text that says you were thinking of them, the plan you actually make, saying the nice thing out loud instead of figuring they know. Small stuff, and it adds up fast.

That''s the catch with this one. The warmth opens the door and then just stands there. Coast on it, assume it runs itself, and you end up with a great connection you never actually used.

