this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed.","tension":"Because this touches Venus, it reaches further than conversation. To feel admired, appreciated, understood is part of what keeps desire alive between two people. When words keep missing that mark, something quietly cools. It is rarely a loss of feeling. It is the slow accumulation of small moments where neither of you felt fully met, until the affection has to work harder to stay warm.","advice":"The work here is not to flatten yourself into someone more agreeable, or to stop saying what is true. It is to get genuinely curious about what this person experiences as care, which may look nothing like your own version of it. We tend to offer love in the language we would want to receive it, and then feel hurt when it does not translate. What lands as tender to you may read as flat to them. What feels honest to them may feel sharp to you.\n\nThis is the slow practice the square asks for. Not better chemistry, you already have that. The harder thing: learning how this particular person receives words, and letting them learn yours. Attraction can survive on its own for a while. What deepens it is the moment one of you stops assuming and starts asking, and the other finally feels seen in the exact place they kept getting missed.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-mercury_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"mercury","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-mercury_trine', 'synastry-venus-trine-mercury', 'relationship-venus-trine-mercury']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-mercury_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-mercury_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Trine Mercury', null, 'With this person, a lot of the attraction is in the conversation.

You may just enjoy talking to them. You like hearing what they have to say. Maybe they make you laugh, tell good stories, or notice things other people miss. Conversation can feel easy because you genuinely enjoy being around them.

When this works, affection tends to show up through everyday conversation. The text that makes you laugh when you''re having a bad day. The little check-in. The running joke that somehow never gets old. Whatever the relationship is, there is often a feeling of being understood through words. You don''t always have to spell out that you care about each other. It''s already already present in how you talk.

One of the nicest things about this connection is feeling seen. This person may put something into words that you''ve been trying to explain for months. They may understand what you''re getting at before you''ve fully figured it out yourself. There can be a real sense of, "Oh, that''s exactly what I meant."

The thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.

The connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"With this person, a lot of the attraction is in the conversation.\n\nYou may just enjoy talking to them. You like hearing what they have to say. Maybe they make you laugh, tell good stories, or notice things other people miss. Conversation can feel easy because you genuinely enjoy being around them.\n\nWhen this works, affection tends to show up through everyday conversation. The text that makes you laugh when you''re having a bad day. The little check-in. The running joke that somehow never gets old. Whatever the relationship is, there is often a feeling of being understood through words. You don''t always have to spell out that you care about each other. It''s already already present in how you talk.\n\nOne of the nicest things about this connection is feeling seen. This person may put something into words that you''ve been trying to explain for months. They may understand what you''re getting at before you''ve fully figured it out yourself. There can be a real sense of, \"Oh, that''s exactly what I meant.\"\n\nThe thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.\n\nThe connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-mercury_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s mind. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"With this person, a lot of the attraction is in the conversation.\n\nYou may just enjoy talking to them. You like hearing what they have to say. Maybe they make you laugh, tell good stories, or notice things other people miss. Conversation can feel easy because you genuinely enjoy being around them.\n\nWhen this works, affection tends to show up through everyday conversation. The text that makes you laugh when you''re having a bad day. The little check-in. The running joke that somehow never gets old. Whatever the relationship is, there is often a feeling of being understood through words. You don''t always have to spell out that you care about each other. It''s already already present in how you talk.\n\nOne of the nicest things about this connection is feeling seen. This person may put something into words that you''ve been trying to explain for months. They may understand what you''re getting at before you''ve fully figured it out yourself. There can be a real sense of, \"Oh, that''s exactly what I meant.\"\n\nThe thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.\n\nThe connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it.","tension":"The thing to watch for is getting a little too comfortable in the conversation itself. It''s easy to enjoy talking so much that you assume everything else is taking care of itself. Sometimes a great conversation can feel like progress when what you really need is action, honesty, or a harder discussion.","advice":"The connection is strongest when all that natural ease between you leads somewhere real, instead of becoming a substitute for it.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":3}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"moon","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-moon_conjunction', 'synastry-venus-conjunction-moon', 'relationship-venus-conjunction-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-moon_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-moon_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Conjunction Moon', null, 'This person may make you feel cared for in a way that is easy to receive. There is a natural softness here, the kind where affection does not have to be earned or pulled out of anyone. You may find yourself relaxing around each other quickly. Being close can feel comfortable instead of complicated, like you do not have to work so hard to feel liked.

At its best, this is one of the sweetest connections to have with someone. The warmth tends to land exactly where it is meant to. You may feel genuinely appreciated, not just wanted or needed. There is often real fondness here, the kind that makes ordinary moments feel special. Sharing a meal, checking in after a long day, sitting together doing nothing in particular can all feel surprisingly nourishing.

The harder part is that comfort can sometimes become the goal instead of closeness. You may avoid difficult conversations, smooth things over too quickly, or tell yourselves that everything is fine because neither of you wants to disrupt the good feeling. But relationships need more than sweetness to grow. They need room for honesty too.

Enjoy how easy this feels. Let yourself take in the affection. Just remember that real intimacy is not only about keeping things pleasant. It is also about trusting the connection enough to tell the truth when something matters.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may make you feel cared for in a way that is easy to receive. There is a natural softness here, the kind where affection does not have to be earned or pulled out of anyone. You may find yourself relaxing around each other quickly. Being close can feel comfortable instead of complicated, like you do not have to work so hard to feel liked.\n\nAt its best, this is one of the sweetest connections to have with someone. The warmth tends to land exactly where it is meant to. You may feel genuinely appreciated, not just wanted or needed. There is often real fondness here, the kind that makes ordinary moments feel special. Sharing a meal, checking in after a long day, sitting together doing nothing in particular can all feel surprisingly nourishing.\n\nThe harder part is that comfort can sometimes become the goal instead of closeness. You may avoid difficult conversations, smooth things over too quickly, or tell yourselves that everything is fine because neither of you wants to disrupt the good feeling. But relationships need more than sweetness to grow. They need room for honesty too.\n\nEnjoy how easy this feels. Let yourself take in the affection. Just remember that real intimacy is not only about keeping things pleasant. It is also about trusting the connection enough to tell the truth when something matters."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The harder part is that comfort can sometimes become the goal instead of closeness. You may avoid difficult conversations, smooth things over too quickly, or tell yourselves that everything is fine because neither of you wants to disrupt the good feeling. But relationships need more than sweetness to grow. They need room for honesty too."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Enjoy how easy this feels. Let yourself take in the affection. Just remember that real intimacy is not only about keeping things pleasant. It is also about trusting the connection enough to tell the truth when something matters."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-moon_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s feelings. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person may make you feel cared for in a way that is easy to receive. There is a natural softness here, the kind where affection does not have to be earned or pulled out of anyone. You may find yourself relaxing around each other quickly. Being close can feel comfortable instead of complicated, like you do not have to work so hard to feel liked.\n\nAt its best, this is one of the sweetest connections to have with someone. The warmth tends to land exactly where it is meant to. You may feel genuinely appreciated, not just wanted or needed. There is often real fondness here, the kind that makes ordinary moments feel special. Sharing a meal, checking in after a long day, sitting together doing nothing in particular can all feel surprisingly nourishing.\n\nThe harder part is that comfort can sometimes become the goal instead of closeness. You may avoid difficult conversations, smooth things over too quickly, or tell yourselves that everything is fine because neither of you wants to disrupt the good feeling. But relationships need more than sweetness to grow. They need room for honesty too.\n\nEnjoy how easy this feels. Let yourself take in the affection. Just remember that real intimacy is not only about keeping things pleasant. It is also about trusting the connection enough to tell the truth when something matters.","tension":"The harder part is that comfort can sometimes become the goal instead of closeness. You may avoid difficult conversations, smooth things over too quickly, or tell yourselves that everything is fine because neither of you wants to disrupt the good feeling. But relationships need more than sweetness to grow. They need room for honesty too.","advice":"Enjoy how easy this feels. Let yourself take in the affection. Just remember that real intimacy is not only about keeping things pleasant. It is also about trusting the connection enough to tell the truth when something matters.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"moon","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-moon_opposition', 'synastry-venus-opposition-moon', 'relationship-venus-opposition-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-moon_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-moon_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Opposition Moon', null, 'There is real warmth here, but one of the biggest lessons in this connection is learning that care does not always look the way you expect it to. You may both want closeness, affection, and emotional connection, yet still find yourselves missing each other from time to time. Not because the love is not there, but because you naturally express it differently.

At its best, this relationship helps you expand your understanding of what it means to give and receive love. This person may show care in ways that are unfamiliar to you, and that can be a gift. It invites you to step outside your usual expectations and notice forms of affection you might otherwise overlook. Growth often happens when we realize there is more than one right way to love someone.

The challenge comes when expectations go unspoken. You may give what feels meaningful to you and feel disappointed when it is not fully appreciated. They may do the same. If you are not careful, you can start telling yourself stories about what the other person''s response means, when in reality both of you may be making sincere efforts.

The opportunity here is communication. Instead of assuming your partner should know what makes you feel loved, teach them. Be curious about what helps them feel cared for too. When both people are willing to learn each other''s language, the connection becomes stronger, warmer, and much easier to trust.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There is real warmth here, but one of the biggest lessons in this connection is learning that care does not always look the way you expect it to. You may both want closeness, affection, and emotional connection, yet still find yourselves missing each other from time to time. Not because the love is not there, but because you naturally express it differently.\n\nAt its best, this relationship helps you expand your understanding of what it means to give and receive love. This person may show care in ways that are unfamiliar to you, and that can be a gift. It invites you to step outside your usual expectations and notice forms of affection you might otherwise overlook. Growth often happens when we realize there is more than one right way to love someone.\n\nThe challenge comes when expectations go unspoken. You may give what feels meaningful to you and feel disappointed when it is not fully appreciated. They may do the same. If you are not careful, you can start telling yourself stories about what the other person''s response means, when in reality both of you may be making sincere efforts.\n\nThe opportunity here is communication. Instead of assuming your partner should know what makes you feel loved, teach them. Be curious about what helps them feel cared for too. When both people are willing to learn each other''s language, the connection becomes stronger, warmer, and much easier to trust."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge comes when expectations go unspoken. You may give what feels meaningful to you and feel disappointed when it is not fully appreciated. They may do the same. If you are not careful, you can start telling yourself stories about what the other person''s response means, when in reality both of you may be making sincere efforts."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The opportunity here is communication. Instead of assuming your partner should know what makes you feel loved, teach them. Be curious about what helps them feel cared for too. When both people are willing to learn each other''s language, the connection becomes stronger, warmer, and much easier to trust."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-moon_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s feelings. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"There is real warmth here, but one of the biggest lessons in this connection is learning that care does not always look the way you expect it to. You may both want closeness, affection, and emotional connection, yet still find yourselves missing each other from time to time. Not because the love is not there, but because you naturally express it differently.\n\nAt its best, this relationship helps you expand your understanding of what it means to give and receive love. This person may show care in ways that are unfamiliar to you, and that can be a gift. It invites you to step outside your usual expectations and notice forms of affection you might otherwise overlook. Growth often happens when we realize there is more than one right way to love someone.\n\nThe challenge comes when expectations go unspoken. You may give what feels meaningful to you and feel disappointed when it is not fully appreciated. They may do the same. If you are not careful, you can start telling yourself stories about what the other person''s response means, when in reality both of you may be making sincere efforts.\n\nThe opportunity here is communication. Instead of assuming your partner should know what makes you feel loved, teach them. Be curious about what helps them feel cared for too. When both people are willing to learn each other''s language, the connection becomes stronger, warmer, and much easier to trust.","tension":"The challenge comes when expectations go unspoken. You may give what feels meaningful to you and feel disappointed when it is not fully appreciated. They may do the same. If you are not careful, you can start telling yourself stories about what the other person''s response means, when in reality both of you may be making sincere efforts.","advice":"The opportunity here is communication. Instead of assuming your partner should know what makes you feel loved, teach them. Be curious about what helps them feel cared for too. When both people are willing to learn each other''s language, the connection becomes stronger, warmer, and much easier to trust.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-moon_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"moon","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-moon_sextile', 'synastry-venus-sextile-moon', 'relationship-venus-sextile-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-moon_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-moon_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Sextile Moon', null, 'This connection has a natural warmth to it, but it works best when you put that warmth into action. You may care about each other more than you realize, and the relationship tends to grow through simple, consistent acts of affection. A thoughtful text, remembering something important, checking in when it matters, making the other person feel seen. These small moments carry a lot of weight.

At its best, this is a relationship where kindness builds momentum. When one person makes an effort, the other usually responds. The more intentional you are about showing care, the easier it becomes to create trust, comfort, and closeness. You do not need grand gestures. You need consistency.

The challenge is that both of you may assume the relationship is doing fine because the feelings are there. You care about each other, you enjoy each other, and there may not be much conflict. But that can make it easy to stop reaching for each other. The check-ins happen less often. The compliments stay in your head. The thoughtful gesture never quite happens because you figure they already know how you feel.

Over time, it can be easy to assume the warmth will take care of itself. The connection may still be there, but if neither person is actively showing up for it, something valuable can start to fade into the background. Not because the feelings are gone, but because they are no longer being expressed.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection has a natural warmth to it, but it works best when you put that warmth into action. You may care about each other more than you realize, and the relationship tends to grow through simple, consistent acts of affection. A thoughtful text, remembering something important, checking in when it matters, making the other person feel seen. These small moments carry a lot of weight.\n\nAt its best, this is a relationship where kindness builds momentum. When one person makes an effort, the other usually responds. The more intentional you are about showing care, the easier it becomes to create trust, comfort, and closeness. You do not need grand gestures. You need consistency.\n\nThe challenge is that both of you may assume the relationship is doing fine because the feelings are there. You care about each other, you enjoy each other, and there may not be much conflict. But that can make it easy to stop reaching for each other. The check-ins happen less often. The compliments stay in your head. The thoughtful gesture never quite happens because you figure they already know how you feel.\n\nOver time, it can be easy to assume the warmth will take care of itself. The connection may still be there, but if neither person is actively showing up for it, something valuable can start to fade into the background. Not because the feelings are gone, but because they are no longer being expressed."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that both of you may assume the relationship is doing fine because the feelings are there. You care about each other, you enjoy each other, and there may not be much conflict. But that can make it easy to stop reaching for each other. The check-ins happen less often. The compliments stay in your head. The thoughtful gesture never quite happens because you figure they already know how you feel."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Over time, it can be easy to assume the warmth will take care of itself. The connection may still be there, but if neither person is actively showing up for it, something valuable can start to fade into the background. Not because the feelings are gone, but because they are no longer being expressed."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-moon_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s feelings. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This connection has a natural warmth to it, but it works best when you put that warmth into action. You may care about each other more than you realize, and the relationship tends to grow through simple, consistent acts of affection. A thoughtful text, remembering something important, checking in when it matters, making the other person feel seen. These small moments carry a lot of weight.\n\nAt its best, this is a relationship where kindness builds momentum. When one person makes an effort, the other usually responds. The more intentional you are about showing care, the easier it becomes to create trust, comfort, and closeness. You do not need grand gestures. You need consistency.\n\nThe challenge is that both of you may assume the relationship is doing fine because the feelings are there. You care about each other, you enjoy each other, and there may not be much conflict. But that can make it easy to stop reaching for each other. The check-ins happen less often. The compliments stay in your head. The thoughtful gesture never quite happens because you figure they already know how you feel.\n\nOver time, it can be easy to assume the warmth will take care of itself. The connection may still be there, but if neither person is actively showing up for it, something valuable can start to fade into the background. Not because the feelings are gone, but because they are no longer being expressed.","tension":"The challenge is that both of you may assume the relationship is doing fine because the feelings are there. You care about each other, you enjoy each other, and there may not be much conflict. But that can make it easy to stop reaching for each other. The check-ins happen less often. The compliments stay in your head. The thoughtful gesture never quite happens because you figure they already know how you feel.","advice":"Over time, it can be easy to assume the warmth will take care of itself. The connection may still be there, but if neither person is actively showing up for it, something valuable can start to fade into the background. Not because the feelings are gone, but because they are no longer being expressed.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-moon_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"moon","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-moon_square', 'synastry-venus-square-moon', 'relationship-venus-square-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-moon_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-moon_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Square Moon', null, 'The care is there, but the delivery can be off. You may both want to make each other feel loved, yet keep missing the mark. One person gives what they would want to receive, while the other is left thinking, "That is not really what I needed."

The good news is that there is usually genuine affection underneath the frustration. You likely want the best for each other. The challenge is that good intentions do not automatically create emotional connection. If you keep assuming the other person should just know what works, you can end up feeling disappointed even when both of you are trying.

Over time, these small misses can start to tell a bigger story. You may begin to think your needs are not important, while they may feel like nothing they do is ever enough. That is when a simple misunderstanding turns into resentment.

Be direct. Tell this person what helps you feel cared for. Ask them what matters to them too. Stop grading each other on mind-reading. This connection gets stronger when you focus less on how love should look and more on whether it is actually reaching the other person.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"The care is there, but the delivery can be off. You may both want to make each other feel loved, yet keep missing the mark. One person gives what they would want to receive, while the other is left thinking, \"That is not really what I needed.\"\n\nThe good news is that there is usually genuine affection underneath the frustration. You likely want the best for each other. The challenge is that good intentions do not automatically create emotional connection. If you keep assuming the other person should just know what works, you can end up feeling disappointed even when both of you are trying.\n\nOver time, these small misses can start to tell a bigger story. You may begin to think your needs are not important, while they may feel like nothing they do is ever enough. That is when a simple misunderstanding turns into resentment.\n\nBe direct. Tell this person what helps you feel cared for. Ask them what matters to them too. Stop grading each other on mind-reading. This connection gets stronger when you focus less on how love should look and more on whether it is actually reaching the other person."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Over time, these small misses can start to tell a bigger story. You may begin to think your needs are not important, while they may feel like nothing they do is ever enough. That is when a simple misunderstanding turns into resentment."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Be direct. Tell this person what helps you feel cared for. Ask them what matters to them too. Stop grading each other on mind-reading. This connection gets stronger when you focus less on how love should look and more on whether it is actually reaching the other person."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-moon_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s feelings. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"The care is there, but the delivery can be off. You may both want to make each other feel loved, yet keep missing the mark. One person gives what they would want to receive, while the other is left thinking, \"That is not really what I needed.\"\n\nThe good news is that there is usually genuine affection underneath the frustration. You likely want the best for each other. The challenge is that good intentions do not automatically create emotional connection. If you keep assuming the other person should just know what works, you can end up feeling disappointed even when both of you are trying.\n\nOver time, these small misses can start to tell a bigger story. You may begin to think your needs are not important, while they may feel like nothing they do is ever enough. That is when a simple misunderstanding turns into resentment.\n\nBe direct. Tell this person what helps you feel cared for. Ask them what matters to them too. Stop grading each other on mind-reading. This connection gets stronger when you focus less on how love should look and more on whether it is actually reaching the other person.","tension":"Over time, these small misses can start to tell a bigger story. You may begin to think your needs are not important, while they may feel like nothing they do is ever enough. That is when a simple misunderstanding turns into resentment.","advice":"Be direct. Tell this person what helps you feel cared for. Ask them what matters to them too. Stop grading each other on mind-reading. This connection gets stronger when you focus less on how love should look and more on whether it is actually reaching the other person.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-moon_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"moon","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-moon_trine', 'synastry-venus-trine-moon', 'relationship-venus-trine-moon']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-moon_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-moon_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Trine Moon', null, 'This relationship can feel easy in the best way. You may find yourself relaxing around this person instead of wondering where you stand. Affection tends to flow naturally, and being kind to each other does not feel like work. There is often a sense of emotional safety here that makes it easier to let your guard down and be yourself.

At its best, this connection reminds you that love does not always have to be complicated. You may feel accepted, appreciated, and genuinely cared for. This person can bring out a softer side of you, not because they demand it, but because you feel comfortable enough to show it. There is less pressure to perform and more room to simply be.

The challenge is not conflict so much as taking each other for granted. When something feels this natural, it is easy to assume it will take care of itself. You may stop noticing the small things that make the relationship work because they have become so familiar.

Do not coast on good chemistry. Keep showing up. Keep making the effort to connect. The warmth between you is a gift, but it is not self-sustaining. The relationships that last are the ones where people keep choosing each other.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This relationship can feel easy in the best way. You may find yourself relaxing around this person instead of wondering where you stand. Affection tends to flow naturally, and being kind to each other does not feel like work. There is often a sense of emotional safety here that makes it easier to let your guard down and be yourself.\n\nAt its best, this connection reminds you that love does not always have to be complicated. You may feel accepted, appreciated, and genuinely cared for. This person can bring out a softer side of you, not because they demand it, but because you feel comfortable enough to show it. There is less pressure to perform and more room to simply be.\n\nThe challenge is not conflict so much as taking each other for granted. When something feels this natural, it is easy to assume it will take care of itself. You may stop noticing the small things that make the relationship work because they have become so familiar.\n\nDo not coast on good chemistry. Keep showing up. Keep making the effort to connect. The warmth between you is a gift, but it is not self-sustaining. The relationships that last are the ones where people keep choosing each other."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is not conflict so much as taking each other for granted. When something feels this natural, it is easy to assume it will take care of itself. You may stop noticing the small things that make the relationship work because they have become so familiar."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Do not coast on good chemistry. Keep showing up. Keep making the effort to connect. The warmth between you is a gift, but it is not self-sustaining. The relationships that last are the ones where people keep choosing each other."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-moon_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s feelings. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This relationship can feel easy in the best way. You may find yourself relaxing around this person instead of wondering where you stand. Affection tends to flow naturally, and being kind to each other does not feel like work. There is often a sense of emotional safety here that makes it easier to let your guard down and be yourself.\n\nAt its best, this connection reminds you that love does not always have to be complicated. You may feel accepted, appreciated, and genuinely cared for. This person can bring out a softer side of you, not because they demand it, but because you feel comfortable enough to show it. There is less pressure to perform and more room to simply be.\n\nThe challenge is not conflict so much as taking each other for granted. When something feels this natural, it is easy to assume it will take care of itself. You may stop noticing the small things that make the relationship work because they have become so familiar.\n\nDo not coast on good chemistry. Keep showing up. Keep making the effort to connect. The warmth between you is a gift, but it is not self-sustaining. The relationships that last are the ones where people keep choosing each other.","tension":"The challenge is not conflict so much as taking each other for granted. When something feels this natural, it is easy to assume it will take care of itself. You may stop noticing the small things that make the relationship work because they have become so familiar.","advice":"Do not coast on good chemistry. Keep showing up. Keep making the effort to connect. The warmth between you is a gift, but it is not self-sustaining. The relationships that last are the ones where people keep choosing each other.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-neptune_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"neptune","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-neptune_conjunction', 'synastry-venus-conjunction-neptune', 'relationship-venus-conjunction-neptune']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-neptune_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-neptune_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Conjunction Neptune', null, 'This person can awaken a kind of love that feels both familiar and longed for, as though something in you has been waiting for their arrival.

The attraction can feel immediate, as though something in you recognizes each other before there is enough history to explain why. The Neptune person may be captivated by the Venus person''s beauty, charm, or perceived goodness, seeing them through a lens that turns ordinary details into something meaningful. The Venus person may feel cherished, admired, and deeply appreciated, sometimes to a degree that feels almost magical.

There can be a visible charge around this connection. Other people may notice the way you look at each other, the way the room seems to narrow when you are together, the way both of you seem caught inside something that does not include anyone else yet. Sometimes the spell is not private. Sometimes the people around you can see it before you know what to call it.

At its best, this aspect reaches the places that expect disappointment and offers something different. The Venus person may feel more willing to offer affection without guarding every feeling. The Neptune person may feel less alone in their longing, as though something they have been searching for has finally taken shape. Together, you may create a kind of intimacy that feels imaginative, romantic, and deeply moving. Even the smallest exchanges can seem touched by something larger than themselves.

But the conjunction can make the dream too powerful.

The Neptune person may begin loving the image as much as the person. The Venus person may begin performing the image because being adored this way feels good. Over time, the pedestal becomes heavy. You cannot have an ordinary mood. You cannot need too much. You cannot be inconvenient without the dream flickering.

Reality always arrives. And when it does, there can be a moment of grief. Not because the love was false, but because no human being can fully embody a dream. The challenge is letting the relationship become real without treating reality as a loss.

The work is to choose the real person again and again. Let the romance stay alive, but do not ask anyone to become a symbol.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can awaken a kind of love that feels both familiar and longed for, as though something in you has been waiting for their arrival.\n\nThe attraction can feel immediate, as though something in you recognizes each other before there is enough history to explain why. The Neptune person may be captivated by the Venus person''s beauty, charm, or perceived goodness, seeing them through a lens that turns ordinary details into something meaningful. The Venus person may feel cherished, admired, and deeply appreciated, sometimes to a degree that feels almost magical.\n\nThere can be a visible charge around this connection. Other people may notice the way you look at each other, the way the room seems to narrow when you are together, the way both of you seem caught inside something that does not include anyone else yet. Sometimes the spell is not private. Sometimes the people around you can see it before you know what to call it.\n\nAt its best, this aspect reaches the places that expect disappointment and offers something different. The Venus person may feel more willing to offer affection without guarding every feeling. The Neptune person may feel less alone in their longing, as though something they have been searching for has finally taken shape. Together, you may create a kind of intimacy that feels imaginative, romantic, and deeply moving. Even the smallest exchanges can seem touched by something larger than themselves.\n\nBut the conjunction can make the dream too powerful.\n\nThe Neptune person may begin loving the image as much as the person. The Venus person may begin performing the image because being adored this way feels good. Over time, the pedestal becomes heavy. You cannot have an ordinary mood. You cannot need too much. You cannot be inconvenient without the dream flickering.\n\nReality always arrives. And when it does, there can be a moment of grief. Not because the love was false, but because no human being can fully embody a dream. The challenge is letting the relationship become real without treating reality as a loss.\n\nThe work is to choose the real person again and again. Let the romance stay alive, but do not ask anyone to become a symbol."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The Neptune person may begin loving the image as much as the person. The Venus person may begin performing the image because being adored this way feels good. Over time, the pedestal becomes heavy. You cannot have an ordinary mood. You cannot need too much. You cannot be inconvenient without the dream flickering.\n\nReality always arrives. And when it does, there can be a moment of grief. Not because the love was false, but because no human being can fully embody a dream. The challenge is letting the relationship become real without treating reality as a loss."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The work is to choose the real person again and again. Let the romance stay alive, but do not ask anyone to become a symbol."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-neptune_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s dreams. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"This person can awaken a kind of love that feels both familiar and longed for, as though something in you has been waiting for their arrival.\n\nThe attraction can feel immediate, as though something in you recognizes each other before there is enough history to explain why. The Neptune person may be captivated by the Venus person''s beauty, charm, or perceived goodness, seeing them through a lens that turns ordinary details into something meaningful. The Venus person may feel cherished, admired, and deeply appreciated, sometimes to a degree that feels almost magical.\n\nThere can be a visible charge around this connection. Other people may notice the way