 relationship can become heavy.\n\nOne person may take on the job of staying lovely, forgiving, inspiring, or easy to adore. The other may settle into the dream and resist seeing what is real. It can feel romantic at first. Eventually it can become exhausting. You may realize that the relationship has been protecting an image instead of getting to know the people inside it.\n\nThere may not be any intentional deception here. More often, both of you are relating to an idea of each other instead of the actual person. You see what you want to see. They do the same. The feelings are real, but feelings alone are not enough to tell you how a relationship will unfold over time.\n\nIn its harder expression, this aspect can move from bliss into confusion. Someone becomes unavailable. Someone stops answering clearly. Promises are made and not kept. The truth gets slippery. Avoidance starts to replace honesty. If gaslighting enters the dynamic, name it as gaslighting, not as chemistry, not as fate, and not as Neptune being romantic.\n\nThe lesson is to stop protecting the dream at the expense of your reality.","tension":"One person may take on the job of staying lovely, forgiving, inspiring, or easy to adore. The other may settle into the dream and resist seeing what is real. It can feel romantic at first. Eventually it can become exhausting. You may realize that the relationship has been protecting an image instead of getting to know the people inside it.\n\nThere may not be any intentional deception here. More often, both of you are relating to an idea of each other instead of the actual person. You see what you want to see. They do the same. The feelings are real, but feelings alone are not enough to tell you how a relationship will unfold over time.\n\nIn its harder expression, this aspect can move from bliss into confusion. Someone becomes unavailable. Someone stops answering clearly. Promises are made and not kept. The truth gets slippery. Avoidance starts to replace honesty. If gaslighting enters the dynamic, name it as gaslighting, not as chemistry, not as fate, and not as Neptune being romantic.","advice":"The lesson is to stop protecting the dream at the expense of your reality.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-neptune_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"neptune","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-neptune_trine', 'synastry-venus-trine-neptune', 'relationship-venus-trine-neptune']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-neptune_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-neptune_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Trine Neptune', null, 'This relationship often carries an easy kind of magic, as though affection and understanding flow naturally between you.

There can be a real sense of peace in each other''s presence. Warmth, kindness, comfort, and the feeling that everything will be okay may come more easily here than they do with most people. Even irritation may pass quickly. You can be annoyed for a moment, then somehow the edge dissolves and you remember why you care.

This connection often feels easy from the start. The Neptune person may notice something beautiful or special about the Venus person that others miss, while the Venus person may feel more relaxed, loving, and open in return. Simply being together can feel comforting, inspiring, and emotionally nourishing.

At its best, this aspect encourages kindness and compassion. The Neptune person brings imagination, sensitivity, and faith in the relationship, while the Venus person helps turn those feelings into something tangible through affection and care. Together, you may find it easier to appreciate beauty, extend forgiveness, and enjoy the simple moments that make life feel meaningful.

Still, Neptune can blur boundaries, even in a flowing aspect like this one.

Because things feel so natural between you, it can be tempting to avoid difficult conversations or overlook issues that need attention. The Venus person may enjoy feeling appreciated and choose not to question certain things. The Neptune person may focus on what is lovely about the relationship and avoid dealing with its more complicated realities. Over time, what goes unsaid can quietly build up.

The challenge is not to lose the magic of the connection, but to stay grounded in what is real.

Let yourself enjoy the romance, the peace, the kindness, and the sense of possibility. Just make sure there is room for the messy conversations too.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This relationship often carries an easy kind of magic, as though affection and understanding flow naturally between you.\n\nThere can be a real sense of peace in each other''s presence. Warmth, kindness, comfort, and the feeling that everything will be okay may come more easily here than they do with most people. Even irritation may pass quickly. You can be annoyed for a moment, then somehow the edge dissolves and you remember why you care.\n\nThis connection often feels easy from the start. The Neptune person may notice something beautiful or special about the Venus person that others miss, while the Venus person may feel more relaxed, loving, and open in return. Simply being together can feel comforting, inspiring, and emotionally nourishing.\n\nAt its best, this aspect encourages kindness and compassion. The Neptune person brings imagination, sensitivity, and faith in the relationship, while the Venus person helps turn those feelings into something tangible through affection and care. Together, you may find it easier to appreciate beauty, extend forgiveness, and enjoy the simple moments that make life feel meaningful.\n\nStill, Neptune can blur boundaries, even in a flowing aspect like this one.\n\nBecause things feel so natural between you, it can be tempting to avoid difficult conversations or overlook issues that need attention. The Venus person may enjoy feeling appreciated and choose not to question certain things. The Neptune person may focus on what is lovely about the relationship and avoid dealing with its more complicated realities. Over time, what goes unsaid can quietly build up.\n\nThe challenge is not to lose the magic of the connection, but to stay grounded in what is real.\n\nLet yourself enjoy the romance, the peace, the kindness, and the sense of possibility. Just make sure there is room for the messy conversations too."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Because things feel so natural between you, it can be tempting to avoid difficult conversations or overlook issues that need attention. The Venus person may enjoy feeling appreciated and choose not to question certain things. The Neptune person may focus on what is lovely about the relationship and avoid dealing with its more complicated realities. Over time, what goes unsaid can quietly build up."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The challenge is not to lose the magic of the connection, but to stay grounded in what is real.\n\nLet yourself enjoy the romance, the peace, the kindness, and the sense of possibility. Just make sure there is room for the messy conversations too."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-neptune_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s dreams. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This relationship often carries an easy kind of magic, as though affection and understanding flow naturally between you.\n\nThere can be a real sense of peace in each other''s presence. Warmth, kindness, comfort, and the feeling that everything will be okay may come more easily here than they do with most people. Even irritation may pass quickly. You can be annoyed for a moment, then somehow the edge dissolves and you remember why you care.\n\nThis connection often feels easy from the start. The Neptune person may notice something beautiful or special about the Venus person that others miss, while the Venus person may feel more relaxed, loving, and open in return. Simply being together can feel comforting, inspiring, and emotionally nourishing.\n\nAt its best, this aspect encourages kindness and compassion. The Neptune person brings imagination, sensitivity, and faith in the relationship, while the Venus person helps turn those feelings into something tangible through affection and care. Together, you may find it easier to appreciate beauty, extend forgiveness, and enjoy the simple moments that make life feel meaningful.\n\nStill, Neptune can blur boundaries, even in a flowing aspect like this one.\n\nBecause things feel so natural between you, it can be tempting to avoid difficult conversations or overlook issues that need attention. The Venus person may enjoy feeling appreciated and choose not to question certain things. The Neptune person may focus on what is lovely about the relationship and avoid dealing with its more complicated realities. Over time, what goes unsaid can quietly build up.\n\nThe challenge is not to lose the magic of the connection, but to stay grounded in what is real.\n\nLet yourself enjoy the romance, the peace, the kindness, and the sense of possibility. Just make sure there is room for the messy conversations too.","tension":"Because things feel so natural between you, it can be tempting to avoid difficult conversations or overlook issues that need attention. The Venus person may enjoy feeling appreciated and choose not to question certain things. The Neptune person may focus on what is lovely about the relationship and avoid dealing with its more complicated realities. Over time, what goes unsaid can quietly build up.","advice":"The challenge is not to lose the magic of the connection, but to stay grounded in what is real.\n\nLet yourself enjoy the romance, the peace, the kindness, and the sense of possibility. Just make sure there is room for the messy conversations too.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-pluto_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-pluto_conjunction', 'synastry-venus-conjunction-pluto', 'relationship-venus-conjunction-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-pluto_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-pluto_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Conjunction Pluto', null, 'The attraction here can feel immediate, consuming, and hard to explain.

Venus-Pluto conjunctions often create a powerful magnetic pull. The Pluto person may feel intensely drawn to the Venus person''s beauty, softness, affection, or desirability. The Venus person may feel wanted in a way that feels rare, almost overwhelming, as though the Pluto person sees something in them that others only skim past.

At first, this can feel incredible. The chemistry can be strong, the emotional charge difficult to ignore, and the sense of recognition deeply intoxicating. The Pluto person often wants access to more than surface affection. They want the deeper layer, the hidden desire, the part of the Venus person that is not offered casually.

At its best, this aspect can create deep intimacy. It can help both people become more honest about what they want, what they fear, and how vulnerable it feels to be desired deeply. Love can become transformative here, not because it is easy, but because it asks both people to show up with less pretense.

But this aspect can become consuming quickly. The desire to be close can become the need to possess. Attraction can become obsession. The Pluto person may become controlling, jealous, or fixated on maintaining access to the Venus person. The Venus person may begin to feel dependent on the Pluto person''s attention, approval, or desire. This is one of the clearest Venus-Pluto indicators of a bond that can be hard to leave when it is handled poorly. The intensity can feel like proof that the connection matters, even when the relationship is costing one or both people their peace.

The lesson is simple: being wanted deeply is not the same as being loved well.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"The attraction here can feel immediate, consuming, and hard to explain.\n\nVenus-Pluto conjunctions often create a powerful magnetic pull. The Pluto person may feel intensely drawn to the Venus person''s beauty, softness, affection, or desirability. The Venus person may feel wanted in a way that feels rare, almost overwhelming, as though the Pluto person sees something in them that others only skim past.\n\nAt first, this can feel incredible. The chemistry can be strong, the emotional charge difficult to ignore, and the sense of recognition deeply intoxicating. The Pluto person often wants access to more than surface affection. They want the deeper layer, the hidden desire, the part of the Venus person that is not offered casually.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can create deep intimacy. It can help both people become more honest about what they want, what they fear, and how vulnerable it feels to be desired deeply. Love can become transformative here, not because it is easy, but because it asks both people to show up with less pretense.\n\nBut this aspect can become consuming quickly. The desire to be close can become the need to possess. Attraction can become obsession. The Pluto person may become controlling, jealous, or fixated on maintaining access to the Venus person. The Venus person may begin to feel dependent on the Pluto person''s attention, approval, or desire. This is one of the clearest Venus-Pluto indicators of a bond that can be hard to leave when it is handled poorly. The intensity can feel like proof that the connection matters, even when the relationship is costing one or both people their peace.\n\nThe lesson is simple: being wanted deeply is not the same as being loved well."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But this aspect can become consuming quickly. The desire to be close can become the need to possess. Attraction can become obsession. The Pluto person may become controlling, jealous, or fixated on maintaining access to the Venus person. The Venus person may begin to feel dependent on the Pluto person''s attention, approval, or desire. This is one of the clearest Venus-Pluto indicators of a bond that can be hard to leave when it is handled poorly. The intensity can feel like proof that the connection matters, even when the relationship is costing one or both people their peace."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The lesson is simple: being wanted deeply is not the same as being loved well."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-pluto_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s depth and power. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"The attraction here can feel immediate, consuming, and hard to explain.\n\nVenus-Pluto conjunctions often create a powerful magnetic pull. The Pluto person may feel intensely drawn to the Venus person''s beauty, softness, affection, or desirability. The Venus person may feel wanted in a way that feels rare, almost overwhelming, as though the Pluto person sees something in them that others only skim past.\n\nAt first, this can feel incredible. The chemistry can be strong, the emotional charge difficult to ignore, and the sense of recognition deeply intoxicating. The Pluto person often wants access to more than surface affection. They want the deeper layer, the hidden desire, the part of the Venus person that is not offered casually.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can create deep intimacy. It can help both people become more honest about what they want, what they fear, and how vulnerable it feels to be desired deeply. Love can become transformative here, not because it is easy, but because it asks both people to show up with less pretense.\n\nBut this aspect can become consuming quickly. The desire to be close can become the need to possess. Attraction can become obsession. The Pluto person may become controlling, jealous, or fixated on maintaining access to the Venus person. The Venus person may begin to feel dependent on the Pluto person''s attention, approval, or desire. This is one of the clearest Venus-Pluto indicators of a bond that can be hard to leave when it is handled poorly. The intensity can feel like proof that the connection matters, even when the relationship is costing one or both people their peace.\n\nThe lesson is simple: being wanted deeply is not the same as being loved well.","tension":"But this aspect can become consuming quickly. The desire to be close can become the need to possess. Attraction can become obsession. The Pluto person may become controlling, jealous, or fixated on maintaining access to the Venus person. The Venus person may begin to feel dependent on the Pluto person''s attention, approval, or desire. This is one of the clearest Venus-Pluto indicators of a bond that can be hard to leave when it is handled poorly. The intensity can feel like proof that the connection matters, even when the relationship is costing one or both people their peace.","advice":"The lesson is simple: being wanted deeply is not the same as being loved well.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-pluto_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-pluto_opposition', 'synastry-venus-opposition-pluto', 'relationship-venus-opposition-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-pluto_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-pluto_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Opposition Pluto', null, 'This person may pull at your desire in a way that feels magnetic and unsettling at the same time. There is often a strong attraction here, but it can come with a sense of imbalance. The Pluto person may seem to reach the Venus person''s deeper wants, insecurities, and need for validation while remaining somewhat harder to read themselves. The Venus person may feel deeply desired, but also exposed, vulnerable, or unsure of where they stand.

At its healthiest, this aspect can bring honesty to the surface. The Pluto person may help the Venus person recognize what they truly want in love, where they seek approval, and where they have confused being desired with being secure. The Venus person can soften the Pluto person''s intensity, helping them experience love with more openness and less control.

But this aspect can also become a power struggle around love and desire. One person may reach while the other withdraws. One person may need reassurance while the other protects their power by staying mysterious, unavailable, or hard to pin down. Jealousy, possessiveness, testing, and withdrawal games can emerge when fear takes over. The bond can become difficult to step away from, because it activates desire so strongly. Wanting someone can begin to feel like needing them. Being wanted can begin to feel like proof of worth.

The work is staying anchored in your own value. Both people need to be honest about what they want without using affection, distance, jealousy, or desire as tools for control. This connection can deepen love when vulnerability is respected. Without that respect, attraction can become destabilizing.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person may pull at your desire in a way that feels magnetic and unsettling at the same time. There is often a strong attraction here, but it can come with a sense of imbalance. The Pluto person may seem to reach the Venus person''s deeper wants, insecurities, and need for validation while remaining somewhat harder to read themselves. The Venus person may feel deeply desired, but also exposed, vulnerable, or unsure of where they stand.\n\nAt its healthiest, this aspect can bring honesty to the surface. The Pluto person may help the Venus person recognize what they truly want in love, where they seek approval, and where they have confused being desired with being secure. The Venus person can soften the Pluto person''s intensity, helping them experience love with more openness and less control.\n\nBut this aspect can also become a power struggle around love and desire. One person may reach while the other withdraws. One person may need reassurance while the other protects their power by staying mysterious, unavailable, or hard to pin down. Jealousy, possessiveness, testing, and withdrawal games can emerge when fear takes over. The bond can become difficult to step away from, because it activates desire so strongly. Wanting someone can begin to feel like needing them. Being wanted can begin to feel like proof of worth.\n\nThe work is staying anchored in your own value. Both people need to be honest about what they want without using affection, distance, jealousy, or desire as tools for control. This connection can deepen love when vulnerability is respected. Without that respect, attraction can become destabilizing."},{"h