),
  ('A-venus_B-pluto_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-pluto_sextile', 'synastry-venus-sextile-pluto', 'relationship-venus-sextile-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-pluto_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-pluto_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Sextile Pluto', null, 'This connection has the potential to create deep attraction, trust, and emotional honesty over time. The Pluto person may sense something beneath the Venus person''s surface: a hidden desire, a guarded softness, a deeper need to be loved and chosen. The Venus person may feel drawn to the Pluto person''s depth, intensity, and emotional presence without feeling immediately overwhelmed by it.

There is magnetism here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured consciously, it can become a strong foundation for intimacy. The Pluto person may help the Venus person become more honest about what they want and what they value. The Venus person may help the Pluto person soften their intensity and trust love without needing to control it.

One of the strengths of this aspect is that it does not rush transformation. The opportunity for depth is there, but both people have to engage it. The relationship tends to grow through trust, honest affection, and a willingness to explore what lives beneath attraction.

The challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to enjoy the chemistry without fully exploring the deeper emotional work available between you. If both people avoid vulnerability, the relationship may remain pleasant, magnetic, and supportive, but some of its most transformative gifts may stay unopened.

Let the connection deepen at a pace that feels safe. Be honest about desire without turning it into control. The gift of this aspect is not intensity for its own sake. It is the chance to experience love as something that transforms without consuming.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection has the potential to create deep attraction, trust, and emotional honesty over time. The Pluto person may sense something beneath the Venus person''s surface: a hidden desire, a guarded softness, a deeper need to be loved and chosen. The Venus person may feel drawn to the Pluto person''s depth, intensity, and emotional presence without feeling immediately overwhelmed by it.\n\nThere is magnetism here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured consciously, it can become a strong foundation for intimacy. The Pluto person may help the Venus person become more honest about what they want and what they value. The Venus person may help the Pluto person soften their intensity and trust love without needing to control it.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is that it does not rush transformation. The opportunity for depth is there, but both people have to engage it. The relationship tends to grow through trust, honest affection, and a willingness to explore what lives beneath attraction.\n\nThe challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to enjoy the chemistry without fully exploring the deeper emotional work available between you. If both people avoid vulnerability, the relationship may remain pleasant, magnetic, and supportive, but some of its most transformative gifts may stay unopened.\n\nLet the connection deepen at a pace that feels safe. Be honest about desire without turning it into control. The gift of this aspect is not intensity for its own sake. It is the chance to experience love as something that transforms without consuming."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to enjoy the chemistry without fully exploring the deeper emotional work available between you. If both people avoid vulnerability, the relationship may remain pleasant, magnetic, and supportive, but some of its most transformative gifts may stay unopened."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the connection deepen at a pace that feels safe. Be honest about desire without turning it into control. The gift of this aspect is not intensity for its own sake. It is the chance to experience love as something that transforms without consuming."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-pluto_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s depth and power. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"This connection has the potential to create deep attraction, trust, and emotional honesty over time. The Pluto person may sense something beneath the Venus person''s surface: a hidden desire, a guarded softness, a deeper need to be loved and chosen. The Venus person may feel drawn to the Pluto person''s depth, intensity, and emotional presence without feeling immediately overwhelmed by it.\n\nThere is magnetism here, but it does not force itself. It waits to be chosen. When this connection is nurtured consciously, it can become a strong foundation for intimacy. The Pluto person may help the Venus person become more honest about what they want and what they value. The Venus person may help the Pluto person soften their intensity and trust love without needing to control it.\n\nOne of the strengths of this aspect is that it does not rush transformation. The opportunity for depth is there, but both people have to engage it. The relationship tends to grow through trust, honest affection, and a willingness to explore what lives beneath attraction.\n\nThe challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to enjoy the chemistry without fully exploring the deeper emotional work available between you. If both people avoid vulnerability, the relationship may remain pleasant, magnetic, and supportive, but some of its most transformative gifts may stay unopened.\n\nLet the connection deepen at a pace that feels safe. Be honest about desire without turning it into control. The gift of this aspect is not intensity for its own sake. It is the chance to experience love as something that transforms without consuming.","tension":"The challenge is that potential alone is not enough. It can be easy to enjoy the chemistry without fully exploring the deeper emotional work available between you. If both people avoid vulnerability, the relationship may remain pleasant, magnetic, and supportive, but some of its most transformative gifts may stay unopened.","advice":"Let the connection deepen at a pace that feels safe. Be honest about desire without turning it into control. The gift of this aspect is not intensity for its own sake. It is the chance to experience love as something that transforms without consuming.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-pluto_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-pluto_square', 'synastry-venus-square-pluto', 'relationship-venus-square-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-pluto_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-pluto_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Square Pluto', null, 'This connection can stir desire in a way that feels powerful, uncomfortable, and difficult to ignore. Venus-Pluto squares often arrive with chemistry. Not light chemistry, but the kind that exposes what people want, fear, envy, crave, or feel ashamed of wanting. The Pluto person may activate the Venus person''s deeper insecurities around beauty, desirability, worth, and love. The Venus person may awaken the Pluto person''s hunger for closeness, control, or emotional certainty.

There is often a strong pull toward one another, even when the connection feels complicated. The attraction may feel intense, but not necessarily peaceful. Both people can find themselves drawn into dynamics that feel larger than the moment itself, as though the relationship has tapped into deeper patterns around love, rejection, longing, or power.

At its best, this aspect can be transformative. It can reveal where love has become tangled with control, where desire has become confused with validation, and where old relationship patterns are ready to be seen more clearly. The tension can force honesty about what each person truly wants and what they are afraid of losing.

But pressure is not the same as love. When this aspect becomes unconscious, the relationship can start running on jealousy, testing, withdrawal, rupture, reunion, and emotional intensity. One person may try to regain power by pulling away. The other may chase harder. The connection can become addictive, not because it is healthy, but because the highs and lows keep activating the desire to be chosen. Pay attention to what this bond brings out in you. Do you feel more confident, more honest, and more connected to your own worth? Or do you feel consumed by the need to be wanted, reassured, or chosen?

You do not have to call possession love. You do not have to stay in a painful cycle because the chemistry is strong. The wisdom of this aspect comes from learning the difference between desire that transforms you and desire that destabilizes you.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection can stir desire in a way that feels powerful, uncomfortable, and difficult to ignore. Venus-Pluto squares often arrive with chemistry. Not light chemistry, but the kind that exposes what people want, fear, envy, crave, or feel ashamed of wanting. The Pluto person may activate the Venus person''s deeper insecurities around beauty, desirability, worth, and love. The Venus person may awaken the Pluto person''s hunger for closeness, control, or emotional certainty.\n\nThere is often a strong pull toward one another, even when the connection feels complicated. The attraction may feel intense, but not necessarily peaceful. Both people can find themselves drawn into dynamics that feel larger than the moment itself, as though the relationship has tapped into deeper patterns around love, rejection, longing, or power.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can be transformative. It can reveal where love has become tangled with control, where desire has become confused with validation, and where old relationship patterns are ready to be seen more clearly. The tension can force honesty about what each person truly wants and what they are afraid of losing.\n\nBut pressure is not the same as love. When this aspect becomes unconscious, the relationship can start running on jealousy, testing, withdrawal, rupture, reunion, and emotional intensity. One person may try to regain power by pulling away. The other may chase harder. The connection can become addictive, not because it is healthy, but because the highs and lows keep activating the desire to be chosen. Pay attention to what this bond brings out in you. Do you feel more confident, more honest, and more connected to your own worth? Or do you feel consumed by the need to be wanted, reassured, or chosen?\n\nYou do not have to call possession love. You do not have to stay in a painful cycle because the chemistry is strong. The wisdom of this aspect comes from learning the difference between desire that transforms you and desire that destabilizes you."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"But pressure is not the same as love. When this aspect becomes unconscious, the relationship can start running on jealousy, testing, withdrawal, rupture, reunion, and emotional intensity. One person may try to regain power by pulling away. The other may chase harder. The connection can become addictive, not because it is healthy, but because the highs and lows keep activating the desire to be chosen. Pay attention to what this bond brings out in you. Do you feel more confident, more honest, and more connected to your own worth? Or do you feel consumed by the need to be wanted, reassured, or chosen?"},{"heading":"Advice","body":"You do not have to call possession love. You do not have to stay in a painful cycle because the chemistry is strong. The wisdom of this aspect comes from learning the difference between desire that transforms you and desire that destabilizes you."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-pluto_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"The Venus person''s love meets Pluto''s hunger for depth and control. Magnetic does not automatically mean healthy. The test is whether desire leaves both people freer and more honest, not more afraid.","summaryDeep":"This connection can stir desire in a way that feels powerful, uncomfortable, and difficult to ignore. Venus-Pluto squares often arrive with chemistry. Not light chemistry, but the kind that exposes what people want, fear, envy, crave, or feel ashamed of wanting. The Pluto person may activate the Venus person''s deeper insecurities around beauty, desirability, worth, and love. The Venus person may awaken the Pluto person''s hunger for closeness, control,