o what this bond brings out in you. Do you feel more confident, more honest, and more connected to your own worth? Or do you feel consumed by the need to be wanted, reassured, or chosen?","advice":"You do not have to call possession love. You do not have to stay in a painful cycle because the chemistry is strong. The wisdom of this aspect comes from learning the difference between desire that transforms you and desire that destabilizes you.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-pluto_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"pluto","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-pluto_trine', 'synastry-venus-trine-pluto', 'relationship-venus-trine-pluto']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-pluto_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-pluto_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Trine Pluto', null, 'This connection carries deep attraction without the same level of friction. The Pluto person may be drawn to the Venus person with unusual depth and focus, while the Venus person may feel genuinely desired, valued, and emotionally recognized. There is often a natural trust here, as though affection can deepen without being forced and desire can be expressed without immediately becoming a power struggle.

At its best, this aspect can be deeply healing. The Pluto person may help the Venus person feel more confident in their desirability, more honest about what they want, and more willing to receive love at a deeper level. The Venus person can soften the Pluto person''s intensity, helping them experience closeness with more trust, tenderness, and care.

There is still intensity here. Pluto never keeps love entirely light. But the trine often allows that intensity to move with more ease and less fear. Instead of forcing transformation through jealousy, crisis, or control, this aspect can support it through loyalty, trust, emotional honesty, and deep affection.

The shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to underestimate how much influence it carries. The Venus person may slowly begin organizing their sense of beauty, worth, or desire around the Pluto person''s attention. The Pluto person may not realize how much power their approval or withdrawal has.

Let the love deepen you, but keep your own sense of worth intact. This aspect can offer rare intimacy, but it still asks both people to stay aware of where devotion ends and dependency begins.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection carries deep attraction without the same level of friction. The Pluto person may be drawn to the Venus person with unusual depth and focus, while the Venus person may feel genuinely desired, valued, and emotionally recognized. There is often a natural trust here, as though affection can deepen without being forced and desire can be expressed without immediately becoming a power struggle.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can be deeply healing. The Pluto person may help the Venus person feel more confident in their desirability, more honest about what they want, and more willing to receive love at a deeper level. The Venus person can soften the Pluto person''s intensity, helping them experience closeness with more trust, tenderness, and care.\n\nThere is still intensity here. Pluto never keeps love entirely light. But the trine often allows that intensity to move with more ease and less fear. Instead of forcing transformation through jealousy, crisis, or control, this aspect can support it through loyalty, trust, emotional honesty, and deep affection.\n\nThe shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to underestimate how much influence it carries. The Venus person may slowly begin organizing their sense of beauty, worth, or desire around the Pluto person''s attention. The Pluto person may not realize how much power their approval or withdrawal has.\n\nLet the love deepen you, but keep your own sense of worth intact. This aspect can offer rare intimacy, but it still asks both people to stay aware of where devotion ends and dependency begins."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to underestimate how much influence it carries. The Venus person may slowly begin organizing their sense of beauty, worth, or desire around the Pluto person''s attention. The Pluto person may not realize how much power their approval or withdrawal has."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let the love deepen you, but keep your own sense of worth intact. This aspect can offer rare intimacy, but it still asks both people to stay aware of where devotion ends and dependency begins."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-pluto_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s depth and power. The trine lets them flow together easily.","summaryDeep":"This connection carries deep attraction without the same level of friction. The Pluto person may be drawn to the Venus person with unusual depth and focus, while the Venus person may feel genuinely desired, valued, and emotionally recognized. There is often a natural trust here, as though affection can deepen without being forced and desire can be expressed without immediately becoming a power struggle.\n\nAt its best, this aspect can be deeply healing. The Pluto person may help the Venus person feel more confident in their desirability, more honest about what they want, and more willing to receive love at a deeper level. The Venus person can soften the Pluto person''s intensity, helping them experience closeness with more trust, tenderness, and care.\n\nThere is still intensity here. Pluto never keeps love entirely light. But the trine often allows that intensity to move with more ease and less fear. Instead of forcing transformation through jealousy, crisis, or control, this aspect can support it through loyalty, trust, emotional honesty, and deep affection.\n\nThe shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to underestimate how much influence it carries. The Venus person may slowly begin organizing their sense of beauty, worth, or desire around the Pluto person''s attention. The Pluto person may not realize how much power their approval or withdrawal has.\n\nLet the love deepen you, but keep your own sense of worth intact. This aspect can offer rare intimacy, but it still asks both people to stay aware of where devotion ends and dependency begins.","tension":"The shadow is subtle. Because the connection feels natural, it can be easy to underestimate how much influence it carries. The Venus person may slowly begin organizing their sense of beauty, worth, or desire around the Pluto person''s attention. The Pluto person may not realize how much power their approval or withdrawal has.","advice":"Let the love deepen you, but keep your own sense of worth intact. This aspect can offer rare intimacy, but it still asks both people to stay aware of where devotion ends and dependency begins.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":5}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-saturn_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-saturn_conjunction', 'synastry-venus-conjunction-saturn', 'relationship-venus-conjunction-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-saturn_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-saturn_conjunction","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Conjunction Saturn', null, 'This person can make love feel like something that has to be earned. Their reserved or cautious way of expressing affection may leave you wondering where you stand, even when they care deeply. Around them, old insecurities about being wanted or valued can surface, and you may find yourself putting extra pressure on yourself to get things right. Instead of relaxing into the connection, you may start trying to prove that you are worthy of the love and reassurance you want.

When this connection is functioning well, it can create a meaningful sense of commitment and emotional security. This person may not be naturally expressive or demonstrative with affection, but they often communicate care through reliability, responsibility, and a willingness to stay present when difficulties arise. Their approach to love may be thoughtful and serious, with a focus on creating something stable and lasting.

For many people, that can feel grounding. In a healthy Venus-Saturn dynamic, love is experienced not only through feelings, but through consistent actions. This connection can help you recognize that care is expressed in different ways. Sometimes it is found in words and affection, and sometimes it is reflected in dependability, effort, and follow-through.

At the same time, it is important to notice the difference between healthy emotional steadiness and emotional unavailability. They can look similar on the surface, but they have very different effects on a relationship. If this person has difficulty expressing affection or vulnerability, you may gradually begin lowering your expectations for emotional connection while convincing yourself that loyalty alone should meet your needs. It can be helpful to pay close attention to how you feel about yourself within this relationship. Do you feel accepted and valued, or do you often feel as though you need to prove your worth?

Consistency matters. Commitment matters. But someone staying is not the same thing as someone loving you in a way that meets your emotional needs. If you find yourself regularly longing for affection, attention, or reassurance, it may be worth asking whether loyalty alone is enough to sustain the relationship.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can make love feel like something that has to be earned. Their reserved or cautious way of expressing affection may leave you wondering where you stand, even when they care deeply. Around them, old insecurities about being wanted or valued can surface, and you may find yourself putting extra pressure on yourself to get things right. Instead of relaxing into the connection, you may start trying to prove that you are worthy of the love and reassurance you want.\n\nWhen this connection is functioning well, it can create a meaningful sense of commitment and emotional security. This person may not be naturally expressive or demonstrative with affection, but they often communicate care through reliability, responsibility, and a willingness to stay present when difficulties arise. Their approach to love may be thoughtful and serious, with a focus on creating something stable and lasting.\n\nFor many people, that can feel grounding. In a healthy Venus-Saturn dynamic, love is experienced not only through feelings, but through consistent actions. This connection can help you recognize that care is expressed in different ways. Sometimes it is found in words and affection, and sometimes it is reflected in dependability, effort, and follow-through.\n\nAt the same time, it is important to notice the difference between healthy emotional steadiness and emotional unavailability. They can look similar on the surface, but they have very different effects on a relationship. If this person has difficulty expressing affection or vulnerability, you may gradually begin lowering your expectations for emotional connection while convincing yourself that loyalty alone should meet your needs. It can be helpful to pay close attention to how you feel about yourself within this relationship. Do you feel accepted and valued, or do you often feel as though you need to prove your worth?\n\nConsistency matters. Commitment matters. But someone staying is not the same thing as someone loving you in a way that meets your emotional needs. If you find yourself regularly longing for affection, attention, or reassurance, it may be worth asking whether loyalty alone is enough to sustain the relationship."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"At the same time, it is important to notice the difference between healthy emotional steadiness and emotional unavailability. They can look similar on the surface, but they have very different effects on a relationship. If this person has difficulty expressing affection or vulnerability, you may gradually begin lowering your expectations for emotional connection while convincing yourself that loyalty alone should meet your needs. It can be helpful to pay close attention to how you feel about yourself within this relationship. Do you feel accepted and valued, or do you often feel as though you need to prove your worth?"},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Consistency matters. Commitment matters. But someone staying is not the same thing as someone loving you in a way that meets your emotional needs. If you find yourself regularly longing for affection, attention, or reassurance, it may be worth asking whether loyalty alone is enough to sustain the relationship."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-saturn_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Love that''s serious, loyal, and built to last - and can run short on warmth. The Saturn person commits and stabilizes; the Venus person may feel loved but not adored, or kept at a measured distance. Failure mode: confusing endurance with affection, or letting love feel like an obligation. Show affection actively and don''t ration it; durable and warm are different things, and you want both.","summaryDeep":"This person can make love feel like something that has to be earned. Their reserved or cautious way of expressing affection may leave you wondering where you stand, even when they care deeply. Around them, old insecurities about being wanted or valued can surface, and you may find yourself putting extra pressure on yourself to get things right. Instead of relaxing into the connection, you may start trying to prove that you are worthy of the love and reassurance you want.\n\nWhen this connection is functioning well, it can create a meaningful sense of commitment and emotional security. This person may not be naturally expressive or demonstrative with affection, but they often communicate care through reliability, responsibility, and a willingness to stay present when difficulties arise. Their approach to love may be thoughtful and serious, with a focus on creating something stable and lasting.\n\nFor many people, that can feel grounding. In a healthy Venus-Saturn dynamic, love is experienced not only through feelings, but through consistent actions. This connection can help you recognize that care is expressed in different ways. Sometimes it is found in words and affection, and sometimes it is reflected in dependability, effort, and follow-through.\n\nAt the same time, it is important to notice the difference between healthy emotional steadiness and emotional unavailability. They can look similar on the surface, but they have very different effects on a relationship. If this person has difficulty expressing affection or vulnerability, you may gradually begin lowering your expectations for emotional connection while convincing yourself that loyalty alone should meet your needs. It can be helpful to pay close attention to how you feel about yourself within this relationship. Do you feel accepted and valued, or do you often feel as though you need to prove your worth?\n\nConsistency matters. Commitment matters. But someone staying is not the same thing as someone loving you in a way that meets your emotional needs. If you find yourself regularly longing for affection, attention, or reassurance, it may be worth asking whether loyalty alone is enough to sustain the relationship.","tension":"At the same time, it is important to notice the difference between healthy emotional steadiness and emotional unavailability. They can look similar on the surface, but they have very different effects on a relationship. If this person has difficulty expressing affection or vulnerability, you may gradually begin lowering your expectations for emotional connection while convincing yourself that loyalty alone should meet your needs. It can be helpful to pay close attention to how you feel about yourself within this relationship. Do you feel accepted and valued, or do you often feel as though you need to prove your worth?","advice":"Consistency matters. Commitment matters. But someone staying is not the same thing as someone loving you in a way that meets your emotional needs. If you find yourself regularly longing for affection, attention, or reassurance, it may be worth asking whether loyalty alone is enough to sustain the relationship.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-saturn_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-saturn_opposition', 'synastry-venus-opposition-saturn', 'relationship-venus-opposition-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-saturn_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-saturn_opposition","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Opposition Saturn', null, 'This connection can bring up painful questions about love, worth, and emotional safety. You may find yourself longing for closeness while also feeling unsure whether it is truly available to you. There can be a sense of reaching for one another but missing each other emotionally, as if the care is there yet difficult to feel. One person may seek reassurance and connection, while the other responds with caution, distance, or a need to protect themselves. Over time, this can create frustration, loneliness, or self-doubt if those needs are not talked about openly and compassionately.

When this connection is functioning well, both people have an opportunity to grow. They may help you understand the importance of consistency, reliability, and following through on what you promise. You may help them recognize that love is not only about commitment, but also about emotional presence and making care visible. Together, there is potential to create a healthier balance between responsibility and emotional connection.

The difficulty often arises when the relationship starts orbiting a familiar wound. One person moves toward connection, hoping to feel secure. The other moves away, hoping to feel safe. Without awareness, this dynamic can become its own gravity, pulling both people into roles that leave them feeling unseen, misunderstood, and disconnected from the care that may still be present between them.

This connection asks for honesty about what love actually feels like in practice. Not just what is promised. Not just what is endured. What is actually received. The invitation here is to notice where loyalty has been mistaken for intimacy, or where commitment has been expected to carry the weight of unspoken needs.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection can bring up painful questions about love, worth, and emotional safety. You may find yourself longing for closeness while also feeling unsure whether it is truly available to you. There can be a sense of reaching for one another but missing each other emotionally, as if the care is there yet difficult to feel. One person may seek reassurance and connection, while the other responds with caution, distance, or a need to protect themselves. Over time, this can create frustration, loneliness, or self-doubt if those needs are not talked about openly and compassionately.\n\nWhen this connection is functioning well, both people have an opportunity to grow. They may help you understand the importance of consistency, reliability, and following through on what you promise. You may help them recognize that love is not only about commitment, but also about emotional presence and making care visible. Together, there is potential to create a healthier balance between responsibility and emotional connection.\n\nThe difficulty often arises when the relationship starts orbiting a familiar wound. One person moves toward connection, hoping to feel secure. The other moves away, hoping to feel safe. Without awareness, this dynamic can become its own gravity, pulling both people into roles that leave them feeling unseen, misunderstood, and disconnected from the care that may still be present between them.\n\nThis connection asks for honesty about what love actually feels like in practice. Not just what is promised. Not just what is endured. What is actually received. The invitation here is to notice where loyalty has been mistaken for intimacy, or where commitment has been expected to carry the weight of unspoken needs."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The difficulty often arises when the relationship starts orbiting a familiar wound. One person moves toward connection, hoping to feel secure. The other moves away, hoping to feel safe. Without awareness, this dynamic can become its own gravity, pulling both people into roles that leave them feeling unseen, misunderstood, and disconnected from the care that may still be present between them."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This connection asks for honesty about what love actually feels like in practice. Not just what is promised. Not just what is endured. What is actually received. The invitation here is to notice where loyalty has been mistaken for intimacy, or where commitment has been expected to carry the weight of unspoken needs."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-saturn_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Affection and restriction face off, often through real-world limits: money, distance, timing, or one person''s fear of committing. Failure mode: one chases warmth while the other enforces caution, and both feel starved. Decide together what''s worth committing to, and don''t let one person carry all the longing.","summaryDeep":"This connection can bring up painful questions about love, worth, and emotional safety. You may find yourself longing for closeness while also feeling unsure whether it is truly available to you. There can be a sense of reaching for one another but missing each other emotionally, as if the care is there yet difficult to feel. One person may seek reassurance and connection, while the other responds with caution, distance, or a need to protect themselves. Over time, this can create frustration, loneliness, or self-doubt if those needs are not talked about openly and compassionately.\n\nWhen this connection is functioning well, both people have an opportunity to grow. They may help you understand the importance of consistency, reliability, and following through on what you promise. You may help them recognize that love is not only about commitment, but also about emotional presence and making care visible. Together, there is potential to create a healthier balance between responsibility and emotional connection.\n\nThe difficulty often arises when the relationship starts orbiting a familiar wound. One person moves toward connection, hoping to feel secure. The other moves away, hoping to feel safe. Without awareness, this dynamic can become its own gravity, pulling both people into roles that leave them feeling unseen, misunderstood, and disconnected from the care that may still be present between them.\n\nThis connection asks for honesty about what love actually feels like in practice. Not just what is promised. Not just what is endured. What is actually received. The invitation here is to notice where loyalty has been mistaken for intimacy, or where commitment has been expected to carry the weight of unspoken needs.","tension":"The difficulty often arises when the relationship starts orbiting a familiar wound. One person moves toward connection, hoping to feel secure. The other moves away, hoping to feel safe. Without awareness, this dynamic can become its own gravity, pulling both people into roles that leave them feeling unseen, misunderstood, and disconnected from the care that may still be present between them.","advice":"This connection asks for honesty about what love actually feels like in practice. Not just what is promised. Not just what is endured. What is actually received. The invitation here is to notice where loyalty has been mistaken for intimacy, or where commitment has been expected to carry the weight of unspoken needs.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-saturn_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-saturn_sextile', 'synastry-venus-sextile-saturn', 'relationship-venus-sextile-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-saturn_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-saturn_sextile","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Sextile Saturn', null, 'This connection tends to develop through small, steady choices rather than dramatic moments. Trust is built gradually as both people learn they can rely on each other. Over time, the relationship gains strength from simple acts of dependability, such as keeping promises, being honest, showing up when it matters, and proving through actions that the bond is worth investing in.

When this aspect is working well, it teaches both people that love is something you build, not something you stumble into. Care becomes more intentional. Commitment gives affection somewhere to land. This person may encourage you to honor your needs, strengthen your boundaries, and take your own worth seriously. They can remind you that the relationships that endure are often the ones that are nurtured slowly, with consistency and care.

The invitation here is to participate. Saturn asks for effort, presence, and accountability. If one person waits to feel completely safe before opening up, or if vulnerability stays hidden behind too many defenses, the connection can feel more distant than it needs to. The capacity for devotion exists, but it has to be practiced to become tangible.

This aspect asks for patience without abandoning yourself. It asks for discernment without shutting love out. It asks both people to express care in ways that can actually be felt and received. Over time, this connection can grow into something solid and dependable, built through consistent effort and a shared willingness to care for it intentionally.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection tends to develop through small, steady choices rather than dramatic moments. Trust is built gradually as both people learn they can rely on each other. Over time, the relationship gains strength from simple acts of dependability, such as keeping promises, being honest, showing up when it matters, and proving through actions that the bond is worth investing in.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it teaches both people that love is something you build, not something you stumble into. Care becomes more intentional. Commitment gives affection somewhere to land. This person may encourage you to honor your needs, strengthen your boundaries, and take your own worth seriously. They can remind you that the relationships that endure are often the ones that are nurtured slowly, with consistency and care.\n\nThe invitation here is to participate. Saturn asks for effort, presence, and accountability. If one person waits to feel completely safe before opening up, or if vulnerability stays hidden behind too many defenses, the connection can feel more distant than it needs to. The capacity for devotion exists, but it has to be practiced to become tangible.\n\nThis aspect asks for patience without abandoning yourself. It asks for discernment without shutting love out. It asks both people to express care in ways that can actually be felt and received. Over time, this connection can grow into something solid and dependable, built through consistent effort and a shared willingness to care for it intentionally."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The invitation here is to participate. Saturn asks for effort, presence, and accountability. If one person waits to feel completely safe before opening up, or if vulnerability stays hidden behind too many defenses, the connection can feel more distant than it needs to. The capacity for devotion exists, but it has to be practiced to become tangible."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"This aspect asks for patience without abandoning yourself. It asks for discernment without shutting love out. It asks both people to express care in ways that can actually be felt and received. Over time, this connection can grow into something solid and dependable, built through consistent effort and a shared willingness to care for it intentionally."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-saturn_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A steadying, supportive contact for love and money. Commitment comes without much resistance and the relationship feels grounded. Failure mode: not formalizing what''s quietly solid. Make the steady choice - this aspect rewards building.","summaryDeep":"This connection tends to develop through small, steady choices rather than dramatic moments. Trust is built gradually as both people learn they can rely on each other. Over time, the relationship gains strength from simple acts of dependability, such as keeping promises, being honest, showing up when it matters, and proving through actions that the bond is worth investing in.\n\nWhen this aspect is working well, it teaches both people that love is something you build, not something you stumble into. Care becomes more intentional. Commitment gives affection somewhere to land. This person may encourage you to honor your needs, strengthen your boundaries, and take your own worth seriously. They can remind you that the relationships that endure are often the ones that are nurtured slowly, with consistency and care.\n\nThe invitation here is to participate. Saturn asks for effort, presence, and accountability. If one person waits to feel completely safe before opening up, or if vulnerability stays hidden behind too many defenses, the connection can feel more distant than it needs to. The capacity for devotion exists, but it has to be practiced to become tangible.\n\nThis aspect asks for patience without abandoning yourself. It asks for discernment without shutting love out. It asks both people to express care in ways that can actually be felt and received. Over time, this connection can grow into something solid and dependable, built through consistent effort and a shared willingness to care for it intentionally.","tension":"The invitation here is to participate. Saturn asks for effort, presence, and accountability. If one person waits to feel completely safe before opening up, or if vulnerability stays hidden behind too many defenses, the connection can feel more distant than it needs to. The capacity for devotion exists, but it has to be practiced to become tangible.","advice":"This aspect asks for patience without abandoning yourself. It asks for discernment without shutting love out. It asks both people to express care in ways that can actually be felt and received. Over time, this connection can grow into something solid and dependable, built through consistent effort and a shared willingness to care for it intentionally.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-saturn_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-saturn_square', 'synastry-venus-square-saturn', 'relationship-venus-square-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-saturn_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-saturn_square","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Square Saturn', null, 'This connection has a way of turning relationship tension into a question about your worth. When affection feels limited, inconsistent, or difficult to access, you may start focusing on what you need to do differently to receive more of it. The danger is that their restraint can begin to feel personal, as though the distance between you says something about your value. In reality, what you are experiencing may have far more to do with their fears, defenses, or way of relating than with anything lacking in you.

This aspect asks you to get honest about what love actually feels like. Are you being cared for, or are you constantly trying to earn approval? Are your needs being respected, or are you pushing them aside to keep the relationship working?

The challenge is falling into self-abandonment. You may keep adjusting, waiting, and trying harder, believing that if you are patient enough, easy enough, or understanding enough, the affection you want will finally appear. Flexibility is healthy. Losing yourself to maintain a connection is not. If one person keeps withholding, criticizing, or avoiding vulnerability while the other keeps overextending themselves to compensate, the pattern can become painful and difficult to sustain. But if both people are willing to acknowledge the problem, communicate honestly, and take responsibility for their own insecurities, this aspect can become a turning point rather than a reason for separation.

If someone struggles to give affection, reassurance, or emotional presence, that tells you something about them. It does not automatically tell you something about your value. Too many people stay stuck here, working harder and harder to earn what should be given freely in a healthy relationship. Take the insight this connection offers.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This connection has a way of turning relationship tension into a question about your worth. When affection feels limited, inconsistent, or difficult to access, you may start focusing on what you need to do differently to receive more of it. The danger is that their restraint can begin to feel personal, as though the distance between you says something about your value. In reality, what you are experiencing may have far more to do with their fears, defenses, or way of relating than with anything lacking in you.\n\nThis aspect asks you to get honest about what love actually feels like. Are you being cared for, or are you constantly trying to earn approval? Are your needs being respected, or are you pushing them aside to keep the relationship working?\n\nThe challenge is falling into self-abandonment. You may keep adjusting, waiting, and trying harder, believing that if you are patient enough, easy enough, or understanding enough, the affection you want will finally appear. Flexibility is healthy. Losing yourself to maintain a connection is not. If one person keeps withholding, criticizing, or avoiding vulnerability while the other keeps overextending themselves to compensate, the pattern can become painful and difficult to sustain. But if both people are willing to acknowledge the problem, communicate honestly, and take responsibility for their own insecurities, this aspect can become a turning point rather than a reason for separation.\n\nIf someone struggles to give affection, reassurance, or emotional presence, that tells you something about them. It does not automatically tell you something about your value. Too many people stay stuck here, working harder and harder to earn what should be given freely in a healthy relationship. Take the insight this connection offers."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is falling into self-abandonment. You may keep adjusting, waiting, and trying harder, believing that if you are patient enough, easy enough, or understanding enough, the affection you want will finally appear. Flexibility is healthy. Losing yourself to maintain a connection is not. If one person keeps withholding, criticizing, or avoiding vulnerability while the other keeps overextending themselves to compensate, the pattern can become painful and difficult to sustain. But if both people are willing to acknowledge the problem, communicate honestly, and take responsibility for their own insecurities, this aspect can become a turning point rather than a reason for separation."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"If someone struggles to give affection, reassurance, or emotional presence, that tells you something about them. It does not automatically tell you something about your value. Too many people stay stuck here, working harder and harder to earn what should be given freely in a healthy relationship. Take the insight this connection offers."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-saturn_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Love pressed against limitation. Distance, scarcity, duty, or a reality check - affection that keeps hitting a wall. Failure mode: staying for the structure while the warmth dies, and calling the coldness maturity. Address the chill honestly; commitment without affection is a contract, not a relationship.","summaryDeep":"This connection has a way of turning relationship tension into a question about your worth. When affection feels limited, inconsistent, or difficult to access, you may start focusing on what you need to do differently to receive more of it. The danger is that their restraint can begin to feel personal, as though the distance between you says something about your value. In reality, what you are experiencing may have far more to do with their fears, defenses, or way of relating than with anything lacking in you.\n\nThis aspect asks you to get honest about what love actually feels like. Are you being cared for, or are you constantly trying to earn approval? Are your needs being respected, or are you pushing them aside to keep the relationship working?\n\nThe challenge is falling into self-abandonment. You may keep adjusting, waiting, and trying harder, believing that if you are patient enough, easy enough, or understanding enough, the affection you want will finally appear. Flexibility is healthy. Losing yourself to maintain a connection is not. If one person keeps withholding, criticizing, or avoiding vulnerability while the other keeps overextending themselves to compensate, the pattern can become painful and difficult to sustain. But if both people are willing to acknowledge the problem, communicate honestly, and take responsibility for their own insecurities, this aspect can become a turning point rather than a reason for separation.\n\nIf someone struggles to give affection, reassurance, or emotional presence, that tells you something about them. It does not automatically tell you something about your value. Too many people stay stuck here, working harder and harder to earn what should be given freely in a healthy relationship. Take the insight this connection offers.","tension":"The challenge is falling into self-abandonment. You may keep adjusting, waiting, and trying harder, believing that if you are patient enough, easy enough, or understanding enough, the affection you want will finally appear. Flexibility is healthy. Losing yourself to maintain a connection is not. If one person keeps withholding, criticizing, or avoiding vulnerability while the other keeps overextending themselves to compensate, the pattern can become painful and difficult to sustain. But if both people are willing to acknowledge the problem, communicate honestly, and take responsibility for their own insecurities, this aspect can become a turning point rather than a reason for separation.","advice":"If someone struggles to give affection, reassurance, or emotional presence, that tells you something about them. It does not automatically tell you something about your value. Too many people stay stuck here, working harder and harder to earn what should be given freely in a healthy relationship. Take the insight this connection offers.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"saturn","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-saturn_trine', 'synastry-venus-trine-saturn', 'relationship-venus-trine-saturn']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-saturn_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-saturn_trine","importedStatus":"REVIEWED"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Trine Saturn', null, 'This person can help bring steadiness into your life. They may express care through consistency, reliability, and practical support rather than grand gestures. Over time, their presence can create a sense of trust that feels earned, grounded, and real.

When this connection is working well, the relationship offers stability without demanding that you sacrifice yourself for it. This person may encourage you to take your values seriously, honor your commitments, and recognize your own worth. Their support can help you feel more rooted in what matters and more confident in your ability to build something lasting.

One of the gifts of this aspect is that trust grows through follow-through. Intimacy deepens when people respect each other''s boundaries and show up for one another in meaningful ways. This person may teach you that security is not the opposite of connection. Sometimes it is the very thing that allows connection to deepen.

The challenge is becoming so focused on responsibility that the relationship loses warmth or flexibility. It can be easy to prioritize obligations, routines, or long-term goals while neglecting enjoyment, appreciation, or emotional connection.

The healthiest expression of this aspect balances stability with genuine care. Strong relationships need reliability, but they also need moments of appreciation, openness, and shared enjoyment. When both are present, this connection can become a lasting source of support and growth.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"This person can help bring steadiness into your life. They may express care through consistency, reliability, and practical support rather than grand gestures. Over time, their presence can create a sense of trust that feels earned, grounded, and real.\n\nWhen this connection is working well, the relationship offers stability without demanding that you sacrifice yourself for it. This person may encourage you to take your values seriously, honor your commitments, and recognize your own worth. Their support can help you feel more rooted in what matters and more confident in your ability to build something lasting.\n\nOne of the gifts of this aspect is that trust grows through follow-through. Intimacy deepens when people respect each other''s boundaries and show up for one another in meaningful ways. This person may teach you that security is not the opposite of connection. Sometimes it is the very thing that allows connection to deepen.\n\nThe challenge is becoming so focused on responsibility that the relationship loses warmth or flexibility. It can be easy to prioritize obligations, routines, or long-term goals while neglecting enjoyment, appreciation, or emotional connection.\n\nThe healthiest expression of this aspect balances stability with genuine care. Strong relationships need reliability, but they also need moments of appreciation, openness, and shared enjoyment. When both are present, this connection can become a lasting source of support and growth."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The challenge is becoming so focused on responsibility that the relationship loses warmth or flexibility. It can be easy to prioritize obligations, routines, or long-term goals while neglecting enjoyment, appreciation, or emotional connection."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"The healthiest expression of this aspect balances stability with genuine care. Strong relationships need reliability, but they also need moments of appreciation, openness, and shared enjoyment. When both are present, this connection can become a lasting source of support and growth."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-saturn_trine","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"Loyalty and stability flow naturally. Good for commitment, shared finances, and the long haul. Failure mode: the warmth stays understated. Lock in the security and keep affection visible so stable doesn''t read as distant.","summaryDeep":"This person can help bring steadiness into your life. They may express care through consistency, reliability, and practical support rather than grand gestures. Over time, their presence can create a sense of trust that feels earned, grounded, and real.\n\nWhen this connection is working well, the relationship offers stability without demanding that you sacrifice yourself for it. This person may encourage you to take your values seriously, honor your commitments, and recognize your own worth. Their support can help you feel more rooted in what matters and more confident in your ability to build something lasting.\n\nOne of the gifts of this aspect is that trust grows through follow-through. Intimacy deepens when people respect each other''s boundaries and show up for one another in meaningful ways. This person may teach you that security is not the opposite of connection. Sometimes it is the very thing that allows connection to deepen.\n\nThe challenge is becoming so focused on responsibility that the relationship loses warmth or flexibility. It can be easy to prioritize obligations, routines, or long-term goals while neglecting enjoyment, appreciation, or emotional connection.\n\nThe healthiest expression of this aspect balances stability with genuine care. Strong relationships need reliability, but they also need moments of appreciation, openness, and shared enjoyment. When both are present, this connection can become a lasting source of support and growth.","tension":"The challenge is becoming so focused on responsibility that the relationship loses warmth or flexibility. It can be easy to prioritize obligations, routines, or long-term goals while neglecting enjoyment, appreciation, or emotional connection.","advice":"The healthiest expression of this aspect balances stability with genuine care. Strong relationships need reliability, but they also need moments of appreciation, openness, and shared enjoyment. When both are present, this connection can become a lasting source of support and growth.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"REVIEWED","authoringStatus":"draft","weight":4}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"sun","aspect":"conjunction"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-sun_conjunction', 'synastry-venus-conjunction-sun', 'relationship-venus-conjunction-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-sun_conjunction.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-sun_conjunction","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Conjunction Sun', 'There''s an easy fondness here. One person''s way of being just feels likable to the other, almost without trying. You may enjoy each other''s company right away, and there can be a real sense of being appreciated for who you already are.', 'There''s an easy fondness here. One person''s way of being just feels likable to the other, almost without trying. You may enjoy each other''s company right away, and there can be a real sense of being appreciated for who you already are.

This tends to feel good without needing much explanation. Compliments come more naturally. Affection is easier to show. Being together may feel pleasant, warm, and simple in a way that makes both people want to come back for more. It''s the kind of connection where you actually like the person, not just want their attention.

The thing to watch is that pleasant can stay shallow. If everything stays nice and nobody ever pushes past the easy surface, the connection can stall at "we get along great" without becoming much deeper.

Let yourself enjoy it, but don''t stop at nice. Liking someone is a good start, not the whole story.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There''s an easy fondness here. One person''s way of being just feels likable to the other, almost without trying. You may enjoy each other''s company right away, and there can be a real sense of being appreciated for who you already are.\n\nThis tends to feel good without needing much explanation. Compliments come more naturally. Affection is easier to show. Being together may feel pleasant, warm, and simple in a way that makes both people want to come back for more. It''s the kind of connection where you actually like the person, not just want their attention.\n\nThe thing to watch is that pleasant can stay shallow. If everything stays nice and nobody ever pushes past the easy surface, the connection can stall at \"we get along great\" without becoming much deeper.\n\nLet yourself enjoy it, but don''t stop at nice. Liking someone is a good start, not the whole story."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The thing to watch is that pleasant can stay shallow. If everything stays nice and nobody ever pushes past the easy surface, the connection can stall at \"we get along great\" without becoming much deeper."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Let yourself enjoy it, but don''t stop at nice. Liking someone is a good start, not the whole story."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-sun_conjunction","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s identity. The conjunction fuses them - intense and inseparable.","summaryDeep":"There''s an easy fondness here. One person''s way of being just feels likable to the other, almost without trying. You may enjoy each other''s company right away, and there can be a real sense of being appreciated for who you already are.\n\nThis tends to feel good without needing much explanation. Compliments come more naturally. Affection is easier to show. Being together may feel pleasant, warm, and simple in a way that makes both people want to come back for more. It''s the kind of connection where you actually like the person, not just want their attention.\n\nThe thing to watch is that pleasant can stay shallow. If everything stays nice and nobody ever pushes past the easy surface, the connection can stall at \"we get along great\" without becoming much deeper.\n\nLet yourself enjoy it, but don''t stop at nice. Liking someone is a good start, not the whole story.","tension":"The thing to watch is that pleasant can stay shallow. If everything stays nice and nobody ever pushes past the easy surface, the connection can stall at \"we get along great\" without becoming much deeper.","advice":"Let yourself enjoy it, but don''t stop at nice. Liking someone is a good start, not the whole story.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"sun","aspect":"opposition"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-sun_opposition', 'synastry-venus-opposition-sun', 'relationship-venus-opposition-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-sun_opposition.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-sun_opposition","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Opposition Sun', 'There''s attraction here, but you may not always like or value things in the same way. One person can find the other charming partly because they''re different, but that same difference can also make the connection feel a little uneven.', 'There''s attraction here, but you may not always like or value things in the same way. One person can find the other charming partly because they''re different, but that same difference can also make the connection feel a little uneven.

At its best, this is the pull of someone who brings a different style, mood, or way of showing affection. They may make life feel more interesting, more beautiful, or just less like your usual routine. At its worst, you keep running into the gap between what one person means as love and what the other person actually receives.

The problem is expecting appreciation to look the same on both sides. The attraction may be real, but you may not always agree on what feels thoughtful, romantic, or worth caring about.

Appreciate the difference without making it a test. Find what you both enjoy, instead of trying to win the argument about taste.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There''s attraction here, but you may not always like or value things in the same way. One person can find the other charming partly because they''re different, but that same difference can also make the connection feel a little uneven.\n\nAt its best, this is the pull of someone who brings a different style, mood, or way of showing affection. They may make life feel more interesting, more beautiful, or just less like your usual routine. At its worst, you keep running into the gap between what one person means as love and what the other person actually receives.\n\nThe problem is expecting appreciation to look the same on both sides. The attraction may be real, but you may not always agree on what feels thoughtful, romantic, or worth caring about.\n\nAppreciate the difference without making it a test. Find what you both enjoy, instead of trying to win the argument about taste."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The problem is expecting appreciation to look the same on both sides. The attraction may be real, but you may not always agree on what feels thoughtful, romantic, or worth caring about."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Appreciate the difference without making it a test. Find what you both enjoy, instead of trying to win the argument about taste."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-sun_opposition","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s identity. The opposition pulls them into push-and-pull.","summaryDeep":"There''s attraction here, but you may not always like or value things in the same way. One person can find the other charming partly because they''re different, but that same difference can also make the connection feel a little uneven.\n\nAt its best, this is the pull of someone who brings a different style, mood, or way of showing affection. They may make life feel more interesting, more beautiful, or just less like your usual routine. At its worst, you keep running into the gap between what one person means as love and what the other person actually receives.\n\nThe problem is expecting appreciation to look the same on both sides. The attraction may be real, but you may not always agree on what feels thoughtful, romantic, or worth caring about.\n\nAppreciate the difference without making it a test. Find what you both enjoy, instead of trying to win the argument about taste.","tension":"The problem is expecting appreciation to look the same on both sides. The attraction may be real, but you may not always agree on what feels thoughtful, romantic, or worth caring about.","advice":"Appreciate the difference without making it a test. Find what you both enjoy, instead of trying to win the argument about taste.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-sun_sextile', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"sun","aspect":"sextile"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-sun_sextile', 'synastry-venus-sextile-sun', 'relationship-venus-sextile-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-sun_sextile.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-sun_sextile","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Sextile Sun', 'There''s a warm, likable fit here, and it gets better when both people put something into it. One person''s way of being and the other person''s affection support each other well, but the warmth tends to open more when you actually lean into it.', 'There''s a warm, likable fit here, and it gets better when both people put something into it. One person''s way of being and the other person''s affection support each other well, but the warmth tends to open more when you actually lean into it.

This often shows up as a connection that gets nicer the more you engage. A little appreciation goes a long way. Small kindnesses are noticed. The fondness is available, but it becomes stronger when someone bothers to show it.

Where it falls flat is leaving the good feeling unspoken. Both people may assume the other knows they''re appreciated, and then the connection stays quieter than it needs to be.

Say the nice thing out loud. This one grows every time someone bothers to express it.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There''s a warm, likable fit here, and it gets better when both people put something into it. One person''s way of being and the other person''s affection support each other well, but the warmth tends to open more when you actually lean into it.\n\nThis often shows up as a connection that gets nicer the more you engage. A little appreciation goes a long way. Small kindnesses are noticed. The fondness is available, but it becomes stronger when someone bothers to show it.\n\nWhere it falls flat is leaving the good feeling unspoken. Both people may assume the other knows they''re appreciated, and then the connection stays quieter than it needs to be.\n\nSay the nice thing out loud. This one grows every time someone bothers to express it."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"Where it falls flat is leaving the good feeling unspoken. Both people may assume the other knows they''re appreciated, and then the connection stays quieter than it needs to be."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Say the nice thing out loud. This one grows every time someone bothers to express it."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-sun_sextile","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s identity. The sextile supports them, if you act on it.","summaryDeep":"There''s a warm, likable fit here, and it gets better when both people put something into it. One person''s way of being and the other person''s affection support each other well, but the warmth tends to open more when you actually lean into it.\n\nThis often shows up as a connection that gets nicer the more you engage. A little appreciation goes a long way. Small kindnesses are noticed. The fondness is available, but it becomes stronger when someone bothers to show it.\n\nWhere it falls flat is leaving the good feeling unspoken. Both people may assume the other knows they''re appreciated, and then the connection stays quieter than it needs to be.\n\nSay the nice thing out loud. This one grows every time someone bothers to express it.","tension":"Where it falls flat is leaving the good feeling unspoken. Both people may assume the other knows they''re appreciated, and then the connection stays quieter than it needs to be.","advice":"Say the nice thing out loud. This one grows every time someone bothers to express it.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-sun_square', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"sun","aspect":"square"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-sun_square', 'synastry-venus-square-sun', 'relationship-venus-square-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-sun_square.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-sun_square","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Square Sun', 'There''s attraction here, but it can come with a little friction around affection, taste, or feeling appreciated. One person''s natural style may not quite match how the other person likes to give or receive warmth, so the fondness is real but slightly out of step.', 'There''s attraction here, but it can come with a little friction around affection, taste, or feeling appreciated. One person''s natural style may not quite match how the other person likes to give or receive warmth, so the fondness is real but slightly out of step.

It often shows up in small ways. One person shows they care in a way the other doesn''t fully register. Compliments land oddly. Gestures get misread. Nobody''s being cold; the affection just keeps arriving in the wrong key.

The trap is reading the mismatch as a lack of caring. The feeling may be there, but the delivery keeps getting crossed.

Say what actually makes you feel appreciated instead of waiting to receive it the way you''d give it. This one smooths out when both people stop expecting love to arrive in their exact language.', '{"sections":[{"heading":"Deep meaning","body":"There''s attraction here, but it can come with a little friction around affection, taste, or feeling appreciated. One person''s natural style may not quite match how the other person likes to give or receive warmth, so the fondness is real but slightly out of step.\n\nIt often shows up in small ways. One person shows they care in a way the other doesn''t fully register. Compliments land oddly. Gestures get misread. Nobody''s being cold; the affection just keeps arriving in the wrong key.\n\nThe trap is reading the mismatch as a lack of caring. The feeling may be there, but the delivery keeps getting crossed.\n\nSay what actually makes you feel appreciated instead of waiting to receive it the way you''d give it. This one smooths out when both people stop expecting love to arrive in their exact language."},{"heading":"Tension","body":"The trap is reading the mismatch as a lack of caring. The feeling may be there, but the delivery keeps getting crossed."},{"heading":"Advice","body":"Say what actually makes you feel appreciated instead of waiting to receive it the way you''d give it. This one smooths out when both people stop expecting love to arrive in their exact language."}],"synastryKb":{"id":"A-venus_B-sun_square","kind":"interaspect","plainTranslation":"A''s love and values meets B''s identity. The square puts them in friction.","summaryDeep":"There''s attraction here, but it can come with a little friction around affection, taste, or feeling appreciated. One person''s natural style may not quite match how the other person likes to give or receive warmth, so the fondness is real but slightly out of step.\n\nIt often shows up in small ways. One person shows they care in a way the other doesn''t fully register. Compliments land oddly. Gestures get misread. Nobody''s being cold; the affection just keeps arriving in the wrong key.\n\nThe trap is reading the mismatch as a lack of caring. The feeling may be there, but the delivery keeps getting crossed.\n\nSay what actually makes you feel appreciated instead of waiting to receive it the way you''d give it. This one smooths out when both people stop expecting love to arrive in their exact language.","tension":"The trap is reading the mismatch as a lack of caring. The feeling may be there, but the delivery keeps getting crossed.","advice":"Say what actually makes you feel appreciated instead of waiting to receive it the way you''d give it. This one smooths out when both people stop expecting love to arrive in their exact language.","policy":"Governed by synastry-policy. Descriptive, not deterministic; intensity is never treated as obligation, safety concerns override astrology.","note":"Synced from authored synastry bundle synastry-authored__19_ (2).json.","status":"DRAFT","authoringStatus":"locked","weight":1}}'::jsonb, 'synastry_aspect', 'Seeded from authored synastry KB. summaryShort is preserved as NULL when absent or null.', now()),
  ('A-venus_B-sun_trine', 'synastry', 'in_depth', 'LIVE', 'synastry-aspect', null::date, '{"kind":"interaspect","planetA":"venus","planetB":"sun","aspect":"trine"}'::jsonb, ARRAY['A-venus_B-sun_trine', 'synastry-venus-trine-sun', 'relationship-venus-trine-sun']::text[], '{"contentType":"synastry-kb-seed","source":"packages/astro-knowledge","sourcePath":"packages/astro-knowledge/data/synastry/aspects/A-venus_B-sun_trine.json","collection":"synastry/aspects","kbId":"A-venus_B-sun_trine","importedStatus":"DRAFT"}'::jsonb, 'synastry-kb-v1', null, 'Venus Trine Sun', 'This is a naturally warm, easy kind of connection. One person''s way of being sits well with the other person''s sense of what is lovable, so affection tends to flow without much effort.', 'This is a naturally warm, easy kind of connection. One person''s way of being sits well with the other person''s sense of what is lovable, so affection tends to flow without much effort.

There''s an unforced charm here. You enjoy each other, you appreciate each other, and there usually isn''t much drama around feeling valued. It''s the kind of ease that makes a relationship comfortable to be in and easy to stay close to.

The risk is the usual one with easy contacts: because the warmth comes naturally, neither person may think to deepen it or take care of it. A connection this pleasant can drift on autopilot.

